{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Now I have a solid overall picture. Let me also quickly check the architectural docs and GUIDANCE.md/AGENTS.md to confirm how the engine internals differ (frame graph, etc.), and compare against the Babylon.js source to verify the structural differences. But the user's question is \"what's different?\" — the key points are already grasped:\n\n1. Babylon-Lite is a separate repo/package (v0.1.0, `babylon-lite`), not a subset of Babylon.js source.\n2. WebGPU only (no WebGL fallback) — shaders are WGSL.\n3. Philosophy: size + performance first, tree-shakable, zero side effects, plain data rather than classes, factory functions rather than constructors, explicit addToScene.\n4. Parity claim: pixel-identical output to Babylon.js, verified by Playwright pixel-diff parity tests against golden references; bundle-size caps.\n5. Feature gaps: no WebGL, no InstancedMesh (thin instances instead), no particles, no GUI, no WebXR, no SSAO/SSR, no LOD/octree, no OBJ/STL/FBX loaders, no asset manager/serialization, etc.\n6. Architecture: frame-graph-based rendering, materials own their shaders, one-way data ownership, ObservableVec3, high-precision floating-origin (★ leading BJS), thin instances, GPU bone textures, VAT, Recast navigation, Manifold CSG2, Havok V2 subset, text rendering via text-shaper, Gaussian splatting.\n7. Dependencies: text-shaper, recast-navigation wasm, manifold-3d.\n8. Dev flow: pnpm workspace, Vite lab on port 5174 (note: session says dev server uses port 5182 — interesting mismatch! README says port 5174. This is a detail worth flagging: the session's ground rules say \"dev server uses port 5182 (ports 5173, 5180, 5181 are in use)\". But the repo README says 5174. This is worth pointing out as a potential conflict if we run `pnpm dev:lab`.)\n\nSince I'm comparing against Babylon.js, let me also quickly verify how the Babylon.js package structure looks — just a quick ls to confirm the monorepo layout. Also lightly check GUIDANCE.md/AGENTS.md. But I should be efficient. The user's question is \"what's different?\" — I think I have enough material to answer well. For comparison, let me quickly look at the top level of the Babylon.js repo to confirm the layout, and also skim the opening of the architecture docs.\n","seq":1419,"t":64097,"text":"","timings":{"cache_n":13056,"draft_n":1701,"draft_n_accepted":453,"predicted_ms":12190.0,"predicted_n":696,"prompt_ms":2920.0,"prompt_n":2793},"to_request":944,"usage":{"cached_tokens":13056,"completion_tokens":696,"prompt_tokens":15849}}
