{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Important: `attachFreeControl` is **drag-based** mouse look, not true pointer-lock FPS look (it uses pointer capture + drag delta). The doc comment says \"mouse drag or pointer lock\", but the code shows a drag-based implementation (setPointerCapture, delta while dragging). So FPS needs: pointer lock for look (manual, small custom code — mouse delta while locked), and WASD for movement (attachFreeControl handles WASD but with inertia. For Quake-style, custom movement is needed — air control, no inertia decay, jumping).\n\nAlso, I didn't find a runtime vertex update API in mesh.ts. Let me check more thoroughly: search for \"update\" in the mesh directory, and check `compute-normals.ts` (it computes normals from positions — suggests positions can be modified). And also check the ground creation from heightmap.\n\nFurther checks:\n- `createGround` options — does it support heightmaps?\n- How to delete meshes at runtime (`removeFromScene`)?\n- Thin instance API for debris.\n- Physics: `havok-queries.ts` (raycast API), `havok-heightfield.ts`.\n- Text API for HUD.\n\nLet me batch a few greps together.\n","seq":5661,"t":223597,"text":"","timings":{"cache_n":27136,"draft_n":1197,"draft_n_accepted":346,"predicted_ms":9880.0,"predicted_n":517,"prompt_ms":2580.0,"prompt_n":2224},"to_request":5357,"usage":{"cached_tokens":27136,"completion_tokens":517,"prompt_tokens":29360}}
