{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"One record (map) was discarded by the \"groundedness gate\" — apparently it was judged insufficiently grounded. No problem. The key facts remain in the conversation and the other records. Not going to retry with a longer justification. The conversation itself preserves the details. Moving on.\n\nNow, the response: confirm the scope (\"noise terrain, bots first, multiplayer later\"), mention the navmesh discovery for bots (it's in the conversation above), make my recommendation on the destruction approach (tile removal + noise grid), and propose a transition to the plan phase.\n\nThe user's message was terse and directive — they're steering, not debating. I'll state my recommendation and propose the transition. The transition proposal ends the turn.\n","seq":12439,"t":496198,"text":"\n\nRecorded (one entry — the API-anchor map — got dropped by the groundedness gate; the details are in this conversation and I'll re-ground them against source during planning).\n\nYour scope note sharpens the plan in two ways:\n\n- **Noise terrain** fits the vertex-grid path perfectly: generate heights from a noise function into a `createFlatGroundData` grid (no heightmap image needed), which is exactly the substrate for tile/vertex destruction.\n- **Bots** are the big win: Lite ships a full Recast navigation module (`createNavMesh` from meshes, `computePath`, `createNavCrowd` with `agentGoto`/`updateNavCrowd`, and dynamic obstacles via `addBoxObstacle`/`removeObstacle`) — so bots get real pathfinding on the generated terrain, and `updateNavMeshObstacles` can even let them re-route when terrain is destroyed. Bots can reuse the same character controller + picking + damage pipeline as the player, so multiplayer later is a transport swap, not a rewrite.\n\nMy recommendation stands: **tile removal** as the destruction model (robust physics, real fall-through holes), with vertex displacement of surviving edge tiles as a cheap visual flourish. Multiplayer stays out of scope for this iteration.\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":46848,"draft_n":1358,"draft_n_accepted":344,"predicted_ms":12780.0,"predicted_n":538,"prompt_ms":990.0,"prompt_n":592},"to_request":12069,"usage":{"cached_tokens":46848,"completion_tokens":538,"prompt_tokens":47440}}
