inding before starting). #69 is the constraint. Not a full duplicate → KEEP #3. OK.\n\nAlso double-check #49 vs #46/#45: #49 is a decision synthesizing them; #45/#46 are pointers to individual functions. Not duplicates (different fields, #49 is a conclusion). KEEP.\n\nAnd #66 vs #67/#68: #66 is the API anchors (dropped map record), #67 is scope, #68 is open. #66 is unique content → KEEP.\n\nNow, the output format: exactly 69 lines, nothing else. No extra text. Let me carefully construct the final answer.\n\nOne more sanity check on #42's correction: the original note says \"This is the entire export function surface of the mesh module\" — my correction scopes it to 3 files. Also the original caveat says \"an exported class method or arrow-function const could still exist — I haven't verified that yet\" — my version keeps that caveat. Good.\n\nAnd #35: original says \"No CCD / continuous-collision export visible in the physics API\" — I scoped my correction to the 3 files I grepped. Good.\n\nAlso, should I re-verify #47's line 1043 for applyPhysicsImpulse? From grep output: \"/src/physics/havok.ts:1043:export function applyPhysicsImpulse(world: PhysicsWorld, body: PhysicsBody, impulse: Vec3, point?: Vec3): void;\" Yes, 1043. And 518: \"export function applyPhysicsBodyImpulse(body: PhysicsBody, impulse: Vec3, location: Vec3): void;\" Yes. Good.\n\nFinal output — exactly 69 lines.\n","seq":19433,"t":841234,"text":"\n\n1. REMOVE — stale: the \"which Babylon\" question was resolved in turn 2 and #15 carries the live version.\n2. KEEP\n3. KEEP\n4. KEEP\n5. KEEP\n6. KEEP\n7. KEEP\n8. REMOVE — dup of #69\n9. KEEP\n10. KEEP\n11. KEEP\n12. KEEP\n13. REMOVE — dup of #18\n14. KEEP\n15. KEEP\n16. REMOVE — dup of #12\n17. REMOVE — dup of #11\n18. KEEP\n19. KEEP\n20. KEEP\n21. KEEP\n22. KEEP\n23. KEEP\n24. KEEP\n25. KEEP\n26. KEEP\n27. KEEP\n28. KEEP\n29. KEEP\n30. KEEP\n31. KEEP\n32. KEEP\n33. KEEP\n34. KEEP\n35. UPDATE: No CCD/continuous-collision export visible in the havok.ts,