{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"The user is asking me to reflect on the vite.config.ts read. Let me recall what came back:\n\n1. The head -60 portion showed imports, DemoConfigEntry, readJson, escapeHtml, injectDemoEngineSize, renderPagesDemoCard — demo gallery HTML generation stuff.\n2. The grep for \"port\" showed lines 715–743: `export default defineConfig({` ... and importantly:\n\n```\n// Default interactive port is 5174. Playwright test runs pass LAB_DEV_PORT\n// to spin up an ISOLATED server on a dedicated port (so test traffic never\n// test server so the exact port Playwright waits on is guaranteed; the\nport: Number(process.env.LAB_DEV_PORT) || 5174,\n```\n\nThis is the critical part: the lab's dev server port is `Number(process.env.LAB_DEV_PORT) || 5174`. So to run on port 5182, you set `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182` — no config edit needed. This is critical for the constraint \"dev server must run on port 5182\" and the gotcha interview-t2-1.\n\nOther pointers:\n- DEMO_SOURCE_BASE_URL points to the demos directory `lab/lite/src/demos/` — but our scenes are in `lab/lite/src/lite/`. Hmm, actually the sourceHref uses `src/demos/` for the gallery cards. Interesting — maybe the lite scenes are also served from `src/lite/`? Not sure. This might be relevant for how to register a new scene in the gallery. Actually, the comment at line 607 mentions BJS oracle scenes under `lab/lite/src/bjs/sceneN.ts`. And line 621 has a compat plugin. The vite config has a custom plugin that generates pages — the way a new demo scene gets into the gallery might be via this config's plugin (demos-manifest.json etc.).\n- `public/bundle/demos-manifest.json` — bundle size manifest; bundle-size ceiling spec — related to the bundle size ceiling constraint. Our scene is not a parity scene, so no ceiling entry needed, but the manifest is how sizes are tracked.\n- Lines 718–719: BJS prototype patching, `?raw` WGSL imports — esbuild can't handle them — related to the build/test tooling.\n- Lines 733: directory alias so subpath imports like 'babylon-lite/loader-env/...' work — import aliasing in the lab.\n- Lines 642–656: resolveId compat redirect with the `?compat` query marker — irrelevant for a pure Lite scene.\n- injectDemoEngineSize: reads `window.__DEMO_ENGINE_KB` for the loading overlay — how demo HTML pages are auto-generated.\n- Line 351: api-docs build — irrelevant.\n\nSo the answer:\n\nEXCERPT:\n```\n        // Default interactive port is 5174. Playwright test runs pass LAB_DEV_PORT\n        // to spin up an ISOLATED server on a dedicated port (so test traffic never\n        // test server so the exact port Playwright waits on is guaranteed; the\n        port: Number(process.env.LAB_DEV_PORT) || 5174,\n```\n\nThis is critical: it means port 5182 can be achieved with `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm dev:lab` — no config edit needed.\n\nPOINTERs:\n- `DEMO_SOURCE_BASE_URL` = `https://github.com/BabylonJS/Babylon-Lite/blob/master/lab/lite/src/demos/` — the gallery's source links assume demos are in `src/demos/`, but our scenes are in `src/lite/`; the gallery page generation plugin (renderPagesDemoCard) might need to understand how the new scene gets listed in the lab site (lab/vite.config.ts, top).\n- `readJson(resolve(__dirname, \"public/bundle/demos-manifest.json\"))` — a per-demo bundle size manifest used for gallery cards; the bundle-size ceiling spec reads this (lab/vite.config.ts's injectDemoEngineSize).\n- The vite config defines custom plugins including a compat layer that redirects `@babylonjs/core` to the compat barrel when the importer has a `?compat` query marker — irrelevant for a pure Lite scene, but it explains the BJS oracle scenes in `lab/lite/src/bjs/` (lab/vite.config.ts, lines 607–656).\n- The alias `babylon-lite` → packages/babylon-lite/src and the directory alias for subpath imports — how lab scenes import the engine (lab/vite.config.ts, around line 733).\n\nLet me write this concisely. Keep quotes verbatim, up to 15 lines max.\n","seq":21640,"t":947754,"text":"\n\nEXCERPT:\n```\n        // Default interactive port is 5174. Playwright test runs pass LAB_DEV_PORT\n        // to spin up an ISOLATED server on a dedicated port (so test traffic never\n        // test server so the exact port Playwright waits on is guaranteed; the\n        port: Number(process.env.LAB_DEV_PORT) || 5174,\n```\n\nThat settles the port question: no config edit needed — `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm dev:lab` (or `pnpm exec vite` with the env var) lands the lab on 5182 per the session rule.\n\nPOINTER:\n- The vite config embeds a custom plugin that generates the gallery HTML and links demo sources to `lab/lite/src/demos/` (`DEMO_SOURCE_BASE_URL`) — how a new scene gets listed/served on the lab site is defined here, worth reading when we register the FPS scene (lab/vite.config.ts, top + `renderPagesDemoCard`)\n- `public/bundle/demos-manifest.json` holds per-demo raw/gzip KB measured by the build; gallery cards and `window.__DEMO_ENGINE_KB` read it — the same data the bundle-size ceilings track (lab/vite.config.ts, `injectDemoEngineSize`)\n- A `?compat` query-marker plugin redirects `@babylonjs/core` imports to the compat barrel for the BJS oracle scenes under `lab/lite/src/bjs/` — irrelevant for a pure Lite scene, but explains the repo's dual-scene layout (lab/vite.config.ts, lines 607–656)\n- The config sets the `babylon-lite` alias to `packages/babylon-lite/src` plus a directory alias for sub-path imports — that's how lab scenes import engine modules (lab/vite.config.ts, ~line 733)","timings":{"cache_n":20480,"draft_n":3332,"draft_n_accepted":986,"predicted_ms":29690.0,"predicted_n":1462,"prompt_ms":3560.0,"prompt_n":2751},"to_request":20764,"usage":{"cached_tokens":20480,"completion_tokens":1462,"prompt_tokens":23231}}
