{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"The user is asking me to reflect on the last step (the batch of verification tool calls) and enumerate the decisions made in that step in the form \"DECISION: ... — WHY: ...\".\n\nLet me review what was discovered in the last tool call batch and what was decided:\n\n1. Vite config: `port: Number(process.env.LAB_DEV_PORT) || 5174` — Decision: Launch the dev server with `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm dev:lab` (environment variable override) rather than modifying vite.config.ts. WHY: The config already supports env var override, so no file changes are needed and it complies with the \"5182\" session rule.\n\n2. Scene number: The latest scene is scene251 — Decision: The new FPS scene will be scene252.ts. WHY: That's the next available number after scene251.\n\n3. Navigation plugin: `createNavigationPluginAsync({ locateFile: () => \"/recast-navigation.wasm\" })` with wasm located at lab/public/recast-navigation.wasm — Decision: Bots will use this async plugin creation pattern, and the wasm asset already exists in lab/public. WHY: Verified that it's served the same way as HavokPhysics.wasm.\n\n4. Physics bodies: `createPhysicsAggregate(world, node, PhysicsShapeType.BOX, { mass: 0 })` — Decision: Per-tile static physics bodies will be created via `createPhysicsAggregate` with mass 0 (following the ground pattern in scene40). WHY: scene40 confirms this pattern.\n\n5. World creation: `createHavokWorld(scene, hknp)` — the actual signature takes (scene, hknp, gravity?) and scene40 shows `createHavokWorld(scene, hknp)`. The documentation example shows `await createHavokWorld(scene)`. Hmm, in the map notes from earlier it said createHavokWorld. Line 224: `export function createHavokWorld(scene: SceneContext, hknp: any, gravity?: Vec3)`. And scene40... I didn't look at the top of scene40 in this batch, but in the earlier turn 3 output (b3861acf...), scene40 imports @babylonjs/havok with locateFile. The decision: physics world is created from the `@babylonjs/havok` package using `locateFile: () => \"/HavokPhysics.wasm\"`. This was already recorded as decision interview-t3-f9898-0. In this step I confirmed that `createHavokWorld(scene, hknp)` takes the scene and the wasm init result.\n\n6. Character controller: `getPosition()`, `getVelocity()`, `moveWithCollisions(displacement)`, `supportedState`, `onTriggerCollisionObservable` — Confirmed the API. Decision: Player movement reads position via `getPosition()` and drives the camera; ground detection via `supportedState`. This is more of a confirmation than a new decision.\n\n7. Picking: `createGpuPicker(scene)` exists. Decision: Bullets vs bots via GPU picker picking ray (since character controllers may not be raycastable via physics). Actually, I haven't confirmed yet whether physicsRaycast hits character controllers. This is an open question rather than a decision. I could note \"bullets vs bots via GPU picker\" as a decision — but I haven't fully verified it. I should be honest: what I decided in this step was based on what I saw.\n\n8. Text: `createTextLayer(data, options)` + `createTextRenderer(surface, opts)` + `addTextRendererLayer` — HUD via text layer on the surface context. Confirmed the API exists.\n\n9. `readdirSync(resolve(__dirname, \"lite\"))` on line 120 of vite.config — scene discovery. I didn't fully confirm how the scene list is built, but it reads the directory. Decision: The new scene file inside lab/lite/src/lite/ will be auto-discovered by the lab's vite config (no manifest edit needed) — but I haven't fully verified this. Hmm, line 120: `const liteHtml = readdirSync(resolve(__dirname, \"lite\"))` — this reads the lab/lite directory for HTML files. Scene discovery may be elsewhere. I shouldn't claim this as confirmed.\n\nLet me be careful to only list decisions actually made/confirmed in this step:\n\n- DECISION: Dev server will be launched as `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm dev:lab` — WHY: lab/vite.config.ts already honors the LAB_DEV_PORT env var (falls back to 5174), so no config edit is needed to meet the 5182 session rule.\n- DECISION: New scene will be lab/lite/src/lite/scene252.ts — WHY: existing scenes end at scene251, so 252 is the next free number.\n- DECISION: Bots will use `createNavigationPluginAsync({ locateFile: () => \"/recast-navigation.wasm\" })` — WHY: scene170/171 confirm this is the established lab pattern, and lab/public/recast-navigation.wasm already exists (same service mechanism as HavokPhysics.wasm).\n- DECISION: Per-tile terrain physics will be static bodies via `createPhysicsAggregate(world, node, PhysicsShapeType.BOX, { mass: 0 })` — WHY: scene40 confirms this is the Lite idiom for static boxes, and per-tile bodies can be individually `removePhysicsBody`'d on destruction.\n- DECISION: Player character will be driven via `moveWithCollisions` + `getPosition`/`getVelocity`, with ground detection via `supportedState` — WHY: verified these exact members on PhysicsCharacterController (character-controller.ts:360/371/384/114).\n- DECISION: HUD will use `createTextLayer` + `createTextRenderer`/`addTextRendererLayer` — WHY: verified the text module exports; scenes 180–181 are the reference implementation.\n- DECISION: Bullet hit detection against bots will use the GPU picker (`createGpuPicker`) rather than physics raycast — WHY: character controllers are kinematic, and I haven't verified that physicsRaycast hits them, but the GPU picker reliably picks display meshes.\n\nHmm, the last one is somewhat speculative. But it is a reasonable API choice made in this step. I think it's fair to include with honest reasoning.\n\nAlso: PhysicsBody has `node: SceneNode` — so to read the position of a debris body, read body.node.position. This is a useful decision: debris rendered as thin instances will read `body.node.position` each frame. This was confirmed in this step (PhysicsBody interface at havok.ts:156-167 has `readonly node: SceneNode`).\n\nAlso, the `onPhysicsAfterStep` pattern was confirmed in scene40 — physics stepping is hooked there.\n\nI should keep it concise and list only decisions from this step. I'll list about 6–7.\n","seq":25275,"t":1059702,"text":"\n\nDECISION: Dev server runs as `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm dev:lab` — WHY: lab/vite.config.ts already honors `LAB_DEV_PORT` (falls back to 5174), so the 5182 session rule needs no config edit.\nDECISION: The FPS scene lands at `lab/lite/src/lite/scene252.ts` — WHY: existing scene files end at scene251, so 252 is the next free number.\nDECISION: Bots use `createNavigationPluginAsync({ locateFile: () => \"/recast-navigation.wasm\" })` — WHY: scene170/171 confirm it as the established lab idiom and `lab/public/recast-navigation.wasm` already exists, served like HavokPhysics.wasm.\nDECISION: Per-tile terrain physics = static boxes via `createPhysicsAggregate(world, node, PhysicsShapeType.BOX, { mass: 0 })` — WHY: scene40 confirms this is the Lite idiom for static bodies, and per-tile bodies can be individually removed (`removePhysicsBody`) on destruction.\nDECISION: Player uses `moveWithCollisions` + `getPosition`/`getVelocity`, with ground detection via `supportedState` — WHY: verified those exact members on `PhysicsCharacterController` (character-controller.ts:360/371/384/114).\nDECISION: Debris bodies are rendered as thin instances by reading `body.node.position` each frame — WHY: `PhysicsBody` exposes `node: SceneNode` (havok.ts:156-167), so no extra position-query API is needed.\nDECISION: Bullet-vs-bot hits use the GPU picker (`createGpuPicker`) rather than `physicsRaycast` — WHY: character controllers are kinematic and I have not verified `physicsRaycast` hits them, while the picker reliably hits display meshes.\nDECISION: HUD uses `createTextLayer` + `createTextRenderer`/`addTextRendererLayer` — WHY: verified those exports in the text module; scenes 180–181 are the working references.","timings":{"cache_n":26368,"draft_n":4116,"draft_n_accepted":1415,"predicted_ms":35000.0,"predicted_n":2003,"prompt_ms":620.0,"prompt_n":322},"to_request":24086,"usage":{"cached_tokens":26368,"completion_tokens":2003,"prompt_tokens":26690}}
