{"entry":{"id":"r22627/call_731f2ddafab24ab79ace0962/plan","text":"FPS plan (Quake-style, tile-removal terrain) — new lab demo, NO engine changes:\n\nFILES (all new, under ~/git/reference/Babylon/Babylon-Lite):\n1. lab/lite/scene252.html — copy scene18.html pattern (canvas + /loader.js + module script); auto-discovered by getHtmlInputs() in lab/vite.config.ts. Next free number after scene251.\n2. lab/lite/src/lite/scene252.ts — main scene: 4-phase scaffold (createEngine → build → registerScene → startEngine), Havok world (locateFile \"/HavokPhysics.wasm\"), player, bots, shooting, HUD, game loop.\n3. lab/lite/src/lite/fps-terrain.ts — noise terrain + tile removal: build grid (~256×256 verts over 128×128u), tiles 4×4u → 32×32 = 1024 tiles; per-tile static box bodies (createPhysicsAggregate mass 0, top at tile max height); destroy = remove tile's index range from _cpuIndices, computeNormals, uploadMeshToGPU, removePhysicsBody, addBoxObstacle on navmesh.\n4. lab/lite/src/lite/fps-input.ts — pointer lock + keyboard state (DOM-side; no engine input module exists).\n5. lab/lite/src/lite/fps-audio.ts — Web Audio SFX (gunshot, thud, hit), lazy-init on first gesture, no module-level side effects.\n\nSTEPS:\nS1 Verify remaining API details (read-only): frame-observable name (scene18), physicsRaycast query shape (havok-queries.ts:207), NavMeshParameters usage (scene170), whether controller exposes its shape for friction, bundle-size spec doesn't cover lab scenes.\nS2 fps-terrain.ts: seeded value-noise heights, low-frequency (amp ~5u); createFlatGroundData → mutate positions → computeNormals → uploadMeshToGPU; per-tile static boxes + membership/collide masks; destroyTile() index surgery + re-upload + body removal + nav obstacle.\nS3 scene252.ts: engine/scene/light/camera scaffold; createHavokWorld; terrain via fps-terrain; player = createPhysicsCharacterController (capsule 1.8/0.5), Quake movement in onPhysicsAfterStep (slide friction, air control, jump gated by checkSupport supportedState); camera follow w/ pointer-lock yaw/pitch.\nS4 Shooting: click → ray from eye; physicsRaycast for terrain (hit → destroyTile), manual ray-capsule vs bots (closest wins); fire-rate limit; hit/kill feedback.\nS5 Bots: createNavigationPluginAsync (recast-navigation.wasm) + createNavMesh from terrain mesh; N=4 bots = character controller + NavCrowd agent (agentGoto/findRandomPoint, updateNavCrowd per step); display = thin instances; bots LOS-check player (physicsRaycast) and shoot with distance-based accuracy; damage/respawn both sides.\nS6 HUD: createTextLayer/createTextRenderer (pattern from scenes 180/181) — health, kills, tiles destroyed; crosshair.\nS7 fps-audio.ts wired to events.\nS8 Dev server: LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm dev:lab (vite config reads LAB_DEV_PORT, default 5174); manual playtest checklist: move/slide/jump, mouse look, shoot holes, fall through → respawn, debris, bots patrol+shoot, HUD, audio. Add canvas.dataset.ready/error like scene40 for scriptability.\n\nCHECKS: typecheck (repo script), manual playtest on :5182/lite/scene252.html, confirm bundle-size.spec.ts unaffected, no module-level side effects, no raw GPU handles in scene code.\n\nRISKS: 1024 static bodies init cost (fallback: 8×8u tiles → 256 bodies); navmesh from dense mesh (tune NavMeshParameters); controller shape access for friction (fallback: low friction on terrain tile shapes)."},"kind":"patch","lane":"self-capture","op":"add","seq":25858,"t":1086308}
