{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Let me reflect on what I actually decided in my last step (the verification batch + recording the plan).\n\nIn that step, I made concrete choices that weren't settled previously:\n\n1. **Scene number 252** — decided to use scene252.ts/scene252.html as the new scene. WHY: the largest existing number is scene251, and registration is auto-detected.\n\n2. **File layout: splitting into 5 files** (scene252.ts + fps-terrain.ts + fps-input.ts + fps-audio.ts + scene252.html). WHY: the scene file needs to read like a high-level API demo, and separating DOM input/audio/terrain logic keeps the entry file game-flow-centric.\n\n3. **No engine changes** — the whole FPS uses only existing babylon-lite APIs. WHY: the constraint (don't copy BJS code, tree-shaking, pure state) plus everything needed is already verified to exist.\n\n4. **Arena/terrain parameters**: 128×128u arena, 4×4u tiles → 1024 tiles, about 256×256 vertex grid, per-tile static box with top surface at the tile's max height. WHY: this is the concrete form of tile deletion with a per-tile static body, and 1024 static bodies is a reasonable demo cost (with a fallback to 8×8u → 256 bodies).\n\n5. **Noise parameters**: seeded low-frequency value noise, amplitude about 5u. WHY: gentle noise minimizes the visual/physical mismatch between the mesh surface and the flat-topped tile boxes.\n\n6. **Bullet model**: physicsRaycast for terrain + manual ray-capsule test against bots (nearest hit). WHY: character controllers are not physical raycast targets (probably kinematic), and manual tests against a small number of bots are cheap and deterministic.\n\n7. **Bots: NavCrowd agent + character controller, bots target only the player**. WHY: the crowd gives bot-vs-bot separation for free; bot-vs-bot combat is deferred to keep scope small.\n\n8. **Friction approach**: set low friction on the terrain tile shapes (fallback if the controller's shape is not exposed). WHY: Quake-style sliding, and the controller's shape getter is unverified.\n\n9. **HUD via text layer (scenes 180/181 pattern), audio via Web Audio lazy-initialized on gesture**. WHY: Lite has no GUI/audio; the autoplay policy requires user-gesture initialization.\n\n10. **Dev server: LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm dev:lab**. WHY: the vite config reads LAB_DEV_PORT (default 5174), satisfying the session's port 5182 rule without editing files.\n\n11. **canvas.dataset.ready/error pattern** (like scene40) for scriptability. WHY: it enables Playwright smoke tests later.\n\n12. **Collision layers via membership/collide masks** — actually, that was in the plan as \"membership/collide masks.\" WHY: so bullets/debris/player don't collide with each other.\n\n13. S1 \"verify remaining API details\" — this is a verification step, not a decision.\n\n14. Scene registration: auto-detection, no manifest editing — this is more of a confirmation of a fact than a decision, but \"no manifest editing needed\" is a consequence.\n\nWhich of these are truly new decisions from this step (not from before)? Previous decisions: scope (lab demo, not parity), deferring multiplayer, dev server port constraint, no particles/audio. The user previously approved tile deletion. In this step, I locked in the concrete implementation choices: file layout, scene number, arena parameters, bullet model, bot architecture, friction fallback, LAB_DEV_PORT usage, no engine changes.\n\nI should enumerate these as DECISION lines. Concisely, one per line. Let me pick the ones that matter as build decisions:\n\n- DECISION: Scene file is scene252.ts + scene252.html under lab/lite — WHY: the next free number after scene251, and HTML is auto-detected by getHtmlInputs().\n- DECISION: Split the scene into scene252.ts + fps-terrain.ts + fps-input.ts + fps-audio.ts — WHY: the entry needs to read like a high-level API demo, and DOM input/audio/terrain logic don't belong in the game-flow file.\n- DECISION: No changes to packages/babylon-lite, FPS built purely on existing APIs — WHY: all needed functionality is verified to exist, and the engine's constraints (tree-shaking, pure state) argue against engine changes.\n- DECISION: Arena 128×128u, 4×4u tiles (1024 static box bodies), about 256×256 vertex grid, per-tile box top surface at the tile's max height — WHY: concrete form of tile deletion + per-tile static bodies, with fallback to 8×8u tiles if initialization is slow.\n- DECISION: Bullets hit terrain via physicsRaycast, and bots via manual ray-capsule test (nearest hit) — WHY: character controllers are not reliable physics raycast targets, and a manual test against 4 bots is cheap.\n- DECISION: Bots = character controller + NavCrowd agent, targeting only the player — WHY: the crowd gives bot-vs-bot separation for free, and bot-vs-bot combat is deferred.\n- DECISION: Quake sliding = low friction on the terrain tile shapes (fallback if the controller's shape is not exposed) — WHY: the controller's shape getter is unverified, and terrain friction affects all characters consistently.\n- DECISION: Dev server is launched with LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm dev:lab — WHY: the vite config respects LAB_DEV_PORT (default 5174), satisfying the session's port rule without editing files.\n- DECISION: Add canvas.dataset.ready/error like scene40 — WHY: it makes the scene scriptable for later Playwright smoke tests.\n- DECISION: HUD via createTextLayer (scenes 180/181 pattern), audio via Web Audio lazy-initialized on first gesture — WHY: Lite has no GUI/audio, and the browser's autoplay policy requires gesture-gated initialization.\n\nThat's a good list. Should I also mention the seeded value noise (amplitude about 5u)? This is a parameter choice — include it briefly.\n\nI'll keep it to about 8–10 lines.\n","seq":28239,"t":1188406,"text":"\n\nDECISION: New scene is `scene252.ts` + `scene252.html` under `lab/lite/` — WHY: scene251 is the highest existing number and `getHtmlInputs()` auto-discovers HTML, so no manifest edits.\nDECISION: Split the demo into `scene252.ts` (game flow) + `fps-terrain.ts` + `fps-input.ts` + `fps-audio.ts` — WHY: the entry must read like a high-level API demo, and terrain surgery, DOM input, and audio don't belong in the game-flow file.\nDECISION: Zero changes to `packages/babylon-lite`; the FPS is built purely on existing APIs — WHY: every needed capability (character controller, raycast, navmesh, text, thin instances) was verified present, and engine edits would fight the tree-shaking/pure-state constraints.\nDECISION: Arena 128×128u with 4×4u tiles → 1024 per-tile static box bodies, ~256×256-vertex mesh, box top at tile max height — WHY: concrete realization of tile removal + per-tile static bodies, with 8×8u tiles (256 bodies) as the fallback if world init is slow.\nDECISION: Bullet hits terrain via `physicsRaycast`, hits bots via manual ray-capsule test with closest-hit wins — WHY: character controllers aren't reliable physics-raycast targets, and a manual test against ~4 bots is cheap and deterministic.\nDECISION: Bots are character controllers driven by NavCrowd agents, targeting only the player — WHY: the crowd gives bot-vs-bot separation for free, and bot-vs-bot combat is out of scope this iteration.\nDECISION: Quake-style slide via low friction on the terrain tile shapes, with controller-shape friction as the preferred target if it's exposed — WHY: the controller's shape getter is unverified, and terrain friction applies consistently to player and bots.\nDECISION: Dev server started as `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm dev:lab` — WHY: `lab/vite.config.ts` honors `LAB_DEV_PORT` (default 5174), satisfying the session's port-5182 rule without editing config.\nDECISION: Terrain heights from seeded low-frequency value noise, amplitude ~5u — WHY: gentle noise keeps the flat-topped tile-box physics close to the mesh surface.\nDECISION: Add `canvas.dataset.ready`/`dataset.error` like scene40 — WHY: it makes the scene scriptable for a later Playwright smoke test via `pnpm exec playwright`.","timings":{"cache_n":35072,"draft_n":3850,"draft_n_accepted":1428,"predicted_ms":23670.0,"predicted_n":1978,"prompt_ms":630.0,"prompt_n":347},"to_request":27686,"usage":{"cached_tokens":35072,"completion_tokens":1978,"prompt_tokens":35419}}
