{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"The user is asking about constraints that came to light or were committed to in the step just completed. The step just completed was my last message: I ran verification commands (scene numbers, vite config, nav plugin, text exports, character controller, physics bodies, scene registration HTML pattern, moveWithCollisions) and recorded the plan with update_record.\n\nWhat constraints surfaced in that step?\n\n1. **Dev server port**: vite.config.ts reads `LAB_DEV_PORT` env var, default is 5174. Session rule says use 5182. So the constraint is: the dev server must be launched with `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182` (this is already recorded as a constraint in the working set — r11177/call_b04dd22925274eb0b6579989/constraint and interview-t2-1). Was it \"surfaced in this step\"? I confirmed the mechanism (LAB_DEV_PORT env var), which is new info — the exact way to override the port. But the constraint itself (port 5182) was known before. Hmm. What I confirmed in this step is the means: `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm dev:lab`. The constraint \"dev server on 5182\" is pre-existing. The env var override mechanism is a fact, not a constraint.\n\n2. **Scene registration**: new scenes require an HTML file in `lab/lite/` matching the pattern (canvas id=\"renderCanvas\", /loader.js, module script to /lite/src/lite/sceneN.ts) — auto-discovered by getHtmlInputs(). This is more of a fact/requirement than a \"must never do\" constraint. Is it a constraint the project must follow? It's a requirement: new lab scenes must be registered via an HTML file in lab/lite/ following the scene18 pattern, and must use sceneN.html + sceneN.ts naming. This surfaced in this step.\n\n3. **Scene numbering**: use scene252 (next free number after scene251). That's a decision, not a constraint.\n\n4. **No engine changes**: I committed in the plan to no changes to packages/babylon-lite — everything uses existing APIs. That's a commitment/decision I made in this step. Is it a constraint? It's a design decision that the rest of the project should follow: don't modify the engine package; lab scenes only. I think it's a constraint worth listing as a commitment: \"FPS is built entirely from existing Babylon-Lite APIs; no changes to packages/babylon-lite.\"\n\n5. **Wasm assets**: the scene must reference /HavokPhysics.wasm and /recast-navigation.wasm, which are served from lab/public (both files confirmed to exist). That's a fact.\n\n6. **GUIDANCE.md rules** (no module-level side effects, etc.) were already recorded before this step.\n\nThe question says \"only constraints surfaced in this step.\" So what should be limited to what became clear in the last step (verification + plan recording):\n\n- CONSTRAINED: new lab scenes must be registered as HTML pages in lab/lite/ (sceneN.html + src/lite/sceneN.ts) following the scene18 pattern — this is how the gallery auto-discovers scenes; without the HTML file the scene won't exist. This is a requirement surfaced in this step.\n- CONSTRAINED: dev server port override must be done via the LAB_DEV_PORT env var (vite config default is 5174) — the session rule of 5182 is enforced by `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm dev:lab`. The constraint (5182) was pre-existing, but the enforcement mechanism surfaced in this step. I'll include it framed as the mechanism.\n- COMMITTED: no engine changes — build the demo entirely from existing APIs in packages/babylon-lite; new files only under lab/lite/. This is a commitment I made in the plan this step.\n\nAnything else? \"Scene number: use scene252, next free number\" — that's a decision, not a constraint. \"Physics bodies must be tied to a SceneNode (createPhysicsAggregate requires a node)\" — that's an API fact that constrains implementation (per-tile bodies need nodes). You could call it a constraint the implementation must follow, but it's more of a fact about the API. The question is about constraints the rest of the project must follow — a requirement, environmental limitation, compatibility rule, something that must never be done.\n\nI think the clean list is:\n\nCONSTRAINT: new lab scenes must be registered as a paired HTML page in lab/lite/ (sceneN.html loading /loader.js + /lite/src/lite/sceneN.ts, canvas id=\"renderCanvas\") — auto-discovered by vite's getHtmlInputs(); a scene with no HTML page won't appear in the lab.\nCONSTRAINT: dev server must be launched with LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 (vite config defaults to 5174; session rule requires 5182).\nCONSTRAINT: the FPS must be built entirely from existing Babylon-Lite APIs — no changes to packages/babylon-lite; new files only under lab/lite/ (scene252.html, scene252.ts, fps-terrain.ts, fps-input.ts, fps-audio.ts).\n\nShould I also mention \"canvas id must be renderCanvas\" — that's part of the HTML pattern constraint.\n\nWhat about wasm paths: the scene must load the physics/nav wasm from lab/public root paths (\"/HavokPhysics.wasm\", \"/recast-navigation.wasm\") — those files exist there. That's a fact, and arguably a requirement. Could be included: CONSTRAINT: physics and nav wasm must be loaded via locateFile from lab/public root paths (\"/HavokPhysics.wasm\", \"/recast-navigation.wasm\") — both assets confirmed to exist there. Hmm, that's more fact than constraint. The \"must never do\" framing: don't assume other wasm locations. I'll include it lightly or skip. Since it's a compatibility rule for how to load assets in the lab, I'll include it.\n\nKeep it concise: list each item on its own line prefixed with CONSTRAINT:.\n","seq":28760,"t":1210807,"text":"\n\nCONSTRAINT: New lab scenes must be registered as an HTML page in `lab/lite/` following the scene18 pattern (`sceneN.html` with canvas id `renderCanvas`, `/loader.js`, and a module script pointing at `/lite/src/lite/sceneN.ts`) — the gallery auto-discovers scenes via `getHtmlInputs()` in `lab/vite.config.ts`, so a scene file without its HTML page won't exist in the lab.\nCONSTRAINT: The dev server must be started with `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182` — `lab/vite.config.ts` defaults to port 5174 and only honors the `LAB_DEV_PORT` env var, so plain `pnpm dev:lab` would violate the session's port-5182 rule.\nCONSTRAINT: The FPS is built entirely from existing Babylon-Lite APIs — no changes to `packages/babylon-lite`; all new files live under `lab/lite/` (scene252.html, scene252.ts, fps-terrain.ts, fps-input.ts, fps-audio.ts).\nCONSTRAINT: Physics and navigation wasm must be loaded via `locateFile` from the lab root paths `/HavokPhysics.wasm` and `/recast-navigation.wasm` (both confirmed present in `lab/public/`) — don't introduce other asset locations.","timings":{"cache_n":35072,"draft_n":3535,"draft_n_accepted":1120,"predicted_ms":21630.0,"predicted_n":1625,"prompt_ms":630.0,"prompt_n":324},"to_request":28252,"usage":{"cached_tokens":35072,"completion_tokens":1625,"prompt_tokens":35396}}
