ion: I grepped havok.ts (get/set functions) and character-controller.ts. I did NOT grep havok-collision.ts. The \"bullets may tunnel\" concern is moot because bullets are instant rays (plan S4). So I'll UPDATE: \"CCD/tunneling concern is moot — plan's bullets are instant rays (S4), not projectiles; havok.ts + character-controller.ts now checked, havok-collision.ts still unchecked.\"\n\nActually, is that one line reasonable? Yes.\n\nLet me reconsider #2: \"No runtime vertex-update export found (grep covered 3 of ~25 mesh files) — in-place deformation off the table unless via uploadMeshToGPU rebuild or tile deletion; non-function exports unchecked.\" The plan chose tile deletion via uploadMeshToGPU. So the conclusion is settled. I'll UPDATE: \"Settled: plan uses tile deletion via uploadMeshToGPU rebuild (S2), so in-place deformation is confirmed off the table; no further mesh-file audit needed.\"\n\nNow let me reconsider #3. Let me finalize the UPDATE. I verified this session: setPhysicsBodyLinearVelocity at :1056, getPhysicsBodyLinearVelocity at :1063. The note claims applyPhysicsImpulse :1043, setPhysicsBodyLinearVelocity :1063, removePhysicsBody :1112, line 518 = applyPhysicsBodyImpulse. The :1063 attribution to setPhysicsBodyLinearVelocity is wrong (it's get). I'll UPDATE: \"Debris functions confirmed, but line numbers drift: setPhysicsBodyLinearVelocity is at :1056 (note's :1063 is getPhysicsBodyLinearVelocity); applyPhysicsImpulse/removePhysicsBody/line-518 not re-verified this session.\"\n\nHmm, that's clunky but honest. Let me keep it.\n\nActually, wait — do I want to be this pedantic about line numbers? The audit says \"Judge against everything that has actually happened in this session.\" I did actually verify setPhysicsBodyLinearVelocity:1056 and getPhysicsBodyLinearVelocity:1063. So the note's \":1063\" for setPhysicsBodyLinearVelocity is factually wrong per my verification. I should correct it. Yes, UPDATE.\n\nLet me now also double check #26 and #27 and 