sion. KEEP (not contradicted).\n\n#55: evidence with the port code. The note has a slightly garbled quote (the middle line is truncated: \"so test traffic never / test server so the exact port...\"). But the key line `port: Number(process.env.LAB_DEV_PORT) || 5174` is confirmed. KEEP.\n\n#75: I'll KEEP.\n\n#91: This is the big UPDATE. Let me make sure it's one line. Yes, it's one line (long). Good.\n\nNow, one concern: #94 (the plan) and #95 (tile removal decision) and #82 (arena details) all overlap heavily. But they're the plan-of-record and the user-approval. I'll KEEP all three (they're the authoritative plan). The audit is about correctness, and these are correct.\n\nLet me reconsider #92 (scope) vs #53 (decision: FPS as new lab demo not parity). #92: \"Scope: turn the getting-started example into a Quake-style FPS as a new lab demo (lab/lite/, not a parity scene). Terrain noise + destructible. Bots in scope, multiplayer deferred.\" #53: \"The FPS is built as a new lab demo entry under lab/lite/, not as a parity scene (no golden reference, no pixel-diff spec, no bundle-ceiling entry) — WHY: it's a game demo.\" These overlap. #92 is the scope statement (from the user), #53 is the decision. Not exact dups (#53 adds the WHY and the \"no bundle-ceiling entry\" detail). I'll KEEP both. Actually, is #92 dup of #53? #92 has \"terrain noise + destructible, bots in scope, multiplayer deferred\" which #53 doesn't. #53 has \"no golden reference, no pixel-diff, no bundle-ceiling entry, WHY\" which #92 doesn't. So they're complementary. KEEP both.\n\nOK I'm fairly confident. Let me also reconsider #47 (HUD via GPU text) vs #62 (HUD uses createTextLayer + createTextRenderer) vs #78 (text multi-stage). #47 is the decision (GPU text path, not GUI). #62 is the specific API decision. #78 is the gotcha (multi-stage). All complementary. KEEP all.\n\nLet me reconsider #54 (no particles/audio constraint) vs #15 (Lite omits particles, GUI, etc.). #15 is a broad gotcha about what Lite