{"entry":{"id":"interview-t5-4","text":"gotcha: The lab gallery is built by a custom Vite plugin (`readdirSync(resolve(__dirname, \"lite\"))` at vite.config.ts:120), and `DEMO_SOURCE_BASE_URL` points at `lab/lite/src/demos/` while scenes actually live in `lab/lite/src/lite/` — IMPLICATION: I must read the plugin's scene-list construction and check how a new scene file gets registered in the gallery before assuming dropping `scene252.ts` in is enough."},"fork":28769,"kind":"patch","op":"retire","seq":33400,"t":1441077}
{"entry":{"id":"interview-t5-5","text":"gotcha: The character controller's ground state lives on `CharacterSurfaceInfo` (character-controller.ts:110-114), not as a direct controller getter — the public surface I verified is only `getPosition`/`getVelocity`/`moveWithCollisions`/`onTriggerCollisionObservable` — IMPLICATION: I need to find how to read the last `supportedState` (event or method) for jump gating before implementing movement; I won't assume one exists."},"fork":28769,"kind":"patch","op":"retire","seq":33401,"t":1441077}
{"entry":{"id":"interview-t5-6","text":"decision: Bullet-vs-bot hits use the GPU picker (`createGpuPicker`) rather than `physicsRaycast` — WHY: character controllers are kinematic and I have not verified `physicsRaycast` hits them, while the picker reliably hits display meshes."},"fork":28769,"kind":"patch","op":"retire","seq":33402,"t":1441077}
{"entry":{"id":"interview-t5-f24085-1","text":"decision: The FPS scene lands at `lab/lite/src/lite/scene252.ts` — WHY: existing scene files end at scene251, so 252 is the next free number."},"fork":28769,"kind":"patch","op":"retire","seq":33403,"t":1441077}
{"entry":{"id":"interview-t5-f25985-2","text":"gotcha: there is no `getPhysicsBodyPosition` — `PhysicsBody` exposes `node: SceneNode` and the engine syncs body→node each step, so positions are read off `body.node.position` — IMPLICATION: debris thin-instance matrices come from node positions, and every per-tile static box needs its own transform node (1024 extra nodes in the scene graph)."},"fork":28769,"kind":"patch","op":"retire","seq":33404,"t":1441077}
{"entry":{"id":"interview-t5-f27685-7","text":"decision: Dev server started as `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm dev:lab` — WHY: `lab/vite.config.ts` honors `LAB_DEV_PORT` (default 5174), satisfying the session's port-5182 rule without editing config."},"fork":28769,"kind":"patch","op":"retire","seq":33405,"t":1441077}
{"entry":{"id":"interview-t5-f28251-1","text":"constraint: The dev server must be started with `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182` — `lab/vite.config.ts` defaults to port 5174 and only honors the `LAB_DEV_PORT` env var, so plain `pnpm dev:lab` would violate the session's port-5182 rule."},"fork":28769,"kind":"patch","op":"retire","seq":33406,"t":1441077}
{"entry":{"id":"interview-t5-f28251-2","text":"constraint: The FPS is built entirely from existing Babylon-Lite APIs — no changes to `packages/babylon-lite`; all new files live under `lab/lite/` (scene252.html, scene252.ts, fps-terrain.ts, fps-input.ts, fps-audio.ts)."},"fork":28769,"kind":"patch","op":"retire","seq":33407,"t":1441077}
{"entry":{"id":"audit-28769-91","text":"Anchors (verified) — player/bot = createPhysicsCharacterController (moveWithCollisions + checkSupport/CharacterSupportedState); bullet hits = physicsRaycast (terrain) + manual ray-capsule (bots), not the GPU picker; terrain surgery = createFlatGroundData + computeNormals + uploadMeshToGPU; debris = thin instances; HUD = createTextLayer/createTextRenderer (scenes 180-181); bots = navigation (createNavMesh, NavCrowd/agentGoto/updateNavCrowd, addBoxObstacle); physics = createHavokWorld + per-tile static boxes (createPhysicsAggregate), HavokPhysics.wasm from lab/public/."},"fork":28769,"kind":"patch","op":"supersede","seq":33408,"supersedes":"r11177/call_3e0014035cb94159a810d363/map","t":1441077}
