{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"The user is saying \"Sounds good, build it.\" — so we're now in the build phase. The plan is already recorded. Let's start the build.\n\nFirst, let me re-read GUIDANCE.md. It's a must-read at session start and after compaction (interview-t2-13). Also, I should verify the remaining API details (S1) — some of that work has already been done according to the working set:\n- audit-28769-1: havok.ts + character-controller.ts verified, havok-collision.ts not yet verified\n- audit-28769-3: Debris functions confirmed, but line numbers have drifted\n- audit-28769-30: References to FPS-relevant scenes confirmed\n- audit-28769-36: onTriggerCollisionObservable confirmed\n- audit-28769-6: Port is resolved\n- audit-28769-91: Anchors verified\n\nSo S1 is mostly done. The remaining verification items are:\n- Name of the frame observable (scene18)\n- Query shape of physicsRaycast (havok-queries.ts:207)\n- Usage of NavMeshParameters (scene170)\n- Whether the controller exposes its shape for friction\n- That the bundle-size spec doesn't cover lab scenes\n\nLet's start by re-reading GUIDANCE.md (must), then do the remaining S1 verifications, and then write code.\n\nActually, per the ground rules: \"When the plan's steps are complete, call propose_phase_transition.\" We're currently in the build phase. The plan's steps are S1 through S8.\n\nLet's proceed one step at a time:\n\nS1: Verify remaining API details (read-only).\n\nFirst, read GUIDANCE.md (required after compaction). Then do the S1 checks. Let's run these in parallel:\n1. Read GUIDANCE.md\n2. Read scene18.ts to get the frame observable name\n3. Read around line 207 of havok-queries.ts to confirm the query shape of physicsRaycast\n4. Read scene170.ts to confirm NavMeshParameters usage\n5. Check the controller's shape exposure (character-controller.ts)\n6. Check whether bundle-size.spec.ts covers lab scenes\n\nLet's run these all together.\n","seq":33567,"t":1462255,"t