{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Good progress. Next, what's needed:\n1. The signature of `createFlatGroundData` and the shape of `GroundData` — check create-ground.ts.\n2. How a Mesh holds GPU data, and how to replace it — need to check how the mesh's `_gpu` is used, and whether there's a way to swap out a mesh's GPU buffers. `uploadMeshToGPU` returns a `MeshGPU` handle. Need to find where a mesh's `_gpu` field is set, and how the renderable reads it.\n3. `createPhysicsAggregate` for a static tile — a node is required. What can be used as a node? A Mesh. Could also create a small invisible mesh per tile, but… that would mean 1024 meshes in the scene. Hmm, that's heavy. Actually wait — a better approach: create the static box on an actual mesh node. But 1024 meshes… the plan said \"per-tile static box bodies (createPhysicsAggregate mass 0…)\". interview-t5-2 noted \"per-tile static colliders need one node per tile. Need to verify that empty/invisible nodes can be created.\"\n\nLet me check how createPhysicsAggregate works and whether it can create a node. Also check the options for createPhysicsBody.\n\n4. Check the text module flow of scene180/181.\n5. Check the thin instances API.\n6. Check the `physicsRaycast` query shape — done: `RaycastQuery` with `membership`, `collideWith`, `shouldHitTriggers`.\n7. Check `setPhysicsShapeMaterial` (friction) — havok.ts:971.\n8. Check the signature of `removePhysicsBody`.\n9. Check `createPhysicsCharacterController` and the controller's shape access.\n10. Check `scene18.html` — already grabbed it in the turn 5 file (saved at 595 bytes). Let me read it.\n\nAlso check the scene-config.json requirements — per GUIDANCE §2, when adding a new scene, we need to add it to rollup inputs, Playwright parity tests, reference screenshots, thumbnails, gallery cards, bundle size ceilings, and scene-config.json. But — this is a game demo, not a parity scene (decision interview-t4-f13394-1: \"The FPS is built as a new lab demo entry under lab/lite/, not as a parity scene (no golden reference, no pixel-diff spec, no bundle ceiling entry)\"). Auto-discovery via getHtmlInputs() means that a new sceneN.html + sceneN.ts will be picked up without editing the manifest.\n\nHmm, but wait — according to interview-t5-1, the vite config generates gallery HTML that links to demo sources under lab/lite/src/demos/. And getHtmlInputs() auto-discovers HTML. Let me re-check how lab scenes are discovered. In fact, per audit-28769-30, scene files now extend up to scene251. So scene252.ts + scene252.html should be auto-discovered. Good.\n\nNow, about bundle-size.spec.ts: SCENES = allScenes.filter(s => s.maxRawKB != null) — scenes come from scene-config.json. Since our scene isn't in scene-config.json, the bundle size spec won't cover it.\n\nNow let me check the remaining API details:\n- create-ground.ts (shape of GroundData)\n- mesh.ts — how the mesh holds _gpu, and whether there's a way to replace the GPU data\n- character-controller.ts — the signature of createPhysicsCharacterController, access to the shape\n- scene180/181 text\n- thin instances\n- scene18.html\n- createPhysicsAggregate options\n- removePhysicsBody\n- addBoxObstacle for navmesh\n\nLet me run these in a batch.\n","seq":34702,"t":1521895,"text":"\n\nS1 is mostly settled. Now checking the remaining details: ground data shape, mesh GPU swap, character controller API, text flow, thin instances, and scene18.html.\n\n\n\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":25088,"draft_n":2751,"draft_n_accepted":808,"predicted_ms":22720.0,"predicted_n":1201,"prompt_ms":3600.0,"prompt_n":3404},"to_request":33961,"usage":{"cached_tokens":25088,"completion_tokens":1201,"prompt_tokens":28492}}
