{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"In this step, I performed S1 verification. Let me enumerate the decisions/confirmations made in this step:\n\n1. `resizeMeshGeometry` was discovered as the appropriate seam for terrain destruction — better than a raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + `_gpu` swap. The plan called for \"index surgery + computeNormals + uploadMeshToGPU\", but I've decided to use `resizeMeshGeometry` instead. Because it bumps the renderable version (re-recording of cached bundles) and preserves the CPU geometry.\n\n2. Per-tile static bodies: use `createTransformNode` + `createPhysicsBody(world, node, STATIC)` + `createPhysicsShape` + `setPhysicsBodyShape` (not `createPhysicsAggregate`. Because it requires a Mesh) — the node doesn't need to be added to the scene (proven by the character controller). This resolves the open question from interview-t5-2.\n\n3. The controller exposes friction as public fields `staticFriction`/`dynamicFriction` — so Quake-style sliding can be done directly on the controller (no need for the fallback of terrain-shape friction).\n\n4. Frame observable = `onBeforeRender(scene, cb)`. Confirmed.\n\n5. Havok loading pattern confirmed from scene40: `await HavokPhysics({locateFile: () => \"/HavokPhysics.wasm\"})` → `createHavokWorld(scene, hknp, gravity)`.\n\n6. The query shape of physicsRaycast is confirmed: `RaycastQuery {membership, collideWith, shouldHitTriggers}` — so collision layer filtering is available for bullets.\n\n7. Text HUD path: scene181 shows `createTextRenderable` + `addTextRenderable(scene, text)` for in-scene 3D text — my HUD is in-world text. Meanwhile, scene180's `createTextLayer`/`createTextRenderer` is a standalone 2D overlay path (no scene). Hmm — which one should I use for the HUD? The HUD should be screen-space (health, kill count, crosshair). scene180's TextRenderer path is a 2D overlay — this is the right one for the HUD. scene181's text renderable is in-world 3D text. So for a screen-space HUD, use createTextLayer + createTextRenderer (the scene180 pattern). This is the decision: HUD = scene180's 2D TextRenderer path.\n\n8. FreeCamera has `_yaw`/`_pitch` internal fields — for the FPS camera, I plan to drive yaw/pitch manually. I could use a FreeCamera and set the position every frame, and manipulate `_yaw`/`_pitch` directly (the @internal fields are accessible from source code). Or, build the view matrix myself. I haven't fully decided yet — but the fact that FreeCamera exposes _yaw/_pitch as @internal is useful. Let me record that I'll drive a FreeCamera's position + _yaw/_pitch directly (the lab's scene code is written against the source, so @internal is fine).\n\n9. Confirmed that the bundle-size spec only covers scenes with maxRawKB in scene-config.json — scene252 isn't included there, so it's unaffected.\n\n10. Confirmed NavMeshParameters from scene170 — for a 128×128 arena, walkableSlopeAngle 90, cs/ch tuned to a coarse scale.\n\n11. The createNavCrowd + addAgent parameters pattern is confirmed (scene170).\n\n12. Confirmed the existence of thin instance APIs: setThinInstances, setThinInstanceMatrix, setThinInstanceCount, etc. — for bot display.\n\nI should list these concisely.\n","seq":41327,"t":1798745,"text":"\n\nDECISION: Terrain re-upload uses `resizeMeshGeometry(engine, mesh, positions, normals, indices, uvs)` instead of raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + `_gpu` swap — WHY: it's the purpose-built in-place seam that bumps `_renderableVersion` so cached draw bundles re-record, and retains `_cpuPositions`/`_cpuIndices` for picking (mesh-factories.ts:106).\nDECISION: Per-tile static colliders are `createTransformNode` + `createPhysicsBody(world, node, STATIC)` + `createPhysicsShape` + `setPhysicsBodyShape`, with the node never added to the scene — WHY: `createPhysicsAggregate` requires a Mesh (would force 1024 real meshes), while the character controller proves a bare TransformNode anchors a physics body fine (character-controller.ts:335).\nDECISION: Quake-style slide is driven by the controller's public `staticFriction`/`dynamicFriction` fields — WHY: the shape-access fallback in the plan is unnecessary; the friction knobs are exposed directly on `PhysicsCharacterController` (character-controller.ts:283-285).\nDECISION: HUD uses the 2D overlay path (`loadFont` → `createDefaultTextData` → `createTextLayer` → `createTextRenderer` → `registerTextRenderer`, scene180 pattern), not the in-world `createTextRenderable` (scene181) — WHY: the HUD (health/kills/crosshair) is screen-space and scene180 is the standalone 2D text reference.\nDECISION: FPS camera is a `FreeCamera` whose `position` and `_yaw`/`_pitch` are driven manually each frame from pointer-lock deltas — WHY: FreeCamera exposes `position: ObservableVec3` plus `_yaw`/`_pitch` fields (free-camera.ts:19-33), and `attachFreeControl` is for orbit-style control, not mouse-look.\nDECISION: Bullet/terrain collision filtering uses `physicsRaycast`'s `RaycastQuery { membership, collideWith }` masks — WHY: confirmed the query shape at havok-queries.ts:207 and the per-shape mask setters at havok.ts:578/589, so bullets can target only terrain+debris.\nDECISION: `bundle-size.spec.ts` does not cover scene252 — WHY: it only tests scenes with `maxRawKB` in scene-config.json, and this game demo gets no entry there (consistent with the \"not a parity scene\" decision).\nDECISION: NavCrowd setup follows scene170 verbatim (`createNavCrowd(nav, maxAgents, maxAgentRadius)`, `addAgent` with radius/height/maxSpeed/separationWeight) — WHY: it's the established lab idiom and gives bot-vs-bot separation for free.","timings":{"cache_n":49408,"draft_n":3423,"draft_n_accepted":934,"predicted_ms":40780.0,"predicted_n":1423,"prompt_ms":290.0,"prompt_n":126},"to_request":40409,"usage":{"cached_tokens":49408,"completion_tokens":1423,"prompt_tokens":49534}}
