{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"The user is asking me to enumerate the constraints that were revealed in the step I just completed (the S1 verification batch). Let me think about what I learned in this step.\n\nWhat I verified in this step:\n1. Re-read GUIDANCE.md — most of the constraints in there were already recorded in previous sessions (WebGPU only, tree-shaking, no module-level side effects, no GPU handles, bundle size, etc.). Those were already known.\n2. The frame observable is `onBeforeRender(scene, cb)` — this is a fact, not a constraint.\n3. scene40's Havok pattern — fact.\n4. `createFlatGroundData` returns GroundData — fact.\n5. `resizeMeshGeometry` is an in-place seam — this is a decision/fact, not a constraint.\n6. The controller exposes `staticFriction`/`dynamicFriction` as public fields — fact.\n7. scene180/181 text flow — fact.\n8. `createPhysicsAggregate` takes a Mesh node. `createPhysicsBody` takes a SceneNode. TransformNode is invisible — this affects design decisions, but is it a constraint? \"Physics bodies are node-anchored\" was already recorded (interview-t5-2).\n9. scene-config.json is only for parity scenes — the bundle-size spec only covers scenes that have maxRawKB in scene-config.json — this was already a planned item (S1 check), and now confirmed.\n10. `resizeMeshGeometry` \"recomputes bounds\" and retains CPU geometry — fact.\n11. Thin instance API — fact.\n12. `addBoxObstacle(plugin, position, halfExtents, angle)` — fact.\n13. FreeCamera has `@internal` `_yaw`/`_pitch` fields — interesting. FreeCamera exposes yaw/pitch as @internal fields. In lab scene code, internal members can be read with full typing (per the 4b′ note in GUIDANCE: \"Internal code reads fields directly with full TypeScript typing\"). Hmm, but is it a constraint? It's a fact about the API shape.\n14. NavMeshParameters — scene170 shows the full parameter set — fact.\n15. `createNavCrowd(nav, 10, 0.1)` + `addAgent(crowd, position, params)` — fact.\n\nThe question is specifically: \"Did you learn or commit to any constraints that the rest of this project must follow — requirements, environmental limits, compatibility rules, things that must never be done? Enumerate each on its own line as CONSTRAINT: <rule>. Only constraints that surfaced in this step.\"\n\nNew constraints that surfaced in this step (not already recorded):\n\n1. Terrain geometry replacement must go through `resizeMeshGeometry` (not raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + manual `_gpu` swap) — this is because it bumps `_renderableVersion` on every registered scene, forcing cached draw bundles to re-record. Otherwise, they'd keep binding the old buffers that are about to be freed. This is a genuine compatibility rule I learned in this step: raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + `_gpu` assignment bypasses the version bump and the deferred destruction safety. Actually, wait — is this a \"constraint\" or a \"decision\"? It's a rule the terrain surgery code must follow: use resizeMeshGeometry for in-place geometry replacement. I think it's worth recording as a constraint on the implementation.\n\n2. The character controller's friction is set via the controller's public fields `staticFriction`/`dynamicFriction` (defaults 0/1) — not via shape material. Hmm, this is more of a fact/pointer than a constraint.\n\n3. The bundle-size spec only covers scenes with `maxRawKB` in scene-config.json. Since scene252 isn't in scene-config.json, it's unaffected — this is a confirmation of an existing plan assumption, not a new constraint.\n\n4. `createPhysicsAggregate` requires a Mesh node. For per-tile static bodies, use `createPhysicsBody(world, node, STATIC)` + `createPhysicsShape` + `setPhysicsBodyShape` with a TransformNode (the controller proves that a TransformNode works and is invisible). This is a design constraint for the terrain module: per-tile bodies must be attached to a TransformNode, not a Mesh (to avoid 1024 meshes/draw calls). This surfaced in this step — I confirmed that createPhysicsAggregate's signature is `node: Mesh`, while createPhysicsBody takes a SceneNode. I think this is a genuine constraint that should be followed: per-tile static bodies use TransformNode + createPhysicsBody (STATIC) + box shape. Because createPhysicsAggregate requires a Mesh.\n\n5. FreeCamera's `_yaw`/`_pitch` are @internal — the FPS camera code must read/write them directly (per GUIDANCE 4b′, internal code reads fields directly). This is a fact, but it also means \"don't look for a public rotation API on FreeCamera.\"\n\n6. The text HUD in a 3D scene uses `createTextRenderable` + `addTextRenderable(scene, text)` (scene181's pattern), not `createTextRenderer` (scene180's standalone 2D path). This is a constraint on S6: in-scene HUD uses createTextRenderable. scene180's standalone path was recorded earlier (interview-t5-f25985-4 says \"S6 should copy the scene180/181 flow verbatim\"), but now it's clarified: scene180 = standalone TextRenderer, scene181 = TextRenderable inside a scene. So the constraint is: HUD in a 3D scene = createTextRenderable + addTextRenderable.\n\n7. `updateNavMeshObstacles`/`addBoxObstacle` call `_waitForFullTileCacheUpdate` — synchronous blocking update loop. Not a constraint per se.\n\n8. Physics: `scene.fixedDeltaMs = 1000 / PHYSICS_FPS` — scene40 sets this. The FPS scene must set fixedDeltaMs for the physics step. Fact/pointer.\n\nAlso, per GUIDANCE §2 \"When adding a new scene, always…\", the nine items (rollup inputs, parity tests, reference screenshots, thumbnails, gallery cards, bundle ceilings, scene-config.json) — but our decision (interview-t4-f13394-1) is that this is a lab demo entry, not a parity scene, and auto-discovery via getHtmlInputs() means no manifest edit is needed. Hmm, but does this demo entry still need a gallery card? The decision says \"no golden reference, no pixel-diff spec, no bundle ceiling entry.\" That was already recorded. Not new in this step.\n\nLet me be careful: \"Only constraints that surfaced in this step.\" The step just completed was S1 verification (a batch of greps). The constraints that surfaced there:\n\n- CONSTRAINT: In-place terrain geometry replacement must use `resizeMeshGeometry` (mesh-factories.ts). Because raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + `_gpu` assignment skips the `_renderableVersion` bump and deferred buffer destruction, so cached draw bundles keep binding freed buffers.\n- CONSTRAINT: Per-tile static physics bodies must be attached to a `TransformNode` via `createPhysicsBody(world, node, STATIC)` + `createPhysicsShape` + `setPhysicsBodyShape` — `createPhysicsAggregate` requires a `Mesh` node, and creating 1024 meshes would add draw calls.\n- CONSTRAINT: In-scene HUD (3D scene) must use `createTextRenderable` + `addTextRenderable` (scene181's pattern), not the standalone `createTextRenderer` path (scene180 is a 2D-only path with no scene).\n- CONSTRAINT: FPS camera control must write FreeCamera's `@internal` `_yaw`/`_pitch` fields directly — there is no public rotation API on FreeCamera.\n- CONSTRAINT: The physics scene must set `scene.fixedDeltaMs` (e.g., 1000/60). Otherwise the character controller's step is a no-op (moveWithCollisions early-returns when `world._timestep` is 0). Hmm — actually this is derived: moveWithCollisions checks `if (!deltaTime || deltaTime <= 0) return;`. If fixedDeltaMs isn't set, does _timestep default to something? scene40 explicitly sets `scene.fixedDeltaMs = 1000 / PHYSICS_FPS`. So yes, the constraint is: set scene.fixedDeltaMs for physics-driven movement.\n\nAlso, the controller's friction fields: `staticFriction` (default 0) and `dynamicFriction` (default 1) are public fields on the controller — for Quake-style sliding, set `staticFriction`/`dynamicFriction` on the controller, not on the terrain shape. This is a design decision surfaced in this step, which supersedes the plan's risk note \"controller shape access for friction (fallback: low friction on terrain tile shapes)\" — the controller exposes friction directly. Should I record it as a constraint? It's more of a decision. The question asks for constraints — \"requirements, environmental limits, compatibility rules, things that must never be done.\" Controller friction fields are a pointer/decision, not a constraint. I'll mention it briefly, but the CONSTRAINT lines should be reserved for genuine rules.\n\nActually, let me reconsider #3: is it a constraint? It's a \"must follow\" rule for S6: use createTextRenderable for in-scene HUD. Yes, it constrains the implementation.\n\n#4: writing to @internal fields — per GUIDANCE 4b′, this is allowed (\"Internal code reads fields directly with full TypeScript typing\"). The constraint is that no public rotation API exists, so direct field access is required.\n\nOne more: `resizeMeshGeometry` retains CPU geometry (`_cpuPositions` etc.) — so the terrain module should track its own index arrays and pass them to resizeMeshGeometry. Not a constraint.\n\nAnother possibility: the `physicsRaycast` query uses `membership`/`collideWith` masks defaulting to `~0` — to filter bullets vs. debris, use `setPhysicsShapeFilterMembershipMask`/`setPhysicsShapeFilterCollideMask`. That was already recorded (interview-t3-6).\n\nI think the main new constraints are these:\n\n1. Terrain re-upload must go through `resizeMeshGeometry` (never raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + `_gpu` assignment) — otherwise cached draw bundles bind freed buffers (missing the `_renderableVersion` bump + deferred destruction).\n2. Per-tile static bodies: `createPhysicsAggregate` requires a Mesh node, so use a TransformNode + `createPhysicsBody` (STATIC) + `createPhysicsShape`/`setPhysicsBodyShape` — one invisible TransformNode per tile, no extra meshes/draw calls.\n3. In-scene HUD: `createTextRenderable` + `addTextRenderable` (scene181's pattern). The standalone `createTextRenderer` path (scene180) is 2D-only with no scene.\n4. FPS camera: FreeCamera has no public rotation API — write `@internal` `_yaw`/`_pitch` directly (allowed by GUIDANCE 4b′).\n5. Physics stepping requires `scene.fixedDeltaMs` (e.g., 1000/60). The character controller's `moveWithCollisions` is a no-op without a timestep.\n\nShould I also record these via update_record? The user's message is a meta-question asking for enumeration. I should answer the question. I can also record via update_record — but the instruction is to answer the question. I'll answer concisely with CONSTRAINT lines. Should I also call update_record? The question is \"did you learn or commit to any constraints… enumerate each on its own line.\" The expected answer is a list. I'll provide just the list. Recording is a \"never required\" option. To keep the turn clean, I'll answer without tool calls — actually, recording the constraints is genuinely useful. But the user's pause is asking for a direct answer. I'll answer directly. I can also update_record in the same turn — the tool is \"never required.\" I'll just answer. Hmm, but if I record, future turns will have them. The user explicitly asked for enumeration, suggesting they want to see them. I'll provide the list, and also record them to the working set (useful, not intrusive). Actually — let me keep it simple and just answer. The user will probably record/act on the answer. But the working set is my memory. Recording costs nothing. I'll do both: update_record (constraint field) + the answer.\n\nWait, I should be careful not to fabricate: the claim that raw uploadMeshToGPU + _gpu assignment is unsafe is derived from the resizeMeshGeometry doc comment (\"Any cached draw recordings that captured raw buffer handles… must re-record, or they'll keep binding the old buffers we're about to free\"). Yes, that's exactly what the comment says. Good.\n\nClaim #2: createPhysicsAggregate's signature is `node: Mesh` — verified at havok.ts:1141. createPhysicsBody takes `node: SceneNode` — verified at :448. TransformNode works as a physics node — verified in the character controller's constructor (creates a TransformNode, doesn't add it to the scene, and the body is created on it). Good.\n\nClaim #3: scene180's header says \"Standalone 2D text path: no scene, no camera\" — verified. scene181 uses createTextRenderable + addTextRenderable in a 3D scene — verified.\n\nClaim #4: FreeCamera interface — `_yaw`, `_pitch` are @internal — verified at free-camera.ts:30-33. No public rotation field. Verified.\n\nClaim #5: moveWithCollisions early-returns when `!deltaTime || deltaTime <= 0` (deltaTime = world._timestep) — verified. scene40 sets scene.fixedDeltaMs — verified. The implication (that fixedDeltaMs drives _timestep) is a reasonable inference from scene40's pattern + the controller's guard. I'll phrase it as: physics-driven movement requires scene.fixedDeltaMs to be set (scene40's pattern), because moveWithCollisions is a no-op without a timestep.\n\nFormat: one CONSTRAINT per line. I'll keep each line concise.\n","seq":43699,"t":1888134,"text":"\n\nCONSTRAINT: Terrain geometry replacement must go through `resizeMeshGeometry` (mesh-factories.ts), never raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + manual `_gpu` assignment — it bumps every registered scene's `_renderableVersion` (forcing cached draw bundles to re-record) and defers old-buffer destruction until the GPU drains; skipping it leaves cached bundles binding freed buffers.\nCONSTRAINT: Per-tile static physics bodies must be node-anchored to invisible `TransformNode`s via `createPhysicsBody(world, node, STATIC)` + `createPhysicsShape` + `setPhysicsBodyShape` — `createPhysicsAggregate` requires a `Mesh` node (havok.ts:1141), and 1024 extra meshes would add draw calls; the character controller (character-controller.ts) proves a TransformNode works as a physics node without being added to the scene.\nCONSTRAINT: The in-scene HUD must use `createTextRenderable` + `addTextRenderable(scene, text)` (scene181 pattern) — scene180's `createTextRenderer`/`registerTextRenderer` path is explicitly standalone 2D (\"no scene, no camera\") and is the wrong tool for a 3D overlay.\nCONSTRAINT: FPS mouse-look must write FreeCamera's `@internal` `_yaw`/`_pitch` fields directly (free-camera.ts:30-33) — there is no public rotation API on FreeCamera, and GUIDANCE 4b′ permits reading/writing `@internal` members in scene code.\nCONSTRAINT: The scene must set `scene.fixedDeltaMs` (e.g. `1000/60`, scene40 pattern) — `moveWithCollisions`/`integrate` are no-ops when the world timestep is zero, so physics-driven player/bot movement silently dies without it.\n\nAlso surfaced (decision, not constraint): controller friction is set via public fields `staticFriction`/`dynamicFriction` on `PhysicsCharacterController` (defaults 0/1) — this resolves the plan's open risk about controller-shape access; no terrain-shape friction fallback needed.\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":49408,"draft_n":8393,"draft_n_accepted":2618,"predicted_ms":88500.0,"predicted_n":3817,"prompt_ms":280.0,"prompt_n":103},"to_request":41338,"usage":{"cached_tokens":49408,"completion_tokens":3817,"prompt_tokens":49511}}
