{"kind":"delta","request":40538,"seq":44713,"t":1939480,"tool_call":{"arguments":"{\"field\": \"evidence\", \"content\": \"S1 verification results (all confirmed in packages/babylon-lite/src):\\n- Frame observable: onBeforeRender(scene, cb) at scene/scene-core.ts:236.\\n- physicsRaycast(world, from, to, query) — query: {membership?, collideWith?, shouldHitTriggers?}, defaults ~0; result has hitPoint/hitNormal/hitDistance/body (physics/havok-queries.ts:207).\\n- Controller friction is exposed as public fields on PhysicsCharacterController: staticFriction (default 0), dynamicFriction (default 1) — no need to touch terrain shape masks for slide.\\n- resizeMeshGeometry(engine, mesh, positions, normals, indices, uvs?, ...) (mesh-factories.ts:~103) is the in-place geometry replacement seam: reallocates GPU buffers, bumps every registered scene's _renderableVersion so cached bundles re-record, updates _cpuPositions/_cpuNormals/_cpuIndices. THIS is the tile-removal path (not raw uploadMeshToGPU).\\n- createFlatGroundData({width, height, subdivisions}) → {positions, normals, uvs, indices}; grid is (subdiv+1)² verts, row 0 at z=-height/2, col 0 at x=-width/2; quad (row,col) indices at offset (row*subdiv + col)*6.\\n- createMeshFromData(engine, name, positions, normals, indices, uvs?, ...) — mesh factory; retains _cpuPositions/_cpuIndices for picking.\\n- Havok: const hknp = await HavokPhysics({locateFile: () => \\\"/HavokPhysics.wasm\\\"}); const world = createHavokWorld(scene, hknp, {x:0,y:-9.8,z:0}); scene.fixedDeltaMs = 1000/60 (scene40 pattern).\\n- Static per-tile bodies: createPhysicsBody(world, node: SceneNode, PhysicsMotionType.STATIC) + createPhysicsShape(world, {type: BOX, parameters: {extents}}) + setPhysicsBodyShape(world, body, shape); TransformNode (not added to scene) is valid — character controller does exactly this. removePhysicsBody(world, body) for removal. setPhysicsShapeMaterial(world, shape, friction, restitution) for slide friction.\\n- Controller: createPhysicsCharacterController(world, pos, {capsuleHeight, capsuleRadius}); getPosition/setPosition/getVelocity/setVelocity/moveWithCollisions(displacement)/integrate(dt, surfaceInfo, gravity)/checkSupport(dt, direction)/dispose; onTriggerCollisionObservable (character-controller.ts:1348).\\n- FreeCamera: world matrix = mat4LookAtLH(position, target, up); position/target are ObservableVec3 (auto-dirty). _yaw/_pitch are internal, only used by attachFreeControl. FPS camera: set cam.position + cam.target each frame from player eye + (yaw,pitch).\\n- HUD: registerTextRenderer registers a rendering context on the surface (registration order = render order; scene first, text renderer second → text on top); createTextRenderer(engine, {layers, clear: false}) so it doesn't wipe the 3D frame; layers with positionPx; updateDefaultTextData(data, text) to change content (scene180 pattern).\\n- Nav: no agent reposition API — NavCrowd agents drift from controllers; mitigate by re-targeting. addBoxObstacle(plugin, position, halfExtents, angle) exists for holes.\\n- PhysicsWorld._timestep is @internal — use the dt param of onPhysicsAfterStep(world, (timestep) => ...).\\n- Bundle-size spec only covers scenes in scene-config.json with maxRawKB — scene252 unaffected.\"}","id":"call_9ca42a0bf7664fea976df872","index":0,"name":"update_record"}}
