{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Alright. So I'll write `fps-terrain.ts`. Let me design it carefully:\n\n```ts\n// FPS terrain: seeded value-noise heights on a dense grid, one static box collider per tile,\n// and tile removal via index surgery + resizeMeshGeometry.\n\nimport {\n    createFlatGroundData,\n    createMeshFromData,\n    computeNormals,\n    resizeMeshGeometry,\n    createTransformNode,\n    createPhysicsBody,\n    createPhysicsShape,\n    setPhysicsBodyShape,\n    setPhysicsShapeMaterial,\n    removePhysicsBody,\n    addBoxObstacle,\n    PhysicsMotionType,\n    PhysicsShapeType,\n} from \"babylon-lite\";\nimport type { EngineContext, Mesh, PhysicsWorld, NavigationPlugin, PhysicsBody, ObstacleHandle } from \"babylon-lite\";\n\nexport const ARENA_SIZE = 128;\nexport const TILE_SIZE = 4;\nexport const TILE_COUNT = ARENA_SIZE / TILE_SIZE; // 32 tiles per axis\nexport const NOISE_AMPLITUDE = 5;\n\n/** Collision layer for terrain tile boxes. */\nexport const TERRAIN_LAYER = 1;\n\nexport interface FpsTile {\n    tx: number;\n    tz: number;\n    alive: boolean;\n    body: PhysicsBody | null;\n    obstacle: ObstacleHandle | null;\n}\n\nexport interface FpsTerrain {\n    mesh: Mesh;\n    tiles: FpsTile[];\n    destroyedCount: number;\n}\n\n// Seeded PRNG (mulberry32) — no module-level state, all per-call.\nfunction makeRng(seed: number): () => number { ... }\n\n// Low-frequency value noise: coarse random grid, bilinear interp with smoothstep.\nfunction heightAt(x: number, z: number, coarse: Float32Array, gridSize: number): number { ... }\n\nexport function createFpsTerrain(engine: EngineContext, world: PhysicsWorld, seed = 1337): FpsTerrain {\n    const ground = createFlatGroundData({ width: ARENA_SIZE, height: ARENA_SIZE, subdivisions: TILE_COUNT });\n    const cols = TILE_COUNT + 1;\n    // Displace Y with noise\n    for (let row = 0; row < cols; row++) {\n        for (let col = 0; col < cols; col++) {\n            const i = (row * cols + col) * 3;\n            const x = ground.positions[i]!;\n            const z = ground.positions[i + 2]!;\n            ground.positions[i + 1] = heightAt(x, z);\n        }\n    }\n    const normals = computeNormals(ground.positions, ground.indices);\n    const mesh = createMeshFromData(engine, \"fpsTerrain\", ground.positions, normals, ground.indices, ground.uvs);\n    ...\n    // Per-tile static boxes\n    for (let tz = 0; tz < TILE_COUNT; tz++) {\n        for (let tx = 0; tx < TILE_COUNT; tx++) {\n            const yTop = max of 4 corners, yBottom = min\n            const node = createTransformNode(\"fpsTile\", cx, (yTop + yBottom) / 2, cz);\n            const body = createPhysicsBody(world, node, PhysicsMotionType.STATIC);\n            const shape = createPhysicsShape(world, { type: PhysicsShapeType.BOX, parameters: { extents: { x: TILE_SIZE/2, y: (yTop - yBottom)/2 + 1, z: TILE_SIZE/2 } } });\n            setPhysicsBodyShape(world, body, shape);\n            setPhysicsShapeMaterial(world, shape, 0.1, 0);\n            // Membership mask: TERRAIN_LAYER\n            setPhysicsShapeFilterMembershipMask(world, shape, TERRAIN_LAYER);\n            ...\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nWait — I need to check the BOX parameters for `createPhysicsShape`: `PhysicsShapeParameters` — for BOX, is it `extents`? Let me check the PhysicsShapeParameters type. And how does `_buildShapeParams` construct the box parameters in createPhysicsAggregate — I'll read that part to get the exact parameter names.\n\nAlso `setPhysicsShapeFilterMembershipMask(world, shape, mask)` — signature confirmed at havok.ts:578.\n\nLet me check PhysicsShapeParameters.\n","seq":45350,"t":1970867,"text":"","timings":{"cache_n":68096,"draft_n":1708,"draft_n_accepted":828,"predicted_ms":18610.0,"predicted_n":1072,"prompt_ms":1240.0,"prompt_n":455},"to_request":44866,"usage":{"cached_tokens":68096,"completion_tokens":1072,"prompt_tokens":68551}}
