{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"The user is asking about the discoveries made in the step I just completed (the S1 verification batch). Let me look back: what was different from expectations?\n\n1. `resizeMeshGeometry` exists as an in-place geometry replacement — I had planned on a raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + manual `_gpu` swap. This is a discovery: the intended seam is `resizeMeshGeometry`, which bumps the renderable version. This is a \"the API works differently than expected\" — my plan was pointing at a lower-level seam.\n\n2. The controller's friction is exposed as public fields `staticFriction`/`dynamicFriction` — the plan said \"the shape getter on the controller is unverified; if exposed, use the controller-shape friction as the preferred target\" — verified as exposed. This resolves the plan's open question, and is more of a confirmation than a gotcha. But compared to the plan's uncertainty, it's a discovery.\n\n3. The world matrix of FreeCamera is computed from position+target via `mat4LookAtLH`, not from `_yaw`/`_pitch` — `_yaw`/`_pitch` are only used by `attachFreeControl`. My initial expectation (set `_yaw`/`_pitch` directly) was wrong. This is a genuine GOTCHA: the implication is that the FPS camera has to set `cam.position` and `cam.target` every frame.\n\n4. The nav has no agent reposition API — NavCrowd agents can drift from the controller. The plan assumed NavCrowd agents would be fine. Implication: re-targeting is required / a drift mitigation is needed.\n\n5. The HUD's TextRenderer registers as a separate rendering context on the same surface — ordering = registration order; you have to register the scene first and the text renderer later, and use `clear: false`. My expectation was that it would just \"draw on top\"; actually it's a context ordering issue.\n\n6. `PhysicsWorld._timestep` is @internal — I have to use the dt parameter of onPhysicsAfterStep. A minor discovery.\n\n7. `createPhysicsBody` reads the node's transform at creation time (setting QTransform after adding to the world) — this confirms that a static body with a TransformNode works, and it's positioned at the node's position at creation time. This is a confirmation, not a gotcha.\n\n8. update_record got dropped (\"dropped: the groundedness gate kept nothing of it\") — this is a tooling event, not a repository discovery. Should I mention it? The question is about the behavior of the step — the record call was silently dropped. Hmm, that's a harness event, not a repository API discovery. The user's question is about \"an API that works differently than expected, an error and its actual cause, a discovered limitation or unsupported feature.\" The dropped record is not a repository discovery. But it is an actual behavioral difference from expectation — I intended to record the S1 findings and it got dropped. I should probably mention it so I can re-record. Actually, on second thought — let me stay focused on the repo discoveries and just briefly mention the dropped record.\n\nWait, should I re-record right now? The user asked for a pause + enumeration. Let me answer the question, and since the record was dropped, maybe re-record the S1 findings. The user's instruction is: \"enumerate each item on its own line as GOTCHA: ...\". Let me stick to that format. I can add a short note about the dropped record.\n\nLet me carefully write out the gotchas:\n\nGOTCHA: `resizeMeshGeometry(engine, mesh, positions, normals, indices, uvs?)` (mesh-factories.ts) is the intended in-place geometry replacement — it bumps `_renderableVersion` on all registered scenes so cached draw bundles re-record — IMPLICATION: use this for tile removal, not a raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + manual `mesh._gpu` swap (which would leave cached bundles binding freed buffers).\n\nGOTCHA: FreeCamera's world matrix is built from `position`+`target` (`mat4LookAtLH`), not from `_yaw`/`_pitch` (those are internal and only consumed by `attachFreeControl`) — IMPLICATION: the FPS camera has to set `cam.position` and `cam.target` every frame from the player's eye position + (yaw, pitch); setting `_yaw`/`_pitch` alone does nothing.\n\nGOTCHA: NavCrowd has no agent reposition/teleport API — the agent's path can drift from the character controller's actual position — IMPLICATION: drive the bot's controller with the agent's velocity and re-target (`agentGoto`) periodically / on drift; or fall back to `computePath` waypoint following if drift is bad.\n\nGOTCHA: TextRenderer is a separate rendering context on the same surface — render order = registration order in `surface._renderingContexts` — IMPLICATION: register the 3D scene first, the text renderer later, and create it with `clear: false` so it doesn't clear the 3D frame.\n\nGOTCHA: `PhysicsWorld._timestep` is @internal — IMPLICATION: get dt from the `onPhysicsAfterStep(world, (timestep) => ...)` callback parameter instead.\n\nGOTCHA: The controller's friction is exposed as public fields (`staticFriction`, `dynamicFriction`) on `PhysicsCharacterController` — IMPLICATION: Quake-style slide can be tuned via the controller's fields, no need to reach into the shape's material (the plan's open question is resolved).\n\nHmm, is the last one a \"gotcha\"? It's a confirmation that removes the plan's uncertainty. The user said \"an API that works differently than expected.\" I expected I'd have to hunt for a shape getter; it's just a public field. I'll include it — it changes what I do (simpler).\n\nAlso: the `update_record` call was dropped by the groundedness gate — I should mention it so I can re-record. I'll add a short note at the end.\n\nActually, let me reconsider #1: was it \"different from expectation\"? My plan (S2) said \"index surgery + re-upload + body removal\" via `uploadMeshToGPU`. What I discovered is that there's a dedicated `resizeMeshGeometry` that does exactly that with bundle re-recording. The raw uploadMeshToGPU path would have been wrong (stale draw bundles). Yes, a genuine gotcha.\n\nAnything else? The comment on `createPhysicsBody` \"add to the world first, then set the transform (Havok resets the transform on add)\" — that's an implementation detail, confirmed to work. Not a gotcha.\n\nThe winding order / index offset of `createFlatGroundData` — confirmed as expected. Not a gotcha.\n\nKeep the list tight — 5–6 items.\n","seq":45968,"t":1998973,"text":"\n\nGOTCHA: `resizeMeshGeometry(engine, mesh, positions, normals, indices, uvs?)` (mesh-factories.ts) is the dedicated in-place geometry-replacement seam — it bumps every registered scene's `_renderableVersion` so cached draw bundles re-record — IMPLICATION: tile removal must use it, not a raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + manual `mesh._gpu` swap (which would leave cached bundles binding the freed buffers).\nGOTCHA: FreeCamera's world matrix is built from `position` + `target` via `mat4LookAtLH`; `_yaw`/`_pitch` are internal and only consumed by `attachFreeControl` — IMPLICATION: the FPS camera must set `cam.position` and `cam.target` each frame from the player's eye + (yaw, pitch); setting `_yaw`/`_pitch` alone changes nothing.\nGOTCHA: NavCrowd has no agent reposition/teleport API — the agent's simulated position can drift from the character controller's real position — IMPLICATION: drive the bot controller with the agent's velocity and re-target via `agentGoto` periodically/on drift; fall back to `computePath` waypoint-following if drift gets bad.\nGOTCHA: A TextRenderer is a separate rendering context on the same surface, and render order = registration order in `surface._renderingContexts` — IMPLICATION: register the 3D scene first and the text renderer second, and create it with `clear: false` so it overlays instead of wiping the 3D frame.\nGOTCHA: `PhysicsWorld._timestep` is `@internal` — IMPLICATION: read dt from the `onPhysicsAfterStep(world, (timestep) => ...)` callback parameter instead.\nGOTCHA: The controller's friction is plain public fields (`staticFriction`, `dynamicFriction`) on `PhysicsCharacterController` — the plan's open question (\"does the controller expose its shape for friction?\") resolves as: no shape access needed, tune the fields directly — IMPLICATION: Quake slide is tuned via controller fields + `setPhysicsShapeMaterial` on the tile shapes, both already planned.\n\nAlso noting: my `update_record` call for the S1 findings was dropped by the groundedness gate (\"kept nothing of it\"), so those notes are not in the working set — I'll re-record the key ones before writing code.","timings":{"cache_n":68096,"draft_n":4088,"draft_n_accepted":1396,"predicted_ms":50190.0,"predicted_n":1980,"prompt_ms":730.0,"prompt_n":218},"to_request":44823,"usage":{"cached_tokens":68096,"completion_tokens":1980,"prompt_tokens":68314}}
