{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Let me look back on what I found in this step (the S1 verification batch). Are there any discrepancies between the plan's assumptions and reality?\n\n1. **`resizeMeshGeometry`** — The plan (recorded in r22627) says \"destroy = remove the tile's index range from _cpuIndices, computeNormals, uploadMeshToGPU, removePhysicsBody, addBoxObstacle\". Actual finding: `resizeMeshGeometry(engine, mesh, positions, normals, indices, uvs?)` is the appropriate seam — it replaces the GPU geometry in place, bumps `_renderableVersion` so cached bundles get re-recorded, and updates the `_cpuPositions/_cpuNormals/_cpuIndices` copies. If you do a raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + manual `_gpu` swap, the cached draw bundle won't be re-recorded (the comment in mesh-factories.ts explicitly states that a version bump is required). This is a genuine \"works differently than expected\" discovery — the plan said uploadMeshToGPU, but the actually correct API is resizeMeshGeometry.\n\n2. **`createPhysicsAggregate` takes a `Mesh`** — the plan assumed a per-tile static box via createPhysicsAggregate, but the type signature is `node: Mesh`. A TransformNode is not a Mesh, so I'll have to use createPhysicsBody + createPhysicsShape + setPhysicsBodyShape directly. The TransformNode itself works (createPhysicsBody takes a SceneNode), and I've confirmed that the initial transform is read from the node at creation time. So: the plan's \"createPhysicsAggregate\" was slightly wrong — it works, but only if the node is a Mesh. For invisible per-tile colliders, the correct call is createPhysicsBody + createPhysicsShape + setPhysicsBodyShape.\n\n3. **The controller's friction is exposed as a public field** — the plan (interview-t5-f27685-6) said \"the controller's shape getter is unverified, and terrain friction applies consistently to the player and bots\" with the fallback of \"low friction on the terrain tile shape\". Actual: `staticFriction`/`dynamicFriction` are public fields on the controller — so Quake-style sliding can be set directly on the controller (default staticFriction=0, dynamicFriction=1 — note that this is the opposite of what one might expect).\n\n4. **NavCrowd has no agent reposition API** — the plan said \"N=4 bots = character controller + NavCrowd agent (agentGoto/findRandomPoint, updateNavCrowd per step)\". Actual: navigation.ts has no setAgentPosition — agents drift from the controller's position due to collisions. Need to mitigate (re-targeting) or fall back to computePath.\n\n5. **PhysicsWorld._timestep is @internal** — the controller uses it internally, but scene code shouldn't read it. Use the `timestep` parameter of onPhysicsAfterStep instead.\n\n6. **FreeCamera's world matrix is built from position+target** (mat4LookAtLH), not from _yaw/_pitch — _yaw/_pitch are only used by attachFreeControl. So the FPS camera must set position+target every frame, not yaw/pitch. This is different from the plan's \"camera follow via pointer-lock yaw/pitch\" — I still track yaw/pitch as game state, but I have to write to cam.position/cam.target.\n\n7. **`applyPhysicsImpulse` does not exist** — audit-28769-3 lists it as a confirmed debris function, but the actual export is `applyPhysicsBodyImpulse` (havok.ts:~513). The old note was wrong.\n\n8. **Bundle size spec** — confirmed that only scenes in scene-config.json that have maxRawKB are targeted — no issue, no surprise.\n\n9. **TextRenderer ordering** — registerTextRenderer registers a rendering context on the surface. Order = registration order. The scene is registered first → text is drawn on top. This is as expected, not a gotcha.\n\n10. **createFlatGroundData winding/index layout** — no problem, matches the plan's calculation.\n\n11. **`_cpuIndices` is updated by resizeMeshGeometry** — meaning on each destruction, we should read from mesh._cpuIndices (or track our own array). No problem.\n\nThe user is specifically asking about \"the step just completed\" — that is, the S1 verification step. What to list as genuine gotchas:\n\n- resizeMeshGeometry vs uploadMeshToGPU (the plan was wrong about the seam)\n- createPhysicsAggregate's node: Mesh (not TransformNode) — need createPhysicsBody+createPhysicsShape\n- Controller friction as a public field (the plan's uncertainty is resolved — works differently than the fallback assumed)\n- NavCrowd has no agent reposition\n- FreeCamera's matrix comes from position+target, not from _yaw/_pitch\n- applyPhysicsImpulse → applyPhysicsBodyImpulse (name correction)\n- PhysicsWorld._timestep is @internal — use the callback's dt\n\nThese are discoveries from this step. I'll list them in GOTCHA format.\n","seq":46985,"t":2050413,"text":"\n\nGOTCHA: the plan's terrain-rebuild seam was `uploadMeshToGPU` + manual `_gpu` swap, but the correct API is `resizeMeshGeometry(engine, mesh, positions, normals, indices, uvs?)` (mesh-factories.ts) — it reallocates buffers in place AND bumps every registered scene's `_renderableVersion` so cached draw bundles re-record; a raw `uploadMeshToGPU` swap would keep stale buffer bindings — IMPLICATION: destroyTile must call `resizeMeshGeometry`, and must read fresh geometry from `mesh._cpuIndices`/`_cpuPositions` each time (resize updates those copies), not from a cached copy I own.\nGOTCHA: `createPhysicsAggregate(world, node, ...)` is typed `node: Mesh`, not `SceneNode` — a bare TransformNode per tile won't compile against it — IMPLICATION: per-tile static boxes must be built with `createPhysicsBody(world, node, PhysicsMotionType.STATIC)` + `createPhysicsShape(world, {type: BOX, parameters: {extents}})` + `setPhysicsBodyShape(world, body, shape)` (the character controller proves TransformNode + physics body works; `createPhysicsBody` reads `node.position`/`rotationQuaternion` at creation, so the node must be positioned before the call).\nGOTCHA: the controller's friction is exposed as plain public fields (`staticFriction` default 0, `dynamicFriction` default 1) on `PhysicsCharacterController` — the plan's fallback assumed I'd tune friction on the terrain tile shapes — IMPLICATION: Quake slide is set on the controller fields directly (low `dynamicFriction`), and terrain-shape friction (`setPhysicsShapeMaterial`) is a secondary lever for bots/debris only.\nGOTCHA: `FreeCamera`'s world matrix is computed from `position` + `target` (`mat4LookAtLH`), not from `_yaw`/`_pitch` (those are internal state only `attachFreeControl` consumes) — IMPLICATION: the FPS camera must write `cam.position` and `cam.target` every frame from player eye + yaw/pitch; I keep yaw/pitch as game state but never expect the camera to expose a rotation setter.\nGOTCHA: NavCrowd has no agent reposition API (navigation.ts exports only `addAgent`/`getAgentPosition`/`getAgentVelocity`/`agentGoto`/`updateNavCrowd`) — the plan assumed `agentGoto`+`updateNavCrowd` per step would keep bots glued to their controllers — IMPLICATION: nav agents will drift from colliding controllers; I must re-target periodically (and fall back to `computePath` waypoint steering if drift causes stuck bots during playtest), and the drift check belongs in the bot update.\nGOTCHA: `PhysicsWorld._timestep` is `@internal` — IMPLICATION: game code must take the timestep from the `onPhysicsAfterStep(world, (timestep) => ...)` callback parameter, not from the world.\nGOTCHA: the debris impulse export is `applyPhysicsBodyImpulse(body, impulse, location)` — the working-set note's `applyPhysicsImpulse` is a wrong name — IMPLICATION: import `applyPhysicsBodyImpulse` (havok.ts) for debris kicks; note it takes the body, not the world.","timings":{"cache_n":70912,"draft_n":4228,"draft_n_accepted":1215,"predicted_ms":50010.0,"predicted_n":1819,"prompt_ms":760.0,"prompt_n":165},"to_request":45977,"usage":{"cached_tokens":70912,"completion_tokens":1819,"prompt_tokens":71077}}
