{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"User's question: In the step just completed (S1 verification + S2 fps-terrain.ts creation), was there anything that worked differently than expected? Let me look back on the discoveries from this step:\n\n1. `resizeMeshGeometry` — expected to use raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + manual `_gpu` swap, but discovered that `resizeMeshGeometry` is the intended in-place seam (bumps `_renderableVersion` so cached bundles get re-recorded). This is more than just \"works differently\" — it's a correction to the plan. The plan said \"index surgery + re-upload via uploadMeshToGPU.\"\n\n2. Controller friction: The plan said \"the controller shape getter is unverified\" and \"if exposed, controller shape friction is the preferred target, otherwise terrain friction.\" In reality, the controller exposes `staticFriction`/`dynamicFriction` as public fields — meaning we can control slide via the controller.\n\n3. FreeCamera: Discovered that the world matrix is derived from `position` + `target` (mat4LookAtLH), and `_yaw`/`_pitch` are only used by attachFreeControl. Expected to control `_yaw`/`_pitch` directly, but instead should set position+target every frame.\n\n4. Nav agents: No reposition API — NavCrowd agents drift from the controller; need mitigation via re-targeting. This is a limitation.\n\n5. Static bodies get their transform from the node at creation time (not synced) — this is expected for STATIC, but worth noting: node changes are not reflected.\n\n6. `PhysicsWorld._timestep` is @internal — use the dt parameter of onPhysicsAfterStep.\n\n7. TextRenderer HUD: registerTextRenderer registers a rendering context on the surface; order = registration order; scene first, text after → text on top; `clear: false` is required. This was a design question that was resolved, not necessarily a \"different from expected\" item.\n\n8. `applyPhysicsImpulse` (the old name in the notes) is actually `applyPhysicsBodyImpulse` — a naming correction.\n\n9. Mesh vertex layout: row 0 is at z=-height/2 — affects tile index calculations; not unexpected, but a detail.\n\n10. In my fps-terrain.ts, I wrote a placeholder bug in tileFromPoint and fixed it — this is my own mistake, not an API discovery. Should I mention it? The question is \"was there anything that worked differently than expected — an API that works differently, an error and its actual cause…\" The placeholder was my own mistake that I fixed within the same step. It's not an API discovery. I don't think it's needed, but being honest might be good. The instructions say \"list only discoveries from this step.\" My own typo isn't a discovery about the codebase. I'll omit it… Actually, hmm — \"an error and its actual cause\" — the placeholder was an error I introduced and fixed myself. Mentioning it wouldn't be useful. I'll omit it.\n\nLet me focus on genuine API discoveries from this step:\n\n- GOTCHA: The plan's re-upload path (raw uploadMeshToGPU + manual _gpu swap) is superseded by resizeMeshGeometry (mesh-factories.ts) — it's the intended in-place seam that bumps _renderableVersion so cached draw bundles get re-recorded, and also retains the CPU copy. IMPLICATION: Use resizeMeshGeometry for tile removal (already reflected in fps-terrain.ts).\n\n- GOTCHA: PhysicsCharacterController exposes friction as public fields (staticFriction default 0, dynamicFriction default 1) — not via shape access. IMPLICATION: Quake-style slide is controlled via cc.staticFriction/cc.dynamicFriction; the \"controller shape getter unverified\" risk is resolved.\n\n- GOTCHA: FreeCamera's world matrix is built from position+target (mat4LookAtLH); _yaw/_pitch are internal state only for attachFreeControl. IMPLICATION: FPS camera is driven by setting cam.position and cam.target every frame from the player's eye position + (yaw, pitch); don't write to _yaw/_pitch.\n\n- GOTCHA: The navigation API has no agent reposition/teleport — only agentGoto(dest). IMPLICATION: NavCrowd agents will drift from the character controller when collisions occur; mitigate by re-targeting (agentGoto) periodically or on arrival; fall back to computePath waypoint following if drift is too large.\n\n- GOTCHA: PhysicsWorld._timestep is @internal. IMPLICATION: Get dt from the onPhysicsAfterStep callback's parameter.\n\n- GOTCHA: Static physics bodies take their transform from the node only at creation time (no sync). IMPLICATION: Tile box positions are baked in; TransformNodes can be placed beforehand — no issue for us, but we must not expect later node moves to move the box.\n\n- GOTCHA: The old note's name `applyPhysicsImpulse` is actually `applyPhysicsBodyImpulse` (havok.ts:~513). IMPLICATION: Use applyPhysicsBodyImpulse for debris knockback.\n\n- GOTCHA: TextRenderer is a separate rendering context on the surface; render order = registration order. IMPLICATION: Register the scene first, then the text renderer with clear:false so that the HUD is drawn on top of the 3D frame.\n\nAll of these are from this step (S1 verification). Let me summarize concisely, one per line.\n","seq":48515,"t":2141935,"text":"\n\nGOTCHA: `resizeMeshGeometry` (mesh-factories.ts) is the intended in-place geometry swap — it bumps every registered scene's `_renderableVersion` so cached draw bundles re-record, and refreshes `_cpuPositions/_cpuNormals/_cpuIndices` — IMPLICATION: tile removal uses `resizeMeshGeometry`, not a raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + manual `_gpu` swap as the plan's wording suggested (already written that way in fps-terrain.ts).\nGOTCHA: `PhysicsCharacterController` exposes friction as public fields (`staticFriction` default 0, `dynamicFriction` default 1) — there is no shape accessor needed — IMPLICATION: Quake slide is tuned via `cc.staticFriction`/`cc.dynamicFriction`; the plan's \"controller shape getter unverified\" risk is resolved in favor of the controller fields.\nGOTCHA: `FreeCamera`'s world matrix is built from `position` + `target` (`mat4LookAtLH`); `_yaw`/`_pitch` are internal state only `attachFreeControl` uses — IMPLICATION: the FPS camera is driven by setting `cam.position` and `cam.target` each frame from the player's eye + (yaw, pitch); do not write `_yaw`/`_pitch`.\nGOTCHA: the navigation API has no agent reposition/teleport — only `agentGoto(dest)` — IMPLICATION: NavCrowd agents will drift from character controllers when collisions divert them; mitigate by re-targeting on arrival/periodically, and fall back to `computePath` waypoint-following if drift degrades.\nGOTCHA: `PhysicsWorld._timestep` is `@internal` — IMPLICATION: read dt from the `onPhysicsAfterStep(world, (timestep) => ...)` callback parameter, not from the world.\nGOTCHA: static physics bodies take their transform from the node only at creation (no ongoing sync, unlike ANIMATED) — IMPLICATION: tile box positions are baked at creation; TransformNodes must be placed correctly up front and later node moves won't move the box.\nGOTCHA: the debris impulse function is `applyPhysicsBodyImpulse` (havok.ts), not `applyPhysicsImpulse` as the older note said — IMPLICATION: use `applyPhysicsBodyImpulse` for debris knockback.\nGOTCHA: `registerTextRenderer` registers a separate rendering context on the surface and render order is registration order — IMPLICATION: register the 3D scene first, then the HUD `TextRenderer` with `clear: false`, so text draws on top of the frame instead of wiping it.","timings":{"cache_n":76544,"draft_n":3675,"draft_n_accepted":1200,"predicted_ms":47260.0,"predicted_n":1725,"prompt_ms":2700.0,"prompt_n":862},"to_request":47520,"usage":{"cached_tokens":76544,"completion_tokens":1725,"prompt_tokens":77406}}
