{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"The user is asking me to reflect on the immediately preceding step (my last message and tool activity) and enumerate the decisions made.\n\nWhat happened in the immediately preceding step:\n1. Confirmed that `createPhysicsBody` reads `node.position`/`node.rotationQuaternion` at creation time → confirmed that the per-tile TransformNode approach works for static bodies.\n2. Confirmed that `setPhysicsBodyLinearVelocity` is at :1056 (and that `applyPhysicsBodyImpulse` is the actual name).\n3. Checked the parameter shape of the BOX shape: `parameters: { extents, center? }`.\n4. Confirmed that all the required symbols are exported from the `babylon-lite` barrel.\n5. Wrote `fps-terrain.ts` — this is where the actual build decisions were made:\n   - Arena 128×128u, tiles 4×4u, 32×32 tiles, 33×33 vertex grid (subdivisions = TILE_COUNT = 32)\n   - Noise: seeded mulberry32 PRNG, coarse 8×8 value noise grid, bilinear interpolation with smoothstep, amplitude 5u\n   - Per-tile static box: top face at the tile's maximum corner height, minimum half-height 0.5 to avoid degenerate boxes, center at yTop - halfH\n   - Friction 0.1, restitution 0 on tile shapes\n   - TERRAIN_LAYER = 1 membership mask on tile shapes, collide mask left at default\n   - destroyTerrainTile: index surgery on `_cpuIndices`, computeNormals, resizeMeshGeometry (not raw uploadMeshToGPU), removePhysicsBody, addBoxObstacle\n   - `tileFromPoint(terrain, x, z)` for bullet→tile mapping (originally wrote it as a placeholder, then fixed it in the second tool call)\n   - Module structure: fps-terrain.ts is exported as `createFpsTerrain(engine, world, seed)`, `tileFromPoint`, `destroyTerrainTile`, `terrainHeightAt`, constants.\n\nAlso, I made a decision to use `resizeMeshGeometry` as the re-upload seam (rather than raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + `_gpu` swap) — this was decided in this step (well, it was confirmed in an earlier tool call in this same step's batch, but the decision to use it was baked into the file I wrote in this step).\n\nThe user is asking only about decisions from this step. Let me enumerate:\n\n1. DECISION: Use `resizeMeshGeometry` (not raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + manual `_gpu` swap) as the re-upload seam for tile removal — because it bumps the renderable version so cached draw bundles get re-recorded, and it maintains the CPU geometry copy.\n2. DECISION: Mesh density = 33×33 vertices (subdivisions = 32), one quad per tile — because tile removal (rather than vertex-level digging) means the grid only needs to align with the tile grid.\n3. DECISION: Per-tile static box with top face at the tile's maximum corner height, minimum half-height 0.5 — because flat tiles produce degenerate boxes, and the max-height top face prevents the character from falling through.\n4. DECISION: Tile shape friction 0.1 / restitution 0 — because we need Quake-style ground slide and no bounce.\n5. DECISION: TERRAIN_LAYER = 1 membership mask on tile shapes, collide mask left at default — because bullet raycasts filter to terrain-only via the query's membership, while the controller still collides.\n6. DECISION: Terrain noise = seeded mulberry32 + 8×8 coarse value noise grid, bilinear interpolation with smoothstep, amplitude 5u — because it's allocation-free, deterministic, and low-frequency, and keeps the tile boxes close to the mesh.\n7. DECISION: destroyTerrainTile reads `_cpuIndices`/`_cpuPositions`/`_cpuUvs` from the mesh (updated by resizeMeshGeometry) — because the CPU copy is the single source of truth after each re-upload.\n8. DECISION: `tileFromPoint(terrain, x, z)` maps raycast hit points to tiles — because a body→tile map is unnecessary; the tile containing the hit point is the tile to destroy.\n9. DECISION: Tile transform nodes are created but not added to the scene — because static bodies capture the node's transform at creation time (confirmed in createPhysicsBody), so invisible nodes suffice.\n\nThat's it. Keep it concise, one per line.\n","seq":49365,"t":2177115,"text":"\n\nDECISION: Tile removal re-uploads via `resizeMeshGeometry` (not raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + manual `_gpu` swap) — WHY: it bumps every registered scene's `_renderableVersion` so cached draw bundles re-record, and maintains the `_cpu*` copies.\nDECISION: Grid density is 33×33 vertices (subdivisions = 32, one quad per tile) — WHY: destruction is tile removal, so the mesh only needs to align with the tile grid, not the 256×256 vertex-level density of the earlier in-place-deformation idea.\nDECISION: Per-tile static box has its top at the tile's max corner height with a minimum half-height of 0.5 — WHY: flat tiles would produce degenerate zero-height boxes, and a max-height top guarantees characters never fall through the box edge.\nDECISION: Tile shape material is friction 0.1 / restitution 0 — WHY: Quake-style ground slide wants low friction and no bounce on the surfaces both player and bots stand on.\nDECISION: Tile shapes get membership mask `TERRAIN_LAYER = 1` with the collide mask left at default — WHY: bullet raycasts can filter to terrain-only via the query's membership, while character controllers still collide with the tiles.\nDECISION: Terrain heights come from a seeded mulberry32 PRNG driving an 8×8 coarse value-noise grid with smoothstep bilinear interpolation, amplitude 5u — WHY: deterministic, allocation-free, low-frequency enough that flat-topped tile boxes stay close to the mesh surface.\nDECISION: `destroyTerrainTile` reads `_cpuIndices`/`_cpuPositions`/`_cpuUvs` off the mesh each call rather than caching private copies — WHY: `resizeMeshGeometry` refreshes those fields, so the mesh is the single source of truth after every re-upload.\nDECISION: Bullet→tile mapping uses `tileFromPoint(terrain, x, z)` on the raycast hit point — WHY: no body→tile map is needed; the tile containing the hit point is the tile to destroy.\nDECISION: Per-tile TransformNodes are created but never added to the scene — WHY: `createPhysicsBody` captures the node's transform at creation (verified in havok.ts:448), so invisible nodes are enough for static colliders.","timings":{"cache_n":77312,"draft_n":2898,"draft_n_accepted":1084,"predicted_ms":34100.0,"predicted_n":1498,"prompt_ms":380.0,"prompt_n":110},"to_request":48526,"usage":{"cached_tokens":77312,"completion_tokens":1498,"prompt_tokens":77422}}
