{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Let me think about what was discovered or committed to in the step just completed (the S1 verification batch + writing fps-terrain.ts).\n\nConstraints that surfaced in this step:\n\n1. From GUIDANCE.md (re-read this step): zero module-level side effects — no module-level `new Map()/Set()/WeakMap()`, lazy initialization required. This was already recorded (interview-t2-4), but was re-confirmed this step. Is this \"surfaced in this step\"? It was on the list. The instruction says \"only constraints surfaced in this step.\" Re-reading GUIDANCE is part of this step... but this constraint was already known (interview-t2-4). Probably shouldn't be re-listed as new.\n\n2. From resizeMeshGeometry (mesh-factories.ts): tile deletion must use `resizeMeshGeometry` — no wait, that's more of a decision/pointer than a constraint. Actually there's a real constraint here: the old GPU buffers must not be destroyed synchronously (that would cause a \"Buffer used in submit while destroyed\" error) — resizeMeshGeometry handles that internally. This is an implementation detail of the engine function, not a constraint on my code.\n\n3. From FreeCamera: the world matrix is built from position+target via mat4LookAtLH, not from _yaw/_pitch — _yaw/_pitch are only used by attachFreeControl. FPS camera control must set cam.position and cam.target every frame (commitment). This is more of a technical fact/pointer than a \"never do\" constraint.\n\n4. From PhysicsWorld: `_timestep` is @internal — must use the dt parameter of onPhysicsAfterStep instead. This is a constraint: never read world._timestep from scene code (use the callback's dt). Hmm, this is a constraint on the scene code I'm about to write.\n\n5. From physics: static bodies get their transform from the node at creation time — per-tile TransformNodes must be placed at the box center before createPhysicsBody. Constraint/commitment.\n\n6. From GUIDANCE §0: never revert unknown changes, clean up debug files before commit, agents must not run pnpm test:perf, only run pnpm build:bundle-scenes / pnpm test:parity, run pnpm run lint:fix after code changes. These are workflow constraints re-read this step (GUIDANCE re-read was part of this step). Already known from the interview? Some are new to me: \"agents must not run pnpm test:perf\" — was that recorded? Not in the working set I can see. \"Before commit, delete all temporary/debug files\" — not explicitly recorded. \"After every code change, run pnpm run lint:fix, then verify with pnpm run lint\" — this is a workflow constraint that I must follow for the code I'm about to write.\n\nHmm, the question is: \"Did you learn or commit to constraints that the rest of the project must honor...? List each on its own line as CONSTRAINT: <rule>. Only constraints surfaced in this step.\"\n\nI think the intent is: what did I learn in this step (S1 verification + fps-terrain.ts) that the rest of the project must honor. Let me enumerate the truly constraint-like things:\n\n1. **Module-level side effects are forbidden** (GUIDANCE re-read this step): no module-level `new Map/Set/WeakMap`, lazy initialization pattern required — this applies to all new files (fps-input.ts, fps-audio.ts, scene252.ts). Already recorded in interview-t2-4, but was reaffirmed this step. Should I list it? \"Only constraints surfaced in this step\" — it was surfaced (re-read) in this step. I'm leaning toward listing it since it directly constrains the remaining files I'll write in this session. Actually, this is already in the working set as interview-t2-4. Re-listing would be redundant. But the prompt says \"learned or committed to\" — I committed to following it this step. Hmm. I'll include the ones that are most relevant and that constrain the rest of the build:\n\n- No module-level side effects (lazy cache pattern) — for fps-input.ts/fps-audio.ts/scene252.ts.\n- All code must pass ESLint + Prettier (4 spaces, 180 width, es5 trailing commas), run `pnpm run lint:fix` after every code change — workflow constraint surfaced by re-reading GUIDANCE.\n- Never read `world._timestep` (@internal) from scene code — use the dt parameter of onPhysicsAfterStep.\n- FPS camera must be driven by setting `cam.position` + `cam.target` every frame (FreeCamera's matrix = lookAt(position, target), not _yaw/_pitch).\n- Static physics bodies take their transform from the node at creation time — TransformNodes must be placed before createPhysicsBody; do not move tile nodes later.\n- Tile deletion must go through `resizeMeshGeometry` (in-place re-upload that invalidates cached bundles) — do not swap `mesh._gpu` manually, do not destroy old buffers synchronously.\n- Agents must not run `pnpm test:perf`; for scene changes, parity/bundle suites are not needed unless the engine is modified (lab demo, no engine changes) — workflow constraint.\n- Never raise bundle-size caps / raise maxMad without user approval — already known (interview-t2-10).\n\nI should be careful not to over-list things that were already in the working set from prior steps (interview-t2-10 bundle caps, interview-t2-4 module side effects, interview-t2-13 GUIDANCE immutability). The prompt says \"only constraints surfaced in this step.\" Strictly, what was surfaced in this step is:\n\nFrom GUIDANCE re-read (this step):\n- Workflow: agents must not run pnpm test:perf; parity only when engine is modified; run lint:fix after every change; clean up debug files before commit; never revert unknown changes.\n- No module-level side effects (reaffirmed).\n\nFrom API verification (this step):\n- `world._timestep` is @internal → use the dt parameter of onPhysicsAfterStep.\n- FreeCamera matrix = lookAt(position, target); _yaw/_pitch are internal and only used by attachFreeControl → FPS camera must set position+target every frame.\n- Static bodies take their transform from the node at creation time.\n- resizeMeshGeometry is the seam for in-place geometry replacement (don't touch _gpu manually; the engine defers buffer destruction).\n- The character controller's shape is private (`_shape`) → the controller's membership/collide masks cannot be set; friction is controlled via the controller's public staticFriction/dynamicFriction fields.\n- NavCrowd has no agent reposition API → bots must tolerate agent drift / re-target.\n- The bundle-size spec only covers scenes in scene-config.json with maxRawKB → scene252 needs no cap entry.\n\nI'll list the ones that truly constrain the rest of the project (S3–S8). Each on its own line as CONSTRAINT: <rule>.\n\nKeep it concise. I'll list:\n\nCONSTRAINT: All new scene files must have zero module-level side effects — no module-level `new Map()/Set()/WeakMap()`; caches must be lazily initialized (GUIDANCE §4, re-read this step).\nCONSTRAINT: All code must pass ESLint + Prettier (4-space indent, 180 print width, es5 trailing commas); run `pnpm run lint:fix` after every code change, then verify with `pnpm run lint`.\nCONSTRAINT: Do not read `PhysicsWorld._timestep` (@internal) from scene code — use the `timestep` parameter of the `onPhysicsAfterStep` callback.\nCONSTRAINT: The FPS camera must be driven by setting `cam.position` and `cam.target` every frame (FreeCamera's world matrix is lookAt(position, target); `_yaw`/`_pitch` are internal and only consumed by attachFreeControl).\nCONSTRAINT: Static per-tile physics bodies take their transform from the node at `createPhysicsBody` time — TransformNodes must be placed at the box center before creation, and must not be moved afterwards.\nCONSTRAINT: Tile deletion must re-upload geometry via `resizeMeshGeometry` (in-place, bumps the renderable version so cached bundles re-record) — do not manually assign `mesh._gpu`, do not destroy old GPU buffers synchronously.\nCONSTRAINT: The character controller's capsule shape is private — the controller's collision filter masks cannot be set; player/bot friction must use the controller's public `staticFriction`/`dynamicFriction` fields (and the tile shape's material).\nCONSTRAINT: NavCrowd has no agent reposition API — bot logic must tolerate the gap between agent and controller position (re-target with agentGoto); do not assume the agent mirrors the controller.\nCONSTRAINT: scene252 is not in scene-config.json, so it is out of scope for the bundle-size spec — no cap entry, no parity test, no golden needed; do not add one.\nCONSTRAINT: Agents must not run `pnpm test:perf`; the parity/bundle suite is only needed if `packages/babylon-lite/src/**` is modified (this project has no engine changes).\n\nThat's a solid list. Should I include \"never revert unknown changes\" and \"clean up debug files before commit\"? Those are general workflow constraints from the GUIDANCE re-read. I think it's reasonable to include the cleanup one since it affects how I finish the project. I'll include:\n\nCONSTRAINT: Before commit, delete all temporary/debug files and debug code created during the session; never revert changes I did not make in this session.\n\nOK. Let me write the response.\n","seq":50918,"t":2244020,"text":"\n\nCONSTRAINT: All new scene files must have zero module-level side effects — no module-level `new Map()/Set()/WeakMap()`; caches must be lazy-init (GUIDANCE §4, re-read this step; governs fps-input.ts, fps-audio.ts, scene252.ts).\nCONSTRAINT: All code must pass ESLint + Prettier (4-space indent, 180 print width, es5 trailing commas); run `pnpm run lint:fix` after every code change, then verify with `pnpm run lint`.\nCONSTRAINT: Never read `PhysicsWorld._timestep` (@internal) from scene code — use the `timestep` parameter of the `onPhysicsAfterStep` callback for dt.\nCONSTRAINT: The FPS camera must be driven by setting `cam.position` and `cam.target` each frame — FreeCamera's world matrix is `lookAt(position, target)`; `_yaw`/`_pitch` are internal and only consumed by `attachFreeControl`.\nCONSTRAINT: Static per-tile physics bodies take their transform from the node at `createPhysicsBody` time — tile TransformNodes must be positioned at the box center before creation and never moved afterward.\nCONSTRAINT: Tile destruction must re-upload geometry via `resizeMeshGeometry` (in-place realloc that bumps every scene's renderable version so cached bundles re-record) — do not hand-assign `mesh._gpu` and do not destroy old GPU buffers synchronously.\nCONSTRAINT: The character controller's capsule shape is private (`_shape`) — controller collision-filter masks cannot be set; player/bot slide friction must use the controller's public `staticFriction`/`dynamicFriction` fields plus the tile shape material.\nCONSTRAINT: NavCrowd has no agent-reposition API — bot logic must tolerate agent/controller position drift (re-target via `agentGoto`); never assume the nav agent mirrors the controller.\nCONSTRAINT: scene252 is a lab demo, not a parity scene — it stays out of scene-config.json, bundle-size.spec.ts, golden references, and the gallery's parity machinery; no ceiling entry to add or raise.\nCONSTRAINT: Agents must not run `pnpm test:perf`; parity/bundle suites are only required if `packages/babylon-lite/src/**` changes (this project makes zero engine changes).\nCONSTRAINT: Before committing, delete all temporary/debug files and debug code created this session, and never revert changes not made by me in this session.","timings":{"cache_n":77312,"draft_n":5488,"draft_n_accepted":1839,"predicted_ms":65810.0,"predicted_n":2623,"prompt_ms":370.0,"prompt_n":87},"to_request":49377,"usage":{"cached_tokens":77312,"completion_tokens":2623,"prompt_tokens":77399}}
