 to set the sky color in scene252.\n\nI'll quote verbatim, up to about 15 lines max. The relevant lines:\n\n```\n45:    clearColor: GPUColorDict;\n...\n150:        clearColor: { r: 0.2, g: 0.2, b: 0.3, a: 1.0 },\n```\n\nHowever, the EXCERPT should be a verbatim quote — I'll quote the interface line and the default-value line with context. I'll keep it to about 15 lines or fewer.\n\nVerbatim from the output:\n\n```\n~/git/reference/Babylon/Babylon-Lite/packages/babylon-lite/src/scene/scene-core.ts:45:    clearColor: GPUColorDict;\n~/git/reference/Babylon/Babylon-Lite/packages/babylon-lite/src/scene/scene-core.ts:150:        clearColor: { r: 0.2, g: 0.2, b: 0.3, a: 1.0 },\n```\n\nAnd from the second command's output (the SceneContext interface — wait, that was the second bash result, and the user said \"a large amount of material\" from one bash — actually the message says \"bash of grep -rn clearColor ... approximately 3480 characters\". The output of the second command included the SceneContext interface. Hmm, the user is asking about the entire ingestion. The 3480 characters probably includes both results. In any case, I'll quote the critical parts.\n\nThe critical part is: `clearColor: GPUColorDict;` on the public SceneContext interface (line 45), and the default `{ r: 0.2, g: 0.2, b: 0.3, a: 1.0 }` (line 150). Because in scene252.ts I need to set the sky color — this confirms that `scene.clearColor` is a settable public field, no additional API needed.\n\nAlso, `fog: FogConfig | null` — a FogConfig type exists — pointer for later (visuals).\n\n`imageProcessing: ImageProcessingConfig` — pointer (gamma/tone mapping, could matter for visuals).\n\n`environmentPrimaryColor?: [number, number, number]` — pointer (environment color without a cubemap).\n\nAlright, let me write the response.\n","seq":51749,"t":2285694,"text":"\n\nEXCERPT:\n```\n45:    clearColor: GPUColorDict;\n...\n150:        clearColor: { r: 0.2, g: 0.2, b: 0.3, a: 1.0 },\n```\nplus, from the `SceneContext` interface dump in the same output:\n```\n    /** Surface this scene renders into. Set at scene-creation time and immutable\n     *  afterwards — the default render task is sized and MSAA-matched to this surface,\n     *  and `registerScene` attaches the scene to it. For the engine's primary surface\n     *  (the common single-canvas case) this is the engine itself. The owning engine is\n     *  reachable via `scene.surface.engine`. */\n    readonly surface: SurfaceContext;\n    clearColor: GPUColorDict;\n    camera: Camera | null;\n```\nLoad-bearing: `clearColor` is a plain public mutable field on `SceneContext` (default `{r:0.2,g:0.2,b:0.3,a:1}`), so scene252 sets the sky with `scene.clearColor = {...}` — no extra API to hunt for.\n\nPOINTER: `fog: FogConfig | null` exists on `SceneContext` (scene-core.ts:57) — the engine has fog; a light distance fog could improve visibility on the 128×128u arena if the playtest looks flat.\nPOINTER: `imageProcessing: ImageProcessingConfig` on `SceneContext` (scene-core.ts:48) — tone-mapping/gamma knob; may matter if the standard material looks off under the hemispheric light.\nPOINTER: `environmentPrimaryColor?: [number, number, number]` + `envRotationY` (scene-core.ts:66-69) — background color from the environment path; alternate to `clearColor` if fog/depth-fade interactions look wrong.\nPOINTER: `createSceneContext(surface, options)` takes a `SurfaceContext` and `EngineContext extends SurfaceContext` (scene-core.ts:144) — confirms `createSceneContext(engine)` is the idiom the lab scenes use; matters if I ever need a second surface (I don't).","timings":{"cache_n":79616,"draft_n":3003,"draft_n_accepted":1141,"predicted_ms":40150.0,"predicted_n":1570,"prompt_ms":810.0,"prompt_n":236},"to_request":50932,"usage":{"cached_tokens":79616,"completion_tokens":1570,"prompt_tokens":79852}}
