{"kind":"delta","request":54758,"seq":55246,"t":2467224,"tool_call":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"// Web Audio SFX for the FPS demo. Lite has no audio by design, so sounds are\\n// synthesized on the DOM side with Web Audio. The AudioContext is created lazily\\n// on the first user gesture (browser autoplay policy) — no module-level side effects.\\n\\nexport interface FpsAudio {\\n    /** Call from a user gesture (e.g. pointer lock) to unlock audio. */\\n    unlock(): void;\\n    gunshot(): void;\\n    hit(): void;\\n    thud(): void;\\n    damage(): void;\\n}\\n\\nexport function createFpsAudio(): FpsAudio {\\n    let ctx: AudioContext | null = null;\\n\\n    const ensure = (): AudioContext | null => {\\n        if (!ctx) {\\n            try {\\n                ctx = new AudioContext();\\n            } catch {\\n                return null;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        if (ctx.state === \\\"suspended\\\") {\\n            void ctx.resume();\\n        }\\n        return ctx;\\n    };\\n\\n    const playNoise = (seconds: number, startFreq: number, endFreq: number, gain: number): void => {\\n        const c = ensure();\\n        if (!c) {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        const t = c.currentTime;\\n        const buf = c.createBuffer(1, Math.max(1, Math.floor(c.sampleRate * seconds)), c.sampleRate);\\n        const data = buf.getChannelData(0);\\n        for (let i = 0; i < data.length; i++) {\\n            data[i] = Math.random() * 2 - 1;\\n        }\\n        const src = c.createBufferSource();\\n        src.buffer = buf;\\n        const filter = c.createBiquadFilter();\\n        filter.type = \\\"lowpass\\\";\\n        filter.frequency.setValueAtTime(startFreq, t);\\n        filter.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(Math.max(40, endFreq), t + seconds);\\n        const g = c.createGain();\\n        g.gain.setValueAtTime(gain, t);\\n        g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.001, t + seconds);\\n        src.connect(filter);\\n        filter.connect(g);\\n        g.connect(c.destination);\\n        src.start(t);\\n        src.stop(t + seconds);\\n    };\\n\\n    const playTone = (freq: number, seconds: number, gain: number, type: OscillatorType = \\\"sine\\\"): void => {\\n        const c = ensure();\\n        if (!c) {\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        const t = c.currentTime;\\n        const osc = c.createOscillator();\\n        osc.type = type;\\n        osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(freq, t);\\n        const g = c.createGain();\\n        g.gain.setValueAtTime(gain, t);\\n        g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.001, t + seconds);\\n        osc.connect(g);\\n        g.connect(c.destination);\\n        osc.start(t);\\n        osc.stop(t + seconds);\\n    };\\n\\n    return {\\n        unlock(): void {\\n            ensure();\\n        },\\n        gunshot(): void {\\n            playNoise(0.15, 3000, 200, 0.4);\\n        },\\n        hit(): void {\\n            playTone(880, 0.08, 0.25);\\n        },\\n        thud(): void {\\n            playNoise(0.25, 500, 60, 0.5);\\n            playTone(90, 0.2, 0.3);\\n        },\\n        damage(): void {\\n            playTone(220, 0.15, 0.3, \\\"sawtooth\\\");\\n        },\\n    };\\n}\", \"path\": \"~/git/reference/Babylon/Babylon-Lite/lab/lite/src/lite/fps-audio.ts\"}","id":"call_7aeae3d31f6c4eb5ae5bb3da","index":1,"name":"write"}}
{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"All confirmed:\n- `mat4Compose(tx, ty, tz, qx, qy, qz, qw, sx, sy, sz)` returns a new Mat4 (no result parameter). Allocate a Mat4 per instance per frame — a small allocation, but it's fine for 36 instances. Or use `mat4ComposeInto`? Is that exported? Probably not. 36 × 64-byte allocations per frame is negligible.\n- `raycast(nav, start, end)`: hit=true means blocked (0 < t < 1). So LOS is clear when hit=false.\n- `TextRendererOptions.clear` — \"set to false for HUD overlays so the text pass preserves the existing scene color\" — exactly what I need.\n- `setPhysicsBodyMass` is exported (index:617).\n- `raycast` is exported (index:678).\n- `createBox(engine, size)`.\n\nNow I'll write the three remaining files. First fps-input.ts, then fps-audio.ts, then scene252.ts, and finally scene252.html.\n","seq":55247,"t":2467225,"text":"\n\nAll APIs confirmed. Writing `fps-input.ts` and `fps-audio.ts`:\n\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":92160,"draft_n":2961,"draft_n_accepted":1929,"predicted_ms":39010.0,"predicted_n":2352,"prompt_ms":3310.0,"prompt_n":1698},"to_request":54758,"usage":{"cached_tokens":92160,"completion_tokens":2352,"prompt_tokens":93858}}
