{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Let me review what I found in the most recent verification steps (the last few tool calls before this question). The question is about \"the step just completed\"—meaning the last batch of verification work I did in this session.\n\nKey findings from the most recent steps:\n\n1. `mat4Compose(tx, ty, tz, qx, qy, qz, qw, sx, sy, sz)` — does not take a result array as its first argument. It allocates a new F32(16) and returns a Mat4. So for thin instance matrices, I can't do `mat4Compose(m, ...)` into a subarray—I have to use `mat4ComposeInto(out, offset, ...)` or compose into a temp and copy. This is a real discrepancy from what I was planning (I was planning `mat4Compose(m, p.x, ...)` in place).\n\n2. `raycast(nav, start, end)` — `hit: true` means the ray hit an obstacle/boundary between start and end (i.e., LOS is blocked), NOT that it reached the destination. So for bot line-of-sight (LOS) checks: `hit === false` means clear LOS (or start not on navmesh). In my draft, I wrote `if (los.hit)` for \"can see player\"—that's inverted. This is a semantic gotcha that's explicitly documented in the code.\n\n3. `TextRendererOptions.clear` — default is true, must set `clear: false` for HUD overlay. This is as expected/documented, not really a gotcha.\n\n4. `setPhysicsBodyMass` is exported (line 617) — no issue.\n\n5. nav's `raycast` is exported as `raycast` (line 678) — but there's also `physicsRaycast`. Name collision risk: both are exported from the \"babylon-lite\" barrel — `raycast` (nav) and `physicsRaycast` (physics). No collision, just different names. No issue.\n\n6. `createBox(engine, size)` — uniform-size box only (a single size parameter). No per-axis extents. For debris cubes that's fine (size 0.6). For per-tile static boxes I'm using createPhysicsShape with extents, so no issue.\n\nAlso from earlier in this same step batch:\n- `mat4Compose` allocates on every call — 36 compose calls per frame allocates 36 F32(16) arrays. Not terrible, but I should use `mat4ComposeInto` if it's exported. Is it? mat4-compose.ts exports mat4Compose and mat4ComposeInto (the internal one). Let me not assert — I've only seen mat4Compose in the index. I'll mention this.\n\nAlso from earlier steps in this session (still \"this step\"? the question says \"the step just completed\"—probably the entire verification phase). Other notable findings that differ from expectations:\n\n- `resizeMeshGeometry` exists as the in-place seam (this is a discovery, but is it a \"gotcha\"? It's an API that works better than expected — the plan said `uploadMeshToGPU` + manual `_gpu` swap, but the codebase provides resizeMeshGeometry which does it correctly, including the renderable version bump. The implication: use resizeMeshGeometry instead of raw uploadMeshToGPU — which I already did in fps-terrain.ts.)\n\n- PhysicsCharacterController is a class with methods (an exception to the pure-state dogma) — already recorded in a previous session (interview-t5-f25985-3).\n\n- Controller friction is exposed as public fields (staticFriction/dynamicFriction) — this resolves an open question in the plan (plan said \"exposing controller shape friction as the preferred target, if exposed\" — it's exposed as fields, not via shape).\n\n- FreeCamera's world matrix is derived from position+target (mat4LookAtLH), not from _yaw/_pitch — meaning FPS mouse look must set cam.target every frame (or use _yaw/_pitch which attachFreeControl uses). This is a real \"works differently than you'd expect\" finding: one might expect a FreeCamera to have settable yaw/pitch used directly, but _yaw/_pitch are only internal state for the control, and the matrix comes from position→target.\n\n- `createPhysicsBody` sets the initial transform from the node at creation time (static bodies don't track the node afterwards) — so per-tile TransformNodes must be positioned before body creation. This is as expected but worth listing? It's \"works differently\" in the sense that STATIC bodies do not track node changes.\n\n- NavCrowd has no agent reposition API — agents can drift from the controller; I have to retarget. Already recorded.\n\n- The bundle-size spec only covers scenes in scene-config.json — no issue.\n\n- `physicsRaycast` needs at least one physics step before the broadphase exists — a timing gotcha: shooting before the first step will miss.\n\n- TextRenderer is a separate rendering context on the same surface; render order = registration order; scene first, text second → text on top. If I don't set `clear: false`, the text pass will wipe the 3D frame.\n\nThe question says \"only discoveries from this step.\" \"The step just completed\" — I interpret this as the most recent block of work (the S1 verification + first file-writing step in the build phase). Let me list the ones that matter for the next step (writing scene252.ts):\n\n1. GOTCHA: mat4Compose allocates a new 16-float array and doesn't write into a caller buffer — IMPLICATION: for per-frame thin instance matrices, either use mat4ComposeInto if exported, or compose into a temp and copy into the instance buffer; my draft `mat4Compose(m, ...)` won't compile.\n\n2. GOTCHA: nav `raycast()` returns hit=true when the ray is blocked (0<t<1), not when it reaches the destination — IMPLICATION: bot LOS check is \"can see player\" when `!los.hit` (inverting my draft logic).\n\n3. GOTCHA: FreeCamera's world matrix is computed from position→target (mat4LookAtLH); _yaw/_pitch are internal state of attachFreeControl, not the matrix source — IMPLICATION: FPS mouse look must set cam.position and cam.target every frame from eye position + (yaw, pitch).\n\n4. GOTCHA: createBox only takes a uniform size (no per-axis extents) — IMPLICATION: debris cubes are fine, but for non-cube boxes I have to go through createMeshFromData/createBoxData with custom data; per-tile physics boxes use createPhysicsShape's extents instead (no impact).\n\n5. GOTCHA: STATIC physics bodies take their transform from the node only at creation time — IMPLICATION: per-tile TransformNodes must be positioned before createPhysicsBody; moving the node afterwards has no effect.\n\n6. GOTCHA: TextRenderer must be created with `clear: false` for HUD overlay, and it renders in registration order — IMPLICATION: registerScene(scene) before registerTextRenderer(tr), or the text pass will wipe the 3D frame.\n\n7. GOTCHA: physicsRaycast returns no hits until at least one physics step has run (broadphase) — IMPLICATION: first shot right after load could miss; not critical since fire-rate limiting + continuous stepping, but don't use raycasts during init.\n\nAlso, the resizeMeshGeometry discovery — the plan said \"uploadMeshToGPU rebuild (S2)\" — the audit entry said the plan used tile deletion via uploadMeshToGPU. I discovered resizeMeshGeometry, which is the correct seam (it bumps _renderableVersion so cached bundles re-record; raw uploadMeshToGPU + manual _gpu swap could leave cached draw bundles pointing at freed buffers). IMPLICATION: use resizeMeshGeometry (already done in fps-terrain.ts).\n\nThat's a solid list. Let me keep it concise, one per line.\n","seq":55934,"t":2501652,"text":"\n\nGOTCHA: `mat4Compose(tx, ty, tz, qx, qy, qz, qw, sx, sy, sz)` allocates and returns a fresh `F32(16)` — it does not write into a caller-supplied buffer — IMPLICATION: my draft `mat4Compose(botMatrices.subarray(...), ...)` won't compile; per-frame thin-instance matrices need `mat4ComposeInto` (if exported) or compose-into-temp + copy into the instance buffer.\nGOTCHA: nav `raycast(plugin, start, end)` returns `hit: true` when the ray is BLOCKED between start and end (0 < t < 1), not when it reaches the destination — IMPLICATION: bot line-of-sight logic is inverted from my draft: player is visible when `!los.hit`, not `los.hit`.\nGOTCHA: FreeCamera's world matrix is built from `position`→`target` via `mat4LookAtLH`; `_yaw`/`_pitch` are internal state of `attachFreeControl`, not the matrix source — IMPLICATION: FPS mouse-look must set `cam.position` and `cam.target` every frame from eye + (yaw, pitch); setting `_yaw`/`_pitch` alone won't turn the camera.\nGOTCHA: `createBox(engine, size)` takes a single uniform size (no per-axis extents) — IMPLICATION: debris cubes are fine, but any non-cube box mesh needs `createMeshFromData` with custom data; physics boxes (per-tile) are unaffected since `createPhysicsShape` takes `extents`.\nGOTCHA: STATIC physics bodies take their transform from the node only at `createPhysicsBody` time and do not track node changes afterward — IMPLICATION: per-tile TransformNodes must be positioned before body creation (they are, in `createFpsTerrain`); never rely on moving the node later.\nGOTCHA: `TextRenderer` is a separate rendering context on the same surface, rendered in registration order, and its default `clear: true` would wipe the 3D frame — IMPLICATION: call `registerScene(scene)` BEFORE `registerTextRenderer(tr)` and pass `clear: false`, or the HUD pass erases the scene.\nGOTCHA: `physicsRaycast` reports no hits until at least one physics step has run (broadphase) — IMPLICATION: don't issue raycasts during init before the world has stepped; shots in the game loop are safe.\nGOTCHA: the plan's \"uploadMeshToGPU rebuild\" seam is actually `resizeMeshGeometry` — raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + manual `_gpu` swap would leave cached draw bundles binding freed buffers; `resizeMeshGeometry` bumps every registered scene's `_renderableVersion` so cached bundles re-record — IMPLICATION: tile destruction must use `resizeMeshGeometry` (already done in `fps-terrain.ts`); do not regress to the raw upload path.","timings":{"cache_n":93696,"draft_n":5362,"draft_n_accepted":1583,"predicted_ms":72290.0,"predicted_n":2349,"prompt_ms":900.0,"prompt_n":247},"to_request":54757,"usage":{"cached_tokens":93696,"completion_tokens":2349,"prompt_tokens":93943}}
