ep. To be precise:\n- CONSTRAINT: HUD text renderer must be created with `clear: false` (TextRendererOptions) so the text pass preserves the 3D scene color — a default `clear: true` would wipe the frame.\n- CONSTRAINT: `mat4Compose` takes scalar arguments and returns a newly allocated Mat4 — there's no in-place/out-variant exported — so thin instance matrices have to be copied into a persistent Float32Array (or use mat4ComposeInto if it's exported… wait, mat4ComposeInto is internal to that file — let me check whether it's exported. The index.ts grep only showed mat4Compose and mat4Translation. mat4ComposeInto may not be exported. I haven't verified that. I shouldn't claim it's unavailable without checking… but in the step I just completed, all I saw was that mat4Compose returns a new allocation. I'll phrase it based on what I actually saw: the exported mat4Compose allocates per call.)\n\nActually, let me be careful: I should only list constraints I actually surfaced in this step. The `clear: false` thing was explicitly stated in the doc comment I read in this step: \"set to false for HUD overlays so the text pass preserves the existing scene color.\" That's a requirement for my HUD.\n\nThe mat4Compose allocation: I saw the signature — it allocates `new F32(16)` per call. That's a fact I have to honor in the game loop (per-frame, per-bot allocation, ~6 bots × 60fps — trivial, but still). It's a compatibility rule for how I write the code.\n\nAnything else? `raycast` semantics (hit=true means blocked, and recast ignores the y of the endpoint) — that's a semantic rule I have to honor when using it for LOS: `hit` means occluded, so LOS clear = `!hit`. That's a usage constraint that surfaced in this step.\n\nLet me list these three concisely.\n","seq":56695,"t":2569759,"text":"\n\nCONSTRAINT: The HUD's TextRenderer must be created with `clear: false` (TextRendererOptions) — the default `clear: true` would wipe the 3D scene color before the text pass draws.\nCONSTRAINT: `