ate a node. In the fix: `createTransformNode(\"fpsDebris\", x, y, z)`.\n\n19. **Player's initial invulnerability**: invulnerableUntil = 3 — but gameTime starts at 0 and damagePlayer checks `gameTime < invulnerableUntil` → the first 3 seconds are invulnerable ✓ good.\n\n20. **Bot's first re-target**: nextRetarget = 0 → immediate re-target on the first step ✓.\n\n21. **`player.checkSupport` returns info that should be disposed of?** — it allocates; no problem.\n\n22. **Thin instance matrices for hidden instances**: `m.fill(0); m[15] = 1` — scale 0 via a zero matrix… a zero matrix is a singular matrix — could that cause GPU culling issues? The standard way to hide is scale 0: a diagonal matrix with 0s on the diagonal and 1 in [15]. A completely zero matrix (with m[15]=1) is a degenerate transform — the instance is rendered at the origin with scale 0 → no visible pixels, but the matrix is singular — the GPU handles it fine (the vertex collapses to a point). OK, but cleaner would be: a scale-0 diagonal matrix. Either works; keeping fill(0)+m[15]=1.\n\n23. **Bot display orientation**: `mat4Compose(p.x, p.y, p.z, 0, sin(h/2), cos(h/2), 0, 1,1,1)` — a quaternion for a Y-axis rotation of angle h: q = (0, sin(h/2), 0, cos(h/2)) ✓ (x=0, y=sin, z=0, w=cos). I passed (0, sin, cos, 0) — wait, the order of mat4Compose is (tx,ty,tz, qx,qy,qz,qw, sx,sy,sz). I wrote `mat4Compose(p.x, p.y, p.z, 0, Math.sin(bot.heading / 2), Math.cos(bot.heading / 2), 0, 1, 1, 1)` → qx=0, qy=sin(h/2), qz=cos(h/2), qw=0. That's wrong — qz should be 0 and qw should be cos(h/2). Bug: I put cos in the qz slot and 0 in the qw slot.\n\n24. **Bot's y-velocity gravity and nav velocity**: bot.velY accumulates; the nav's av.y is probably 0; the bot falls under gravity ✓. But when the bot walks up a slope, the controller's collision pushes it up — no problem.\n\n25. **`updateNavCrowd` dt**: physics dt ✓.\n\n26. **Physics raycast \"run at least one physics step first so the broadphase exists\"** — the first shot can only happen after the player locks the pointer and clicks; by then many steps have run ✓.\n\n27. **Havok + recast wasm are both loaded from the lab root** ✓ confirmed in lab/public/.\n\n28. **`scene.fixedDeltaMs`** — the physics step uses this ✓ (scene40 pattern).\n\n29. **Playwright smoke test** — later (S8); canvas.dataset.ready ✓.\n\n30. **`createFlatGroundData` UV winding and tile index mapping** — verified ✓.\n\n31. **Terrain normals after destruction** — computeNormals(positions, next) ✓.\n\n32. **`resizeMeshGeometry` with uvs** — I pass `m._cpuUvs` ✓ (mesh-factories stores _cpuUvs on resize; createMeshFromData also stores it — I confirmed \"mirror createMeshFromData\" in the resize comment ✓).\n\n33. **Bundle: dynamic import of `@babylonjs/havok`** — static import in scene252 (like scene40) ✓.\n\n34. **Lint: `no-console`** — I use console.error in the catch — allowed ✓.\n\n35. **Prettier formatting** — not yet run; will be fixed by `pnpm run lint:fix`.\n\n36. **`input.onFire(tryFire)`** — tryFire uses `gameTime` (physics time) for rate limiting — the fire event is DOM-driven; no problem.\n\n37. **`document.pointerLockElement`** — standard ✓.\n\n38. **Audio context resume is async** — voided ✓.\n\n39. **`canvas.requestPointerLock().catch`** — TS: requestPointerLock returns Promise<void> in the modern lib.dom ✓.\n\n40. **`findRandomPointAroundCircle(nav, bp, 20)`** — bp is a Vec3 (the controller's center, ~0.9 above the surface) — the navmesh snaps to the nearest poly ✓.\n\n41. **Player spawns at (0, -40), arena is 128×128 → z ranges from -64..64 ✓ inside.\n\n42. **Bot spawns (±30, ±30) + radius 8 → inside ✓.\n\n43. **`raycast` (nav) start point must be findable**: bot surface position — if the bot stands where a tile was destroyed (fell in and respawned), no problem.\n\n44. **`physicsRaycast` from eye — if the player is inside a hole (falling), the ray hits the box's side… the box has been removed ✓.\n\n45. **Debris and player capsule collision**: the character controller pushes dynamic bodies (characterStrength 1e38) — debris gets blown away ✓ (desirable).\n\n46. **`setThinInstances` every frame** — writes the buffer; no problem.\n\n47. **`mat4Compose` returns a new Mat4 (F32 16) every call** — 36 allocations per frame; acceptable but could be hoisted. Not a correctness issue.\n\n48. **HUD `maxWidth: 1200`** — the text \"HP 100 KILLS 12 TILES 350\" fits ✓.\n\n49. **`createTextLayer` data** — the same TextData (hudData) is shared between layers? No — hudData is only for hudLayer; crossData is for crossLayer ✓.\n\n50. **Text renderer + scene both on the same surface: MSAA?** — scene's swapchain overlay… `configureSwapchainOverlayScene` — if a second context (text) is registered after the scene, the text draws directly to the swapchain without MSAA. A slight visual difference, no problem.\n\n51. **`engine` passed to createTextRenderer** — engine is a SurfaceContext ✓ (createTextRenderer(surface: SurfaceContext, opts)).\n\n52. **`loadFont(\"/fonts/Inter.ttf\")`** — lab/public/fonts/Inter.ttf — does it exist? scene180 uses \"/fonts/Inter.ttf\" ✓ it exists.\n\nNow, the open items that could affect subsequent work:\n\n- scene252.ts has a broken `createTransformNodeLazy` stub (returns null) + a module-level `debrisNodePool` — must be fixed (spawnDebris will crash at runtime).\n- Bug in the u formula in rayVsCapsule (`hh * e` should be `e`).\n- Bot matrix quaternion bug (qz/qw swapped).\n- Need to verify the default shape membership mask (whether the controller capsule is hit by the TERRAIN_LAYER raycast query) — add a proximity guard either way.\n- scene252.html is not yet created.\n- Unused type imports (EngineContext, NavigationPlugin, PhysicsWorld, SceneContext) will fail lint.\n- The Debris interface's `body: PhysicsBody` vs. null — type fix.\n- Nav agent re-sync (agentGoto to the bot's position) could cause a chase loop — verify in a playtest.\n- Text renderer drawn on top of the scene — verify visually.\n- Lint/format not yet run.\n- Dev server not yet started; no runtime verification at all yet.\n- The cost of initializing 1024 static bodies is unknown (plan fallback: 8×8u tiles).\n- Navmesh generation cost/quality on a 128×128 mesh at cs=0.5 is unknown.\n- Whether `registerScene` must be called before `registerTextRenderer` — the ordering is correct, but the rendering order is not yet verified.\n- Whether `updateDefaultTextData` triggers a GPU re-layout every time the text changes (performance) — verify in a playtest.\n- The crosshair positionPx assumes a canvas of 1280×720 (fixed in the HTML) ✓.\n\nNext steps (in order):\n1. Fix scene252.ts: replace the broken `createTransformNodeLazy` stub with a direct `createTransformNode` call in spawnDebris (add the import), remove the module-level `debrisNodePool`, fix the Debris interface (body: PhysicsBody | null), fix the u formula in rayVsCapsule, fix the bot quaternion, remove unused type imports, add a self-hit guard to tryFire (ignore terrain hits within ~2u of the eye).\n2. Create scene252.html (copy the scene18.html pattern, title \"Scene 252 — Quake-style FPS\").\n3. Run `pnpm run lint:fix` + `pnpm run lint` to clean up formatting/type errors.\n4. Start the dev server `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm dev:lab` in the background.\n5. Playtest checklist via browser/Playwright: wait for canvas.dataset.ready, check for dataset.error, verify terrain rendering, movement, shooting, tiles, bots, HUD, audio.\n6. Adjust parameters (init time of 1024 bodies, navmesh, friction/slide, bot AI) based on results.\n7. Record decisions/findings; propose a phase transition when S8 is complete.\n\nWait — I should also verify: does the lab's auto-discovery include scene252.html in the gallery? getHtmlInputs() globs lab/lite/*.html — yes, per interview-t5-1/audit. But the gallery card title? The gallery is auto-generated from the HTML. No problem.\n\nAlso — an important open item: I haven't verified that `createTransformNode`'s exported name is exactly `createTransformNode` (confirmed ✓ index:236).\n\nAnother open item: the semantics of `physicsRaycast`'s `membership` — I'm assuming the query's membership is ANDed with the body's membership mask. The doc comment says \"`collideWith`/`membership` filter which bodies the ray can hit (by their shape filter masks)\" ✓ so membership filters by the body's membership mask ✓. The tile's membership = TERRAIN_LAYER = 1 ✓. The default membership of the controller/debris shapes is unknown — the default of HP_Shape_Create. If the default is 0, only the tile matches the query. Debris: I don't set a mask → default. If the default is 0 → the ray doesn't hit debris (no problem, the plan targets only terrain + bots). If the default is ~0 → the ray hits debris/capsules; the self-hit guard handles the player's capsule; hitting debris counts as a terrain hit (a ray hitting debris → hitPoint → tileFromPoint → destroys a tile behind the debris — a bit weird but acceptable).\n\nI should check the default filter info — it's a quick grep. It affects correctness, so I'll list it as an open item.\n\nLet me also re-verify that `setThinInstances` writes to the provided array every time (or caches by version?). Looking at the code: on first call it initializes thinInstances {matrices...}; on subsequent calls — I only saw the first branch. Probably it sets _dirtyMin/_dirtyMax and uploads. If it's comparing… I only saw the first 20 lines. Open item: verify that setThinInstances uploads the matrix changes every frame (or use setThinInstanceMatrix). Actually, there's `flushThinInstances` — maybe setThinInstances just marks dirty and flush uploads? Let me not overthink it; I'll verify with a quick grep in the next step.\n\nI'll structure the answer as requested: OPEN: lines and NEXT: lines.\n","seq":59824,"t":2807621,"text":"\n\nOPEN: scene252.ts currently has a broken placeholder — `createTransformNodeLazy()` returns `null as never` and `spawnDebris` calls it, so debris creation would crash at runtime; there's also a module-level `let debrisNodePool` that violates the zero-side-effects rule and needs removal.\nOPEN: `rayVsCapsule` has a math bug — the segment parameter should be `u = (e - b*c) / det` (a=1), but I wrote `(hh * e - b*c) / det`.\nOPEN: bot display matrix has the quaternion args wrong — I passed qz=cos(h/2), qw=0 instead of qz=0, qw=cos(h/2).\nOPEN: unused type imports in scene252.ts (`EngineContext`, `NavigationPlugin`, `PhysicsWorld`, `SceneContext`) will fail lint; `createTransformNode` import is missing; `Debris.body` is typed `PhysicsBody` but initialized null.\nOPEN: unverified — default shape filter membership mask: if Havok shapes default to `~0` instead of `0`, a `membership: TERRAIN_LAYER` raycast could hit the player's own capsule (controller shape is private, can't set its mask), causing shots to destroy tiles under the player; I plan a <2u self-hit guard regardless, but the default is unconfirmed.\nOPEN: unverified — does `setThinInstances` re-upload matrices on every call, or does it need `flushThinInstances`? (affects per-frame bot/debris rendering).\nOPEN: unverified at runtime — nav agent re-sync (`agentGoto` to bot position when >4u apart) may cause bot/agent chase loops or jitter; playtest will tell.\nOPEN: unverified at runtime — TextRenderer compositing over the 3D scene (registration order scene→text, `clear: false`) is reasoned but not yet seen on screen.\nOPEN: unverified — init cost of 1024 static tile bodies (plan fallback: 8×8u tiles → 256 bodies) and navmesh build cost/quality at cs=0.5 over the 128×128u mesh.\nOPEN: scene252.html does not exist yet; gallery auto-discovery (`getHtmlInputs()`) won't pick up the scene without it.\nOPEN: no lint/format pass has been run on the four new files; dev server not started; zero runtime verification so far.\n\nNEXT: fix scene252.ts — replace the stub with a real `createTransformNode` call in `spawnDebris` (add the import), delete `debrisNodePool`, fix `Debris.body` to `PhysicsBody | null`, fix the `rayVsCapsule` u-formula, fix the bot quaternion args, drop unused type imports, add the self-hit guard in `tryFire`.\nNEXT: create `lab/lite/scene252.html` mirroring scene18.html (canvas id `renderCanvas`, `/loader.js`, module script `/lite/src/lite/scene252.ts`).\nNEXT: check the two small API unknowns (default shape membership mask in `createPhysicsShape`/HP_Shape_Create; `setThinInstances` upload behavior) with a quick grep.\nNEXT: run `pnpm run lint:fix` then `pnpm run lint` to get the new files clean.\nNEXT: start the dev server in the background (`LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm dev:lab`) and playtest scene252.html against the checklist: ready/error dataset, terrain visible, move/slide/jump, mouse look, shoot holes (tiles removed, physics body gone, nav obstacle), fall-through respawn, debris, bots patrol/shoot, HUD updates, audio.\nNEXT: tune what the playtest surfaces (1024-body init time → tile size fallback, navmesh params, slide friction, bot re-target logic) and record findings; when S8 is done, call propose_phase_transition.","timings":{"cache_n":104448,"draft_n":16499,"draft_n_accepted":4585,"predicted_ms":184110.0,"predicted_n":6942,"prompt_ms":3300.0,"prompt_n":684},"to_request":57026,"usage":{"cached_tokens":104448,"completion_tokens":6942,"prompt_tokens":105132}}
