ally made in this step. Let me be honest: the two edits are the decisions. The lint run just surfaced errors.\n\nI'll list those two. I shouldn't fabricate a decision about the computeNormals fix since I haven't made one yet.\n","seq":60834,"t":2873579,"text":"\n\nDECISION: Import `computeNormals` from `babylon-lite/mesh/compute-normals.js` and `createFlatGroundData` from `babylon-lite/mesh/create-ground.js` via subpath — WHY: neither is exported from the `babylon-lite` barrel, and subpath imports are the established lab idiom (scene114).\nDECISION: Drop the unused type imports (`EngineContext`, `NavigationPlugin`, `PhysicsWorld`, `SceneContext`) from scene252.ts — WHY: tsc flagged them as declared-but-never-used (TS6196) since types are inferred from the factory calls.\n\nNote: the lint run surfaced a new, still-unresolved mismatch — `computeNormals` is typed against `number[]` (not `Float32Array`) for its positions arg and return, so my two `computeNormals(...)` call sites in fps-terrain.ts (lines 124-125, 197-198) fail. I have not decided on the fix yet.","timings":{"cache_n":110336,"draft_n":1463,"draft_n_accepted":537,"predicted_ms":12600.0,"predicted_n":746,"prompt_ms":1050.0,"prompt_n":332},"to_request":60622,"usage":{"cached_tokens":110336,"completion_tokens":746,"prompt_tokens":110668}}
