{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"The user is asking me to reflect on the steps I just completed (the last message and its tool activity) and enumerate the decisions made, confirmed, or changed.\n\nWhat happened in the last step? I ran the smoke script with the TMPDIR override, and it failed because the Playwright browser executable doesn't exist at `~/Library/Caches/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1208/...`. In other words, the headless shell browser hasn't been installed.\n\nDecisions/workarounds from this step:\n1. Set TMPDIR to a directory inside the repo (`$PWD/.smoke-tmp`) when running node — because the sandbox refuses writes to the system temp directory (/var/folders/.../T), and Playwright's mkdtemp fails there. This is a workaround for the tooling.\n2. This step also revealed/confirmed that the repo's Playwright browsers aren't installed (the chromium headless shell is missing) — so before any Playwright-based smoke check can run, I need to install the browsers (pnpm exec playwright install chromium — or it might be that the repo's playwright config uses a different channel). Actually, this is more of a discovery than a decision. But a decision that will likely follow: use `pnpm exec playwright install` to get the browsers (following the gotcha, pnpm exec rather than npx).\n3. The smoke script itself: place it at the repo root (fps-smoke.cjs) and delete it before committing — this decision was made in the previous step (when /tmp was refused), not in this step. Hmm, but the TMPDIR override is part of the same workaround lineage. What the user is asking about is \"the step just completed (the last message and its tool activity)\" — my last message was \"Set TMPDIR to a directory inside the repo… retry,\" and the tool call was the bash command that ran the smoke script. So the decisions from this step are:\n   - DECISION: Run the Playwright smoke script with TMPDIR pointing to a directory inside the repo (.smoke-tmp) — because the sandbox refuses mkdtemp in the system temp directory.\n   - Also confirmed: The repo's Playwright browsers aren't installed (headless shell missing) — need to run the install (via pnpm exec, per the gotcha) before the smoke check can run.\n\nIs \"confirmed\" a decision? The user said \"made, confirmed, or changed decisions.\" The missing browsers is a discovery that led to a decision: install the browsers via pnpm exec playwright install. But I haven't actually decided on the command yet… I know the next step will be to install the browsers. I can record it as a decision: use `pnpm exec playwright install chromium` (following the gotcha about rogue npx installs).\n\nLet me keep it concise — only the decisions from this step:\n\n1. DECISION: Run the smoke script with TMPDIR=$PWD/.smoke-tmp (a directory inside the repo) — because the sandbox refuses writes/mkdtemp in the system temp directory (/var/folders/.../T).\n2. DECISION: Install the Playwright browsers via `pnpm exec playwright install` (not npx) — because the repo's browser cache is missing the chromium headless shell, and per the gotcha, npx/npm can spawn a rogue node_modules/playwright.\n\nI think these two are the honest list. I should use update_record to persist the TMPDIR workaround, since it's a gotcha that will be needed for all future Playwright runs in this session. The user asked for a reply — but the tool guidance says to record with update_record when something becomes worth the turn. I'll do both: record and reply. Actually, the user asked for a list in the reply. I can make the update_record call and then reply. The reply should be the list itself.\n\nLet me make the update_record call for the TMPDIR gotcha and the missing browsers, then present the list.\n","seq":63750,"t":3080264,"text":"","timings":{"cache_n":118016,"draft_n":2303,"draft_n_accepted":677,"predicted_ms":39720.0,"predicted_n":1006,"prompt_ms":1060.0,"prompt_n":233},"to_request":63189,"usage":{"cached_tokens":118016,"complet