{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Chrome crashes at startup inside the sandbox: crashpad's bootstrap_check_in is being denied, and the Crashpad directory is also blocked. The sandbox is blocking Chrome's access to `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad`. Even with `--user-data-dir` pointing inside the repo, Chrome still tries to use the system crashpad location.\n\nChrome flags to disable crashpad: `--disable-breakpad` is already there. The crash is coming from the crashpad client's bootstrap check-in being denied by the sandbox's Mach bootstrap. This is a fundamental limitation of the sandbox — I can't launch Chrome from within this sandbox.\n\nAlternative approach: I can't run a browser here. So how do I validate the scene?\n\nOptions:\n1. Ask the user to run the browser validation (they have the GUI).\n2. Validate everything that can be validated without a browser:\n   - Type check / lint: done ✓\n   - The dev server is serving the page: ✓ (200)\n   - Vite transforms the module graph: I can fetch the transformed module via the dev server to confirm the imports resolve (e.g., curl the .ts file through vite).\n   - Logic review.\n\n3. Maybe the sandbox allows launching the browser if I disable crashpad with an env var? The Mach bootstrap denial suggests a system-level restriction (the sandbox is blocking Mach port creation outside the sandbox). `--disable-breakpad` couldn't stop it, because crashpad is compiled in… actually, the SIGABRT was happening in the headless case too. The bootstrap_check_in permission denial is the decisive blow.\n\nWait — actually, let me reconsider: could it be that the sandbox is blocking *Mach bootstrap* in general, and that's why tsx's IPC pipe failed too? No — tsx's failure was a Unix pipe in /var/folders/T (a filesystem EPERM). The Chrome failure is a Mach bootstrap denial — a different mechanism.\n\nHmm, is there a way to run the Playwright browser outside the sandbox? The bash tool says \"network access may be denied\" and writes are sandboxed. I don't have control over the sandbox boundary.\n\nLet me try one more thing: `--disable-crash-reporter`? That's not a Chrome flag. There's `CHROME_DISABLE_CRASHPAD`… doesn't exist.\n\nActually — wait. Let me look at the headless attempt: same SIGABRT. The crashpad bootstrap denial → Chrome aborts. This is a sandbox limitation that can't be worked around with flags.\n\nOkay — decision: in this session I can't do browser validation from inside the sandbox. What I can do:\n1. Verify that the dev server transforms all modules (catches import resolution errors).\n2. Do a careful static review of the logic.\n3. Report to the user with a manual playtest checklist (the plan's S8 explicitly included a manual playtest — that's the user's job, or they can run it in a non-sandboxed shell).\n\nLet me try the module transform check: curl the transformed module through vite to confirm imports resolve. Vite serves /lite/src/lite/scene252.ts as ESM. A curl to http://localhost:5182/lite/src/lite/scene252.ts should return the transformed JS (with imports rewritten). If a module isn't found, vite returns a 500 with an error overlay message.\n\nI'll also curl the subpath imports: /@fs/... hmm, the alias resolves to a path inside the repo. For now let me just curl scene252.ts and follow one level of its imports.\n\nActually, a better way: use node to fetch the page + modules? A curl to the page returns HTML; the modules need to be fetched following the import chain. The simplest: curl each of my own modules through vite:\n- /lite/src/lite/scene252.ts\n- /lite/src/lite/fps-terrain.ts\n- /lite/src/lite/fps-input.ts\n- /lite/src/lite/fps-audio.ts\n\nIf vite can transform them (200 + JS), the imports within them resolve (vite resolves imports at transform time and returns 500 on failure).\n\nThe alias `babylon-lite` → packages/babylon-lite/src — the barrel import `from \"babylon-lite\"` resolves to the index.ts source. The subpath `babylon-lite/mesh/compute-normals.js` → src/mesh/compute-normals.js. Vite handles the .js → .ts resolution.\n\nLet me curl these.\n","seq":65496,"t":3197119,"text":"\n\nChrome can't be launched inside this sandbox (the Mach bootstrap for crashpad is denied) — so browser-based verification will have to be done outside of here. Instead, I'll verify via the dev server that the entire module graph transforms correctly (Vite resolves imports at transform time and returns 500 on failure):\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":123392,"draft_n":3199,"draft_n_accepted":768,"predicted_ms":48740.0,"predicted_n":1225,"prompt_ms":4300.0,"prompt_n":1947},"to_request":64638,"usage":{"cached_tokens":123392,"completion_tokens":1225,"prompt_tokens":125339}}
