sion, Playwright-based smoke/playtest cannot be run; instead verify via static checks (lint/typecheck already pass) and either have the user run the playtest manually or ask how to proceed.\n\nShould I also record these with update_record? The user asked me to pause and answer the question. According to the system prompt, update_record is something I invoke when something becomes worth recording. These are worth recording. But the user's request is specific: list each item on one line as GOTCHA: ... — IMPLICATION: .... I should answer in that format. I can also record them — but the user said \"pause\" and asked a direct question. Let me keep it simple: answer in the requested format. Maybe also run update_record for the two most important ones (browser blocked, dev server path). Actually, the instruction is \"record decisions and learnings with update_record\" — these are learnings. Let me do two quick update_record calls, then answer. Hmm — but the user asked a question that should be answered concisely. Doing tool calls before answering is fine.\n\nActually, let me be careful not to overdo it. The most important ones to record:\n1. Browser automation is blocked in this sandbox (Playwright/Chrome SIGABRT) — the playtest has to be done by the user or by some other means.\n2. dev:lab is blocked → use vite directly.\n\nThese are environmental constraints that will affect the rest of the session. Let me record them and then answer with the full list.\n","seq":66107,"t":3242892,"text":"","timings":{"cache_n":125184,"draft_n":3493,"draft_n_accepted":1032,"predicted_ms":58540.0,"predicted_n":1531,"prompt_ms":1110.0,"prompt_n":240},"to_request":65273,"usage":{"cached_tokens":125184,"completion_tokens":1531,"prompt_tokens":125424}}
