{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Chrome can't be launched inside this sandbox — the crashpad bootstrap check-in gets denied, and it aborts. This is a sandbox limitation, not a code issue. Let me note this as a gotcha for this step.\n\nAlso, the `dev:lab` script first runs a bundle build step (tsx), and it fails in the sandbox (EPERM on the tsx IPC pipe). The workaround is to run `pnpm exec vite` directly in lab/. This is a noteworthy finding from this step.\n\nLet me write down the gotchas from this step (S8 smoke test attempt):\n\n1. GOTCHA: The `dev:lab` script first runs `tsx scripts/build-bundle-scenes.ts && tsx scripts/build-bundle-demos.ts`, and in this sandboxed session it fails with EPERM (because tsx's IPC pipe in /var/folders/.../T is blocked) — IMPLICATION: To start the lab, run `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite` directly inside `lab/`.\n\n2. GOTCHA: Chrome/Playwright can't be launched inside this sandbox — crashpad's bootstrap_check_in gets permission denied (1100), access to `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad` is denied, and it aborts with SIGABRT. Overriding HOME/TMPDIR doesn't solve it — IMPLICATION: In this session, browser-based playtests (S8) can't be executed from within the sandbox. Verification is limited to lint/tsc + the dev server's module conversion, and actual playtests require the user or a non-sandboxed shell.\n\n3. GOTCHA: Playwright's bundled chromium build (1208) doesn't exist — only build 1243 is in the cache, and the repo's tests use `channel: \"chrome\"` (system Chrome) — IMPLICATION: The smoke script must use `channel: \"chrome\"` and must not depend on `npx playwright install`.\n\nWait — are these \"discovered in this step\"? The user is asking about the step I just completed (the smoke test attempt). Yes, all three are from this step.\n\nThe sandbox's /tmp write restriction — this is more of a general sandbox thing, but I discovered it when I tried to write to /tmp/fps-smoke.cjs. Worth including:\n\n4. GOTCHA: The sandbox refuses writes to /tmp and /var/folders (EPERM) — IMPLICATION: Temporary scripts need to be placed inside the repo (and cleaned up before commit per GUIDANCE 0b).\n\nLet me keep the list concise and focused on this step.\n","seq":66430,"t":3265344,"text":"\n\nGOTCHA: `pnpm dev:lab` starts with `tsx scripts/build-bundle-scenes.ts && tsx scripts/build-bundle-demos.ts`, which die in this sandboxed session with EPERM (tsx IPC pipe in `/var/folders/.../T` is blocked) — IMPLICATION: start the lab directly with `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite` from `lab/` (the bundle-build prefix is not needed for dev playtest; vite config still honors `LAB_DEV_PORT`).\nGOTCHA: no browser can be launched from inside this sandbox — Chrome aborts (SIGABRT) because crashpad's Mach `bootstrap_check_in` is denied (1100) and `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad` is unreadable; `HOME`/`TMPDIR` overrides don't help — IMPLICATION: S8's browser playtest cannot be run from here; in-sandbox validation is limited to lint/tsc + dev-server module transforms, and the real playtest must be done by the user (or a non-sandboxed shell).\nGOTCHA: the repo's Playwright (1.58.2) expects bundled chromium build 1208, but the cache only has 1243 — the repo's own configs sidestep this with `channel: \"chrome\"` (system Chrome) plus `--enable-unsafe-webgpu` — IMPLICATION: any ad-hoc Playwright script must use `channel: \"chrome\"` and must not rely on `npx playwright install` (which would also trip the rogue-`node_modules/playwright` gotcha).\nGOTCHA: the sandbox refuses writes to `/tmp` and `/var/folders` (EPERM) — IMPLICATION: temp scripts (like the smoke harness) must live inside the repo and be deleted before commit per GUIDANCE §0b.","timings":{"cache_n":127232,"draft_n":2058,"draft_n_accepted":667,"predicted_ms":19420.0,"predicted_n":961,"prompt_ms":540.0,"prompt_n":96},"to_request":66114,"usage":{"cached_tokens":127232,"completion_tokens":961,"prompt_tokens"