{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Static review found 2 actual bugs:\n\n1. **`rayVsCapsule` returns `t * RAY_RANGE`** — `t` is a parameter along the *unit* direction `fwd`, so `t` is already the distance. Multiplying by RAY_RANGE (100) makes the bot hit distance 100x larger → the bot effectively never wins against terrain hits → the bot can't be hit. Fix: return `t` (and clamp to RAY_RANGE).\n\n2. **Crosshair position**: `canvas.width`/`canvas.height` at HUD creation time — the canvas has no width/height attributes in the HTML (300×150 by default). The engine resizes the surface via `resizeSurface` (engine.ts:395, called at registration time). So `canvas.width/2` = 150/75 → the crosshair ends up at (142, 65) instead of the screen center. Fix: use `window.innerWidth/2` etc. (the lab canvas is fullscreen CSS). Let me check the canvas CSS in scene18.html: it's `width: 100vw; height: 100vh` or the like. scene180's positionPx uses fixed 360/380 — CSS pixels match layer.positionPx units (per the comment at scene180:82). So use window.innerWidth/innerHeight.\n\n3. **Player velocity never resets on landing** — `playerVel.y` accumulates -9.8*dt every step even while standing (moveWithCollisions clamps the penetration, but velocity keeps growing negative). Consequences: (a) terminal-velocity-like downward velocity builds up while standing; (b) running off a ledge starts a fall from high velocity; (c) jumping right after landing — vel.y is set to +7 anyway, so no problem. Fix: after moveWithCollisions, if support is grounded → `playerVel.y = 0`. (Quake: vel.z = 0 on landing.) Also clamp a terminal velocity of -30 for safety.\n\n   Same for the bot: `bot.velY` accumulates the same way — reset to 0 when the bot is on the ground. Bot ground detection: cheap way — if `bot.velY < 0` and the controller's y didn't decrease by more than a small epsilon since the previous step → on the ground → velY = 0. Or just clamp velY's minimum to -30; the bot will settle on the floor (the controller clamps it). For the bot, the simplest and most robust: track the previous y; if the expected drop didn't happen → velY = 0.\n\n   Actually, even simpler for both: if the actual y displacement after moveWithCollisions is smaller than the requested downward displacement (i.e., the controller was blocked), that means contact → zero out vel.y. Let's do that: compute the pre-move y, move, compute the post-move y; if `preY - postY < requestedDrop * 0.5` → grounded → vel.y = 0.\n\n4. **Self-hit guard** (open item f57025-4): add `terr.hitDistance > 2` so that shots that hit near the muzzle don't destroy the tile under the player's feet (in case the player's capsule shows up in the raycast).\n\nLet me also double-check the signature of `updateDefaultTextData` (does it mutate the TextData in place?) — from the barrel export `updateDefaultTextData(data, text)` — I confirmed the name earlier; let me quickly verify the semantics.\n\nAlso, check the canvas CSS in scene18.html and confirm the fullscreen assumption.\n","seq":67817,"t":3396419,"text":"\n\nStatic review found real bugs. Verifying `updateDefaultTextData` semantics and the canvas CSS before fixing:\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":61440,"draft_n":2275,"draft_n_accepted":594,"predicted_ms":16079.999999999998,"predicted_n":919,"prompt_ms":3050.0,"prompt_n":1978},"to_request":67505,"usage":{"cached_tokens":61440,"completion_tokens":919,"prompt_tokens":63418}}
