{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"scene18.html sets `width=\"1280\" height=\"720\"` on the canvas — but my scene252.html probably copied that too. The CSS stretches it to 100vw/100vh. layer.positionPx is in CSS pixels (per the comment in scene180). So the crosshair should be placed at `window.innerWidth/2` (CSS pixels), not `canvas.width/2` (1280 device pixels). If the window is not 1280×720, the crosshair will be off-center.\n\nLet me check scene252.html — I wrote it by mimicking scene18. I'll check it and fix the crosshair to use window.innerWidth/innerHeight.\n\nNext, the fix list:\n1. `rayVsCapsule`: return `t` (already the distance in units of the unit direction), and clamp to RAY_RANGE.\n2. Crosshair: `window.innerWidth / 2 - 8`, `window.innerHeight / 2 - 10`.\n3. Player: reset `playerVel.y = 0` on grounding (measure the actual vs. requested drop), clamp terminal velocity to -30.\n4. Bot: same velY reset via the drop-measurement method.\n5. Self-hit guard: in tryFire, ignore terrain hits with `terr.hitDistance < 2`.\n\nRegarding the player drop measurement:\n```ts\nconst preY = player.getPosition().y;\nplayer.moveWithCollisions({ x: playerVel.x * dt, y: playerVel.y * dt, z: playerVel.z * dt });\nconst postY = player.getPosition().y;\nconst requestedDrop = playerVel.y * dt;\nif (playerVel.y < 0 && preY - postY < requestedDrop * 0.5) {\n    playerVel.y = 0; // landed / floor contact\n}\n```\nHmm — while standing still, vel.y starts at 0, then -= g*dt → -0.16; requestedDrop = -0.0027u; the controller blocks the entire drop → preY - postY ≈ 0 < 0.0013 → vel.y = 0. Next step, same thing. While falling: vel.y grows to -9.8, requestedDrop is -0.16u, the controller actually drops that amount → preY-postY ≈ 0.16 ≥ 0.08 → keep the velocity. Walking off a ledge: same as falling. Landing: blocked → zeroed.\n\nEdge case: walking down a gentle slope — the actual drop partially matches the requested drop; the 0.5 factor tolerates partial contact. Good enough.\n\nTerminal velocity clamp: `if (playerVel.y < -30) playerVel.y = -30;`\n\nBot:\n```ts\nconst preY = bot.cc.getPosition().y;\nbot.cc.moveWithCollisions({ x: av.x * dt, y: bot.velY * dt, z: av.z * dt });\nconst postY = bot.cc.getPosition().y;\nif (bot.velY < 0 && preY - postY < bot.velY * dt * 0.5) {\n    bot.velY = 0;\n}\nif (bot.velY < -30) bot.velY = -30;\n```\n\nNote: `bot.velY * dt * 0.5` is negative; the comparison `preY - postY < (negative value)` — wait: requestedDrop = bot.velY*dt (negative). Condition: actualDrop < requestedDrop*0.5, where requestedDrop*0.5 is also negative… Example: velY=-1, dt=1/60: requestedDrop=-0.0167, *0.5 = -0.0083. actualDrop = preY-postY ≥ 0. Is 0 < -0.0083? No! Sign error. We want \"the actual drop is less than half of the requested drop\": actualDrop < |requestedDrop|*0.5 → `preY - postY < Math.abs(bot.velY * dt) * 0.5`.\n\nSame for the player: `preY - postY < Math.abs(playerVel.y * dt) * 0.5`.\n\nLet me implement all the fixes.\n","seq":68102,"t":3414917,"text":"\n\n`updateDefaultTextData` mutates in place ✓. The canvas has fixed `width=1280 height=720` attributes, but the layer's position is in CSS pixels (scene180:82) — so the crosshair needs to use `window.innerWidth/innerHeight`. Applying the fixes found in the review:\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":63488,"draft_n":2149,"draft_n_accepted":865,"predicted_ms":15410.0,"predicted_n":1172,"prompt_ms":2770.0,"prompt_n":1729},"to_request":67820,"usage":{"cached_tokens":63488,"completion_tokens":1172,"prompt_tokens":65217}}
