{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"The user is asking me to pause and report the gotchas from the steps I just completed. What did I actually do in this session (post-compaction)?\n\nSteps since compaction:\n1. Started the dev server in the background: `cd lab && LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite` — succeeded, confirmed 200 on scene252.html.\n2. Created the Playwright smoke script (fps-smoke.cjs) — it failed:\n   - First: `EPERM mkdtemp '/var/folders/.../T/playwright-artifacts-*'` — the sandbox is blocking the system temp directory.\n   - Tried the `tmpDir` launch option — still EPERM (Playwright was using the system temp before tmpDir took effect, or for other artifacts).\n   - Set the `TMPDIR` env var to a repo-local directory — this fixed the mkdtemp.\n   - Next: \"Executable doesn't exist at .../chromium_headless_shell-1208\" — the cached browser is build 1243, but playwright 1.58.2 expects 1208. So the default `chromium.launch()` will fail.\n   - Checked the repo's playwright.config.ts — the repo uses `channel: \"chrome\"` (system Chrome) with `--enable-unsafe-webgpu`.\n   - Tried `channel: \"chrome\", headless: true` — SIGABRT at launch.\n   - Tried with SwiftShader args — (I swapped args back and forth; the final state was channel chrome, headless false — actually, let me reconstruct: set headless true, SIGABRT; then edited to SwiftShader args, ran, SIGABRT with crashpad error; then reverted to plain args and set headless: false; ran with headless false → SIGABRT with crashpad bootstrap_check_in Permission denied).\n   - Tried overriding HOME — still SIGABRT (crashpad reads ~/Library/Application Support regardless).\n   - Conclusion: browser automation is blocked in this sandbox.\n3. Fell back to non-browser verification:\n   - All four modules return 200 from the Vite dev server (transforms are fine).\n   - Verified via the transformed output that alias resolution works (`babylon-lite` → `packages/babylon-lite/src/index.ts`, subpaths → source files, `@babylonjs/havok` → pnpm store).\n4. Static review of scene252.ts found bugs:\n   - `rayVsCapsule` was returning `t * RAY_RANGE` — since `t` is the parameter along the unit direction, `t` is already the distance; multiplying by RAY_RANGE inflated the bot hit distance by 100x → the bot effectively couldn't be hit. Fixed to `Math.min(t, RAY_RANGE)`.\n   - Crosshair position: used `canvas.width/2` (device px, 1280×720 attributes), but the text layer's positionPx is in CSS pixels (scene180 comment) → the crosshair was off-center unless the window is exactly 1280×720. Needs `window.innerWidth/innerHeight`. Not yet fixed.\n   - Player/bot vertical velocity never resets on landing: `playerVel.y -= GRAVITY*dt` accumulates even while standing (moveWithCollisions clamps the penetration but the velocity keeps growing negative) → running off a ledge starts the fall from high velocity; terminal velocity unbounded. Plan: reset vel.y to 0 when the actual drop is much smaller than the requested drop, and clamp terminal velocity to -30. Not yet fixed.\n   - Self-hit guard (open item f57025-4): decided to add a `terr.hitDistance > 2` guard. Not yet applied.\n\nWait — the user's question is \"in the step you just completed, did anything behave differently than expected\". The most recent step was: verifying `updateDefaultTextData` + the canvas HTML, then fixing the rayVsCapsule return value. But I think they're asking about discoveries from this session segment since compaction (playtest attempt + static review). Let me list all the gotchas discovered in this segment:\n\n1. Sandbox blocks the system temp directory for Playwright/Chrome — both mkdtemp and crashpad bootstrap fail (EPERM). Setting `TMPDIR` to a repo-local directory fixes node-side mkdtemp, but Chrome (channel \"chrome\") still SIGABRTs because crashpad reads `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad` and the Mach bootstrap check-in is denied — overriding HOME doesn't help. IMPLICATION: browser-based smoke/playtest is impossible in this sandbox; verification has to be lint + typecheck + dev-server module transforms + user manual playtest.\n\n2. The repo's Playwright browser cache (build 1243) doesn't match the installed playwright 1.58.2 (expects 1208) — default `chromium.launch()` fails with \"Executable doesn't exist\". IMPLICATION: even outside the sandbox, use `channel: \"chrome\"` per the repo's playwright.config.ts (the repo's idiom), and don't assume the bundled browser works.\n\n3. `rayVsCapsule` bug: in the segment-vs-capsule parameterization using unit direction, `t` is already the distance — my draft was multiplying by RAY_RANGE, inflating bot hit distance by 100x (the bot could never be hit). Fixed to `Math.min(t, RAY_RANGE)`.\n\n4. Text layer's `positionPx` is in CSS pixels, but the canvas has fixed `width=1280 height=720` attributes and is stretched by CSS to 100vw/100vh — so `canvas.width/2` for the crosshair is wrong (device px ≠ CSS px). IMPLICATION: use `window.innerWidth/innerHeight` for the crosshair's positionPx.\n\n5. `playerVel.y`/`bot.velY` accumulate gravity every step even while standing — moveWithCollisions clamps the penetration but doesn't zero the velocity. IMPLICATION: reset vel.y to 0 on ground contact (compare actual drop vs. requested drop) and clamp terminal velocity; otherwise the fall starts from a built-up velocity.\n\nShould I mention the earlier stuff too? The user said \"in the step you just completed\" — probably meaning the work since the last pause. The work since compaction included: starting the dev server (worked as expected — no gotcha, matches the audit-28769-6 prediction), creating and failing the smoke script (multiple gotchas), module verification (as expected), static review (bug discoveries — though these are my own bugs, not API behavior... the rayVsCapsule one is a math bug I wrote myself; is that a \"gotcha\"? It's a discovery from this step. The instruction says \"APIs that behave differently, errors and their actual causes, discovered limitations or unsupported features\". My own math bug is a kind of error discovery, but it's more of a \"fix\" than a gotcha. I'll include it since it materially affects what I do next. Actually, let me narrow the focus: APIs/behavior/limitations that were discovered. My own code bugs are things I'm fixing, not environment gotchas. But it is \"an error and its actual cause\". I'll include the rayVsCapsule one briefly.\n\nAlso: `pnpm dev:lab` failing due to tsx's IPC pipe EPERM — that was discovered before compaction (already recorded in r63755). Skip.\n\nOne more: `TMPDIR` env var fixes node's mkdtemp but not Chrome's crashpad — this is a nuance of gotcha 1.\n\nAlso, the canvas HTML check: scene18.html has `width=\"1280\" height=\"720\"` attributes — my scene252.html mirrors that. Discovery: positionPx is in CSS px (from the scene180 comment), so using canvas.width (device px) is wrong.\n\nI'll format each item as GOTCHA: ... — IMPLICATION: ... on a separate line.\n","seq":71275,"t":3565333,"text":"\n\nGOTCHA: Playwright/Chrome cannot run in this sandbox — node-side `mkdtemp` is EPERM on the system temp dir (fixed with `TMPDIR` pointed at a repo-local dir), but system Chrome (`channel: \"chrome\"`) SIGABRTs at launch because crashpad's Mach bootstrap check-in and `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad` are permission-denied, and overriding `HOME` does not help — IMPLICATION: no browser-based smoke test or playtest is possible from here; verification is lint + typecheck + dev-server module transform + a manual playtest by the user on :5182.\nGOTCHA: the repo's Playwright browser cache (build 1243) does not match the installed playwright 1.58.2 (expects 1208), so default `chromium.launch()` fails with \"Executable doesn't exist\" — IMPLICATION: any future Playwright work must use `channel: \"chrome\"` (the repo's own idiom in playwright.config.ts), not the bundled browser.\nGOTCHA: text-layer `positionPx` is in CSS pixels (scene180 comment: \"CSS pixels — matches layer.positionPx units\"), but the canvas has fixed `width=\"1280\" height=\"720\"` attributes stretched by CSS to 100vw/100vh — IMPLICATION: the crosshair must be positioned with `window.innerWidth/innerHeight`, not `canvas.width/height` (still to fix).\nGOTCHA: `moveWithCollisions` clamps displacement into the floor but never zeroes the velocity — `playerVel.y`/`bot.velY` accumulate `-GRAVITY*dt` every step even while standing, so falls start with built-up velocity and terminal velocity is unbounded — IMPLICATION: reset vel.y to 0 on ground contact (compare actual drop vs requested drop) and clamp a terminal velocity in the physics step (still to fix).\nGOTCHA: in my `rayVsCapsule`, the segment parameter `t` is measured along the unit direction, so `t` already is the distance — my draft returned `t * RAY_RANGE`, inflating bot hit distances 100× (bots would never be hit) — IMPLICATION: fixed to `Math.min(t, RAY_RANGE)`; any other ray tests must be checked for the same unit-direction assumption.","timings":{"cache_n":66304,"draft_n":5110,"draft_n_accepted":1547,"predicted_ms":58590.0,"predicted_n":2277,"prompt_ms":1600.0,"prompt_n":314},"to_request":69809,"usage":{"cached_tokens":66304,"completion_tokens":2277,"prompt_tokens":66618}}
