{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"I'm reflecting on the recent work: I attempted browser-based verification with Playwright and hit several obstacles—temp directory restrictions in the sandbox, missing browser dependencies, and Chrome crashes when trying to use system Chrome. I worked around these by adjusting environment variables and using headless mode, but ultimately had to fall back on static analysis and module transform checks through the dev server. I also identified actual bugs during the static review process.\n\nI'm now documenting the key decisions: browser automation is blocked in this sandbox, so verification shifts to linting, typechecking, and manual testing; the smoke script needs specific flags like TMPDIR redirection and Chrome channel configuration; I found and fixed two real bugs in the distance calculation and crosshair positioning that static review caught; I've confirmed the TextRenderer compositing approach works with proper registration order; and I'm planning to add a self-hit guard to prevent terrain hits from affecting the player.\n","seq":71896,"t":3591505,"text":"\n\nDECISION: Browser-based smoke verification is not possible in this sandbox — WHY: Playwright's mkdtemp is blocked in the system temp dir, the bundled chromium build (1208) is missing from the cache, and system Chrome (channel \"chrome\") SIGABRTs at launch because crashpad's Mach bootstrap check-in is permission-denied, even with `TMPDIR`/`HOME` redirected into the repo.\nDECISION: Validation this session is lint + typecheck + dev-server module-transform checks (all four new modules return 200 through Vite with resolved aliases) + user manual playtest on :5182 — WHY: the dev server is reachable and transforming the full import graph is the deepest verification the sandbox allows.\nDECISION: The `fps-smoke.cjs` script stays in the repo root for the user to run outside the sandbox, and will be deleted before commit — WHY: /tmp is write-blocked so it must live in-repo, and GUIDANCE §0b requires removing temp files before commit.\nDECISION: `rayVsCapsule` must return `Math.min(t, RAY_RANGE)` instead of `t * RAY_RANGE` — WHY: `t` is the parameter along the unit direction `fwd`, so it is already the hit distance; the old scaling made bot hits ~100× farther than terrain hits, so bots could never be shot.\nDECISION: The crosshair layer must be positioned with `window.innerWidth/innerHeight` (CSS pixels), not `canvas.width/height` — WHY: the canvas carries fixed `width=1280 height=720` attributes while `layer.positionPx` is in CSS pixels (scene180's drag code confirms the unit), so device-pixel coordinates would off-center the crosshair.\nDECISION: `updateDefaultTextData(hudData, text)` is the correct in-place HUD update call — WHY: default-text-data.ts:83 confirms it re-lays out the text, extracts new glyphs into the same storage, and updates the run the layer references.\nDECISION: (still to apply) player/bot vertical velocity must be zeroed on floor contact (actual drop < half of requested drop) with a -30u/s terminal clamp — WHY: `moveWithCollisions` clamps penetration but `playerVel.y`/`bot.velY` accumulate -9.8·dt forever while standing, so falling off a ledge would start at high velocity.\nDECISION: (still to apply) `tryFire` should ignore terrain hits with `hitDistance < 2` — WHY: the player's capsule shape mask is unverified (private `_shape`), so a self-hit guard prevents shots from destroying the tile under the player's feet.","timings":{"cache_n":66304,"draft_n":2107,"draft_n_accepted":474,"predicted_ms":24630.0,"predicted_n":775,"prompt_ms":900.0,"prompt_n":330},"to_request":71283,"usage":{"cached_tokens":66304,"completion_tokens":775,"prompt_tokens":66634}}
