{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Let me organize the current state and answer the two questions.\n\nCurrent state: I'm in the middle of fixing bugs found during static review. Just confirmed that the character controller's `_position` is the capsule center (pointA is h*0.5 - r above the center, pointB is h*0.5 - r below the center, i.e., the capsule is centered on `_position`). So `getPosition()` returns the capsule center.\n\nSo the eye is at `center + EYE_HEIGHT (1.5)`. The capsule extends from center-0.9 to center+0.9. So the eye is 0.6 above the top of the capsule. The eye is outside the capsule. Good.\n\nNow let me enumerate the unresolved items:\n\nUnresolved / unverified items:\n1. Runtime behavior of the nav agent re-sync (`agentGoto` to bot position when >4u) — could cause chase loops / jitter. Playtest will reveal.\n2. TextRenderer compositing on top of the 3D scene (registration order scene→text, `clear: false`) — inferred but never actually seen on screen.\n3. Init cost of 1024 static tile bodies + navmesh build cost/quality at cs=0.5 on a 128×128u mesh — never measured.\n4. Default shape filter membership mask — now confirmed that the player capsule has default filter (~0), so it can't be excluded by a raycast filter; the `> 2` distance guard is the mitigation, but it's unverified at runtime whether it fully prevents self-hits (especially aiming straight down).\n5. `setThinInstances` per-frame upload — confirmed that `_version++` and dirty range cause re-upload; so per-frame calls work. Resolved.\n6. Browser validation is blocked in this sandbox (Chrome SIGABRTs at launch due to crashpad/Mach bootstrap EPERM). So runtime validation is impossible here — need lint + typecheck + user manual playtest.\n7. Mouse-look sign convention (yaw/pitch) — unverified; if inverted, one-line fix during playtest.\n8. Whether `updateDefaultTextData`'s in-place mutation actually causes the TextRenderer to re-render the layer — inferred (the layer references the same TextData object); unverified at runtime.\n9. FreeCamera's `cam.position.set` / `cam.target.set` — does the FreeCamera world matrix actually get rebuilt from position+target every frame? Inferred from mat4LookAtLH. Unverified at runtime.\n10. Lint / typecheck hasn't been re-run after my latest edits (rayVsCapsule rewrite, velocity reset, crosshair, Debris.body null, self-hit guard).\n\nWhat I'm concretely planning to do next:\n1. Re-run `pnpm run lint:fix` then `pnpm run lint` to confirm the latest edits pass typecheck/lint.\n2. Record decisions/learnings via update_record (rayVsCapsule fix, velocity reset, crosshair CSS-pixel fix, Debris.body null, self-hit guard, confirmation that setThinInstances re-uploads per frame, confirmation that the controller position is the capsule center).\n3. Report status: browser validation is blocked in the sandbox; provide the user with a manual playtest checklist (S8) + the URL :5182/lite/scene252.html.\n4. Clean up temp files (fps-smoke.cjs, .smoke-tmp, .smoke-home) before finishing (GUIDANCE §0b).\n5. If lint passes, propose a phase transition.\n\nLet me write these out concisely.\n\nActually, I should be careful not to over-claim. Let me organize the unresolved items into ones that truly matter for later work:\n\nOPEN items:\n- Runtime: nav agent re-sync (`agentGoto` at >4u) may cause bot chase loops / jitter — playtest will reveal.\n- Runtime: TextRenderer HUD compositing (scene registered first, `clear: false`) is inferred, never seen on screen.\n- Runtime: FreeCamera driven by per-frame `position`+`target` (lookAt) — unverified at runtime; mouse-look yaw/pitch sign convention unverified (one-line flip if inverted).\n- Runtime: init cost of 1024 static tile bodies + navmesh build at cs=0.5 on 128×128u — never measured; fallback to 8×8u tiles (256 bodies) if slow.\n- The player capsule has default filter (~0) so a bullet raycast can't exclude it by mask; the `terr.hitDistance > 2` self-hit guard is unverified at runtime (especially when aiming straight down at one's own feet).\n- Runtime: `updateDefaultTextData`'s in-place mutation causing the TextRenderer to actually re-render the HUD layer — inferred, unverified.\n- Browser-based validation is blocked in this sandbox (Chrome SIGABRTs at launch, crashpad/Mach EPERM) — no Playwright smoke/playtest possible here; validation = lint + typecheck + user manual playtest.\n- Lint/typecheck hasn't been re-run after the latest batch of edits.\n\nNEXT items:\n1. Run `pnpm run lint:fix` then `pnpm run lint` to confirm the latest edits pass.\n2. Record key learnings/decisions via update_record (rayVsCapsule rewrite, velocity-reset-on-landing, crosshair CSS-pixel fix, Debris.body null type, self-hit guard, setThinInstances per-frame re-upload, controller position = capsule center).\n3. Delete temp/scratch files (fps-smoke.cjs, .smoke-tmp/, .smoke-home/) per GUIDANCE §0b.\n4. Report to user: validation status + manual playtest checklist at :5182/lite/scene252.html.\n5. If lint is clean, propose phase transition.\n\nLet me keep it concise. I don't need to run tools right now — the user asked for a pause and two questions. Let me just answer. But wait — should I run the lint to confirm? The user said \"pause\" and asked two questions. I should answer the questions, not start new work. Let me just answer.\n\nActually, the instructions say \"If you intend to call multiple tools... make all of the independent calls in the same block.\" But the user explicitly asked me to pause and answer two questions. So I should just answer in text, not call tools. Let me do that.\n\nLet me be concise and precise.\n","seq":82038,"t":4116222,"text":"\n\nOPEN: Browser validation is blocked in this sandbox — Chrome SIGABRTs at launch (crashpad/Mach bootstrap EPERM), so no Playwright smoke/playtest possible here; validation is lint + typecheck + your manual playtest on :5182/lite/scene252.html.\nOPEN: Runtime — nav agent re-sync (`agentGoto` to bot pos when >4u apart) may cause bot chase-loops/jitter; playtest will tell.\nOPEN: Runtime — HUD TextRenderer compositing over the 3D frame (scene registered first, `clear: false`) is reasoned from the render-context registry, never seen on screen.\nOPEN: Runtime — `updateDefaultTextData` in-place mutation actually triggering the TextRenderer to re-draw the HUD layer is assumed, unverified.\nOPEN: Runtime — FreeCamera driven by per-frame `position`+`target` (lookAt) and the mouse-look yaw/pitch sign convention are unverified; if look is inverted it's a one-line sign flip.\nOPEN: Runtime — init cost of 1024 static tile bodies + navmesh build at cs=0.5 over 128×128u never measured; fallback is 8×8u tiles (256 bodies) if world init is slow.\nOPEN: The player capsule keeps Havok's default filter (~0), so a bullet raycast can't exclude it by mask; the `terr.hitDistance > 2` self-hit guard is unverified at runtime (esp. aiming straight down at own feet).\nOPEN: Lint/typecheck has not been re-run since my latest batch of edits (rayVsCapsule rewrite, velocity-reset-on-landing, crosshair CSS-pixel fix, `Debris.body` null typing, self-hit guard).\n\nNEXT: Run `pnpm run lint:fix` then `pnpm run lint` to confirm the latest edits typecheck and pass ESLint.\nNEXT: Record the settled learnings via update_record (rayVsCapsule cylindrical+cap rewrite, velocity reset on floor contact, crosshair in CSS pixels, `Debris.body: PhysicsBody | null`, self-hit guard, `setThinInstances` re-uploads per call via `_version` bump, controller `getPosition` = capsule center).\nNEXT: Delete scratch files (fps-smoke.cjs, .smoke-tmp/, .smoke-home/) per GUIDANCE §0b before wrapping up.\nNEXT: Report status to you with the manual playtest checklist (ready/error dataset, move/slide/jump, mouse-look, shoot holes → tile removed + body gone + nav obstacle, fall-through respawn, debris, bots patrol/shoot, HUD, audio).\nNEXT: If lint is clean, call propose_phase_transition.","timings":{"cache_n":97024,"draft_n":4137,"draft_n_accepted":1426,"predicted_ms":57140.0,"predicted_n":2017,"prompt_ms":930.0,"prompt_n":251},"to_request":80874,"usage":{"cached_tokens":97024,"completion_tokens":2017,"prompt_tokens":97275}}
