{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Now I understand the structure. `eyePos()` returns `center.y + EYE_HEIGHT`. EYE_HEIGHT = 1.5.\n\nLet me reconsider. The capsule spans center ± 0.9. The eye is at center + 1.5, which is 0.6 above the top of the capsule. This is a high camera position.\n\nLet me reconsider the approach. I'll do the following:\n1. Lower EYE_HEIGHT to a realistic value (0.7, near the head).\n2. Add a muzzle offset so that the ray origin is outside the capsule.\n\nLet me change EYE_HEIGHT to 0.7 and add a muzzle offset to tryFire.\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether the camera at center + 0.7 looks good. The capsule is a capsule shape for the player, but there's no display mesh for the player (first-person). So the camera is the player. A camera at center + 0.7 is near the head. When the player is standing on the ground, center.y = ground.y + 0.9, so the camera is at ground.y + 1.6. That's a realistic eye height (1.6m).\n\nSo let's do the following:\n1. EYE_HEIGHT = 0.7 (camera at ground + 1.6 when standing).\n2. MUZZLE_OFFSET = 0.8 (ray origin 0.8 in front of the eye, outside the capsule).\n\nLet me make these changes. First, I'll change EYE_HEIGHT.\n","seq":84551,"t":4251036,"text":"","timings":{"cache_n":111616,"draft_n":868,"draft_n_accepted":400,"predicted_ms":12130.0,"predicted_n":524,"prompt_ms":1660.0,"prompt_n":435},"to_request":84320,"usage":{"cached_tokens":111616,"completion_tokens":524,"prompt_tokens":112051}}
