: sed havok-queries.ts 180-260 → physicsRaycast semantics (membership/collideWith, default ~0).\n- Bash: grep character-controller position semantics.\n- Read character-controller.ts 325-369 → capsule shape is centered on _position; getPosition returns center.\n- (Long reasoning about eye height / self-hit occlusion)\n- Read scene252.ts lines 52-65 (constants).\n\nAnd then the user's pause message.\n\nSo \"the step you just completed\" — the most recent step is the whole static review + fixes + investigation into the raycast/capsule filter. The user is asking: did anything in the step I just completed behave differently than expected? List GOTCHA entries.\n\nWhat were the unexpected things in the most recent step (static review + fixes + API investigation)?\n\n1. **The `u` formula in rayVsCapsule was wrong** — that's my own bug, not an API discovery. The question is about APIs that behave differently, errors and their true causes, limitations/unsupported features. My own code bugs are... hmm, \"errors and their true causes\" — I discovered that my own u formula was wrong (missing division by hh). That's a discovery about my own code, not the repo. Probably not what they're after, but it is a discovery from this step. The format says \"an API that works another way, an error and its actual cause, a limitation or unsupported feature you discovered\". My own math bug is an \"error and its actual cause\". I could include it, but I think the intent is repo/API/environment discoveries. Let me focus on those, but the self-hit occlusion discovery is a big one.\n\n2. **The player's capsule cannot be excluded from raycasts** — the character controller's shape is private, default filter is ~0/~0, so a bullet raycast with any membership/collideWith mask will still hit the player's capsule. A raycast returns only the closest hit, so if the eye is inside/at the height of the capsule, the player's own capsule occludes all terrain hits. This is a real limitation discovered this step: — IMPLICATION: the eye must be placed above the capsule top (EYE_HEIGHT ≈ 1.0 from center, i.e., 0.1 above the head) so forward rays clear the capsule; the distance guard alone is insufficient because physicsRaycast returns only the first hit.\n\n   Wait — did I actually confirm that physicsRaycast returns only the first hit? Yes: `HP_QueryCollector_GetCastRayResult(collector, 0)` — index 0, \"return the first body it hits\". Confirmed in the doc comment: \"Cast a ray from from to to and return the first body it hits.\"\n\n3. **`getPosition()` returns the capsule center, not the feet** — I had been assuming/uncertain; confirmed that the capsule spans center ± halfH, and the eye at center+1.5 is 0.6 above the head. Actually, was this \"different than expected\"? In my code I had `EYE_HEIGHT = 1.5` added to the center — the doc example (`createPhysicsCharacterController(world, {x:0,y:1,z:0}, {capsuleHeight:1.8})` and then reading the position to a display mesh) suggests position is the center... the controller's constructor builds the shape around the origin (pointA at +h/2-r, pointB at -h/2+r), so position = center. I expected it might be the feet. This is a discovery about API semantics: — IMPLICATION: spawn/eye/respawn heights must be computed relative to the center (feet = center - 0.9).\n\n4. **`updateDefaultTextData` mutates the TextData in place** (layout + glyph storage + swap run) — that was as expected, no surprise.\n\n5. **scene18.html's canvas has fixed width=1280 height=720 attributes but CSS stretches to 100vw/100vh; positionPx is in CSS pixels** — this is why canvas.width was wrong for the crosshair. A discovery: — IMPLICATION: screen-space text positions must use window.innerWidth/innerHeight, not canvas.width/height.\n\n6. **setThinInstances bumps _version and marks the full range dirty on every call** — so per-frame re-upload works, no flush needed. This resolves an open item as expected — the behavior was verified, not unexpected. Could mention as a confirmation, but the question asks for \"behaved differently than expected\" — this matched expectations (it's designed for this). Skip or mention briefly? The instruction says list each discovery; \"if none, reply NONE\". Only discoveries that were different than expected. The setThinInstances one was as expected (that's how it's designed). Skip.\n\n7. Also, in this step (earlier in the same turn): the Playwright/Chrome discoveries. But the user said \"the step you just completed\" — the most recent step. The Playwright stuff was earlier in this session segment. Hmm. The pause comes right after my read of the constants (lines 52-65). The \"step\" probably means the whole turn since the last user message, which includes both the smoke attempts and the static review. The user's prompt came after all of that. To be safe, I should list all discoveries from this turn/segment:\n\nPlaywright/sandbox:\n- GOTCHA: Playwright's artifact mkdtemp ignores `launch({ tmpDir })` — it creates `playwright-artifacts-*` in the system temp directory before tmpDir is applied; the sandbox denies /var/folders/.../T — IMPLICATION: set `TMPDIR` to a repo-local directory when running node for Playwright.\n- GOTCHA: The ms-playwright cache has browser build 1243, but the repo's playwright 1.58.2 expects 1208, so the default `chromium.launch()` fails with \"Executable doesn't exist\"; the repo's own config uses `channel: \"chrome\"` (system Chrome) — IMPLICATION: launch with `channel: \"chrome\"` + `--enable-unsafe-webgpu` (repo idiom from playwright.config.ts).\n- GOTCHA: System Chrome SIGABRTs at launch in this sandbox (headless and headed): crashpad's Mach bootstrap check-in is denied, and `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad` is EPERM; HOME override doesn't help — IMPLICATION: no browser-based smoke/playtest possible in this session; verification is lint + typecheck + Vite transform (all 4 new files 200), and the user's manual playtest on :5182.\n\nStatic review / API:\n- GOTCHA: `physicsRaycast` returns only the first (closest) hit, and the character controller's capsule has a default filter (~0/~0) and is private — no membership/collideWith mask can exclude the player's own capsule from a bullet raycast — IMPLICATION: if the eye is at capsule height (or inside it), the player's capsule occludes all terrain hits; the eye must be placed above the capsule top (≈ center + 1.0) so forward rays clear it; the `hitDistance > 2` guard alone is insufficient.\n- GOTCHA: `PhysicsCharacterController.getPosition()` returns the capsule center (the shape is built centered on the node), not the feet — IMPLICATION: eye/spawn/respawn heights are computed relative to the center (feet = center − 0.9); the current EYE_HEIGHT = 1.5 puts the eye 0.6 above the head and needs to be lowered to ~1.0.\n- GOTCHA: `scene18.html`'s canvas has fixed `width=1280 height=720` attributes but CSS stretches it to 100vw/100vh, and `positionPx` is in CSS pixels (scene180:82) — IMPLICATION: screen-space HUD positions must use `window.innerWidth/innerHeight`, not `canvas.width/height` (already fixed for the crosshair).\n- Also my own rayVsCapsule u-formula bug — should I list it? It's \"an error and its actual cause\" — I discovered that the u formula I had written was wrong (missing /hh in the first term), and it also missed end-cap hits. I rewrote it. I think it's worth one line since it's an error discovered this step. But the format leans toward API/environment discoveries. I'll include it briefly since it's a real discovery (my math was wrong; the capsule test now handles the cylindrical band + end caps).\n\nHmm, the user's question: \"did anything behave differently than expected — an API that works another way, an error and its actual cause, a limitation or unsupported feature you discovered? List each on its own line... only discoveries from this step.\"\n\nI'll list:\n1. Playwright tmpDir / TMPDIR (environment).\n2. Browser cache mismatch / channel chrome (environment).\n3. Chrome SIGABRT / crashpad (environment — no browser test possible).\n4. physicsRaycast first-hit-only + private capsule filter → self-occlusion (API limitation).\n5. getPosition = capsule center (API semantics).\n6. Canvas attribute vs CSS pixel mismatch (HTML/CSS vs API units).\n7. My rayVsCapsule u bug (error + cause) — include as an error.\n\nThat's thorough. Keep each line concise. Format: GOTCHA: <what is true> — IMPLICATION: <what must be done differently>.\n\nLet me write it up.\n","seq":85223,"t":4287846,"text":"\n\nGOTCHA: Playwright's artifact mkdtemp ignores `launch({ tmpDir })` — it creates `playwright-artifacts-*` in the system temp dir first, and the sandbox denies `/var/folders/.../T` — IMPLICATION: run Playwright node scripts with `TMPDIR` pointed at a repo-local dir (e.g. `TMPDIR=\"$PWD/.smoke-tmp\"`).\nGOTCHA: the ms-playwright cache holds browser build 1243 but the repo's playwright 1.58.2 expects 1208, so default `chromium.launch()` fails with \"Executable doesn't exist\"; the repo's own config launches system Chrome — IMPLICATION: launch with `channel: \"chrome\"` + `--enable-unsafe-webgpu` (playwright.config.ts idiom), never the bundled build.\nGOTCHA: system Chrome SIGABRTs at launch in this sandbox (headless and headed alike) — crashpad Mach bootstrap check-in is denied and `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad` is EPERM; a `HOME` override doesn't redirect it — IMPLICATION: no browser-based smoke/playtest is possible this session; validation is lint + typecheck + Vite transform (all four new files serve 200) plus a user manual playtest on :5182.\nGOTCHA: `physicsRaycast` returns only the first (closest) hit, and the character controller's capsule shape is private with default filter `~0/~0` — no `membership`/`collideWith` mask can exclude the player's own capsule from a bullet raycast — IMPLICATION: with the eye at capsule height the player capsule occludes every terrain hit; the eye must sit above the capsule top (~center + 1.0) so forward rays clear it — the `hitDistance > 2` guard alone is not sufficient.\nGOTCHA: `PhysicsCharacterController.getPosition()` returns the capsule **center** (shape is built centered on the node: pointA +h/2−r, pointB −h/2+r), not the feet — IMPLICATION: eye/spawn/respawn heights are relative to center (feet = center − 0.9); current `EYE_HEIGHT = 1.5` puts the eye 0.6 above the head and must drop to ~1.0.\nGOTCHA: `scene18.html`'s canvas has fixed `width=1280 height=720` attributes while CSS stretches it to 100vw/100vh, and `positionPx` is in CSS pixels (scene180:82) — IMPLICATION: screen-space HUD positions must use `window.innerWidth/innerHeight`, not `canvas.width/height` (crosshair already fixed this way).\nGOTCHA: my `rayVsCapsule` draft had a wrong `u` formula (missing a `/hh` in the first term — derived correctly as `(wy − d.y·c)/(hh(1−d.y²))`) and returned `null` for end-cap hits — IMPLICATION: rewritten with the cylindrical-band solution plus sphere tests for both caps; center shots and top/bottom shots now register.","timings":{"cache_n":105216,"draft_n":11529,"draft_n_accepted":3779,"predicted_ms":169850.0,"predicted_n":5426,"prompt_ms":870.0,"prompt_n":136},"to_request":82054,"usage":{"cached_tokens":105216,"completion_tokens":5426,"prompt_tokens":105352}}
