 doesn't match). So verification is lint + typecheck + user manual playtest. This is a significant operational discovery.\n\nLet me focus on the most important ones that are genuinely \"different from what I expected\" and actionable. The user wants discoveries from this step.\n\nLet me enumerate the ones that are genuine gotchas (things that are true and require different behavior):\n\n1. Character controller's `getPosition()` returns the capsule center (not the feet) — the capsule spans center ± capsuleHeight/2. IMPLICATION: EYE_HEIGHT must be an offset from the center (use ~0.7 to be near the head), and spawn/respawn Y should account for center-based positioning.\n\n2. The character controller's capsule shape is private and no collision filter is set at creation — so the player capsule can't be excluded from `physicsRaycast` via layer masking, and `physicsRaycast` returns only the closest hit. IMPLICATION: the bullet ray must originate from a muzzle offset outside the capsule (0.8 in front of the eye), otherwise the player's own body occludes every terrain hit.\n\n3. Text layer `positionPx` is in CSS pixels, not canvas backing-store pixels — the canvas has fixed 1280×720 attributes but is stretched to 100vw/100vh by CSS. IMPLICATION: center the crosshair with `window.innerWidth/innerHeight`, not `canvas.width/height`.\n\n4. `setThinInstances` marks the whole matrix buffer dirty and bumps the version — no separate flush is needed, and per-frame calls are safe. (This resolves an open question, minor.)\n\n5. Browser automation (Playwright/Chrome) can't launch in this sandbox — crashpad Mach bootstrap is denied and the cached browser build doesn't match. IMPLICATION: runtime verification has to be done via lint + typecheck + user manual playtest on :5182, not via scripted browser tests.\n\nLet me reconsider #4 — is it a gotcha? It's more of a confirmation that resolves an open question. I'll include it but note it's a confirmation. Actually, the user is asking for \"