e, so the player capsule can't be excluded via filtering. Let me state that without overclaiming the exact default value. Actually, I can say the implication holds regardless of the exact default: because the shape is private and unfiltered, we can't guarantee exclusion via a mask, so we use a muzzle offset.\n\nHmm, but actually — if the default membership were `0` (no bits), then a raycast with `collideWith = TERRAIN_LAYER` would not hit the player capsule (since `0 & TERRAIN_LAYER = 0`). In that case, filtering would work. So the exact default matters. I inferred `~0` but didn't verify. Let me be honest: I didn't verify the exact default filter value, so I can't be sure filtering would exclude the player. The safe approach (muzzle offset) works regardless. Let me note this uncertainty.\n\nActually, I realize I should be careful not to overstate. Let me frame the gotcha as: the controller's capsule shape is private and created without any explicit collision filter, so I can't reliably exclude the player's own capsule from the bullet raycast via layer masking — hence the muzzle offset. That's accurate.\n\nLet me finalize the list. I'll keep it to the genuinely useful discoveries from this step.\n\nI think the main ones are:\n1. Character controller position = capsule center (spans ±h/2), not feet.\n2. Player capsule can't be raycast-filtered (private shape, no explicit filter) + raycast returns only closest hit → need muzzle offset.\n3. Text positionPx is in CSS pixels, not canvas pixels → crosshair uses window.innerWidth/innerHeight.\n4. Browser automation is blocked in the sandbox → verify via lint/typecheck/manual playtest.\n\nI'll present these. Let me keep each on its own line in the requested format.\n\nI should be concise. Let me write them out.\n","seq":86319,"t":4363509,"text":"\n\nGOTCHA: `PhysicsCharacterController.getPosition()` returns the capsule **center**, not the feet — the capsule spans `center ± capsuleHeight/2` (confirmed from the constructor: shape built symmetric about the origin, `_position`/`_node.position` is the center) — IMPLICATION: `EYE_HEIGHT` is an offset from center, so a realistic eye is ~0.7 (near the head), and my original 1.5 placed the camera 0.6 above the head; spawn/respawn Y must also be center-based.\n\nGOTCHA: the character controller's capsule shape is private and created with **no explicit collision filter**, and `physicsRaycast` returns only the *closest* hit — so the player's own capsule can't be excluded via layer masking and would occlude every terrain hit — IMPLICATION: the bullet ray must originate from a muzzle offset (~0.8 in front of the eye, outside the 0.5 capsule radius), not from the eye.\n\nGOTCHA: text-layer `positionPx` is in **CSS pixels**, not canvas backing-store pixels — the canvas has fixed `width=1280 height=720` attributes but CSS stretches it to `100vw/100vh` (scene180:82 confirms the units) — IMPLICATION: center the crosshair with `window.innerWidth/innerHeight`, not `canvas.width/height`.\n\nGOTCHA: `setThinInstances` bumps `_version` and marks the whole matrix buffer dirty on each call — no separate flush needed, per-frame calls are safe — IMPLICATION: the open question on per-frame bot/debris matrix updates is resolved; just call it each frame.\n\nGOTCHA: browser automation (Playwright/Chrome) cannot launch in this sandbox — crashpad Mach bootstrap is denied and the cached browser build doesn't match the repo's Playwright — IMPLICATION: runtime verification must be lint + typecheck + a manual playtest on :5182, not a scripted browser smoke test.","timings":{"cache_n":112640,"draft_n":5670,"draft_n_accepted":1918,"predicted_ms":73770.0,"predicted_n":2728,"prompt_ms":1020.0,"prompt_n":210},"to_request":85233,"usage":{"cached_tokens":112640,"completion_tokens":2728,"prompt_tokens":112850}}
