t...\" + read scene252 52-65\n41. Me: edit EYE_HEIGHT 1.5→0.7 + MUZZLE_OFFSET\n42. Me: read scene252 300-317\n43. Me: read scene252 280-309\n44. Me: edit tryFire muzzle offset\n45. Me: \"Let me check the initial player spawn...\" + grep\n46. Me: edit player spawn\n47. Me: edit respawnPlayer\n48. Me: \"Now let me run lint + typecheck...\" + bash lint → passed\n49. Me: \"Lint + typecheck pass. Let me confirm the dev server...\" + curl → 200 but MUZZLE 0\n50. Me: curl grep → stale (EYE_HEIGHT 1.5)\n51. Me: \"The disk file is correct... restart it\" + task_stop bg_a3fd11f4\n52. Me: bash vite background → bg_f4a1f424\n\nSo \"the step you just completed\" — the user is asking about the most recent step. The most recent work was the static review + fixes + lint + dev server restart.\n\nActually, the user's question \"In the step you just completed\" probably refers to the whole recent stretch of work (the static review and fixes). Let me list the discoveries from that work:\n\n1. **`getPosition()` returns the capsule center, not the feet** — the character controller's position is the capsule center; the shape spans center ± halfH. Implication: eye height is an offset from the center (about 0.7), and spawn/respawn Y = terrainHeight + CAP_HEIGHT/2. This changed my EYE_HEIGHT from 1.5 to 0.7 and the spawn from +2 to +CAP_HEIGHT/2.\n\n2. **The player's capsule cannot be filter-excluded from raycasts** — the controller's `_shape` is private, and its default filter membership is `~0` (all layers), so `physicsRaycast` (with any `membership`/`collideWith`) will still hit the player's own capsule. Implication: cast bullet rays from a muzzle offset (0.8 in front of the eye, outside the 0.5 capsule radius) so the ray never starts inside the player's body; otherwise the player's capsule occludes all terrain hits.\n\n3. **The Vite dev server serves stale transforms in this sandbox** — the long-running background vite server kept serving old module content after I edited the file on disk (the file watcher didn't fire). Implication: restart the dev server after code changes (or don't trust that the running server reflects the latest edits) before playtesting.\n\n4. **`setThinInstances` re-uploads via versioning, no separate flush needed** — it bumps `_version` and sets the dirty range, so the buffer is re-uploaded on draw. Implication: per-frame `setThinInstances` calls are fine, no `flushThinInstances` needed. (This resolves an open item.)\n\nWait, is #4 a \"discovery\" or just confirmation? It resolves an open question. It's a discovery about how the API works (versioning, not a separate flush). I'll include it.\n\n5. **`updateDefaultTextData` mutates the TextData in place** — confirmed. This is more confirmation than discovery. Probably skip, or include briefly.\n\n6. **Chrome/Playwright cannot launch in this sandbox** — but that was discovered in the Playwright attempts, which were part of this same post-compaction stretch. Actually, those attempts (SIGABRT) happened in this step too (steps 1-13 above). So it is a discovery from this step. But it was already recorded in the working set (r65273). Hmm. The user says \"Only discoveries from this step.\" The Playwright SIGABRT attempts were in this step (post-compaction). But the working set already has r65273 which says browser automation is blocked. So it's a re-confirmation, not new. I'll skip it since it's already recorded, or mention it briefly. Actually, the user is asking about discoveries that \"behaved differently than expected.\" The Playwright attempts did behave as the working set predicted (blocked). So it's not a surprise. I'll skip.\n\nLet me focus on the genuine new discoveries from the static review + fixes:\n\n1. getPosition() = capsule center (not feet) → eye/spawn offsets are relative to center.\n2. Player capsule can't be filter-excluded (private shape, default membership ~0) → muzzle offset required.\n3. Vite dev server serves stale transforms (watcher doesn't fire in sandbox) → restart after edits.\n4. setThinInstances uses versioning (no flush needed) → per-frame calls are fine.\n\nActually, let me reconsider #1. Was it really \"different than expected\"? I had EYE_HEIGHT = 1.5, assuming it was above the feet or something. The discovery that it's relative to the center changed my understanding. Yes, it's a discovery.\n\nLet me also reconsider: did I discover anything about `checkSupport` or `moveWithCollisions`? No, those were already known.\n\nLet me also reconsider the rayVsCapsule bug — that was my own code bug, not an API discovery. The user is asking about APIs that \"work another way,\" errors and their causes, limitations. My own code bug isn't an API discovery. So I won't list it as a GOTCHA (it's just a bug I fixed). Actually, the user said \"an API that works another way, an error and its actual cause, a limitation or unsupported feature you discovered.\" My own code bug doesn't fit. I'll skip it.\n\nLet me finalize the list. I'll list the genuine API/operational discoveries:\n\nGOTCHA: `PhysicsCharacterController.getPosition()` returns the capsule center (the shape spans center ± capsuleHeight/2), not the feet — IMPLICATION: eye height and spawn/respawn Y must be offsets from the center (eye ≈ center + 0.7; spawn = terrainHeight + capsuleHeight/2), not from the ground.\n\nGOTCHA: the character controller's capsule shape is private (`_shape`) and its default filter membership is `~0` (belongs to every layer), so `physicsRaycast` cannot be filtered to exclude the player's own capsule — IMPLICATION: bullet rays must be cast from a muzzle offset in front of the eye (outside the capsule radius) or the player's capsule occludes every terrain hit.\n\nGOTCHA: the long-running Vite dev server serves stale module transforms in this sandbox (its file watcher does not fire on edits) — IMPLICATION: restart the dev server after code changes before playtesting, or verify served content matches disk.\n\nGOTCHA: `setThinInstances` re-uploads via an internal `_version` bump + dirty range (no separate flush call) — IMPLICATION: per-frame `setThinInstances` calls are safe and sufficient for bot/debris matrices; no `flushThinInstances` needed.\n\nThat's a good list. Let me double-check each is from this step:\n- #1: Yes, discovered when I read character-controller.ts in this step.\n- #2: Yes, discovered when I checked the filter masks and createPhysicsShape in this step.\n- #3: Yes, discovered when curl showed stale content in this step.\n- #4: Yes, discovered when I grepped setThinInstances in this step.\n\nAll four are from this step. Good.\n\nLet me write them concisely.\n","seq":89553,"t":4574184,"text":"\n\nGOTCHA: `PhysicsCharacterController.getPosition()` returns the capsule **center** (shape spans center ± capsuleHeight/2), not the feet — IMPLICATION: eye height and spawn/respawn Y are offsets from the center (eye ≈ center + 0.7; spawn = terrainHeight + capsuleHeight/2), not from the ground plane.\n\nGOTCHA: the character controller's capsule shape is private (`_shape`) and its default filter membership is `~0` (belongs to every layer), so `physicsRaycast` cannot be filtered to exclude the player's own capsule — IMPLICATION: bullet rays must be cast from a muzzle offset in front of the eye (outside the 0.5 capsule radius) or the player's capsule occludes every terrain hit.\n\nGOTCHA: the long-running Vite dev server serves stale module transforms in this sandbox (its file watcher does not fire on disk edits) — IMPLICATION: restart the dev server after code changes before playtesting, or verify served content matches disk.\n\nGOTCHA: `setThinInstances` re-uploads via an internal `_version` bump + dirty range (no separate flush call) — IMPLICATION: per-frame `setThinInstances` calls are safe and sufficient for bot/debris matrices; no `flushThinInstances` needed.","timings":{"cache_n":119296,"draft_n":6846,"draft_n_accepted":2519,"predicted_ms":105010.0,"predicted_n":3497,"prompt_ms":890.0,"prompt_n":