{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Let me reflect on the decisions made in this step (my last message and tool activity).\n\nWhat I did in this step:\n1. Rewrote `rayVsCapsule` — found a bug in the `u` formula, added end-cap handling.\n2. Fixed the player/bot velocity reset on landing (contact detection).\n3. Fixed the crosshair position (window.innerWidth/innerHeight vs canvas.width).\n4. Changed `Debris.body` to `PhysicsBody | null` and cleaned up the cast.\n5. Added the self-hit guard, then replaced it with a muzzle offset approach.\n6. Changed EYE_HEIGHT from 1.5 to 0.7, added MUZZLE_OFFSET.\n7. Fixed the spawn height to standing level.\n8. Ran lint + typecheck (passed).\n9. Restarted the dev server (the old one was serving stale transforms).\n\nLet me list the decisions from this step:\n\n1. DECISION: Rewrote `rayVsCapsule` with the standard cylindrical band + end-cap sphere approach — WHY: the original `u` formula was wrong (returned null for valid center hits) and it missed end-cap hits.\n\n2. DECISION: Reset vertical velocity to 0 on floor contact (measured by comparing actual vs requested drop) — WHY: otherwise fall speed accumulates every step while standing, causing terminal-velocity-like falls when walking off ledges.\n\n3. DECISION: Crosshair positioned via `window.innerWidth/innerHeight` (CSS pixels) rather than `canvas.width/height` — WHY: the canvas has fixed 1280×720 attributes but CSS stretches it to the viewport, and `positionPx` is in CSS pixels (per scene180:82).\n\n4. DECISION: Bullet raycasts originate from a muzzle offset (0.8 units in front of the eye) rather than the eye — WHY: the player's capsule has a default filter (~0) and a private shape that can't be filter-masked, so a ray from inside the capsule would be occluded by the player's own body.\n\n5. DECISION: EYE_HEIGHT = 0.7 (near the head, above the capsule center) — WHY: realistic first-person eye height; combined with the muzzle offset, forward rays clear the player capsule.\n\n6. DECISION: Spawn/respawn at standing height (`terrainHeight + CAP_HEIGHT/2 + 0.1`) rather than 2 units above — WHY: the capsule center should be at feet + half-height so the feet are on the ground.\n\n7. DECISION: `Debris.body` typed as `PhysicsBody | null` — WHY: cleaner than the `null as unknown as PhysicsBody` cast, with proper null guards.\n\n8. DECISION: Restarted the dev server — WHY: the long-running server's file watcher wasn't picking up changes in the sandbox, serving stale transforms.\n\nLet me focus on the decisions about how the project is built (API choices, conventions, structure, tooling, workarounds). The reflection asks specifically about decisions about how the project is built.\n\nLet me list the meaningful ones:\n- Muzzle offset for bullet raycasts (workaround for the private controller shape / default filter).\n- EYE_HEIGHT = 0.7 (API/structure choice).\n- rayVsCapsule rewrite (math fix).\n- Velocity reset on landing (game mechanics).\n- Crosshair via window dimensions (convention).\n- Spawn at standing height.\n- Dev server restart (tooling workaround).\n\nLet me write these out concisely.\n","seq":89869,"t":4595044,"text":"\n\nDECISION: Bullet raycasts originate from a muzzle offset (0.8u in front of the eye) instead of the eye — WHY: the player's capsule has a default `~0` filter and a private shape that can't be filter-masked, so a ray starting inside the capsule would be occluded by the player's own body.\nDECISION: `EYE_HEIGHT = 0.7` (near the head, above the capsule center) — WHY: realistic first-person eye height; with the muzzle offset, forward rays clear the player capsule.\nDECISION: Rewrote `rayVsCapsule` as cylindrical-band + end-cap sphere tests — WHY: the original `u` (axis-parameter) formula was wrong and returned null for valid center hits, and it missed end-cap hits.\nDECISION: Reset vertical velocity to 0 on floor contact (actual-drop vs requested-drop test) for both player and bots — WHY: otherwise fall speed accumulates every step while standing, so walking off a ledge starts a terminal-velocity fall.\nDECISION: Crosshair placed via `window.innerWidth/innerHeight` (CSS pixels), not `canvas.width/height` — WHY: the canvas has fixed 1280×720 attributes but CSS stretches it to the viewport, and `positionPx` is in CSS pixels (scene180:82).\nDECISION: Spawn/respawn at standing height (`terrainHeight + CAP_HEIGHT/2 + 0.1`) instead of 2u above — WHY: the controller's `getPosition()` is the capsule center, so feet-on-ground means center = ground + half-height.\nDECISION: `Debris.body` typed `PhysicsBody | null` with explicit null guards — WHY: cleaner than the `null as unknown as PhysicsBody` cast and satisfies the typecheck.\nDECISION: Restarted the lab dev server (bg_f4a1f424) — WHY: the long-running server's file watcher wasn't picking up edits in this sandbox and was serving stale transforms.","timings":{"cache_n":122624,"draft_n":2142,"draft_n_accepted":892,"predicted_ms":19310.0,"predicted_n":1198,"prompt_ms":1100.0,"prompt_n":162},"to_request":89560,"usage":{"cached_tokens":122624,"completion_tokens":1198,"prompt_tokens":122786}}
