{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"In the previous step (the most recent work), what constraints became apparent or were committed to?\n\nWhat happened in the most recent step:\n1. Fixed the bug in rayVsCapsule (rewrote it).\n2. Discovered that the character controller's `getPosition()` returns the center of the capsule.\n3. Discovered that the player's capsule shape is private and has a default filter of `~0` (belongs to all layers), so it can't be excluded via raycast filtering — committed to the muzzle offset approach (ray origin is 0.8 forward from the eye).\n4. EYE_HEIGHT = 0.7 (near the head), MUZZLE_OFFSET = 0.8.\n5. The dev server's file watcher serves stale content in this sandbox — restart required after edits.\n6. Chrome can't be launched inside the sandbox (crashpad's Mach bootstrap is denied) — no browser-based verification possible in this session.\n7. Lint/typecheck gates pass.\n\nConstraints that surfaced in this step:\n- The player capsule can't be excluded from physics raycasts (private shape, default membership is ~0) — the bullet ray must originate from a muzzle offset outside the capsule. This is a design constraint the project must honor (don't try to filter the player capsule out of raycasts).\n- In this sandbox, the vite dev server's file watcher doesn't reliably pick up edits — restart the server after editing scene files before playtesting.\n- Chrome/Playwright can't be launched inside the sandbox (crashpad's Mach bootstrap EPERM) — no browser-based verification possible. Verify via lint/typecheck + user's manual playtest.\n\nWait — the question is asking about constraints that \"the rest of the project must honor.\" Let me focus on the constraints that surfaced in this step (the recent work after compaction).\n\nConstraints from this step:\n1. CONSTRAINT: The character controller's capsule shape is private and has a default filter membership of ~0 (belongs to all layers), so it can't be excluded from physics raycasts via collision layer filtering — the bullet ray must originate from a muzzle offset outside the player capsule (not from the eye).\n2. CONSTRAINT: In this sandbox, the long-running vite dev server serves stale transformed modules (file watcher doesn't fire) — restart the dev server after editing scene files before verifying/playtesting.\n3. CONSTRAINT: Chrome/Playwright can't be launched inside this sandbox (crashpad's Mach bootstrap is denied → SIGABRT) — no browser-based verification possible. Verify via lint/typecheck + user's manual playtest on :5182.\n\nActually, #3 (Chrome can't be launched) was already recorded in a previous step (r65273). But it was reconfirmed in this step. The question says \"only constraints that surfaced in this step.\" Let me be careful — Chrome's SIGABRT was discovered before compaction (in a previous step). But in this step, I reconfirmed that crashpad's Mach bootstrap is the cause. Hmm.\n\nLet me focus on what truly surfaced in this step (post-compaction work):\n- Muzzle offset constraint (player capsule can't be filtered) — new in this step.\n- Stale dev server / file watcher — new in this step (discovered when curl returned EYE_HEIGHT=1.5 even though the disk had 0.7).\n- The EYE_HEIGHT/muzzle design decision.\n\nThe Chrome SIGABRT root cause (crashpad's Mach bootstrap) was actually first discovered in this step — before compaction, I had only gotten as far as \"executable doesn't exist\" and the first SIGABRT. No wait, let me reconsider. The background tasks section and summary indicated Playwright attempts. The crashpad bootstrap error surfaced in this step's output (the `bootstrap_check_in ... Permission denied` and `settings.dat: Operation not permitted` errors). So the root cause (crashpad/Mach bootstrap) was identified in this step. But the constraint \"no browser automation in the sandbox\" was already established.\n\nLet me list the constraints that truly surfaced in this step:\n1. Player capsule can't be excluded from raycasts → muzzle offset.\n2. Stale dev server → restart after edits.\n\nAnd the confirmation of the root cause of Chrome's SIGABRT (crashpad's Mach bootstrap EPERM) — this reinforces the existing constraint, but the specific mechanism is new. Since it's a constraint on the environment, I'll include it as an environment limit.\n\nLet me write these up concisely.\n","seq":90461,"t":4638724,"text":"\n\nCONSTRAINT: The character controller's capsule shape is private and carries Havok's default filter (membership `~0`, i.e. every layer), so it cannot be excluded from `physicsRaycast` via collision-layer masks — bullet rays must originate from a muzzle offset (in front of the eye, outside the capsule radius), never from the eye/center, or the player's own capsule occludes every terrain hit.\nCONSTRAINT: In this sandbox the long-running Vite dev server serves stale transformed modules (its file watcher does not fire on edits) — restart the dev server after editing scene files before verifying or playtesting, or you will test old code.\nCONSTRAINT: Chrome/Playwright cannot launch in this sandbox — crashpad's Mach `bootstrap_check_in` and `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad` are EPERM, so the browser SIGABRTs at start (headless and headed, regardless of `TMPDIR`/`HOME` overrides) — no browser-based verification is possible here; validate via lint/typecheck plus a user manual playtest on :5182.","timings":{"cache_n":122624,"draft_n":2737,"draft_n_accepted":811,"predicted_ms":42200.0,"predicted_n":1202,"prompt_ms":980.0,"prompt_n":139},"to_request":89880,"usage":{"cached_tokens":122624,"completion_tokens":1202,"prompt_tokens":122763}}
