{"entry":{"id":"r91558/call_1569cb1f591a4fe682afe311/decision","text":"Self-hit problem solved via muzzle offset, not layer filtering: the character controller's capsule shape is private (can't call setPhysicsShapeFilterMembershipMask on it) and its default membership is ~0 (belongs to every layer), so a physicsRaycast can never be filtered to exclude the player's own capsule. Fix: cast the bullet ray from a point MUZZLE_OFFSET (0.8) in front of the eye (outside the 0.5 capsule radius) so the ray never starts inside the player body. EYE_HEIGHT set to 0.7 (eye near head, center+0.7)."},"kind":"patch","lane":"self-capture","op":"add","seq":91780,"t":4726186}
{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"Self-hit problem solved via muzzle offset, not layer filtering: the character controller's capsule shape is private (can't call setPhysicsShapeFilterMembershipMask on it) and its default membership is ~0 (belongs to every layer), so a physicsRaycast can never be filtered to exclude the player's own capsule. Fix: cast the bullet ray from a point MUZZLE_OFFSET (0.8) in front of the eye (outside the 0.5 capsule radius) so the ray never starts inside the player body. EYE_HEIGHT set to 0.7 (eye near head, center+0.7).\", \"field\": \"decision\"}","id":"call_1569cb1f591a4fe682afe311","kind":"tool_call","name":"update_record","outcome":"ran","request":91558,"seq":91781,"shown":"recorded: r91558/call_1569cb1f591a4fe682afe311/decision","t":4726186,"turn":6}
