HT_BROWSERS_PATH` within the repo) or verify the scene by non-browser means.\ninterview-t6-f63754-0\tgotcha: `computeNormals` takes/returns plain `number[]`, not typed arrays (mesh/compute-normals.ts) — IMPLICATION: wrap with `Array.from(...)` and convert the result back to `Float32Array` at both call sites in fps-terrain.ts.\ninterview-t6-f63754-1\tgotcha: `createFlatGroundData` and `computeNormals` are NOT in the `babylon-lite` barrel — IMPLICATION: lab scenes import them via subpath (`babylon-lite/mesh/create-ground.js`, `babylon-lite/mesh/compute-normals.js`), the same idiom scene114/scene17 use.\ninterview-t6-f63754-2\tgotcha: `pnpm dev:lab` fails in this sandbox — the script's `tsx scripts/build-bundle-scenes.ts` step EPERMs on an IPC pipe in the system temp dir — IMPLICATION: start the lab with `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite` from `lab/` directly (skips the bundle build, which a dev playtest doesn't need).\ninterview-t6-f63754-3\tgotcha: the sandbox blocks writes to `/tmp` and the system temp dir (`/var/folders/.../T`) — IMPLICATION: scratch files must live inside the repo (delete before commit per GUIDANCE 0b), and node/Playwright need `TMPDIR` pointed at a repo-local dir.\ninterview-t6-f63754-4\tgotcha: the cached Playwright browsers (build 1243) don't match the repo's playwright 1.58.2 (expects 1208), so default `chromium.launch()` fails with \"Executable doesn't exist\" — IMPLICATION: launch with `channel: \"chrome\"` (system Chrome), which is the repo's own idiom (playwright.config.ts), plus `--enable-unsafe-webgpu` for WebGPU.\ninterview-t6-f63754-5\tgotcha: the plan's \"uploadMeshToGPU rebuild\" seam is actually `resizeMeshGeometry` (mesh-factories.ts) — raw `uploadMeshToGPU` + manual `_gpu` swap would skip the `_renderableVersion` bump that cached draw bundles key off — IMPLICATION: tile destruction must call `resizeMeshGeometry(engine, mesh, positions, normals, indices, uvs)`; it also refreshes `_cpuIndices` for the next surgery.\ninterview-t6-f63754-6\tgotcha: FreeCamera's world matrix is built from `position` + `target` (mat4LookAtLH), not from `_yaw`/`_pitch` (those are only used by `attachFreeControl`) — IMPLICATION: the FPS camera is driven by setting `cam.position` and `cam.target` each frame from eye + (yaw, pitch); don't poke `_yaw`/`_pitch`.\ninterview-t6-f63754-7\tgotcha: NavCrowd has no agent reposition API (only `agentGoto` destinations) — IMPLICATION: nav agents drift from collision-driven controllers; mitigate by re-targeting the agent to the bot's position when they separate >4u, else bots oscillate.\ninterview-t6-f63754-8\tgotcha: `pnpm run lint` = eslint + three `tsc --noEmit` projects (packages, lab, tests) and flags unused type imports (TS6196) — IMPLICATION: `import type` lists must be pruned to exactly what's used; lint is the full typecheck gate, no separate step needed.\ninterview-t6-f66113-0\tgotcha: `pnpm dev:lab` starts with `tsx scripts/build-bundle-scenes.ts && tsx scripts/build-bundle-demos.ts`, which die in this sandboxed session with EPERM (tsx IPC pipe in `/var/folders/.../T` is blocked) — IMPLICATION: start the lab directly with `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite` from `lab/` (the bundle-build prefix is not needed for dev playtest; vite config still honors `LAB_DEV_PORT`).\ninterview-t6-f66113-1\tgotcha: no browser can be launched from inside this sandbox — Chrome aborts (SIGABRT) because crashpad's Mach `bootstrap_check_in` is denied (1100) and `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad` is unreadable; `HOME`/`TMPDIR` overrides don't help — IMPLICATION: S8's browser playtest cannot be run from here; in-sandbox validation is limited to lint/tsc + dev-server module transforms, and the real playtest must be done by the user (or a non-sandboxed shell).\ninterview-t6-f66113-2\tgotcha: the repo's Playwright (1.58.2) expects bundled chromium build 1208, but the cache only has 1243 — the repo's own configs sidestep this with `channel: \"chrome\"` (system Chrome) plus `--en