{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Let me reflect on the step I just completed. The last message was recording a decision about the muzzle offset solution. But the question asks about decisions made, confirmed, or changed in \"the step you just completed (your last message and its tool activity).\"\n\nWait, let me re-read. The last thing I did was a series of edits and then a `update_record` call. The \"step\" here likely refers to the whole build work I just did (the reflection is being asked after I completed the build and was recording findings).\n\nActually, the question is specifically about \"your last message and its tool activity.\" My last message was the `update_record` call recording the muzzle offset decision. But that's just recording something I already decided.\n\nHmm, but I think the intent is to reflect on the build work I just completed in this turn — all the decisions I made while fixing bugs and completing the scene. Let me list the decisions I made in this session's work:\n\n1. **Muzzle offset for self-hits** — I decided to cast the bullet ray from a point in front of the eye (MUZZLE_OFFSET = 0.8) rather than trying to filter out the player's capsule, because the controller's capsule shape is private and its default membership is ~0 (can't be layer-filtered).\n\n2. **EYE_HEIGHT = 0.7** — I set the eye height to 0.7 above the capsule center (near the head) for a realistic first-person camera, combined with the muzzle offset to avoid self-hits.\n\n3. **Rewrote rayVsCapsule** — I replaced the buggy u-formula (which returned null for valid center hits) with a clean cylindrical-band + end-cap (sphere) approach, because the original missed valid hits and end-cap hits.\n\n4. **Velocity reset on floor contact** — I added a check that zeroes playerVel.y / bot.velY when the actual drop is less than half the requested drop (floor contact), because otherwise fall speed accumulates unboundedly while standing.\n\n5. **Terminal velocity clamp (-30)** — I clamped vertical velocity to -30 to prevent unbounded fall speed.\n\n6. **Crosshair in CSS pixels** — I changed the crosshair position from canvas.width/height (fixed 1280×720 attrs) to window.innerWidth/innerHeight, because positionPx is in CSS pixels and the canvas is stretched to 100vw/100vh.\n\n7. **Bot quaternion fix** — I fixed the bot display quaternion to (0, sin(h/2), 0, cos(h/2)) for a Y-axis heading rotation, because the original had cos in the qz slot and 0 in qw (a 180° rotation about a tilted axis).\n\n8. **Debris.body typed as PhysicsBody | null** — I changed the type and removed the `null as unknown as PhysicsBody` cast, adding null guards, for type correctness.\n\n9. **Spawn at standing height** — I changed player spawn from +2 (floating) to +CAP_HEIGHT/2 + 0.1 (feet on ground), so the player starts at standing level.\n\n10. **Restarted dev server** — I stopped the stale dev server and started a fresh one, because the file watcher wasn't picking up my edits (serving stale transforms).\n\nNow, the question is which of these are \"decisions about how this project is built — an API choice, a convention, a structure, a tooling choice, a workaround.\"\n\nLet me filter to the meaningful ones:\n- Muzzle offset (workaround/API choice) — YES\n- EYE_HEIGHT = 0.7 (a tuning choice, but part of the muzzle offset decision) — arguably\n- rayVsCapsule rewrite (a correctness fix, not really a \"build decision\") — it's a fix, but it's a structural choice about how to do the math\n- Velocity reset + terminal clamp (gameplay physics decisions) — YES, these are design decisions\n- Crosshair CSS pixels (a convention/correctness) — YES\n- Bot quaternion (a fix) — it's a fix\n- Debris.body null type (a type correctness) — minor\n- Spawn height (a tuning) — minor\n- Dev server restart (a tooling choice) — YES, this is a tooling/workaround decision\n\nLet me focus on the ones that are genuinely decisions about how the project is built. The most important:\n\n