ly \"about how this project is built.\" The bug fixes (rayVsCapsule, bot quaternion) are correctness fixes, not build decisions — but they do involve approach choices. I'll include the rayVsCapsule rewrite since it's a structural decision about the math approach, but I'll keep it brief.\n\nLet me write the answer concisely, one per line.\n\nActually, re-reading the prompt: \"Did you make, confirm, or change any decision about how this project is built — an API choice, a convention, a structure, a tooling choice, a workaround? List each on its own line.\"\n\nI'll list the meaningful decisions from this step. Let me be judicious:\n\nDECISION: Bullet ray is cast from a muzzle point (0.8 in front of the eye), not the eye — WHY: the player's capsule shape is private and default-membership ~0, so it can't be layer-filtered out of the raycast; starting outside the capsule avoids self-hits.\nDECISION: Eye height set to 0.7 above capsule center — WHY: realistic first-person camera near the head, paired with the muzzle offset.\nDECISION: rayVsCapsule rewritten as cylindrical-band + two end-cap sphere tests — WHY: the original u-formula was wrong (missed valid center hits) and ignored end caps.\nDECISION: player/bot vertical velocity zeroed on floor contact and clamped to -30 — WHY: without it, fall speed accumulates unboundedly while standing.\nDECISION: crosshair positioned via window.innerWidth/innerHeight, not canvas.width/height — WHY: TextLayer positionPx is in CSS pixels and the canvas is stretched to 100vw/100vh (fixed 1280×720 attrs).\nDECISION: bot display quaternion corrected to (0, sin(h/2), 0, cos(h/2)) — WHY: the original put cos in qz and 0 in qw, a 180° rotation about a tilted axis instead of a Y-heading.\nDECISION: Debris.body typed PhysicsBody | null with null guards — WHY: the `null as unknown as PhysicsBody` cast was a type-unsound hack.\nDECISION: player spawns at standing height (terrain + CAP_HEIGHT/2 + 0.1), not +2 — WHY: +2 left the player floating 1.1