{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Let me look back on the steps I just completed. What did I actually do in this turn?\n\n1. Edited `tryFire` to use the muzzle offset, and removed the `> 2` self-hit guard.\n2. Fixed the player's spawn height (from `+ 2` to `+ CAP_HEIGHT/2 + 0.1`).\n3. Ran lint + typecheck — passed.\n4. Discovered that the dev server was serving a stale transform (EYE_HEIGHT 1.5 on disk, but the old 1.5 being served) — restarted the dev server.\n5. Fixed the bot's quaternion bug (qz/qw were swapped).\n6. Verified font existence, HTML page, helper files.\n7. Resolved the working set entry.\n\nThe question is asking about discoveries from \"this step\" — meaning the most recent work. Let me think about what I actually discovered versus what I expected:\n\n1. **The long-running vite dev server was serving a stale transform** — I expected HMR/watcher to pick up the edits, but it was serving old code (EYE_HEIGHT 1.5 vs. the 0.7 on disk). This is a genuine surprise. Already recorded as gotcha r91869.\n\n2. **The bot's quaternion bug** — this was my own bug that I found and fixed. Strictly speaking, it's not an \"API behaves differently\" discovery, but a self-inflicted bug. That said, it does reveal that `mat4Compose` takes (qx, qy, qz, qw) in that order, and I had them wrong. This is more of a \"I made a mistake\" than a \"the API surprised me.\"\n\n3. **The player capsule can't be excluded via filter mask** — I discovered/confirmed that the character controller's capsule shape is private and has a default membership of ~0, so it can't be excluded from physicsRaycast via a layer mask. This is a genuine discovery. Already recorded as decision r91558.\n\nWait, but that was something I'd already recorded in a previous turn. Let me focus on what happened in this specific step/turn.\n\nIn this turn, the actual discoveries were:\n- The dev server's file watcher was serving stale content (a surprise — I expected HMR to work).\n- The bot's quaternion argument order (my own bug, fixed).\n\nLet me reconsider — the question says \"an API that behaves differently, an error and its actual cause, a limitation or unsupported feature you discovered.\"\n\nThe stale dev server thing is the main one. I expected the vite dev server to hot-reload/re-transform after I edited the file, but it kept serving the old transform. The actual cause: in this sandbox, the file watcher doesn't fire on disk edits. So the implication is: restart the dev server after editing.\n\nAre there any others? Let me think about the lint run — that passed cleanly, no surprises.\n\nThe muzzle offset edit — no surprises, it compiled.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the bot's quaternion. I had assumed the quaternion arguments were in some order, but `mat4Compose` is (tx, ty, tz, qx, qy, qz, qw, sx, sy, sz). I had placed cos(h/2) in the qz slot and 0 in qw. The correct Y-axis rotation is (0, sin(h/2), 0, cos(h/2)). So I had qz and qw swapped. This is a self-inflicted bug, but it does reveal the argument order of the API. But I caught it myself by reading the signature, so it's not really a \"discovery\" in the sense of the API surprising me — I was just being careful.\n\nI think the main genuine discovery from this step is the stale dev server. Let me report that.\n\nActually, let me reconsider once more. The instructions say \"only discoveries from this step.\" This step = the turn I just completed. Let me be precise about what happened:\n\n1. Edited tryFire (muzzle offset) — no surprises.\n2. Fixed spawn height — no surprises.\n3. Ran lint — passed, no surprises.\n4. curl'd the dev server — **surprise**: it was serving EYE_HEIGHT 1.5 (stale) when the disk had 0.7.\n5. Restarted the dev server — the new server served the latest.\n6. Read the physics/render sections — found the bot's quaternion bug (my own).\n7. Fixed the quaternion — no surprises.\n8. Ran lint again — passed.\n9. Verified the font, HTML, helper files — all fine.\n\nSo the genuine \"discovery\" is the stale dev server. The quaternion was my own bug that I caught by reading the signature — I could list it, but it's more of a self-correction than an API surprise. That said, it does reveal the argument order of mat4Compose, which I could misremember. But I already knew the signature (I read it). So it's not a discovery.\n\nLet me report the stale dev server as the main gotcha. I'll also note that it's already been recorded.\n\nActually, the question is asking me to list discoveries so they can be recorded. The stale dev server one is already recorded (r91869). But I should still report it since it's a genuine discovery from this step. Let me report it.\n\nAre there any others? Let me think really carefully about whether anything else behaved unexpectedly.\n\n- The `pnpm run lint` command passed on the first try. No surprises.\n- `curl` on the new server worked. No surprises.\n- The font file exists. No surprises.\n\nI think the only genuine discovery is the stale dev server. Let me report that.\n\nWait — one more. When I first curl'd the dev server after editing, the transform didn't have MUZZLE_OFFSET. I attributed this to the stale watcher. But let me double-check: was the server actually serving stale content, or was there some other cause? The disk file had MUZZLE_OFFSET (I verified with grep), but the served transform didn't. So yes, the server was serving stale content. That confirms the watcher issue.\n\nOK, let me report the stale dev server gotcha. I'll note that it's already been recorded, but I'll list it since it's a discovery from this step.\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether I should report anything else. The bot's quaternion — I want to be honest. I made an error in the original code (from a previous turn), and in this step I caught it by reading the mat4Compose signature. The \"discovery\" is that mat4Compose's argument order is (tx,ty,tz,qx,qy,qz,qw,sx,sy,sz), and the Y-rotation quaternion is (0, sin(h/2), 0, cos(h/2)). But since I read the signature to confirm, it's not really a surprise — I was just verifying. I'll mention it as a minor point, but the main one is the dev server.\n\nLet me be concise and report the main discovery.\n","seq":94805,"t":5048292,"text":"\n\nGOTCHA: the long-running vite dev server was serving a stale transform after I edited the file on disk (disk had `EYE_HEIGHT = 0.7` + `MUZZLE_OFFSET`, but the served module still showed `EYE_HEIGHT = 1.5` and no `MUZZLE_OFFSET`) — its file watcher doesn't fire on edits in this sandbox — IMPLICATION: after editing scene files, restart the dev server (`task_stop` + relaunch `cd lab && LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite`) or verify served content via curl before playtesting; don't assume HMR picked up the change. (Already recorded as r91869.)\n\nGOTCHA: `mat4Compose(tx, ty, tz, qx, qy, qz, qw, sx, sy, sz)` — a Y-axis heading rotation is `(0, sin(h/2), 0, cos(h/2))`; my first draft put `cos(h/2)` in the `qz` slot and `0` in `qw`, which is a 180° rotation about a tilted axis, not a heading — IMPLICATION: keep the quaternion as `(0, sin(h/2), 0, cos(h/2))` for bot heading; the capsule is radially symmetric so it doesn't change the look, but it matters if the display ever becomes asymmetric.","timings":{"cache_n":65792,"draft_n":3829,"draft_n_accepted":1285,"predicted_ms":43990.0,"predicted_n":1832,"prompt_ms":1150.0,"prompt_n":598},"to_request":93898,"usage":{"cached_tokens":65792,"completion_tokens":1832,"prompt_tokens":66390}}
