 me think about what's genuinely a constraint the rest of the project must honor:\n\n- The muzzle offset rule: any future shooting/raycasting near the player must originate outside the player capsule, never from the eye/center, because the capsule can't be filter-masked. This is a real constraint for the rest of the project (e.g., if multiplayer is added later, or if bot shooting is added).\n\n- The browser-blocked rule: no browser-based verification is possible in this sandbox; validation must be lint/typecheck/dev-server + user manual playtest. This is an environment limit for the rest of the project.\n\n- The dev-server-watcher rule: after editing scene files, restart the dev server (or verify via curl) before assuming HMR worked. Environment limit.\n\n- The scene252-not-parity rule: scene252 must never be added to scene-config.json, bundle-size.spec.ts, or golden references (it's a game demo). Project rule.\n\nLet me list these. I should be careful to only list constraints surfaced in THIS step. Let me reconsider each:\n\n1. Browser automation blocked — YES, surfaced in this step (I confirmed Chrome SIGABRTs and stated validation is limited).\n2. Dev server watcher stale — YES, surfaced in this step (I restarted the server because it served stale EYE_HEIGHT 1.5).\n3. Controller capsule can't be filter-masked → muzzle offset — YES, committed in this step (the muzzle offset fix).\n4. getPosition() returns center not feet — YES, committed in this step (the spawn height fix).\n5. scene252 not a parity scene — this was decided in an earlier step (interview-t4-f13394-1), but I re-verified it in this step. It's a standing constraint. I'll include it since I committed to it again in this step (verified it's absent and stated it's a game demo).\n\nActually, let me be more careful. The question is quite specific: \"Only constraints surfaced in this step.\" So I should focus on what was newly surfaced or newly committed in this final step.\n\nLet me reconsider the dev server watcher — that was definitely surfaced in this step (I noticed the stale transform and restarted).\n\nThe browser-blocked — surfaced in this step (I stated it clearly in my summary).\n\nThe muzzle offset / capsule-can't-be-masked — committed in this step.\n\nThe getPosition center — committed in this step (spawn fix).\n\nThe scene252-not-parity — re-verified in this step but originally decided earlier. I'll include it as it's a standing constraint I re-affirmed.\n\nHmm, but I want to be honest and precise. Let me list the ones I'm confident were surfaced/committed in this step:\n\n1. Browser automation is blocked in this sandbox (Chrome SIGABRTs on crashpad Mach bootstrap) — no Playwright smoke/playtest possible; validation is lint + typecheck + dev-server module resolution + user manual playtest.\n2. The long-running vite dev server's file watcher does not pick up on-disk edits in this sandbox — restart the dev server after editing scene files (or verify served content via curl) before playtesting.\n3. The character controller's capsule shape is private and carries Havok's default all-layers filter (~0), so it cannot be excluded from physicsRaycast via collision-layer masks — bullet rays must originate from a muzzle offset outside the capsule, never from the eye/center.\n4. PhysicsCharacterController.getPosition() returns the capsule center, not the feet — eye height, spawn, and ground computations must apply the capsule half-height offset.\n5. scene252 is a game demo, not a parity scene — it must stay out of scene-config.json, bundle-size.spec.ts, and golden references; no bundle-size ceiling entry to add or raise.\n\nI think these five are the constraints surfaced/committed in this step. Let me present them clearly.\n\nActually, let me reconsider #5. Was it \"surfaced in this step\"? I verified it (grep showed scene252 absent from scene-config.json and bundle-size.spec.ts) and stated it's a game demo. So yes, I re-affirmed it. But it was originally decided in an earlier step. The question says \"learned of or committed to.\" I committed to it in this step (by verifying and stating it). I'll include it but I'm slightly less confident it's \"new.\" \n\nLet me be honest: I'll list the ones I'm confident about. #1, #2, #3, #4 are clearly from this step. #5 is a re-affirmation. I'll include it since it's a real standing constraint and I did re-commit to it in this step.\n\nLet me write the response concisely.\n","seq":96932,"t":5158562,"text":"\n\nCONSTRAINT: Browser automation is blocked in this sandbox — Chrome SIGABRTs at launch (crashpad's Mach `bootstrap_check_in` and `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad` are EPERM-denied, and the cached Playwright chromium build doesn't match the repo's playwright) — so no Playwright smoke/playtest is possible here; validation is lint + typecheck + dev-server module resolution + a user manual playtest on :5182.\nCONSTRAINT: The long-running vite dev server's file watcher does not pick up on-disk edits in this sandbox (it kept serving a stale transform) — after editing scene files, restart the dev server (or verify served content via curl) before playtesting, or you will test old code.\nCONSTRAINT: The character controller's capsule shape is private and carries Havok's default all-layers filter (`~0` membership), so it cannot be excluded from `physicsRaycast` via collision-layer masks — bullet rays must originate from a muzzle offset outside the capsule, never from the eye/center, or the player's own capsule occludes every terrain hit.\nCONSTRAINT: `PhysicsCharacterController.getPosition()` returns the capsule **center**, not the feet — eye height, spawn, and ground computations must apply the capsule half-height offset (feet = center − capsuleHeight/2).\nCONSTRAINT: scene252 is a game demo, not a parity scene — it must stay out of `scene-config.json`, `bundle-size.spec.ts`, and golden references; there is no bundle-size ceiling entry to add or raise for it.","timings":{"cache_n":68608,"draft_n":4116,"draft_n_accepted":1630,"predicted_ms":29910.0,"predicted_n":2218,"prompt_ms":620.0,"prompt_n":136},"to_request":96341,"usage":{"cached_tokens":68608,"completion_tokens":2218,"prompt_tokens":68744}}
