Watch for fall speed looking wrong — I fixed the accumulated-velocity bug, but it's unverified at runtime.\n3. **Mouse look** — the yaw/pitch sign convention is my best guess. If look feels inverted (X or Y), say so; it's a one-line flip.\n4. **Shooting** — click to fire. Expect: a hole in the terrain (tile removed), you can fall through it, and respawning when you drop out. Shoot a bot to check kill feedback.\n5. **Debris** — chunks should spawn on terrain hits, arc away, and settle.\n6. **Bots** — 4 of them should patrol the terrain and shoot at you when they have line of sight. Watch for stuck/oscillating bots (the nav-agent drift re-sync is unverified).\n7. **HUD** — health, kills, tiles destroyed in the corners; crosshair dead-center (I switched it to CSS pixels — verify it's actually centered at your window size).\n8. **Audio** — gunshot, thud, hit sounds on the respective events.\n\nTwo things I'd especially like your read on: **look direction** and **bot behavior**, since those are the two most-likely-to-be-wrong unverified pieces. Tell me what you see — including anything odd (jitter, floating player, missing HUD, slow load — 1024 static bodies + navmesh build is a runtime cost I never measured, and there's an 8×8u-tile fallback if init is sluggish).","timings":{"cache_n":73472,"draft_n":3227,"draft_n_accepted":859,"predicted_ms":23930.0,"predicted_n":1320,"prompt_ms":2530.0,"prompt_n":1629},"to_request":97600,"usage":{"cached_tokens":73472,"completion_tokens":1320,"prompt_tokens":75101}}
