vasElement | null;\n    if (canvas) {\n        canvas.dataset.error = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err);\n    }\n    console.error(err);\n});\n```\n\nAnd the awaits earlier in main. Let me quote the awaits verbatim. The awaits in main are:\n\n```ts\n    const engine = await createEngine(canvas);\n...\n    const hknp = await HavokPhysics({ locateFile: () => \"/HavokPhysics.wasm\" });\n...\n    const nav = await createNavigationPluginAsync({ locateFile: () => \"/recast-navigation.wasm\" });\n...\n    const font = await loadFont(\"/fonts/Inter.ttf\");\n```\n\nThese are scattered, not contiguous. I need a verbatim quote of max ~15 lines. The tail (registerScene/startEngine/ready/catch) is contiguous and load-bearing: it tells me (a) the ready marker is only set after startEngine, (b) errors go to dataset.error + console.error — the user says no console errors, so the hang is an await that never settles rather than a rejection.\n\nHmm, but actually the most load-bearing part for narrowing down the hang is the fact that there are four awaits and no instrumentation between them. Let me quote the tail block, because it defines what \"stuck at Initializing\" means (ready is only set at the very end) and the catch behavior (no error means non-rejection).\n\nQuestion 2: Pointers — things not needed now but potentially important later:\n\n- `input.onFire(tryFire)` is registered before the physics/render callbacks; also `input.consumeLookDelta()` is consumed in onBeforeRender — the mouse-look sign convention (yaw -= dx * sens) is unverified (playtest item).\n- `main().catch` sets `canvas.dataset.error` — useful for debugging (the user can report dataset.error if it appears).\n- `findRandomPointAroundCircle(nav, { x: s.x, y: 0, z: s.z }, 8)` for bot spawn — y: 0 might be below the terrain? The bot's y = p.y + CAP_HEIGHT/2, where p.y comes from findRandomPointAroundCircle — if the navmesh has y, p.y is the navmesh's y. OK.\n- `const los = raycast(nav, ...)` uses nav