t.ts (scene252.ts).\n8. HUD updates only when the string changes (`lastHudText`) — cheap; `updateDefaultTextData` is the in-place update.\n\nKeep the pointers concise, one per line, with location info.\n\nFormat: EXCERPT: <verbatim quote> followed by a POINTER line. If there's no load-bearing part, NONE.\n\nThe verbatim quote must be exact. Let me copy from the read output:\n\n```\n    await registerScene(scene);\n    registerTextRenderer(tr);\n    await startEngine(engine);\n    canvas.dataset.initMs = String(Math.round(performance.now() - __initStart));\n    canvas.dataset.ready = \"true\";\n}\n\nmain().catch((err) => {\n    const canvas = document.getElementById(\"renderCanvas\") as HTMLCanvasElement | null;\n    if (canvas) {\n        canvas.dataset.error = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err);\n    }\n    console.error(err);\n});\n```\n\nThat's 14 lines. Good. This is load-bearing: it explains why the spinner stays up (ready is only set after startEngine) and why the absence of console errors means the hang is an unsettled await (one of createEngine / HavokPhysics / createNavigationPluginAsync / loadFont / registerScene / startEngine) rather than a rejection.\n\nActually, I should also mention the awaits in the middle of main — I could include a shorter quote of the four awaits, but they're not contiguous. One EXCERPT max. The tail is most load-bearing for the diagnosis. I'll note in the explanation that the awaits in the middle of main are the suspects.\n\nWait — the instructions say \"quote that part verbatim.\" Just one EXCERPT block. Then POINTERS. Keep the response concise.\n","seq":101282,"t":5617709,"text":"\n\nEXCERPT:\n```ts\n    await registerScene(scene);\n    registerTextRenderer(tr);\n    await startEngine(engine);\n    canvas.dataset.initMs = String(Math.round(performance.now() - __initStart));\n    canvas.dataset.ready = \"true\";\n}\n\nmain().catch((err) => {\n    const canvas = document.getElementById(\"renderCanvas\") as HTMLCanvasElement | null;\n    if (canvas) {\n        canvas.dataset.error = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err);\n    }\n    console.error(err);\n});\n```\n\nThat tail is load-bearing for the diagnosis: `dataset.ready` is only set after `startEngine`, so the spinner means the whole `main()` is still in flight; and since `catch` would both set `dataset.error` and `console.error`, your symptom (no console errors) means one of the awaits is settling neither fulfilled nor rejected — a hang, not a failure. The suspect awaits, in order: `createEngine`, `HavokPhysics(...)` (line ~155), `createNavigationPluginAsync(...)` (line ~171), `loadFont(\"/fonts/Inter.ttf\")` (line ~217), then `registerScene`/`startEngine`. All three assets return 200 via curl, so next I'll instrument which await the page is actually stuck on.\n\nPOINTER: `canvas.dataset.initMs` (set from `__initStart` at main's end) is a built-in init-time readout — I can have you read it during playtest to measure the 1024-body + navmesh init cost I never got to measure (scene252.ts, main tail).\nPOINTER: `canvas.dataset.error` is the in-page failure hook — if a later run dies, asking you for `document.getElementById(\"renderCanvas\").dataset.error` beats guessing (scene252.ts, main catch).\nPOINTER: mouse-look signs are unverified — `yaw -= delta.dx * MOUSE_SENS; pitch -= delta.dy * MOUSE_SENS` in `onBeforeRender`; if look feels inverted it's a one-line flip (scene252.ts, render-frame block).\nPOINTER: bot LOS and shooting both use the navmesh `raycast(nav, ...)` with `!los.hit` = clear sight, at 1.2s intervals, distance-based accuracy `Math.max(0.15, 1 - dist / 50)` — the bot behavior you'll judge in playtest (scene252.ts, bot update in `onPhysicsAfterStep`).\nPOINTER: bot spawns use `findRandomPointAroundCircle(nav, { x: s.x, y: 0, z: s.z }, 8)` and set controller Y from the returned navmesh `p.y + CAP_HEIGHT / 2` — if a bot spawns stuck/underground, this is where to look (scene252.ts, bot setup loop).\nPOIN