{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"The loader overlay disappears when `canvas.dataset.loaded === 'true'` or `canvas.dataset.ready === 'true'`. My scene sets `canvas.dataset.ready = \"true\"` after `startEngine` resolves. And the loader displays errors on `window.addEventListener('error')` and `unhandledrejection` — the user reports no error box is shown, so no errors are being thrown.\n\nSo the scene is stalling on an await without throwing. Which await?\n\nOrder of awaits in main():\n1. `createEngine(canvas)` — done (banner is output).\n2. `HavokPhysics({ locateFile: () => \"/HavokPhysics.wasm\" })` — asset is 200.\n3. `createNavigationPluginAsync({ locateFile: () => \"/recast-navigation.wasm\" })` — asset is 200.\n4. `loadFont(\"/fonts/Inter.ttf\")` — asset is 200.\n5. `registerScene(scene)`\n6. `startEngine(engine)`\n\nHmm, wait — there's a key difference from the bundled scene (scene46) shown in the truncated output. Looking at scene46's `registerScene` equivalent:\n\n```js\nawait async function(t){const n=t,r=n.surface;((t,e)=>-1!==t.O.indexOf(e))(r,n)||(await(async t=>{const e=t;for(;e.Et.length>0;){const t=[...e.Et];e.Et=[],await Promise.all(t.map(async t=>t()))}e.P.length=0,e._t++,e.Bt=!0})(t), n.ut.sort(X), await Promise.all(n.ye.we.map(t=>t.Ye?.()).filter(t=>void 0!==t)), n.ye.build(), ...)(u)\n```\n\nSo registerScene awaits pending material processing (`Et` queue — material pipeline construction, including thin-instance dynamic imports), then builds renderables.\n\nNow, scene252's `registerScene` should do the same. The thin-instance material path dynamically imports the thin-instance module — in dev, that's just a module import, no problem.\n\nBut wait — what about `startEngine`? In scene46:\n\n```js\nawait function(t){return new Promise(e=>{let n=!0,r=0;t.ie=o=>{...n&&(n=!1,e()),t.se=requestAnimationFrame(t.ie)},t.se=requestAnimationFrame(t.ie)})}(c)\n```\n\nThe engine loop starts, and the promise resolves after the first frame