e banner narrows the suspect range.\n\n3. **All three assets (HavokPhysics.wasm, recast-navigation.wasm, Inter.ttf) are served with 200** — rules out asset 404s.\n\n4. **registerScene internally awaits pending material/renderable builders, and only runs configureSwapchainOverlayScene if the surface already has contexts** — since I register the scene before the text renderer, no overlay compositing happens. Confirmed my ordering decision.\n\nHmm, but which of these are \"GOTCHA\" level (behaved differently than expected, error cause, limitation)? The question is specifically about discoveries from this step. Let me be honest about what I found:\n\n- GOTCHA: The loader overlay (lab/public/loader.js) hides on either `data-ready` or `data-loaded`, and displays window errors / unhandled rejections as a red box — IMPLICATION: the fact that the user sees neither an error box nor a fade means main() is stuck on an await with no rejection, so the next step is to instrument the stages rather than look for console errors.\n\n- GOTCHA: The \"Babylon Lite v0.1.0 - WebGPU engine\" banner is logged inside createEngine (engine.ts:313) — IMPLICATION: its presence confirms createEngine resolved, so the hang is on a later await (HavokPhysics / createNavigationPluginAsync / loadFont / registerScene / startEngine).\n\n- GOTCHA: All wasm/font assets return 200 through the dev server — IMPLICATION: the hang is not a missing asset; suspect something inside a wasm load promise or the registerScene/startEngine path.\n\nWait, but are these \"discovered this step\"? Yes — I learned the loader.js behavior and the banner's source this step. The asset 200s were also confirmed this step.\n\nActually, one more important thing I noticed in the minified scene46.js: `startEngine`'s frame loop and registerScene internals — I learned the exact internal structure of registerScene/startEngine from the minified bundle. Is there anything unexpected there? One point: registerScene's `await Promise.all(n.ye.w