dy] or canvas[data-loaded], and displays window errors/unhandled rejections as a red error box on the overlay — IMPLICATION: the user's screenshot (no error box, no fade) means main() is stuck on an await that never settles with no rejection, so the next step is to instrument the stages rather than hunt for console errors.\n\nGOTCHA: The \"Babylon Lite v0.1.0 - WebGPU engine\" banner is logged inside createEngine (packages/babylon-lite/src/engine/engine.ts:313) — IMPLICATION: its presence confirms createEngine resolved, so the hang is on a later await (HavokPhysics load, createNavigationPluginAsync, loadFont, or registerScene).\n\nGOTCHA: All three external assets (HavokPhysics.wasm, recast-navigation.wasm, fonts/Inter.ttf) return 200 through the :5182 dev server — IMPLICATION: asset 404s are ruled out; the hang is inside a wasm load/instantiate promise or the registerScene pipeline path.\n\nGOTCHA: From the minified bundle, startEngine resolves on the first requestAnimationFrame callback regardless of whether a frame was drawn — IMPLICATION: startEngine cannot be the hang; the suspects narrow to the three wasm/font awaits or registerScene's awaited pipeline compilation.\n\nHmm, #4 — is that a \"discovery\" or an inference from minified code? I read it from the minified scene46.js in lab/public/bundle/. It's a genuine reading of the actual code path. I think it's legitimate, but I should be careful: the minified bundle is a build artifact of scene46, but the startEngine code is engine code (same across scenes). The engine source is at packages/babylon-lite/src/engine/engine.ts. I could verify against the source... but the task says \"only discoveries from this step.\" I did discover it this step from the minified output. I'll include it, but phrase it carefully as what I read from the minified engine code path.\n\nActually, let me be a bit cautious about overclaiming #4. What I'm confident about: the promise resolves on the first rAF callback (n starts true, n && (n