{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Let me think about what I did in the previous step. I read scene252.ts, checked the assets (all 200), read loader.js, and traced the banner source.\n\nWhat decisions did I make/confirm in that step?\n\nKey findings:\n1. loader.js dismisses the overlay when `canvas.dataset.loaded === 'true'` or `canvas.dataset.ready === 'true'`. My scene only sets `dataset.ready` after `startEngine` resolves. So the spinner stays until `main()` completes fully. This confirms the hang is inside `main()` — an await that never resolves.\n\n2. The banner \"Babylon Lite v0.1.0 - WebGPU engine\" comes from `createEngine` (engine.ts:313). So `createEngine` resolved — the engine is created.\n\n3. All assets (HavokPhysics.wasm, recast-navigation.wasm, Inter.ttf) return 200 — so it's not a missing asset.\n\nWhat did I decide in that step?\n\n- DECISION: The spinner hang means `main()` never reaches `canvas.dataset.ready = \"true\"` — the loader (loader.js) only dismisses on `data-ready`/`data-loaded`, and since the engine banner proves `createEngine` resolved, the stall is one of the subsequent awaits (HavokPhysics, createNavigationPluginAsync, loadFont, registerScene, startEngine). — WHY: loader.js waits for data-ready/data-loaded and the banner is logged inside createEngine.\n\nHmm, but did I \"decide\" this, or just discover it? The instruction says: \"Did you make, confirm, or change any decision about how this project is built — an API choice, a convention, a structure, a tooling choice, a workaround?\"\n\nDiagnostic conclusions are more like findings than build decisions. But a workaround/tooling choice: I might decide to add `canvas.dataset.loaded` markers per stage for diagnostics. But I haven't done that yet — I haven't made that decision yet.\n\nLet me be careful. In that step:\n- I confirmed that the assets are served correctly (200) — this is a confirmation, and it rules out an asset issue.\n- I confirmed that the loader only dismisses on data-ready/data-loaded — this shapes how I debug (I can instrument with dataset attributes).\n- I confirmed that the engine banner is logged inside createEngine — so createEngine succeeded.\n\nThese are confirmations about how the project works (the loader's contract, the engine's banner). I think the fair answer is:\n\n1. DECISION: Debugging the stuck spinner by instrumenting `canvas.dataset` stage markers in scene252.ts — WHY: loader.js only dismisses on data-ready/data-loaded, so per-stage dataset attributes are the observable seam (and my scene already uses dataset.initMs/ready).\n\nHmm, but I haven't actually done that yet. I'm at the stage of about to decide on next steps.\n\nLet me reconsider what I actually established in that step:\n\n1. Confirmed: All three wasm/font assets return 200 via the dev server — so the stall is not a failed asset fetch.\n2. Confirmed: loader.js only dismisses the overlay when `canvas.dataset.loaded === 'true'` or `canvas.dataset.ready === 'true'`; my scene only sets `data-ready` at the very end of main() (after startEngine), so a perpetual spinner means main() hasn't completed.\n3. Confirmed: The \"Babylon Lite v0.1.0 - WebGPU engine\" banner is logged inside createEngine (engine.ts:313), so createEngine resolved and the stall is a later await (HavokPhysics, createNavigationPluginAsync, loadFont, registerScene, or startEngine).\n\nThese are confirmations of how the project is built (the loader's contract, the engine's banner). I think the fair answer is to list these as confirmations. And the resulting diagnostic approach (instrument the dataset stages) is a tooling/workaround decision I'm making in response.\n\nLet me write this concisely.\n","seq":105355,"t":5867184,"text":"\n\nDECISION: The spinner stall means `main()` never completes — I'll instrument `scene252.ts` with per-stage `canvas.dataset` markers to find which await hangs — WHY: `loader.js` only dismisses the overlay on `data-ready`/`data-loaded`, and my scene sets `data-ready` only after `startEngine`, so a perpetual spinner pins the stall to init.\nDECISION: The hang is one of the post-engine awaits (HavokPhysics, createNavigationPluginAsync, loadFont, registerScene, startEngine), not an asset fetch — WHY: all three assets (HavokPhysics.wasm, recast-navigation.wasm, Inter.ttf) return 200, and the \"Babylon Lite v0.1.0 - WebGPU engine\" banner is logged inside `createEngine` (engine.ts:313), proving that step resolved.","timings":{"cache_n":112128,"draft_n":2247,"draft_n_accepted":743,"predicted_ms":37690.0,"predicted_n":1064,"prompt_ms":490.0,"prompt_n":119},"to_request":104749,"usage":{"cached_tokens":112128,"completion_tokens":1064,"prompt_tokens":112247}}
