{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"User's question: In the steps I just completed (reading loader.js, reading fps-terrain.ts, grepping createNavigationPluginAsync/loadFont), did anything behave differently than I expected?\n\nLet me think about what I discovered in the steps I just completed:\n\n1. loader.js: The spinner disappears when `canvas.dataset.loaded === 'true'` or `canvas.dataset.ready === 'true'`. It has an error box that displays on `window.error` and `unhandledrejection`. My scene only sets `dataset.ready` after `startEngine` resolves. This is as expected — matches the design. There's also a `data-loaded` signal I haven't set — but that's a test-level signal, and ready is sufficient.\n\n2. fps-terrain.ts: Bounded, no infinite loops. Nothing unexpected.\n\n3. grep results:\n   - `createNavigationPluginAsync(options?: { locateFile?: (url: string) => string })` — matches my usage. No issue.\n   - `loadFont(url)` — fetch + throw on !ok. Matches my usage. No issue.\n\nWas there anything in the steps I just completed that differed from expectations? Hmm. Let me think carefully:\n\n- One thing: the loader's error box is displayed on `window.addEventListener('error')` and `unhandledrejection`. My `main().catch()` sets `canvas.dataset.error` and does `console.error(err)` — the user should see both a console error and a red error box. The user reported neither. So it's not an exception — it's a hang. This is an observation, but it's an inference, not an API-level discrepancy.\n\n- The `data-loaded` attribute: the loader also disappears on `data-loaded` — I didn't know about `data-loaded` (I had assumed it was only `data-ready`). This is a minor discovery: the loader accepts either `data-loaded` or `data-ready`. Implication: I could set `data-loaded` earlier... but actually that's not a fix for the hang.\n\n- Banner source: `console.log(`${versionToLog} - WebGPU engine`)` at engine.ts:313 — this happens inside createEngine. Confirms that the engine was created. No issue.\n\nHonestly, the steps I just completed confirmed that the API matches my usage — nothing worked differently than expected. The grep confirmed that both `createNavigationPluginAsync({ locateFile })` and `loadFont(url)` are used correctly.\n\nWait — is there anything in the grep that was unexpected? `loadFont` uses `TextShaperFont.load(data)` — it's a vendored text-shaper. `createFontFromBuffer` — synchronous after fetch. Nothing unexpected.\n\n`createNavigationPluginAsync` — \"the recast wasm is lazy-loaded inside createNavigationPluginAsync\" — this is as expected.\n\nSo the honest answer is: nothing in the steps I just completed differed from expectations. The loader.js read confirmed my understanding (spinner disappears on data-ready; error box on window error/unhandledrejection — neither of which has fired, so it's a hang, not a throw). I could also mention the `data-loaded` alternative, but that's a detail, not a discrepancy.\n\nThe instruction says: \"Only discoveries from this step. If none, answer NONE.\"\n\nI think the correct answer is NONE — everything I confirmed matched my expectations. The grep confirmed that my API usage matches the actual signatures.\n\nNo wait, let me double-check one more thing: in the scene46 bundle code I read (which was part of the grep output), I saw the registration flow of `registerScene` and the loop of `startEngine`. The startEngine promise: `t.Oe=requestAnimationFrame(t.Le)` — the first frame resolves. Nothing unexpected.\n\nOne more point: the scene46 bundle shows `u.fixedDeltaMs=1e3/60` — matches my use of fixedDeltaMs. No issue.\n\nSo: NONE. Or should I list the `data-loaded` discovery? That's a fact I learned (the loader disappears on either data-loaded or data-ready), but it's not \"an API that works differently than expected\" — I didn't expect anything different. The guidance says to enumerate \"APIs that work differently, errors and their actual causes, discovered limitations or unsupported features.\" The `data-loaded` thing is neither a discrepancy nor an error. It's just additional information.\n\nI'll answer NONE.\n","seq":106030,"t":5902386,"text":"\n\nNONE","timings":{"cache_n":119808,"draft_n":2296,"draft_n_accepted":611,"predicted_ms":33390.0,"predicted_n":939,"prompt_ms":900.0,"prompt_n":276},"to_request":105360,"usage":{"cached_tokens":119808,"completion_tokens":939,"prompt_tokens":120084}}
