c function startEngine` (grep found nothing) — the location/signature I was assuming is wrong.\n2. `registerScene` awaits `buildScene` + `_preload` promises + a conditional `swapchain-overlay.js` import — the hang candidate is broader than just \"material processing.\" Specifically, `buildScene` is the next function to read.\n\nShould I mention the swapchain overlay ordering? It's conditional: only if `surface._renderingContexts.length > 0` at registerScene time. Since I register the scene first, it's zero, so this path is skipped. So it's not an actual finding that changes my approach — skip it, or mention it briefly? The instructions say \"only findings from this step\" — I did discover that the overlay path exists inside registerScene, but I already knew it from previous notes (interview-t6-f56700-5). Not new. Skip.\n\nThe tile-cache navmesh finding (maxObstacles) was from the previous step (reading navigation.ts), not this step. So don't include it.\n\nSo, two gotchas. Let me write them concisely.\n","seq":108175,"t":6037818,"text":"\n\nGOTCHA: `grep \"export async function startEngine\"` in `packages/babylon-lite/src/engine/engine.ts` returned nothing — the declaration I assumed (async, in engine.ts) doesn't exist there as I expected — IMPLICATION: locate the real `startEngine` export (it may be a non-async `export function` returning a Promise, or live in another file) before reasoning about which await can hang.\nGOTCHA: `registerScene` (scene-core.ts:400) is `await buildScene(scene)` + `await Promise.all(task._preload)` + conditional `swapchain-overlay.js` import, not just \"material pipeline processing\" — IMPLICATION: the init hang candidate is broader than material processing; read `buildScene` next (it's where material pipelines + thin-instance imports run) rather than assuming the stall is in `startEngine`.","timings":{"cache_n":122880,"draft_n":3066,"draft_n_accepted":865,"predicted_ms":48890.0,"predicted_n":1303,"prompt_ms":10070.0,"prompt_n":2685},"t