{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"`startEngine` is simple: rAF loop, resolve after the first frame. If `renderFrame` throws, the Promise won't resolve, and the error will be caught by window.onerror → an error box will appear in the loader. The user isn't seeing an error box.\n\n`buildScene` runs the deferred builders. These are the material pipeline builders. If a builder never resolves... hmm.\n\nWait — I just realized I should check `renderFrame` and the frame loop more carefully. Because if startEngine's first frame ran and resolved, `dataset.ready` should be set and the spinner should disappear. Neither is happening. So the hang is before startEngine: `buildScene` (deferred builders) or `_preload` or `frameGraph.build()`.\n\nNo wait, hold on. Let me rethink this from scratch. What if main() isn't even being executed? What if the module import graph failed silently? No — Vite should show an error overlay.\n\nWhat if `createEngine` resolved but `document.getElementById(\"renderCanvas\")`... no, that's fine.\n\nHmm, let me look at the deferred builders. When does a material push to `_deferredBuilders`? When `addToScene` is called on a mesh with a material. In scene252:\n- terrain.mesh + terrainMat\n- botMesh + botMat (thin instances)\n- debrisMesh + debrisMat (thin instances)\n\nThe builder for the standard material creates renderables and pipelines. These are async (device.createRenderPipeline). If the pipeline compilation fails, the Promise rejects → `Promise.all` rejects → buildScene rejects → registerScene rejects → main().catch → console.error + dataset.error + error box in the loader. The user says there's no error box...\n\nHmm, wait, let me actually re-verify: does the loader's error box show up on `console.error`? No — the loader watches `window.error` and `window.unhandledrejection`. `main().catch()` handles the rejection, so `unhandledrejection` won't fire. But `console.error(err)` inside the catch should print to the console. The user says the console only shows the banner. So there's no rejection.\n\nSo: no rejection, no error, and the spinner keeps spinning forever. The only remaining possibilities:\n1. A Promise that never settles: a deferred builder or `_preload` that never resolves.\n2. A synchronous block on the main thread (the spinner animation stops — the user might not have noticed).\n\nRegarding #2: the synchronous sections of main() include:\n- createFpsTerrain: 1024 tiles × ~6 wasm calls. Finite, probably 0.5–2 seconds.\n- createNavMesh: recast build over 2048 triangles. Finite, fast.\n- createNavCrowd + 4× addAgent: fast.\n\nThese shouldn't take more than a few seconds total. The user said \"never reaches the game\" — I'd guess they waited more than 30 seconds.\n\nSo #1: a Promise that never settles. Which Promises are involved?\n- buildScene: the deferred builders (material pipeline builds).\n- _preload: `ctx._frameGraph._tasks.map(task => task._preload?.())`.\n\nLet me look at the frame graph tasks — specifically, the standard material renderable task's `_preload`, and the thin instance task. Maybe something in the thin instance path is awaiting a Promise that only gets resolved when the engine starts rendering (a deadlock!). That would be a classic hang: registerScene waits for the preload, and the preload waits for the first frame, but the first frame doesn't start until registerScene completes... no wait, startEngine is separate from registerScene. The engine loop doesn't start until startEngine is called. So if a preload needs the render loop, it will deadlock forever.\n\nLet me look at the frame graph task preloads. Specifically, the thin instance task and the standard material task.\n\nNo, wait. Let me reconsider. What do other scenes that use thin instances do? Are there any lab scenes that use thin instances? Scene 113–115 (picking)... let me check which lab scenes use setThinInstances — if a lab scene uses thin instances and works, then the thin instance preload path is fine.\n\nLet me grep for setThinInstances in the lab scenes.\n","seq":108238,"t":6043346,"text":"\n\n`startEngine` resolves after the first rAF frame — if we reached that point, the spinner should either disappear or show an error box. Neither is happening, so the hang is inside `registerScene` → `buildScene` (deferred material builders) or the frame graph's `_preload` step. The main suspect is the thin-instance path (which I'm not using in any other scene). Let me check which lab scenes use thin instances, and take a look at their preload.\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":125952,"draft_n":2779,"draft_n_accepted":758,"predicted_ms":38210.0,"predicted_n":1155,"prompt_ms":2080.0,"prompt_n":851},"to_request":107539,"usage":{"cached_tokens":125952,"completion_tokens":1155,"prompt_tokens":126803}}
