{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Confirmed: `addBoxObstacle` throws `\"Navmesh has no tile cache. Build with maxObstacles > 0 to enable obstacles.\"` — my navmesh is built without `maxObstacles`, so the first tile destruction will throw an exception inside `tryFire` (called from an input event handler) → error box. That's a runtime bug, but it's not the cause of the initialization hang.\n\nAlso confirmed: the doc example on line 21 shows `createNavMesh(nav, [...], { ..., maxObstacles: 32, tileSize: 32 })` — tileSize is also required for the tile cache (\"Tile cache config: requires tileSize, expectedLayersPerTile, maxObstacles\").\n\nLet me check what params are needed: `maxObstacles`, `tileSize`, and maybe `expectedLayersPerTile`. Let me look at lines 245–270 of navigation.ts.\n\nOK, about the hang. Time to measure. Add console.warn stage markers to main(). Actually — wait, one more idea. Let me look at the vite transform that the dev server serves for scene252.ts and check for any subtle issues... I already confirmed the served content matches disk.\n\nNo, actually, let me think about one more possibility I haven't sufficiently considered: **`createFpsTerrain` is blocking the main thread for a long time**. 1024 tiles × 6 wasm calls = about 6000 wasm calls. Each wasm call via emscripten has overhead. If each call is about 1ms (possible for shape creation with mass properties etc.), that's 6 seconds. HP_Shape_CreateBox + SetMaterial + filter mask... probably 100–500µs each → 1–3 seconds total. The user probably waited longer than that, but I can't be sure.\n\nBut here's the thing: even if createFpsTerrain takes 5 seconds, the spinner should eventually go away. The user said \"never gets to the game\" — that suggests a long wait.\n\nAnd the navmesh: `createNavMesh` over 2048 triangles — recast's navmesh generation is probably 50–200ms.\n\nSo the synchronous work totals maybe 2–5 seconds. Then the awaits: Havok (fast), nav plugin (fast), font (fast), registerScene (fast), startEngine (1 frame). If everything works, the whole initialization should be under 10 seconds.\n\nThe user's report says it's stuck indefinitely. So something isn't resolving. Stage markers will tell me exactly where.\n\nPlan:\n1. Add `console.warn(\"scene252: <stage>\")` markers at each boundary in main() (before/after each await, and after heavy synchronous sections).\n2. Fix the navmesh tile cache bug (add maxObstacles + tileSize to createNavMesh params) — this is a real bug either way.\n3. Ask the user to reload and tell me the last marker.\n\nWait — actually, I want to be careful about how much debug code I add. GUIDANCE says console.warn is allowed (only console.log is forbidden). Stage markers are the minimum reasonable instrumentation. I'll remove them once diagnosis is done.\n\nLet me write the markers. Stages:\n1. \"engine\" — after createEngine\n2. \"havok\" — after await HavokPhysics\n3. \"terrain\" — after createFpsTerrain (the heavy synchronous part)\n4. \"nav-plugin\" — after await createNavigationPluginAsync\n5. \"navmesh\" — after createNavMesh (synchronous)\n6. \"bots\" — after bot creation\n7. \"font\" — after await loadFont\n8. \"registered\" — after await registerScene\n9. \"started\" — after await startEngine\n\nActually, let me make it simpler: one marker after each await/heavy step, with a timestamp to show where time is being spent:\n\n```ts\nconst mark = (stage: string): void => {\n    console.warn(`scene252: ${stage} +${Math.round(performance.now() - __initStart)}ms`);\n};\n```\n\nAnd call mark(\"engine\"), mark(\"havok\"), mark(\"terrain\"), mark(\"nav-plugin\"), mark(\"navmesh\"), mark(\"bots\"), mark(\"font\"), mark(\"registered\"), mark(\"started\").\n\nThe timing info is a bonus — it'll also tell me if createFpsTerrain is taking forever.\n\nAlso, I'll fix the navmesh params. Let me check what the tile cache needs: I'll look at lines 245–275 of navigation.ts.\n","seq":109831,"t":6144186,"text":"\n\nConfirmed — `addBoxObstacle` throws an exception on a solo navmesh (\"Navmesh has no tile cache. Build with `maxObstacles > 0`...\"). So my tile destruction handling crashes on the first shot. That's a real bug, but it's not the cause of the init hang. Let me check what the tile cache config requires, then instrument `main()` with stage markers so we can pinpoint where the hang is.\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":129280,"draft_n":2548,"draft_n_accepted":816,"predicted_ms":40490.0,"predicted_n":1180,"prompt_ms":3910.0,"prompt_n":1912},"to_request":109104,"usage":{"cached_tokens":129280,"completion_tokens":1180,"prompt_tokens":131192}}
