{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Got it. `maxObstacles > 0` requires a tile cache, and `tileSize` defaults to 32. I'll add `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` to my `createNavMesh` call. The arena is 128×128u, so with tileSize 32 that's 4×4 = 16 tiles — no problem. Up to 64 destroyed tiles should be plenty.\n\nNext, instrumentation. I'll add stage markers to `main()` in scene252.ts. I'll add a small `mark` helper and place a marker after each heavy step / await. I'll also fix the navmesh parameters in the same edit batch.\n\nLet me write the edits:\n\n1. Inside `main()`, after `const __initStart = performance.now();`, add the following:\n```ts\nconst mark = (stage: string): void => {\n    console.warn(`scene252 init: ${stage} +${Math.round(performance.now() - __initStart)}ms`);\n};\n```\n\n2. Add markers:\n- After `createEngine`: `mark(\"engine\");`\n- After `createHavokWorld`: `mark(\"havok\");`\n- After `createFpsTerrain`: `mark(\"terrain\");`\n- After `createNavigationPluginAsync`: `mark(\"nav-plugin\");`\n- After `createNavMesh`: `mark(\"navmesh\");`\n- After bot creation: `mark(\"bots\");`\n- After `loadFont`: `mark(\"font\");`\n- After `registerScene`: `mark(\"registered\");`\n- After `startEngine`: `mark(\"started\");`\n\n3. Fix the navmesh parameters:\n```ts\ncreateNavMesh(nav, [terrain.mesh], {\n    cellSize: 0.5,\n    agentHeight: CAP_HEIGHT,\n    agentRadius: CAP_RADIUS,\n    agentClimb: 0.8,\n    maxObstacles: 64,\n    tileSize: 32,\n});\n```\n\nHmm, wait — one thing to consider: `maxObstacles: 64` — if the player destroys more than 64 tiles, `addBoxObstacle` will return null (r.success is false → null) — and my code already handles null. Good.\n\nLet me apply these edits.\n","seq":110249,"t":6234093,"text":"\n\nI've grasped the overall picture. I'll make two changes to `scene252.ts`:\n\n1. **Fix the navmesh**: Add `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` so that `addBoxObstacle` works when tiles are destroyed (currently it throws an exception on the first shot).\n2. **Add stage markers** (`console.warn`, allowed under the guidelines) at each await point in `main()`, so that the next reload will precisely reveal which step is hanging.\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":0,"draft_n":1813,"draft_n_accepted":1014,"predicted_ms":12580.0,"predicted_n":1273,"prompt_ms":60210.0,"prompt_n":59720},"to_request":109837,"usage":{"cached_tokens":0,"completion_tokens":1273,"prompt_tokens":59720}}
