{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"This step was interrupted by the user. Let me think about what happened in the last step that differed from expectations.\n\n1. The first `edit` failed: \"0 occurrences found\" — I constructed the old_string from my own summary's memory, but the actual file had different content (in the summary I wrote `createHavokWorld(scene, await HavokPhysics(...))` as one line, but in the actual file it was split into two lines with `const hknp = await HavokPhysics(...)`; the camera/light setup was in between; the clearColor values were also different, 0.04 vs 0.05). So the expected mismatch was: the file on disk had diverged from what I remembered. The implication: read the file before editing. Don't rely on the summary's memory of the exact text.\n\n2. The parameters of `createNavMesh` in the file (`cs`, `ch`, `walkableSlopeAngle`, `walkableHeight`, `walkableClimb`, `walkableRadius`, `maxEdgeLen`, `maxSimplificationError`, `minRegionArea`, `mergeRegionArea`, `maxVertsPerPoly`, `detailSampleDist`, `detailSampleMaxError`) — the interface I read in navigation.ts had these names, and they matched. So no surprise there.\n\n3. Important discovery: `addBoxObstacle` throws \"Navmesh has no tile cache. Build with `maxObstacles > 0` to enable obstacles.\" — my navmesh was being built without `maxObstacles`, so the first tile destruction should throw an exception. This is a discovery: a solo navmesh does not support dynamic obstacles; the tile cache needs `maxObstacles > 0` (tileSize defaults to 32). Implication: the createNavMesh call needs `maxObstacles` + `tileSize` (done).\n\n4. `startEngine` is `export function startEngine(engine): Promise<void>` — not `export async function` — a minor thing, probably not worth listing.\n\n5. `registerScene` calls `buildScene(scene)` and awaits the deferred builders + `_preload` — the hang candidates are narrowed down to the registerScene/startEngine path. That's analysis, not a \"different behavior\" discovery.\n\nSo the discoveries that actually differ from expectations in this step are:\n- The edit failed because the actual file contents differed from what I remembered (the summary's memory of the code was stale/inaccurate). Implication: always read the file before editing.\n- `addBoxObstacle` requires a tile-cache navmesh (`maxObstacles > 0`); the navmesh built without it throws an exception at runtime. Implication: the createNavMesh call needed `maxObstacles`/`tileSize` (already fixed).\n\nAlso, the signature of `createNavigationPluginAsync` was confirmed — it matches what I used, so no surprise.\n\nShould I list the edit failure? The instructions say: \"APIs that behave differently, errors and their actual causes, discovered limitations or unsupported features.\" The edit failure is an error, and its actual cause is that the file on disk had diverged from my memory. It's borderline — it's not a repo discovery, it's a process mistake. But it is an \"error and its actual cause.\" I'll include it concisely.\n\nThe navmesh obstacle thing is the most important one.\n\nShould I also mention that the dev server needed a restart? That was already known from the working set (not new in this step). No.\n\nKeep it concise, one line each.\n","seq":112129,"t":6340773,"text":"\n\nGOTCHA: `addBoxObstacle` (navigation.ts:647) throws \"Navmesh has no tile cache. Build with `maxObstacles > 0` to enable obstacles\" — a solo navmesh (my current `createNavMesh` call) can't take dynamic obstacles — IMPLICATION: the navmesh must be built with `maxObstacles > 0` (tile cache; `tileSize` defaults to 32) or every tile destruction throws at runtime — fixed by adding `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` to the params in scene252.ts.\nGOTCHA: my first `edit` failed (0 occurrences) because I reconstructed `main()`'s text from memory — the on-disk file had diverged (separate `hknp` line, camera/light setup between engine and physics, different clearColor values) — IMPLICATION: always `