{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"The new server is serving the updated code (marker + maxObstacles fix).\n\nNow I need to ask the user to reload the page and report back. But wait — before that, let me think about whether I can do better than a round-trip with the user.\n\nActually — hold on. Let me reconsider the problem once more. I've been assuming the hang is at one of the awaits inside main(). But let me reconsider the possibility that `createFpsTerrain` is blocking the main thread for a long time. Actually, the markers should reveal that too: if \"havok\" is displayed but \"terrain\" doesn't show up for a long time, then terrain creation is the bottleneck.\n\nAlso — one more thought about what could actually be hanging. Let me look at the physics world creation: `createHavokWorld(scene, hknp, gravity)`. What does this do? If it registers the physics step with the scene's frame loop... that's fine.\n\nAnd what about `createPhysicsCharacterController` — it creates a Havok body. That's fine.\n\nActually, let me look at one more suspicious point: `onPhysicsAfterStep` / the physics world's step. If `createHavokWorld` hooks into the scene's render loop via a callback, and that callback (my game loop) throws an exception... the error would propagate → window error → error box. The user hasn't seen that.\n\nI think the instrumentation is the right move. Let me also consider: is there a way to test in this sandbox... according to the working set, no browser can be launched (Chrome SIGABRTs). So the user has to do it.\n\nLet me also double-check whether there are any other issues in the rest of scene252.ts I should look at while I'm waiting. Let me skim the middle section (game loop, physics step, fire) to see if there's anything that could hang... Actually, the game loop runs inside a callback after startEngine — if the hang is happening before startEngine, it's not relevant to the spinner.\n\nBut wait — actually, there's one more possibility I should rule out: what if `registerScene` → `buildScene` → deferred builder is waiting on something that requires the render loop to start (a deadlock)? I looked at `_preload` — it's just an import. And `buildScene` runs the `_deferredBuilders` — the material builders. Let me quickly check what the standard material's deferred builder awaits... Actually, the other lab scenes work with standard materials + thin instances, so this path is proven.\n\nThe combination that's unique to scene252 is: TextRenderer on the same surface as the scene. But the TextRenderer is registered after registerScene — so it can't affect registerScene. And startEngine's first frame runs both contexts — if the text context's `_record()` throws an exception → error box. The user hasn't seen that.\n\nSo: the instrumentation will answer this. Let me ask the user to reload and report back.\n\nNo wait — one more static check I can do: let me look at `createHavokWorld` and see whether it does anything async-like, or whether it could block. Let me take a quick look. And `createPhysicsCharacterController` too. Actually, no — I'm overthinking this. The markers will tell me. Let me ask the user.\n\nActually, hold on, let me reconsider one more time. There's one thing I haven't verified: **`createEngine(canvas)`** — does it require a WebGPU-unsupported path? No — the banner was displayed, and it resolved.\n\nOkay, let me also check the output file to make sure the new dev server started up cleanly.\n","seq":112277,"t":6348266,"text":"\n\nThe new server is serving the instrumented code. Let me confirm it started cleanly.\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":68864,"draft_n":2443,"draft_n_accepted":576,"predicted_ms":27640.0,"predicted_n":925,"prompt_ms":740.0,"prompt_n":232},"to_request":111595,"usage":{"cached_tokens":68864,"completion_tokens":925,"prompt_tokens":69096}}
