{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"The user is asking me to reflect on the step I just completed and enumerate the decisions made.\n\nThe step I just completed was:\n1. Read `createNavigationPluginAsync` and `loadFont` — confirmed that both resolve or throw, so they can't hang silently.\n2. Read `registerScene` and `startEngine` — confirmed that startEngine resolves after the first rAF frame, and that registerScene → buildScene → _preload are simple dynamic imports.\n3. Discovered a real bug: `createNavMesh` without `maxObstacles` builds a solo navmesh, and `addBoxObstacle` throws an exception (\"Navmesh has no tile cache\").\n4. Decided to add `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` to the createNavMesh call in scene252.ts.\n5. Decided to instrument main() with console.warn stage markers (engine, havok, terrain, nav-plugin, navmesh, bots, font, pre-register, registered, started) in order to empirically pinpoint the cause of the hang.\n6. Restarted the dev server (stopping bg_f4a1f424 and starting bg_ec39a3f1). This is because in this sandbox the long-running vite watcher serves stale transforms.\n\nDecisions from this step:\n- DECISION: The navmesh in scene252.ts is built with `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` (tile-cache navmesh) — reason: `addBoxObstacle` for destroyed tiles throws on a solo navmesh (\"Navmesh has no tile cache. Build with maxObstacles > 0\").\n- DECISION: Instrument the await boundaries of main() in scene252.ts with console.warn stage markers (with millisecond offsets) — reason: the spinner hang is at an await that never settles, and the markers will definitively identify which stage is hanging on the next reload.\n- DECISION: Restart the dev server (bg_ec39a3f1) after editing — reason: in this sandbox the long-running vite watcher doesn't pick up edits on disk (stale transforms).\n\nWait — the dev server restart is a known constraint from before, but it's an action/decision that was carried out in this step. I think it's fair to include it as a decision about how to verify things.\n\nAlso, should I include the decision that \"console.warn is the permitted channel for instrumentation\" — this is part of the marker decision.\n\nI'll go with enumerating these three.\n","seq":112562,"t":6361351,"text":"\n\nDECISION: scene252's navmesh is now built as a tile-cache navmesh (`maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` in the `createNavMesh` call) — WHY: `addBoxObstacle` (navigation.ts:647) throws \"Navmesh has no tile cache\" on a solo navmesh, so my tile-destruction path would have crashed on the first shot.\nDECISION: `main()` in scene252.ts is instrumented with `console.warn` stage markers (engine/havok/terrain/nav-plugin/navmesh/bots/font/pre-register/registered/started, with ms offsets) — WHY: the spinner stall is an await that never settles (no error box, no rejection), and stage markers are the fastest way to pin down which stage hangs on the next reload; `console.warn` is the only console channel ESLint allows here.\nDECISION: Restarted the lab dev server (stopped bg_f4a1f424, started bg_ec39a3f1 on :5182) after the edits — WHY: the long-running vite watcher in this sandbox doesn't pick up on-disk edits and serves stale transforms, so the new markers would never be served without a restart.","timings":{"cache_n":68864,"draft_n":1561,"draft_n_accepted":588,"predicted_ms":19260.0,"predicted_n":811,"prompt_ms":680.0,"prompt_n":159},"to_request":112134,"usage":{"cached_tokens":68864,"completion_tokens":811,"prompt_tokens":69023}}
