{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"The server is running and serving the instrumented scene. Next, I need to ask the user to reload and report the last marker.\n\nBut wait — before asking the user, let me reconsider whether I can identify the hang myself. Let me think very carefully about what's unique to scene252:\n\n1. Physics world + 1024 static bodies + character controller — proven in scene40 (though scene40 has far fewer bodies).\n2. Nav plugin + navmesh + crowd — proven in scene170.\n3. Text renderer on the same surface as the 3D scene — scene180 is standalone (no 3D scene), scene181 uses world-space text renderables (not a TextRenderer). **So the combination of TextRenderer + 3D scene on the same surface is unproven in the lab!**\n\nHmm, interesting. But the TextRenderer is registered after registerScene, and startEngine is awaited after that. If the first frame throws in the text context's `_record()` → error box. The user says there's no error box...\n\nWait, actually — let me re-check the loader's error box logic. According to my notes: \"lab/public/loader.js dismisses the spinner on either canvas[data-ready] or canvas[data-loaded], and has a built-in error box that displays window errors and unhandled rejections on the overlay.\"\n\nSo the error box displays on `window` errors and unhandled rejections. `main().catch` handles the rejection → no unhandledrejection. But `console.error(err)` should still show up in the console. The user says the console only shows the banner. So there's no rejection, and no window error.\n\nTherefore: a Promise that never settles, or a blocked main thread. The markers will tell us which stage.\n\nActually — hmm, wait. Let me reconsider one more thing: **what if the hang is inside `createFpsTerrain` — specifically, one of the 1024 `createPhysicsBody`/`createPhysicsShape` calls is blocking on the wasm side?** For example, if HP_Body_Create has a bug in the mass calculation for a degenerate box... My notes: \"the top face of the box is at the max corner height of the tile, with a minimum half-height of 0.5\" — so the box is non-degenerate.\n\nBut — what if `setPhysicsShapeFilterMembershipMask` with TERRAIN_LAYER... no, that's fine.\n\nOr — what if `createFpsTerrain` is actually running normally, and the hang is in `createNavMesh` — the recast build. If recast's `generateTileCache` hangs (infinite loop in wasm)... it's possible, but that would be an engine bug. With my new `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` parameters, the navmesh is now a tile-cache build rather than a solo build! Wait — that changes the navmesh build path. If the tile-cache path has a bug... but it should work — is it used in scene170/171? Let me check what scene170 passes. Actually, my notes say scene170/171 is the established idiom for navmesh. Let me check whether they use maxObstacles.\n\nHmm, this is important: if the tile-cache path is broken, my \"fix\" could cause the hang. Let me check scene170's createNavMesh call.\n","seq":112878,"t":6375334,"text":"\n\nThe server is healthy. One thing to double-check: my `maxObstacles` fix switches the navmesh from the solo path to the tile-cache path — I want to confirm that the tile-cache path actually works in the lab (scene170/171).\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":68864,"draft_n":2128,"draft_n_accepted":608,"predicted_ms":24450.0,"predicted_n":912,"prompt_ms":1930.0,"prompt_n":1295},"to_request":112282,"usage":{"cached_tokens":68864,"completion_tokens":912,"prompt_tokens":70159}}
