{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"The user is asking me to pause and list the constraints that became clear or were committed to in the step I just completed.\n\nWhat did I do in this step?\n1. Read navigation.ts — discovered that `createNavMesh` only builds a tile-cache navmesh when `maxObstacles > 0`, and that `addBoxObstacle` throws an exception (\"Navmesh has no tile cache. Build with `maxObstacles > 0` to enable obstacles.\") against a solo navmesh. This is a hard requirement: for dynamic obstacle insertion (tile destruction), the navmesh must be built with `maxObstacles > 0` (+ `tileSize`).\n2. Confirmed that `loadFont` throws on failure — not a constraint.\n3. Confirmed that `createNavigationPluginAsync` lazily loads the recast wasm — not a constraint per se.\n4. Read registerScene/startEngine — these are engine-internal behavior, not project constraints.\n5. Discovered the correct `NavMeshParameters` field names (cs, ch, walkableSlopeAngle...) — the earlier note was wrong, but this is more of a correction than a constraint.\n6. Restarted the dev server — this was already a known constraint (the stale transform issue) and was not newly discovered in this step.\n\nConstraint that became clear in this step:\n- CONSTRAINT: For `addBoxObstacle`/`addCylinderObstacle` to work, the navmesh must be built with `maxObstacles > 0` (tile-cache navmesh, with `tileSize`); calling these against a solo navmesh throws. So for tile destruction in scene252, `createNavMesh` must include `maxObstacles` (and `tileSize`).\n\nThis is the main one. Anything else?\n\n- `tileSize` is required/recommended for the tile cache — default is 32. This is part of the same constraint.\n- `loadFont`/`createNavigationPluginAsync` reject on failure — meaning hangs can't occur from these. Not a constraint to be followed.\n\nI think there's exactly one constraint that should be recorded. The user said \"only constraints that became clear in this step.\" The navmesh tile-cache requirement became clear in this step (I discovered it, committed to adding maxObstacles: 64 + tileSize: 32, and actually edited the file).\n\nThe dev server restart gotcha was already known from previous steps (recorded in the working set), so it's not new in this step.\n\nLet me answer concisely.\n","seq":112957,"t":6380232,"text":"\n\nCONSTRAINT: Dynamic navmesh obstacles require a tile-cache navmesh — `createNavMesh` must be passed `maxObstacles > 0` (with `tileSize`) or `addBoxObstacle`/`addCylinderObstacle` throw (\"Navmesh has no tile cache\"); scene252's tile destruction depends on this, so its navmesh params now include `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32`.","timings":{"cache_n":68864,"draft_n":1442,"draft_n_accepted":434,"predicted_ms":17600.0,"predicted_n":640,"prompt_ms":630.0,"prompt_n":136},"to_request":112568,"usage":{"cached_tokens":68864,"completion_tokens":640,"prompt_tokens":69000}}
