{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Both scene170 and scene171 use a solo navmesh (no maxObstacles). In other words, the tile cache path (`maxObstacles > 0`) has not been proven in the lab scenes. Hmm.\n\nBut wait — is the tile cache path used in tests? Let me check the tests... Actually, the recast-navigation package has its own tests. But for the purposes of this debug session, the key question is: does the tile cache build hang?\n\nThe code path is: `plugin._generators.generateTileCache(positions, indices, cfg, false)` — this is a wasm call, and it should either return a result or throw an exception. If `result.success` is false → throw → error box. If it hangs inside the wasm... that would be a recast bug, and it's hard to imagine with a small mesh (2048 triangles).\n\nAlso, my scene currently uses `maxObstacles: 64` — meaning the navmesh build is now the tile cache version. If that's what's hanging, the marker will show \"nav-plugin\" but no \"navmesh\".\n\nOK — I've done all the static analysis I can. Time to ask the user to reload and report the last stage marker. Let me also give them the exact thing to check:\n\n1. Reload http://localhost:5182/lite/scene252.html\n2. Open the DevTools console\n3. Tell me the last \"scene252 init: <stage>\" line that was displayed\n\nAlso — I should record the state. Let me update the working set with what I did:\n- Instrumented main() with stage markers (console.warn)\n- Fixed the navmesh to use the tile cache (maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32) — required for addBoxObstacle\n- Restarted the dev server (bg_ec39a3f1)\n\nAnd record the unresolved questions: which stage is hanging.\n\nLet me write the response to the user.\n","seq":113544,"t":6405393,"text":"\n\nBoth lab navmesh scenes use the solo path, so the tile-cache path is new territory for this lab — but it's a synchronous wasm call that throws on failure, and the stage markers will catch it if it's the culprit.\n\nHere's where things stand:\n\n**What I ruled out statically:**\n- All three assets (`HavokPhysics.wasm`, `recast-navigation.wasm`, `Inter.ttf`) return 200.\n- `loadFont`, `createNavigationPluginAsync`, `HavokPhysics` all either resolve or reject (a rejection would show an error box + `console.error` — you see neither).\n- `startEngine` resolves on the first frame or throws (error box) — so the stall is *before* it.\n- `fps-terrain.ts` has no unbounded loops; the 1024-body init is slow but finite.\n\n**What I changed:**\n1. **Instrumented `main()`** in `scene252.ts` with `console.warn` stage markers (`engine`, `havok`, `terrain`, `nav-plugin`, `navmesh`, `bots`, `font`, `pre-register`, `registered`, `started`) — each prints its elapsed ms, so we'll see both *where* it hangs and *how long* the terrain/body init takes.\n2. **Fixed a real bug**: `createNavMesh` now passes `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32`. Without a tile-cache navmesh, `addBoxObstacle` throws `\"Navmesh has no tile cache\"` — the first shot at the terrain would have crashed the game.\n3. Restarted the dev server (the old one was serving stale transforms in this sandbox); confirmed the new server on :5182 serves the instrumented code.\n\n**Please reload `http://localhost:5182/lite/scene252.html`** and tell me the **last** `scene252 init: <stage>` line that appears in the console (or, if it hangs mid-stage, which two markers bookend the silence). That will pin the hang to a single await and I can go straight at it.","timings":{"cache_n":71424,"draft_n":2037,"draft_n_accepted":604,"predicted_ms":23650.0,"predicted_n":895,"prompt_ms":1200.0,"prompt_n":635},"to_request":112952,"usage":{"cached_tokens":71424,"completion_tokens":895,"prompt_tokens":72059}}
