{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Let me reflect on what happened in the immediately preceding step (and the tool activity that accompanied it).\n\nIn the previous step, I:\n1. Discovered that `addBoxObstacle` throws an exception on a solo navmesh — it requires `maxObstacles > 0` (tile cache).\n2. Read the `NavMeshParameters` interface and confirmed the correct parameter names (`cs`, `ch`, `tileSize`, `maxObstacles`, `expectedLayersPerTile`).\n3. Applied edits to scene252.ts: added a `mark()` stage marker (console.warn) at each await stage, and added `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` to the `createNavMesh` call.\n4. Stopped the old dev server (bg_f4a1f424) and started a new one (bg_ec39a3f1) to avoid the issue of stale transforms.\n5. Verified that the delivered transform contains the markers + maxObstacles.\n6. Checked scene170/171 to confirm the navmesh idiom — scene170 doesn't use maxObstacles (solo), and scene171 explicitly uses `maxObstacles: 0`.\n\nDecisions made in this step:\n\nDECISION: To diagnose the initialization hang, I added console.warn stage markers (a `mark()` helper) to main() in scene252.ts — why: since I can't launch a browser in this sandbox, I need to have the user reload and report the last stage reached.\n\nDECISION: I added `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` to scene252's `createNavMesh` call — why: `addBoxObstacle` throws \"Navmesh has no tile cache\" on a solo navmesh, so tile destruction (adding nav obstacles) will crash on the first shot.\n\nDECISION: Restarted the dev server (stopped bg_f4a1f424, started bg_ec39a3f1) — why: the long-running vite server in this sandbox doesn't reflect on-disk edits (stale transforms).\n\nDECISION: `console.warn` is permissible as debug instrumentation (only console.log is forbidden by GUIDANCE §6) — why: lint forbids console.log but allows warn/error/time/trace.\n\nAre these \"decisions about how this project is built — API choices, conventions, structure, tooling choices, workarounds\"?\n\n- Adding the navmesh `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` is an API choice/workaround for tile destruction to work. Yes.\n- Stage markers are a diagnostic workaround (temporary). It's a decision to instrument with console.warn.\n- Restarting the dev server is a tooling workaround based on a known gotcha.\n- The choice of `maxObstacles: 64` — the specific value of 64 (the maximum number of obstacles) — is a parameter choice.\n\nI should enumerate these. Note: these are decisions from \"this step\" — the immediately preceding message/tool activity. The reflection request states \"only decisions from this step, not from earlier ones.\"\n\nI'll enumerate them concisely.\n","seq":114751,"t":6569688,"text":"\n\nDECISION: Added `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` to scene252's `createNavMesh` call — WHY: `addBoxObstacle` throws \"Navmesh has no tile cache\" on a solo navmesh, so tile-destruction nav obstacles would crash on the first shot.\nDECISION: Instrumented `main()` in scene252.ts with a `mark()` helper emitting `console.warn` stage markers (engine/havok/terrain/nav-plugin/navmesh/bots/font/pre-register/registered/started) — WHY: browser automation is blocked in this sandbox, so the user's reload will reveal exactly which await hangs.\nDECISION: Used `console.warn` (not `console.log`) for the instrumentation — WHY: GUIDANCE §6 forbids `console.log` but permits warn/error/time/trace.\nDECISION: Restarted the dev server (stopped bg_f4a1f424, launched bg_ec39a3f1 on :5182) — WHY: the long-running vite watcher serves stale transforms in this sandbox, so served code must match disk before the user reloads.","timings":{"cache_n":71936,"draft_n":1848,"draft_n_accepted":667,"predicted_ms":24550.0,"predicted_n":931,"prompt_ms":760.0,"prompt_n":224},"to_request":114215,"usage":{"cached_tokens":71936,"completion_tokens":931,"prompt_tokens":72160}}
