{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"In this step (the current turn), what did I learn or commit to?\n\n1. `createNavMesh` only builds a tile-cache navmesh when `maxObstacles > 0`; `addBoxObstacle` throws an exception on a solo navmesh (\"Navmesh has no tile cache. Build with `maxObstacles > 0` to enable obstacles.\"). Therefore, to enable dynamic obstacles, the navmesh must be built with `maxObstacles > 0` (and `tileSize` defaults to 32). This is a constraint discovered in this step.\n\n2. Scene 170/171 does not exercise the tile-cache path (scene 171 explicitly uses `maxObstacles: 0`, and scene 170 does not use maxObstacles) — therefore the tile-cache navmesh path is unverified in the lab. This is more of an \"open/unverified\" note than a constraint. Hmm — it means I should be cautious about my changes. I could phrase it as: the tile-cache navmesh path is unverified in the lab; verify it during playtesting. This is a caveat, and can be considered a constraint on what I know, but it's more like an open item.\n\n3. The stage markers via console.warn are temporary debug code and must be removed before commit (GUIDANCE §0b). This is a commitment I made — I added console.warn markers to scene252.ts and must remove them once diagnosis is complete. Is this a \"constraint that the rest of the project must respect\"? It's a follow-up on cleanup. I think it's worth recording as a constraint: the scene252.ts console.warn stage markers are temporary and must be removed before commit.\n\n4. The dev server restart requirement — this was already known (the working set has a note about stale transforms) and it's not new in this step.\n\n5. `NavMeshParameters` uses abbreviated names (cs, ch, walkableSlopeAngle...) — this is a compatibility fact I learned in this step (I initially used the wrong names in an edit). This is more of a fact/pointer than a constraint.\n\nTherefore, the constraints specific to this step:\n- CONSTRAINT: `addBoxObstacle`/`addCylinderObstacle` throws an exception unless the navmesh is built with `maxObstacles > 0` (tile-cache path); scene252's navmesh must keep `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` — otherwise, tile destruction will crash on the first shot.\n- CONSTRAINT: The console.warn stage markers added to scene252.ts's main() are temporary instrumentation and must be removed before commit (GUIDANCE §0b).\n\nMaybe this too:\n- CONSTRAINT: In this sandbox, the Vite dev server must be restarted after editing scene files (stale transforms) — but this was already known from before this step, and was just applied. It's not \"emerged in this step.\" Skip.\n\nI'll keep it to these two.\n","seq":115011,"t":6583520,"text":"\n\nCONSTRAINT: Navmesh dynamic obstacles require the tile-cache build path — `addBoxObstacle`/`addCylinderObstacle` throw (\"Navmesh has no tile cache\") unless `createNavMesh` is called with `maxObstacles > 0` (navigation.ts:697); scene252 must keep `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` or tile destruction crashes on the first shot.\nCONSTRAINT: The `console.warn` stage markers added to `main()` in scene252.ts are temporary instrumentation for diagnosing the init hang — they must be deleted once the stall is identified, per GUIDANCE §0b (no debug code in committed code).","timings":{"cache_n":71936,"draft_n":1750,"draft_n_accepted":543,"predicted_ms":12790.0,"predicted_n":793,"prompt_ms":750.0,"prompt_n":201},"to_request":114758,"usage":{"cached_tokens":71936,"completion_tokens":793,"prompt_tokens":72137}}
