{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"So `init` is:\n```js\nconst init = async impl => {\n  if (Raw.Module !== undefined) return;\n  if (impl) {\n    Raw.Module = await impl();  // ← This is where the wasm factory gets called\n  } else { ... }\n  ...\n};\n```\n\nSo the hang is inside `impl()` — that is, the emscripten wasm factory: `wasmFactory({ locateFile })`. This does the following:\n1. Fetches `/recast-navigation.wasm`\n2. Instantiates it\n3. Runs the startup code\n4. Returns the module\n\nThis works in scene170. In scene252, it hangs — after the Havok wasm has been instantiated.\n\nLet's look at the emscripten glue code for the recast wasm and check the browser loading path. Let me search for how it fetches and instantiates.\n","seq":117015,"t":6758331,"text":"\n\nThe hang is inside the emscripten wasm factory (`impl()` → `Raw.Module = await impl()`). Let me inspect the recast wasm glue's browser load path and check for any global-state interaction with Havok.\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":120320,"draft_n":686,"draft_n_accepted":265,"predicted_ms":10000.0,"predicted_n":363,"prompt_ms":4510.0,"prompt_n":1042},"to_request":116837,"usage":{"cached_tokens":120320,"completion_tokens":363,"prompt_tokens":121362}}
