{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"So `createNavigationPluginAsync` → `_ensureRecast` → `core.init(wasmFactory.bind(null, { locateFile }))`.\n\nIn `core.init`:\n```js\nconst init = async impl => {\n  if (Raw.Module !== undefined) return;\n  if (impl) {\n    Raw.Module = await impl();   // ← wasmFactory({locateFile})\n  } else { ... }\n  // then creates instances, classes, etc.\n};\n```\n\n`wasmFactory` is the default export of `@recast-navigation/wasm/wasm`, i.e., `recast-navigation.wasm.js`. This is an emscripten module. When you call it, it returns a Promise (moduleRtn) that resolves when the runtime has been initialized.\n\nThe emscripten module does the following:\n1. Fetches the wasm binary via `findWasmBinary()` → `locateFile(\"recast-navigation.wasm.wasm\")` → `\"/recast-navigation.wasm\"` (via our locateFile). Good.\n2. `instantiateAsync` → `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` or `instantiateArrayBuffer`.\n3. `receiveInstance` → `assignWasmExports` → `removeRunDependency(\"wasm-instantiate\")`.\n4. After runDependencies reach 0, `dependenciesFulfilled` → `initRuntime` → `wasmExports[\"h\"]()` → then moduleRtn is resolved.\n\nWait, let me check the end. The Promise `moduleRtn` is `new Promise((resolve,reject)=>{readyPromiseResolve=resolve;readyPromiseReject=reject})`.\n\nWhere does `readyPromiseResolve` get called? It should be in the startup processing. Let me search for where readyPromiseResolve is called. Typically, emscripten calls `dependenciesFulfilled`, which then calls `init()`... let me search for `readyPromiseResolve` in the glue code.\n\nActually, let me rethink. The key question is: why does scene252 hang while scene170 works? Both use the same `createNavigationPluginAsync`. The difference is: scene252 loads Havok first, then loads recast. scene170 only loads recast (probably).\n\nWait — actually, let me check whether scene170 also loads Havok. Let me verify. Actually, the difference might be something else. Let me think about what's different.\n\nActually, wait. Let me rethink the whole thing. The user says scene170 works and scene252 hangs on the nav-plugin. But maybe the issue isn't with recast at all. Let me re-read the markers:\n\n- engine +22ms\n- havok +64ms\n- terrain +90ms\n- (nav-plugin never outputs)\n\nSo it's hanging on `createNavigationPluginAsync`. But scene170 does the same thing and works.\n\nLet me check: does scene170 also load Havok first? If so, the Havok+recast combination works there. Let me check scene170.\n\nActually, let me reconsider a more subtle possibility. Let me look at the emscripten glue code more carefully, specifically where readyPromiseResolve is called and whether there's a dependency on `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming`.\n\nActually, a very important clue: `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` requires that the response's MIME type be `application/wasm`. If the dev server serves the wasm with the wrong MIME type, `instantiateStreaming` fails, and the code falls back to `instantiateArrayBuffer`. So that should still work.\n\nHmm, but wait. Let me reconsider. Let me look at what could cause an infinite hang (never resolving).\n\nLet me search the glue code for `readyPromiseResolve` and the `init` startup processing.\n","seq":117851,"t":6853376,"text":"","timings":{"cache_n":67840,"draft_n":2058,"draft_n_accepted":668,"predicted_ms":29830.0,"predicted_n":962,"prompt_ms":1560.0,"prompt_n":709},"to_request":117292,"usage":{"cached_tokens":67840,"completion_tokens":962,"prompt_tokens":68549}}
