{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Now I have both emscripten glue codes. Let me compare the key parts.\n\nHavok's `run()` function:\n```js\nfunction run(){\n  if(runDependencies>0){return}\n  if(!calledPrerun){calledPrerun=1;preRun();if(runDependencies>0){return}}\n  function doRun(){\n    if(calledRun)return;\n    calledRun=1;\n    Module[\"calledRun\"]=1;\n    if(ABORT)return;\n    initRuntime();\n    preMain();\n    readyPromiseResolve(Module);\n    Module[\"onRuntimeInitialized\"]?.();\n    if(shouldRunNow)callMain();\n    postRun()\n  }\n  if(Module[\"setStatus\"]){...}\n  else{doRun()}\n}\n...\nrun();\nmoduleRtn=readyPromise;\n```\n\nSo Havok's module, when called, immediately runs `run()` synchronously (at the end of the IIFE). It sets up `dependenciesFulfilled=runCaller` and calls `run()`. Since `runDependencies` starts at 0 but `createWasm()` calls `addRunDependency(\"wasm-instantiate\")` making it 1, the first `run()` returns early (runDependencies>0). Then when wasm instantiates, `removeRunDependency` → `dependenciesFulfilled` → `runCaller` → `run()` again → now runDependencies==0 → `doRun()` → `readyPromiseResolve(Module)`.\n\nOK so Havok works.\n\nNow recast's glue. Let me recall the end of recast's glue:\n```js\n...\nif(runtimeInitialized){moduleRtn=Module}else{moduleRtn=new Promise((resolve,reject)=>{readyPromiseResolve=resolve;readyPromiseReject=reject})}\n```\n\nAnd earlier I saw:\n```\ndependenciesFulfilled=run\n```\nand `readyPromiseResolve?.(Module)`.\n\nLet me look at recast's `run` and startup more carefully. The recast glue is a NEWER emscripten build (it uses `updateMemoryViews`, `addOnPreRun`, etc., and the `moduleRtn` is set at the very end based on `runtimeInitialized`).\n\nThe key difference: In recast's glue, the startup `run()` — let me find where it's called. In the newer emscripten, the pattern is:\n```js\nvar calledRun;\ndependenciesFulfilled=function runCaller(){if(!calledRun)run();if(!calledRun)dependenciesFulfilled=runCaller};\nfunction run(){...}\nrun();  // or via postRun\n```\n\nActually, I need to see the actual `run` and how `readyPromiseResolve?.(Module)` gets called in recast. Let me grep for the run function and its invocation in the recast glue.\n\nActually, the crucial question remains: WHY does recast hang when loaded after Havok but not alone?\n\nLet me think about the ONE shared global resource: `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming`. Both use it. But that's a browser API, not shared state.\n\nWait — actually, let me reconsider. Let me look at the recast glue's `instantiateAsync` again:\n```js\nasync function instantiateAsync(binary,binaryFile,imports){\n  if(!binary&&typeof WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming==\"function\"){\n    try{\n      var response=fetch(binaryFile,{credentials:\"same-origin\"});\n      var instantiationResult=await WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming(response,imports);\n      return instantiationResult\n    }catch(reason){\n      err(`wasm streaming compile failed: ${reason}`);\n      err(\"falling back to ArrayBuffer instantiation\")\n    }\n  }\n  return instantiateArrayBuffer(binaryFile,imports)\n}\n```\n\nAnd `createWasm`:\n```js\nasync function createWasm(){\n  function receiveInstance(instance,module){...removeRunDependency(\"wasm-instantiate\");return wasmExports}\n  addRunDependency(\"wasm-instantiate\");\n  function receiveInstantiationResult(result){return receiveInstance(result[\"instance\"])}\n  var info=getWasmImports();\n  if(Module[\"instantiateWasm\"]){...}\n  wasmBinaryFile??=findWasmBinary();\n  var result=await instantiateAsync(wasmBinary,wasmBinaryFile,info);\n  var exports=receiveInstantiationResult(result);\n  return exports\n}\n```\n\nSo `createWasm` is async and is called at module load (top-level, I believe). Let me check: is `createWasm()` called at the top level of the recast glue, or is it lazy?\n\nActually, in the recast glue, the last line I saw was:\n```js\nif(runtimeInitialized){moduleRtn=Module}else{moduleRtn=new Promise((resolve,reject)=>{readyPromiseResolve=resolve;readyPromiseReject=reject})}\n```\n\nSo `moduleRtn` is the returned Promise. But where is `createWasm()` invoked and where does `readyPromiseResolve` get called? Let me find the `run` function and its invocation in the recast glue.\n\nLet me grep for the run function and its invocation in the recast glue.\n","seq":121155,"t":7035499,"text":"","timings":{"cache_n":74240,"draft_n":2443,"draft_n_accepted":941,"predicted_ms":31580.0,"predicted_n":1290,"prompt_ms":24300.0,"prompt_n":16270},"to_request":120484,"usage":{"cached_tokens":74240,"completion_tokens":1290,"prompt_tokens":90510}}
