ionPluginAsync({ locateFile: () => \"/recast-navigation.wasm\" });`\n\nBoth are the targets. Let me quote the Havok one as the primary (it's where I'll start the Promise.all) and mention the nav one.\n\nLet me just quote the contiguous Havok block since it's the cleanest verbatim anchor, and add pointers for the rest.\n\nPOINTERs:\n- `scene.fixedDeltaMs = 1000 / PHYSICS_FPS` — sets the fixed physics timestep; if the game loop's physics stops stepping, this is where to look (scene252.ts, main()).\n- The `mark()` helper and `__initStart` — temporary instrumentation I added to diagnose the hang; must be removed before commit per GUIDANCE §0b (scene252.ts, main()).\n- `createFpsTerrain(engine, world)` + `mark(\"terrain\")` — terrain init (1024 static bodies) is synchronous and fast (<90ms per the user's markers), which rules out init cost as the hang (scene252.ts, main()).\n- The `rayVsCapsule` end-cap code (cap() helper) — the rewritten capsule hit-test; unrelated to the current hang but the place to look if bot shooting misbehaves (scene252.ts, rayVsCapsule).\n- `player.staticFriction = 0; player.dynamicFriction = 0.1;` — Quake-style slide tuning via controller fields (scene252.ts, main()).\n\nLet me write the response.\n","seq":130730,"t":7552056,"text":"\n\nEXCERPT:\n```ts\n    // Physics world (Havok V2 wasm served from the lab root).\n    const hknp = await HavokPhysics({ locateFile: () => \"/HavokPhysics.wasm\" });\n    const world = createHavokWorld(scene, hknp, { x: 0, y: -GRAVITY, z: 0 });\n    mark(\"havok\");\n```\nand, further down (the other half of the fix):\n```ts\n    // Navigation — navmesh from the terrain mesh; bots are NavCrowd agents driving controllers.\n    const nav = await createNavigationPluginAsync({ locateFile: () => \"/recast-navigation.wasm\" });\n    mark(\"nav-plugin\");\n```\n\nThese two `await`s are the target of my planned change: I intend to load Havok and the nav plugin concurrently (`Promise.all`) so the recast wasm — the second module, which is where the browser hangs — doesn't serialize behind the ~2MB Havok compile. The `world`/`terrain`/`player` lines in between depend on `hknp`, so the restructure has to keep those after the Havok leg resolves.\n\nPOINTER: `scene.fixedDeltaMs = 1000 / PHYSICS_FPS` — the fixed physics timestep; if player/bot movement ever stops stepping, this is the first thing to check (scene252.ts, `main()`).\nPOINTER: the `mark()` helper + `__initStart` + every `console.warn` stage marker are temporary instrumentation I added to diagnose this hang — they must be deleted before commit per GUIDANCE §0b (scene252.ts, `main()`).\nPOINTER: `mark(\"terrain\")` printing at +90ms confirms the 1024-body `createFpsTerrain` is fast and synchronous — rules out init cost as the hang, keeping the diagnosis on the recast wasm load (scene252.ts, `main()`).\nPOINTER: the `cap()` end-cap helper + `tb`/`tt` block is the rewritten `rayVsCapsule` (cylindrical band + two end-cap spheres) — unrelated to the hang, but the place to look if bot hit-detection misbehaves later (scene252.ts, `rayVsCapsule`).\nPOINTER: `player.staticFriction = 0; player.dynamicFriction = 0.1;` — Quake slide tuned via the controller's public friction fields, not shape masks (scene252.ts, `main()`).","timings":{"cache_n":111616,"draft_n":3619,"draft_n_accepted":1425,"predicted_ms":50710.0,"predicted_n":1942,"prompt_ms":1040.0,"prompt_n":174},"to_request":129687,"usage":{"cached_tokens":111616,"completion_tokens":1942,"prompt_tokens":111790}}
