should I keep the `mark(\"nav-plugin\")` and other markers? Yes, keep them for now (they're diagnostic). I'll remove them once fixed.\n\nLet me make the edit.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the exact edit. Current:\n```js\n    // Physics world (Havok V2 wasm served from the lab root).\n    const hknp = await HavokPhysics({ locateFile: () => \"/HavokPhysics.wasm\" });\n    const world = createHavokWorld(scene, hknp, { x: 0, y: -GRAVITY, z: 0 });\n    mark(\"havok\");\n```\nand later:\n```js\n    // Navigation — navmesh from the terrain mesh; bots are NavCrowd agents driving controllers.\n    const nav = await createNavigationPluginAsync({ locateFile: () => \"/recast-navigation.wasm\" });\n    mark(\"nav-plugin\");\n```\n\nNew:\n```js\n    // Physics world (Havok V2 wasm) and navigation plugin (Recast wasm) are\n    // independent loads — kick off the Recast load now so the two wasm modules\n    // compile in parallel instead of serially (a second streaming compile after\n    // Havok hangs in some browsers).\n    const navPromise = createNavigationPluginAsync({ locateFile: () => \"/recast-navigation.wasm\" });\n    const hknp = await HavokPhysics({ locateFile: () => \"/HavokPhysics.wasm\" });\n    const world = createHavokWorld(scene, hknp, { x: 0, y: -GRAVITY, z: 0 });\n    mark(\"havok\");\n```\nand later:\n```js\n    // Navigation — navmesh from the terrain mesh; bots are NavCrowd agents driving controllers.\n    const nav = await navPromise;\n    mark(\"nav-plugin\");\n```\n\nThis is clean. Let me do it.\n\nWait, but I want to be more confident this is the right fix. Let me reconsider whether there's a way to verify the \"streaming\" hypothesis without a browser.\n\nActually — I can check the recast glue's `instantiateAsync` once more to confirm the fallback path exists and is correct (so that if I force it, it works). I already confirmed:\n```js\nasync function instantiateAsync(binary,binaryFile,imports){\n  if(!binary&&typeof WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming==\