{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Let me organize the situation.\n\nPhase: test. Task: diagnose the scene252 initialization hang (spinner stops after the \"terrain\" marker, the nav-plugin marker is never printed, no error).\n\nEvidence gathered so far in this session:\n- The markers in scene252.ts's main() are: engine (+22ms), havok (+64ms), terrain (+90ms), then it hangs at `createNavigationPluginAsync` (served line 154 / disk line 194).\n- All three assets return 200; the recast wasm that's served is byte-identical to lab/public and the real file, and its content-type is application/wasm.\n- scene170–175 are recast-only and work; scene252 is the only scene that loads both Havok and recast.\n- Node test (lab/.smoke-tmp/load-order.mjs): Havok→recast loaded fine in 64ms with wasmBinary preloaded — no pure JS collision. Note: the Node test bypassed fetch/streaming (preloaded wasmBinary) and used WebAssembly.instantiate, not instantiateStreaming.\n- Recast's glue code (0.43.0) uses `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` first, falling back to `instantiateArrayBuffer` on error. If the streaming path hangs (never settles) rather than rejects, the fallback will never fire — this matches \"await never settles, no error.\"\n- Hypothesis: in the user's browser, `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` for the second wasm module (recast, after Havok) never settles. Alternative hypotheses: the dynamic imports inside `_ensureRecast` hang (unlikely — Vite pre-bundles; scene170 uses the same imports), or something else in scene252's context.\n\nOpen items:\n1. Root cause unconfirmed — the leading hypothesis (the second wasm's instantiateStreaming never settles after Havok) is unverified in the browser; the Node test bypassed streaming.\n2. Whether the fix (parallelizing the loads / forcing the ArrayBuffer path) actually works — requires a reload by the user.\n3. All the runtime items from earlier: mouse-look signs, HUD compositing, bot drift, debris rendering, respawn