ne.\" I'll just output the lines, maybe with a short header. Keep it tight.\n","seq":133235,"t":7699629,"text":"\n\nOPEN: Is the hang really the browser's `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` for the second wasm (recast after Havok) — my Node test pre-seeded `wasmBinary`, so it bypassed the streaming path and doesn't rule out a streaming-specific never-settling hang.\nOPEN: Could a synchronous hang between `mark(\"terrain\")` and the nav await (e.g. `createPhysicsCharacterController`) produce the identical symptom — not yet ruled out; needs a temp marker after player creation.\nOPEN: Do the three dynamic imports inside `_ensureRecast` (core / generators / `wasm/wasm` subpath) resolve in scene252's much larger module graph — assumed fine because scene170 works, but unverified here.\nOPEN: Will parallelizing the two wasm loads actually fix it — unverified, needs your reload.\nOPEN: The `console.warn` stage markers + `mark()` helper in `main()` are temporary instrumentation that must be deleted before commit (GUIDANCE §0b).\nOPEN: Scratch to delete before commit: `fps-smoke.cjs`, `.smoke-tmp/`, `lab/.smoke-tmp/`, `.smoke-home/`.\nOPEN: Lint/typecheck hasn't been re-run since the marker + `maxObstacles` edit batch.\nOPEN: Does scene252 need a rollup input / gallery card / thumbnail in `lab/vite.config.ts`, or is `getHtmlInputs()` auto-discovery sufficient — still unchecked.\nOPEN: All runtime behavior remains unverified (mouse-look signs, HUD compositing, bot drift re-sync, debris node write-back, respawn, audio, crosshair centering) — blocked on a successful load + your playtest.\nOPEN: The sandbox Vite watcher serves stale transforms — every edit needs a dev-server restart before you reload.\n\nNEXT: Edit `scene252.ts` — `Promise.all([HavokPhysics(...), createNavigationPluginAsync(...)])` so both wasm loads start concurrently, and add a temp `mark(\"player\")` after controller creation to rule out a synchronous hang before the nav await.\nNEXT: Restart the dev server (b