{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"The user wants me to reflect on the step I just completed and list any decisions I made, confirmed, or changed. Let me review what I did in this step.\n\nIn this step, I:\n1. Investigated the spinner hang — determined it's the recast wasm load (second wasm module after Havok) hanging in the browser, via `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming`.\n2. Ran a Node test proving Havok→recast loads fine (no JS collision).\n3. Verified the served wasm is valid.\n4. Confirmed scene252 is the only scene combining both wasm modules.\n5. Made a code change: parallelized the Havok and Recast loads (navPromise started before the Havok await).\n6. Restarted the dev server.\n\nThe decisions I made in THIS step:\n- DECISION: The root cause of the init hang is the recast wasm (second module) compiling via `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` after Havok — WHY: Node loads both fine (rules out JS collision), served wasm is valid, scene252 is the only scene combining both, and terrain init was fast.\n- DECISION: Fix by loading the two independent wasm modules in parallel (start `createNavigationPluginAsync` before awaiting `HavokPhysics`) — WHY: avoids serializing the two streaming compiles, which is the likely trigger.\n- DECISION: Restarted the dev server after editing — WHY: the stale-transform gotcha (watcher doesn't pick up edits in this sandbox).\n\nThese are decisions from this step. Let me list them. The reflection asks specifically about \"how this project is built — an API choice, a convention, a structure, a tooling choice, a workaround.\"\n\nThe parallel-load change is a structural/tooling decision. The root-cause diagnosis is a decision about the build. The dev server restart is a tooling workaround.\n\nLet me list each on its own line.\n","seq":134547,"t":7767986,"text":"\n\nDECISION: The scene252 init hang is the Recast wasm (the second wasm module) stalling in `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` after Havok has compiled — WHY: Node loads Havok→recast cleanly in 64ms (rules out a JS/wasm collision), the served recast wasm is valid (correct `application/wasm` MIME, identical bytes), scene252 is the only scene combining both modules (170–175 are recast-only), and terrain init was fast (<90ms), so the stall is the browser-side second streaming compile.\nDECISION: Load the two independent wasm modules in parallel — start `createNavigationPluginAsync` (assign to `navPromise`) before awaiting `HavokPhysics`, then `await navPromise` later — WHY: it stops serializing the two streaming compiles, which is the likely trigger, and is also a genuine init-speed improvement.\nDECISION: Restart the lab dev server (stop bg_ec39a3f1, relaunch as bg_08df777b on :5182) after editing scene252.ts — WHY: the long-running Vite watcher serves stale transforms in this sandbox, so the served code must match disk before the user reloads.","timings":{"cache_n":117504,"draft_n":1239,"draft_n_accepted":505,"predicted_ms":18050.0,"predicted_n":682,"prompt_ms":1060.0,"prompt_n":221},"to_request":134182,"usage":{"cached_tokens":117504,"completion_tokens":682,"prompt_tokens":117725}}
