ation\tfiles: listed node_modules/@recast-navigation\nmechanical/package.json\tfiles: package.json\nmechanical/packages/babylon-lite/package.json\tfiles: packages/babylon-lite/package.json\nmechanical/tests/lite/parity/bundle-size.spec.ts\tfiles: tests/lite/parity/bundle-size.spec.ts\nr109646/call_1fbb82370ed6484a973e2436/gotcha\taddBoxObstacle/addCylinderObstacle (navigation.ts:647/663) throw \"Navmesh has no tile cache. Build with `maxObstacles > 0` to enable obstacles.\" unless createNavMesh was given maxObstacles > 0 — tile-cache config also needs tileSize + expectedLayersPerTime per navigation.ts:255 (doc example line 21: { maxObstacles: 32, tileSize: 32 }). scene252 builds a solo navmesh and calls addBoxObstacle in destroyTerrainTile → first terrain shot will throw. This is a runtime bug, NOT the init-spinner hang (which is still being diagnosed via stage markers).\nr11177/call_83149a63ed4b48e18cc9a43c/decision\tScope: turn the getting-started example into a Quake-style FPS as a new lab demo (lab/lite/, not a parity scene). Terrain is procedurally generated from noise and destructible. AI bots are in scope for this iteration; multiplayer is explicitly deferred (\"bots first, multiplayer later\").\nr22627/call_731f2ddafab24ab79ace0962/plan\tFPS plan (Quake-style, tile-removal terrain) — new lab demo, NO engine changes:\\n\\nFILES (all new, under ~/git/reference/Babylon/Babylon-Lite):\\n1. lab/lite/scene252.html — copy scene18.html pattern (canvas + /loader.js + module script); auto-discovered by getHtmlInputs() in lab/vite.config.ts. Next free number after scene251.\\n2. lab/lite/src/lite/scene252.ts — main scene: 4-phase scaffold (createEngine → build → registerScene → startEngine), Havok world (locateFile \"/HavokPhysics.wasm\"), player, bots, shooting, HUD, game loop.\\n3. lab/lite/src/lite/fps-terrain.ts — noise terrain + tile removal: build grid (~256×256 verts over 128×128u), tiles 4×4u → 32×32 = 1024 tiles; per-tile static box bodies (createPhysicsAggregate mass 0, top at tile max height); destroy = remove tile's index range from _cpuIndices, computeNormals, uploadMeshToGPU, removePhysicsBody, addBoxObstacle on navmesh.\\n4. lab/lite/src/lite/fps-input.ts — pointer lock + keyboard state (DOM-side; no engine input module exists).\\n5. lab/lite/src/lite/fps-audio.ts — Web Audio SFX (gunshot, thud, hit), lazy-init on first gesture, no module-level side effects.\\n\\nSTEPS:\\nS1 Verify remaining API details (read-only): frame-observable name (scene18), physicsRaycast query shape (havok-queries.ts:207), NavMeshParameters usage (scene170), whether controller exposes its shape for friction, bundle-size spec doesn't cover lab scenes.\\nS2 fps-terrain.ts: seeded value-noise heights, low-frequency (amp ~5u); createFlatGroundData → mutate positions → computeNormals → uploadMeshToGPU; per-tile static boxes + membership/collide masks; destroyTile() index surgery + re-upload + body removal + nav obstacle.\\nS3 scene252.ts: engine/scene/light/camera scaffold; createHavokWorld; terrain via fps-terrain; player = createPhysicsCharacterController (capsule 1.8/0.5), Quake movement in onPhysicsAfterStep (slide friction, air control, jump gated by checkSupport supportedState); camera follow w/ pointer-lock yaw/pitch.\\nS4 Shooting: click → ray from eye; physicsRaycast for terrain (hit → destroyTile), manual ray-capsule vs bots (closest wins); fire-rate limit; hit/kill feedback.\\nS5 Bots: createNavigationPluginAsync (recast-navigation.wasm) + createNavMesh from terrain mesh; N=4 bots = character controller + NavCrowd agent (agentGoto/findRandomPoint, updateNavCrowd per step); display = thin instances; bots LOS-check player (physicsRaycast) and shoot with distance-based accuracy; damage/respawn both sides.\\nS6 HUD: createTextLayer/createTextRenderer (pattern from scenes 180/181) — health, kills, tiles destroyed; crosshair.\\nS7 fps-audio.ts wired to events.\\nS8 Dev server: LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm dev:lab (vite config reads LAB_DEV_PORT, default 5174); manual playtest checklist: move/slide/jump, mouse look, shoot holes, fall through → respawn, debris, bots patrol+shoot, HUD, audio. Add canvas.dataset.ready/error like scene40 for scriptability.\\n\\nCHECKS: typecheck (repo script), manual playtest on :5182/lite/scene252.html, confirm bundle-size.spec.ts unaffected, no module-level side effects, no raw GPU handles in scene code.\\n\\nRISKS: 1024 static bodies init cost (fallback: 8×8u tiles → 256 bodies); navmesh from dense mesh (tune NavMeshParameters); controller shape access for friction (fallback: low friction on terrain tile shapes).\nr25861/call_7a361bc371cf49e581771afd/decision\tTerrain destruction = tile removal (user-approved): index surgery on one dense grid mesh + per-tile static box physics bodies; destroy = drop tile's indices, recompute normals, re-upload, removePhysicsBody, addBoxObstacle on navmesh. No engine changes — everything via existing public API. Arena 128×128u, tiles 4×4u (1024 tiles), mesh ~256×256 verts; fallback to 8×8u tiles if static-body init is slow.\nr35651/call_65a9672390dd40b18139c3bd/gotcha\tPhysicsCharacterController exposes friction as public fields (staticFriction default 0, dynamicFriction default 1); its capsule _shape is private. Quake-style slide = set cc.dynamicFriction low (e.g. 0.2) directly — no setPhysicsShapeMaterial on tile shapes needed, and no shape access to hunt for. Plan's \"controller-shape friction if exposed\" is satisfied via the fields, not via a shape.\nr35651/call_6ab8a776fbbe4ff0996cd2e4/gotcha\tTwo distinct text paths exist: scene180 uses createTextRenderer (standalone 2D overlay, no scene/camera) while scene181 uses createTextRenderable + addTextRenderable(scene, text) (in-scene world-space text). The plan lumped them as \"createTextLayer/createTextRenderer\" — for the HUD I must decide screen-space (180) vs world-space (181) and verify whether a TextRenderer composites over a 3D scene before writing S6.\nr35651/call_847e6d8ad46a49e8a9bd38d6/gotcha\tresizeMeshGeometry(engine, mesh, positions, normals, indices, uvs?, ...) in mesh-factories.ts:104 is the correct in-place geometry-swap seam for tile removal — it bumps every registered scene's _renderableVersion (so cached draw bundles re-record) and defers old-buffer destruction until submitted work drains. Raw uploadMeshToGPU + manual mesh._gpu assignment would leave cached bundles binding freed buffers (\"Buffer used in submit while destroyed\") — the plan's S2 \"uploadMeshToGPU\" step must use resizeMeshGeometry instead.\nr37345/call_0005a55ea369431eb2e302a4/gotcha\tFreeCamera has no public yaw/pitch — only @internal _yaw/_pitch (free-camera.ts:31-33); orientation is yaw/pitch-derived, `target` is only initial data. FPS mouse look must write cam._yaw/cam._pitch directly each frame (lab scene code may read/write @internal fields per dogma); exact sign convention vs view-matrix build still to verify before playtest.\nr37345/call_2fa6327821d246d6aeadf5c1/gotcha\tThe plan's terrain re-upload seam (raw uploadMeshToGPU + mesh._gpu swap) is wrong: raw swap leaves cached draw bundles binding freed buffers. The intended seam is resizeMeshGeometry(engine, mesh, positions, normals, indices, uvs?) (mesh-factories.ts) — reallocates buffers, defers old-buffer destruction until GPU drain, bumps _renderableVersion on all registered scenes so cached bundles re-record, and refreshes _cpuPositions/_cpuNormals/_cpuIndices. destroyTile() must use it.\nr37345/call_4bf6d56016a941f899f27e39/gotcha\tcreatePhysicsAggregate is typed `node: Mesh` (havok.ts:1141) — per-tile static boxes can't use it on invisible transform nodes. Per-tile bodies need the manual path: createTransformNode + createPhysicsBody(world, node, PhysicsMotionType.STATIC) + createPhysicsShape(BOX, {extents}) + setPhysicsBodyShape — the same pattern the character controller uses internally (character-controller.ts constructor).\nr37345/call_532b6495b9ae43068115bf7f/decision\tController friction IS exposed — as public fields on PhysicsCharacterController: staticFriction (default 0) and dynamicFriction (default 1), plus maxSlopeCosine. Quake-style slide = tune cc.staticFriction/dynamicFriction per controller; no engine change, no need for the terrain-shape-friction fallback (though low tile-shape friction still helps consistency).\nr37345/call_7509c67d5e9749b1b0a76431/gotcha\tscene180's text path is standalone 2D (no scene, no camera — TextRenderer on the canvas alone). An in-scene HUD must use scene181's path: createTextRenderable(data, {opacity}) + addTextRenderable(scene, text) — text lives in WORLD space (position + scaling), so screen-locked HUD elements (health/kills/crosshair) need per-frame repositioning relative to the camera, unless a 2D TextRenderer can be verified to layer over a 3D scene (unverified).\nr41338/call_caa2ea0f76064dc3b0e7fa9c/constraint\tS1 constraints surfaced: (1) terrain re-upload must use resizeMeshGeometry (bumps _renderableVersion + defers buffer destruction; raw uploadMeshToGPU+_gpu swap keeps cached bundles binding freed buffers); (2) per-tile static bodies need TransformNode + createPhysicsBody(STATIC)+createPhysicsShape+setPhysicsBodyShape — createPhysicsAggregate requires a Mesh node; (3) in-scene HUD = createTextRenderable+addTextRenderable (scene181), NOT createTextRenderer (scene180 is standalone 2D); (4) FPS mouse-look writes FreeCamera @internal _yaw/_pitch directly (no public rotation API); (5) scene.fixedDeltaMs must be set or moveWithCollisions/integrate are no-ops. Decision: controller friction via public staticFriction/dynamicFriction fields (defaults 0/1) — resolves plan's friction-shape risk.\nr63189/call_341bf58c985441b5a75ca83a/gotcha\tPlaywright smoke scripts in this sandbox: (1) system temp dir /var/folders/.../T is write-blocked — run node with TMPDIR pointed at a repo-local dir (e.g. TMPDIR=\"$PWD/.smoke-tmp\" node fps-smoke.cjs) or chromium.launch({tmpDir}) alone is not enough; (2) the repo's Playwright browser cache is missing the chromium headless shell — must run `pnpm exec playwright install` (never npx, per the rogue node_modules/playwright gotcha) before any Playwright launch works.\nr63755/call_be86e39b5d5c4e11ad52368a/gotcha\tOperational gotchas this session (sandbox + tooling): (1) `pnpm dev:lab` EPERMs (tsx IPC pipe in system temp) — use `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite` from lab/ instead; (2) sandbox blocks /tmp and /var/folders T — scratch files go in-repo (delete before commit), node needs TMPDIR in-repo; (3) Playwright default launch fails (cached browser build 1243 vs playwright 1.58.2 expecting 1208) — launch `channel: \"chrome\"` + `--enable-unsafe-webgpu` (repo idiom); (4) computeNormals is number[]-based and createFlatGroundData/computeNormals need subpath imports (babylon-lite/mesh/*.js), not the barrel.\nr65273/call_1e7cec3d3238496f8a89ec80/gotcha\tBrowser automation is blocked in this sandbox: Playwright mkdtemp fails (sandbox denies /var/folders/T), bundled chromium build missing (cache has 1243, playwright 1.58.2 wants 1208), and system Chrome (channel: \"chrome\", headed or headless) SIGABRTs at launch because crashpad bootstrap + ~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome are EPERM. IMPLICATION: no Playwright smoke/playtest possible this session — validation is lint + typecheck + user manual playtest on :5182.\nr65273/call_e94c2b70aad3480cb99b67bb/gotcha\t`pnpm dev:lab` fails in this sandbox (its tsx bundle-build step needs an IPC pipe in the system temp dir → EPERM). Working alternative: `cd lab && LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite` (verified serving on 5182, scene252.html → 200).\nr91558/call_1569cb1f591a4fe682afe311/decision\tSelf-hit problem solved via muzzle offset, not layer filtering: the character controller's capsule shape is private (can't call setPhysicsShapeFilterMembershipMask on it) and its default membership is ~0 (belongs to every layer), so a physicsRaycast can never be filtered to exclude the player's own capsule. Fix: cast the bullet ray from a point MUZZLE_OFFSET (0.8) in front of the eye (outside the 0.5 capsule radius) so the ray never starts inside the player body. EYE_HEIGHT set to 0.7 (eye near head, center+0.7).\nr91784/call_04d1c180396b4941b6968645/gotcha\tBrowser automation is blocked in this sandbox: Playwright's bundled chromium build is missing (cache has 1243, playwright 1.58.2 wants 1208) and system Chrome (channel:\"chrome\") SIGABRTs at launch because crashpad's Mach bootstrap_check_in + ~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad are EPERM-denied. IMPLICATION: no Playwright smoke/playtest possible this session — validation is lint + typecheck + dev-server module-graph resolution (curl each module through vite, confirm 200 + imports resolve to /@fs/... source paths).\nr91869/call_dfb9616e51df42a6bdb365a4/gotcha\tThe long-running vite dev server's file watcher does NOT pick up edits in this sandbox — it kept serving a stale transform (EYE_HEIGHT 1.5) after I changed the file on disk (EYE_HEIGHT 0.7). IMPLICATION: after editing scene files, restart the dev server (task_stop + relaunch `cd lab && LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite`) before playtesting, or verify served content via curl rather than assuming HMR worked.\n24 older entries shortened\n","render_budget_tokens":40000,"render_fits":true,"render_over_budget":"tier","render_reduced":24,"render_tokens":39984,"seq":137509,"t":8156816,"tail_tokens":4000,"tool_outputs":"reference","turn_steps_compacted":0,"turn_steps_kept":1,"window":163840}
