ports:\n```\nimport(\"@recast-navigation/core\")\nimport(\"@recast-navigation/generators\")\nimport(\"@recast-navigation/wasm/wasm\")\n```\n\nThese are resolved by Vite at transform time. When I moved `createNavigationPluginAsync` to be called EARLIER (before `await HavokPhysics`), the module graph is the SAME (the function is still imported at the top). So no change there.\n\nHmm. But actually — the dynamic imports are resolved the same regardless of when the function is called. So no.\n\nOK, let me just verify all the modules and the HTML. Let me curl them all.\n\nActually, you know what — let me reconsider the possibility that this is a **browser cache / stale module** issue and the simplest fix is to have the user hard-reload. But the user already reloaded 3 times.\n\nLet me verify the dependency modules transform correctly. If one of them is broken (e.g., a Vite transform error), that would block the whole module graph.\n\nLet me curl fps-terrain.js, fps-audio.js, fps-input.js, and check the HTML.\n\nLet me do that now.\n","seq":138937,"t":8346505,"text":"\n\nThe served entry transform is complete and correct (ends with `main().catch(...)`), and my change sits *after* `createEngine` — so it can't stop the \"engine\" marker from printing. That means the module graph itself isn't executing: one of the *imported* modules is likely failing to load/transform, which blocks the whole entry before `main()` runs. Let me check every dependency and the HTML page.\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":0,"draft_n":10101,"draft_n_accepted":2956,"predicted_ms":81710.0,"predicted_n":4399,"prompt_ms":107510.0,"prompt_n":93676},"to_request":137510,"usage":{"cached_tokens":0,"completion_tokens":4399,"prompt_tokens":93676}}
