{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"The user wants me to reflect on the step I just completed (my last message and its tool activity) and list any decisions I made, confirmed, or changed about how this project is built.\n\nLet me reflect on what I did in my last step:\n1. I stopped the dev server (bg_08df777b).\n2. I ran `vite build` in the background — it completed successfully in ~16s, producing `dist/`.\n3. I verified the build output: `dist/lite/scene252.html`, `dist/assets/lite/scene252-Q0CsJAaq.js`, and the wasm + font assets copied to `dist/`.\n4. I started `vite preview --port 5182 --strictPort` in the background.\n\nDecisions made in this step:\n- DECISION: Use a production build (`vite build`) + `vite preview` served on port 5182 instead of the Vite dev server — WHY: the dev server transforms modules on demand and is too slow to load within the browser's ~8-second window (confirmed by scene2/scene40 also stalling), whereas a pre-bundled static build loads fast.\n- DECISION: The build emits `dist/lite/scene252.html` (keyed by `lite/scene252` from `getHtmlInputs()`), not `dist/scene252.html` — WHY: `getHtmlInputs()` maps `lite/*.html` to `lite/<name>` input keys, so the preview URL is `/lite/scene252.html`.\n- DECISION: `vite preview` needs `--port 5182 --strictPort` because the config only sets `server.port` (dev), not `preview.port` — WHY: preview defaults to 4173, so the port must be passed on the CLI to honor the session's 5182 rule.\n- DECISION: The production build copies `public/` (HavokPhysics.wasm, recast-navigation.wasm, fonts/Inter.ttf) into `dist/` — WHY: Vite copies the publicDir to outDir by default, so the wasm/font assets are served alongside the static build with no extra config.\n\nWait — are these \"decisions about how this project is built\"? Let me reconsider. The user asks specifically about decisions on \"how this project is built — an API choice, a convention, a structure, a tooling choice, a workaround.\"\n\nLet me filter:\n1. Production build + preview on 5182 instead of dev server — this is a tooling choice / workaround. YES, this is a decision.\n2. The build output path (`dist/lite/scene252.html`) — this is a structure fact I confirmed, not really a \"decision I made.\" But it's a confirmed structural fact about the build. Hmm. It's more of a confirmation than a decision. But it's relevant to how the project is built/served.\n3. `vite preview --port 5182 --strictPort` — this is a tooling choice (CLI flag) to honor the port rule. YES.\n4. `public/` copied to `dist/` — this is a confirmed fact about Vite's default behavior, not a decision I made. But it's relevant.\n\nLet me reconsider what counts as a \"decision\" here. The user wants decisions I MADE, CONFIRMED, or CHANGED. So confirmed facts count too.\n\nLet me list the meaningful ones:\n- DECISION: Serve a production build (`vite build` → `vite preview`) on 5182 instead of the Vite dev server — WHY: the dev server's on-demand transforms are too slow for the browser's ~8s load window (scene2/scene40 also stall), while the static pre-bundled build loads fast.\n- DECISION: The preview port must be passed as `--port 5182 --strictPort` on the CLI — WHY: the lab's vite.config.ts only configures `server.port` (dev), not `preview.port`, so preview would otherwise default to 4173 and violate the session's 5182 rule.\n- DECISION (confirmed): the build outputs the lab scenes under `dist/lite/` (e.g. `dist/lite/scene252.html`) keyed by `getHtmlInputs()` — WHY: `getHtmlInputs()` maps `lite/*.html` to `lite/<name>` rollup input keys, so the preview URL is `/lite/scene252.html`, not `/scene252.html`.\n- DECISION (confirmed): the wasm + font assets (HavokPhysics.wasm, recast-navigation.wasm, fonts/Inter.ttf) are copied from `lab/public/` into `dist/` by Vite's default publicDir handling — WHY: so the static build serves them at the same root paths (`/HavokPhysics.wasm`, `/recast-navigation.wasm`, `/fonts/Inter.ttf`) the scene code expects via `locateFile`.\n\nThese are all decisions/facts from this step about how the project is built/served.\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether I should include the \"confirmed\" ones. The user said \"Did you make, confirm, or change any decision about how this project is built.\" So confirmed decisions count. The build output structure and the publicDir copy are confirmed facts about the build. I'll include them but mark them as confirmed.\n\nLet me be concise and list each on its own line.\n\nActually, I want to make sure I'm only listing decisions from THIS step (the last message and its tool activity), not earlier ones. My last message was:\n- Stopping the dev server + starting the build (bg_f720c9bb).\n- Checking build progress (completed in 15.96s).\n- Verifying dist/ assets.\n- Finding scene252.html is at dist/lite/scene252.html.\n- Starting vite preview --port 5182 --strictPort (bg_9133947c).\n\nSo the decisions from this step are:\n1. Production build + preview on 5182 (the main approach).\n2. Preview port via CLI flag.\n3. Build output structure (dist/lite/scene252.html).\n4. publicDir copy to dist/.\n\nLet me write these out concisely.\n\nI should keep it focused and not over-list. Let me list the 4 meaningful ones.\n","seq":147453,"t":8908789,"text":"\n\nDECISION: Serve a production build (`vite build` → `vite preview`) on 5182 instead of the Vite dev server — WHY: the dev server's on-demand transforms are too slow for the browser's ~8s load window (scene2/scene40 also stall), while the pre-bundled static build loads fast.\nDECISION: Pass the preview port as `--port 5182 --strictPort` on the CLI — WHY: the lab's vite.config.ts only sets `server.port` (dev), not `preview.port`, so preview would otherwise default to 4173 and break the session's 5182 rule.\nDECISION (confirmed): the build emits lab scenes under `dist/lite/` (e.g. `dist/lite/scene252.html`), so the preview URL is `/lite/scene252.html` — WHY: `getHtmlInputs()` maps `lite/*.html` to `lite/<name>` rollup input keys, not flat names.\nDECISION (confirmed): the wasm + font assets (`HavokPhysics.wasm`, `recast-navigation.wasm`, `fonts/Inter.ttf`) are copied from `lab/public/` into `dist/` by Vite's default publicDir handling — WHY: so the static build serves them at the same root paths the scene code requests via `locateFile`, with no extra config.","timings":{"cache_n":118784,"draft_n":2674,"draft_n_accepted":1344,"predicted_ms":39210.0,"predicted_n":1726,"prompt_ms":1060.0,"prompt_n":194},"to_request":146678,"usage":{"cached_tokens":118784,"completion_tokens":1726,"prompt_tokens":118978}}
