{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Let me reflect on the step I just completed — the last message and its tool activity.\n\nIn this step, I:\n1. Stopped the slow dev server (bg_08df777b).\n2. Ran `vite build` in `lab/` (production build) → `dist/`.\n3. Started `vite preview --port 5182 --strictPort` to serve the static build.\n4. Verified all assets served 200.\n\nNow, did I make, confirm, or change any decision about how this project is built — an API choice, a convention, a structure, a tooling choice, a workaround?\n\nLet me think about what decisions were made in THIS step:\n\n1. **DECISION: Serve the lab via a production build (`vite build` → `vite preview`) on port 5182 instead of the Vite dev server** — WHY: the dev server transforms modules on demand and is too slow to serve within the browser's ~8-second window, while a pre-bundled static build loads fast.\n\nThis is a tooling choice / workaround decision. It's about how the project is served/tested.\n\n2. **DECISION: The preview server uses `--port 5182 --strictPort`** — WHY: to keep the session's port 5182 rule and avoid auto-increment.\n\nHmm, is this a separate decision? It's part of the same decision (serving on 5182). I could fold it in.\n\n3. **DECISION: Keep the stage markers (console.warn) in the production build** — WHY: they're still needed to diagnose where the init hangs, and will be removed before commit per GUIDANCE §0b.\n\nThis is a decision about what to include in the build. It's a workaround/diagnostic choice.\n\nLet me reconsider — the question asks specifically about \"how this project is built — an API choice, a convention, a structure, a tooling choice, a workaround.\"\n\nThe main decision in this step is the tooling choice: use a production build + preview server instead of the dev server for serving/testing.\n\nLet me also reconsider: did I make a decision about the build itself? The build used the existing `vite build` config (which builds all HTML inputs via `getHtmlInputs()`). I didn't change the build config. So no decision there.\n\nLet me list the decisions:\n\n1. DECISION: Serve the lab for playtesting via a production build (`vite build` in `lab/` → `vite preview` on :5182) rather than the Vite dev server — WHY: the dev server's on-demand transforms are too slow to load within the browser's ~8-second window, while the pre-bundled static build loads fast.\n\n2. DECISION: Keep the temporary `console.warn` stage markers in the production build for now — WHY: they're still needed to pinpoint which init await hangs, and will be stripped before commit per GUIDANCE §0b.\n\nAre there any others? Let me think...\n\n- The choice to use `vite preview` (vs. a different static server like `serve` or `python -m http.server`) — this is part of decision 1 (using Vite's own preview is the natural tooling choice since the build is Vite's).\n\n- The `--strictPort` flag — part of decision 1.\n\nI think the two main decisions are:\n1. Production build + preview instead of dev server (tooling choice / workaround).\n2. Keep stage markers in the build (diagnostic workaround).\n\nLet me also reconsider whether \"serving on 5182\" is a decision. The session rule is port 5182, so that's not a new decision — it's a constraint. The decision is to use preview (not dev) on that port.\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether the preview-vs-dev decision is really about \"how this project is built.\" It's more about how it's served/tested. But the question says \"an API choice, a convention, a structure, a tooling choice, a workaround\" — a tooling choice for serving/testing fits.\n\nLet me finalize my list. I'll list the two decisions.\n\nActually, I want to be careful not to over-list. Let me focus on the genuine decisions:\n\n1. The production-build + preview server approach (instead of dev server) — this is the key tooling decision.\n2. Keeping the stage markers in the build — this is a diagnostic decision.\n\nBoth are from this step. Let me write them.\n\nWait — is keeping the markers really a \"decision about how this project is built\"? It's about what content is in the build. It's a workaround (keeping debug code temporarily). I think it qualifies as a workaround decision.\n\nLet me write the response concisely.\n","seq":148252,"t":8958235,"text":"\n\nDECISION: Serve the lab for playtesting via a production build (`vite build` in `lab/` → `vite preview --port 5182 --strictPort`) instead of the Vite dev server — WHY: the dev server's on-demand module transforms are too slow to load within the browser's ~8-second window, while the pre-bundled static `dist/` loads fast.\nDECISION: Keep the temporary `console.warn` init-stage markers in the production build for now — WHY: they're still needed to pinpoint which init await hangs, and will be stripped before commit per GUIDANCE §0b.","timings":{"cache_n":120064,"draft_n":2135,"draft_n_accepted":880,"predicted_ms":19060.0,"predicted_n":1185,"prompt_ms":2810.0,"prompt_n":1375},"to_request":147943,"usage":{"cached_tokens":120064,"completion_tokens":1185,"prompt_tokens":121439}}
