window.innerWidth/innerHeight`, not `canvas.width/height`.\ninterview-t6-f85232-3\tgotcha: `setThinInstances` bumps `_version` and marks the whole matrix buffer dirty on each call — no separate flush needed, per-frame calls are safe — IMPLICATION: the open question on per-frame bot/debris matrix updates is resolved; just call it each frame.\ninterview-t6-f85232-4\tgotcha: browser automation (Playwright/Chrome) cannot launch in this sandbox — crashpad Mach bootstrap is denied and the cached browser build doesn't match the repo's Playwright — IMPLICATION: runtime verification must be lint + typecheck + a manual playtest on :5182, not a scripted browser smoke test.\ninterview-t6-f86326-0\tdecision: Bullet raycasts now originate from a muzzle point 0.8u in front of the eye (`MUZZLE_OFFSET`), not from the eye — WHY: the character controller's capsule shape is private and can't be filter-masked (default membership `~0`), so a ray starting inside the player's own capsule would hit the player capsule first and occlude every terrain hit.\ninterview-t6-f86326-1\tdecision: `EYE_HEIGHT` lowered from 1.5 to 0.7 above the capsule center — WHY: `getPosition()` returns the capsule *center*, so 1.5 floated the camera 0.6 above the head; 0.7 puts the eye near the head (~1.6m above ground when standing).\ninterview-t6-f86326-2\tdecision: Removed the `terr.hitDistance > 2` self-hit guard — WHY: the muzzle offset already guarantees the ray never starts inside the player capsule, so the distance-based workaround is redundant.\ninterview-t6-f86326-3\tdecision: `Debris.body` typed `PhysicsBody | null` (dropped the `null as unknown as PhysicsBody` cast) with null-guards in the render/expiry loops — WHY: debris slots start empty and only gain a body on spawn, so the type should reflect that instead of papering over it with a cast.\ninterview-t6-f86903-0\tconstraint: `PhysicsCharacterController`'s capsule shape is created internally (`_shape`, via `createPhysicsShape`) and is private — scene code cannot access or filter-mask it, so the player's/bots' controller capsules can never be excluded from `physicsRaycast` via collision layers; shooting rays must originate outside the player capsule (muzzle offset) to avoid self-hits.\ninterview-t6-f86903-1\tconstraint: `PhysicsCharacterController.getPosition()` returns the capsule **center**, not the feet — ground/feet level is `position.y - capsuleHeight/2`, so every eye-height, spawn, and ground computation must apply that half-height offset.\ninterview-t6-f86903-2\tconstraint: Shapes created via `createPhysicsShape` carry Havok's default all-layers filter (`~0`) because Lite never sets one — collision-layer filtering only excludes a shape if its membership is explicitly set with `setPhysicsShapeFilterMembershipMask`, so \"default\" never means \"excluded\".\ninterview-t6-f87832-0\tgotcha: `PhysicsCharacterController.getPosition()` returns the capsule **center** (shape spans center ± capsuleHeight/2), not the feet — IMPLICATION: eye height and spawn/respawn Y are offsets from the center (eye ≈ center + 0.7; spawn = terrainHeight + capsuleHeight/2), not from the ground plane.\ninterview-t6-f87832-1\tgotcha: the character controller's capsule shape is private (`_shape`) and its default filter membership is `~0` (belongs to every layer), so `physicsRaycast` cannot be filtered to exclude the player's own capsule — IMPLICATION: bullet rays must be cast from a muzzle offset in front of the eye (outside the 0.5 capsule radius) or the player's capsule occludes every terrain hit.\ninterview-t6-f87832-2\tgotcha: the long-running Vite dev server serves stale module transforms in this sandbox (its file watcher does not fire on disk edits) — IMPLICATION: restart the dev server after code changes before playtesting, or verify served content matches disk.\ninterview-t6-f87832-3\tgotcha: `setThinInstances` re-uploads via an internal `_version` bump + dirty range (no separate flush call) — IMPLICATION: per-frame `setThinInstances` calls are safe and sufficient for bot/debris matrices; no `flushThinInstances` needed.\ninterview-t6-f89559-0\tdecision: Bullet raycasts originate from a muzzle offset (0.8u in front of the eye) instead of the eye — WHY: the player's capsule has a default `~0` filter and a private shape that can't be filter-masked, so a ray starting inside the capsule would be occluded by the player's own body.\ninterview-t6-f89559-1\tdecision: `EYE_HEIGHT = 0.7` (near the head, above the capsule center) — WHY: realistic first-person eye height; with the muzzle offset, forward rays clear the player capsule.\ninterview-t6-f89559-2\tdecision: Rewrote `rayVsCapsule` as cylindrical-band + end-cap sphere tests — WHY: the original `u` (axis-parameter) formula was wrong and returned null for valid center hits, and it missed end-cap hits.\ninterview-t6-f89559-3\tdecision: Reset vertical velocity to 0 on floor contact (actual-drop vs requested-drop test) for both player and bots — WHY: otherwise fall speed accumulates every step while standing, so walking off a ledge starts a terminal-velocity fall.\ninterview-t6-f89559-4\tdecision: Crosshair placed via `window.innerWidth/innerHeight` (CSS pixels), not `canvas.width/height` — WHY: the canvas has fixed 1280×720 attributes but CSS stretches it to the viewport, and `positionPx` is in CSS pixels (scene180:82).\ninterview-t6-f89559-5\tdecision: Spawn/respawn at standing height (`terrainHeight + CAP_HEIGHT/2 + 0.1`) instead of 2u above — WHY: the controller's `getPosition()` is the capsule center, so feet-on-ground means center = ground + half-height.\ninterview-t6-f89559-6\tdecision: `Debris.body` typed `PhysicsBody | null` with explicit null guards — WHY: cleaner than the `null as unknown as PhysicsBody` cast and satisfies the typecheck.\ninterview-t6-f89559-7\tdecision: Restarted the lab dev server (bg_f4a1f424) — WHY: the long-running server's file watcher wasn't picking up edits in this sandbox and was serving stale transforms.\ninterview-t6-f89879-0\tconstraint: The character controller's capsule shape is private and carries Havok's default filter (membership `~0`, i.e. every layer), so it cannot be excluded from `physicsRaycast` via collision-layer masks — bullet rays must originate from a muzzle offset (in front of the eye, outside the capsule radius), never from the eye/center, or the player's own capsule occludes every terrain hit.\ninterview-t6-f89879-1\tconstraint: In this sandbox the long-running Vite dev server serves stale transformed modules (its file watcher does not fire on edits) — restart the dev server after editing scene files before verifying or playtesting, or you will test old code.\ninterview-t6-f89879-2\tconstraint: Chrome/Playwright cannot launch in this sandbox — crashpad's Mach `bootstrap_check_in` and `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad` are EPERM, so the browser SIGABRTs at start (headless and headed, regardless of `TMPDIR`/`HOME` overrides) — no browser-based verification is possible here; validate via lint/typecheck plus a user manual playtest on :5182.\ninterview-t6-f90466-0\tgotcha: No browser can launch in this sandbox — Playwright's bundled chromium is a build mismatch (cache has 1243, playwright 1.58.2 wants 1208) and system Chrome (`channel: \"chrome\"`, the repo's own idiom) SIGABRTs because crashpad's Mach bootstrap is denied (EPERM on `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad`); overriding HOME/TMPDIR doesn't help — IMPLICATION: no Playwright smoke/playtest is possible this session; validation is lint + typecheck + dev-server transform checks, and the real playtest falls to the user on :5182.\ninterview-t6-f90466-1\tgotcha: a long-running vite dev server serves stale module transforms after on-disk edits (its file watcher doesn't fire in the sandbox — scene252.ts kept serving `EYE_HEIGHT = 1.5` after I changed it) — IMPLICATION: after editing scene files, restart the dev-server background task (or curl the served transform and diff