{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Let me reflect on the step I just completed. I made an edit to scene252.html to add an inline script that creates a visible overlay element for init progress.\n\nDid I make, confirm, or change any decision about how this project is built?\n\nLet me think about what decisions were made in this step:\n\n1. I decided to render init progress as visible DOM text (an overlay div) rather than relying on console output — because the user's browser only captures screenshots and an empty console. This is a diagnostic approach decision.\n\n2. I decided to put the overlay element creation in an inline script in the HTML (before the module script) rather than in the module itself — so that we can distinguish \"HTML loaded but module never arrived\" from \"module loaded but init hangs.\" This is a structural/tooling decision.\n\nWait — but these are decisions I made in this step. Let me re-read the prompt: \"Did you make, confirm, or change any decision about how this project is built — an API choice, a convention, a structure, a tooling choice, a workaround?\"\n\nThe inline script approach is a workaround for the limited test browser. It's a diagnostic aid. Is it a \"decision about how this project is built\"? It's more of a diagnostic instrumentation decision. But it does change the structure of the HTML file (adding an inline script).\n\nHmm. Let me think about whether this counts. The prompt is asking me to record decisions. The key decision here is:\n\nDECISION: Render scene252's init progress + errors as visible on-page text (a fixed overlay div) instead of console output — WHY: the test browser only yields a screenshot and an empty console, so on-page text is the only observable channel.\n\nDECISION: Create the overlay element in an inline script in scene252.html (before the module script) rather than in the module — WHY: it lets a screenshot distinguish \"HTML loaded but module never arrived\" from \"module loaded but init hangs.\"\n\nThese are decisions I made in this step. Let me record them.\n\nActually — wait. Let me reconsider. The prompt says \"Only decisions from this step, not earlier ones.\" So I should only record decisions from THIS step (the edit I just made).\n\nIn this step, I:\n1. Decided to use on-page text (overlay) for init progress — because the browser only gives screenshots + empty console.\n2. Decided to put the overlay creation in an inline HTML script (before the module) — to distinguish HTML-loaded from module-loaded.\n\nBoth are decisions from this step. Let me record them.\n\nBut — I should be careful. The decision to use on-page text was prompted by the user's request (\"Could you make scene252 show its init progress and any error as text on the page itself\"). So it's somewhat user-directed. But the specific choice of HOW (inline script in HTML vs. module-level, the element structure, the error handlers) is my decision.\n\nLet me record the decisions concisely.\n\nActually — let me reconsider whether these are \"decisions about how this project is built.\" The inline script is a diagnostic aid that I'll presumably remove later (it's temporary instrumentation). So it's not a permanent build decision. But the prompt is asking me to record decisions, and these are decisions I made in this step.\n\nLet me record them. The key decisions:\n1. On-page overlay for init progress (vs. console) — because the test browser only captures screenshots + empty console.\n2. Inline script in HTML creates the overlay before the module — to distinguish HTML-loaded from module-loaded in a screenshot.\n\nLet me write these out.\n\nActually — I want to be precise. Let me think about whether there's a risk I'm over-recording. The prompt is specifically about \"how this project is built — an API choice, a convention, a structure, a tooling choice, a workaround.\" \n\nThe on-page overlay is a workaround (for the limited test browser). The inline script placement is a structural choice. Both qualify.\n\nLet me record them.\n","seq":153223,"t":9354863,"text":"\n\nDECISION: Render scene252's init progress and any error as visible on-page text (a fixed high-z-index overlay div) instead of relying on console output — WHY: the test browser only yields a screenshot and an empty console, so on-page text is the only channel I can observe.\nDECISION: Create that overlay element in an inline (non-module) script in `scene252.html` that runs before the module script, with `window` error/unhandledrejection handlers, and have `scene252.ts` take the element over by id — WHY: a screenshot can then distinguish \"HTML loaded but the module never arrived\" (stuck on \"waiting for module…\") from \"module loaded but an init await hangs\" (stuck on a stage), and any load-time error is captured on-page.","timings":{"cache_n":66816,"draft_n":1876,"draft_n_accepted":766,"predicted_ms":17820.0,"predicted_n":1034,"prompt_ms":730.0,"prompt_n":165},"to_request":152865,"usage":{"cached_tokens":66816,"completion_tokens":1034,"prompt_tokens":66981}}
