scenes\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Workflow Directives\n\n### 0. Never Revert Unknown Changes (Critical)\n\n- **Never run `git checkout --`, `git restore`, or `git reset` on files you did not personal […]\n\n> NOTE: Relevant memory truncated for prompt budget.\n\n### a tool result (compaction-6/message-2)\n\n[…] been removed. Downstream sampling of an RT is handled uniformly by the copy-to-texture / post-process vertex shaders' single unconditional UV convention, so there is no per-RT `flipY` field to set or override.\n\n---\n\n## Target API Shape\n\n```typescript\nasync function main(): Promise<void> {\n    const engine = await createEngine(canvas);\n    const scene = createSceneContext(engine);\n\n    addToScene(scene, await loadGltf(engine, \"https://playground.babylonjs.com/scenes/BoomBox.glb\"));\n    await loadEnvironment(scene, \".../environment.env\");\n\n    // Components are plain data — scene is the owner\n    const light = createHemisphericLight([0, 1, 0], 0.7);\n    addToScene(scene, light);\n\n    const camera = createDefaultCamera(scene);\n    camera.alpha += Math.PI;\n\n    // Materials own their renderable builders — no explicit pipeline building\n    await registerScene(scene); // builds deferred work, partitions renderables\n    await startEngine(engine); // resolves after first frame rendered; renders all registered scenes\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Workflow Directives\n\n### 0. Never Revert Unknown Changes (Critical)\n\n- **Never run `git checkout --`, `git restore`, or `git reset` on files you did not personal […]\n\n> NOTE: Relevant memory truncated for prompt budget.\n\n</system-reminder>","turn":14}
