undle was compiled.\n\nHmm. Let me think about this differently.\n\nActually — let me reconsider. Maybe the production build is not the right path. Let me go back to the dev server and work on the actual problem (the recast wasm hang).\n\nBut — the dev server's slow transforms make it hard to diagnose. The browser times out before the modules load.\n\nWait — but on the dev server, the browser DID get to \"terrain +90ms\". So the dev server CAN serve the modules (slowly, but the browser made it to terrain). So the dev server is usable.\n\nThe production build is WORSE (createEngine hangs). So the production build is not a good path.\n\nLet me go back to the dev server. But — I need to fix the recast wasm hang.\n\nActually — let me reconsider the recast wasm hang. The hypothesis is that `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` hangs for the recast wasm. The fix is to force the ArrayBuffer path.\n\nLet me implement the fix: monkey-patch `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` to reject (so the recast glue falls back to the ArrayBuffer path).\n\nBut — where to put the monkey-patch? It needs to be applied BEFORE the recast wasm is loaded. So I'll put it at the start of `main()` (before `createNavigationPluginAsync`).\n\nActually — let me reconsider. The monkey-patch is a global mutation (it changes `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` for the whole page). This is a bit invasive. But it's a diagnostic fix (to test the hypothesis).\n\nLet me implement it:\n```ts\n// Force the recast wasm to use the ArrayBuffer path (WebAssembly.instantiate)\n// instead of the streaming path (WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming), which hangs\n// in this browser. The recast glue falls back to the ArrayBuffer path if\n// instantiateStreaming rejects.\nconst origInstantiateStreaming = WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming;\nWebAssembly.instantiateStreaming = (async () => {\n    throw new Error(\"force ArrayBuffer path\");\n}) as typeof WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming;\n```\n\nWait — but this would break the Havok