{"kind":"delta","request":166145,"seq":166672,"t":10109191,"tool_call":{"arguments":"{\"file_path\": \"~/git/reference/Babylon/Babylon-Lite/lab/lite/src/lite/scene252.ts\", \"old_string\": \"const mark = (stage: string): void => {\\n        const ms = Math.round(performance.now() - __initStart);\\n        console.warn(`scene252 init: ${stage} +${ms}ms`);\\n        if (overlay) {\\n            overlay.textContent += `\\\\n  ${stage} +${ms}ms`;\\n        }\\n    };\\n    const engine = await createEngine(canvas);\\n    mark(\\\"engine\\\");\", \"new_string\": \"const mark = (stage: string): void => {\\n        const ms = Math.round(performance.now() - __initStart);\\n        console.warn(`scene252 init: ${stage} +${ms}ms`);\\n        if (overlay) {\\n            overlay.textContent += `\\\\n  ${stage} +${ms}ms`;\\n        }\\n    };\\n    // This browser stalls on WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming for the second wasm\\n    // module (recast after Havok) — the promise never settles, so the emscripten\\n    // glue's ArrayBuffer fallback (which only runs on a rejection) is unreachable.\\n    // Force streaming to reject so both wasm loads take the ArrayBuffer path.\\n    WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming = (async () => {\\n        throw new Error(\\\"scene252: forcing ArrayBuffer wasm path\\\");\\n    }) as typeof WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming;\\n    mark(\\\"force-arraybuffer\\\");\\n    const engine = await createEngine(canvas);\\n    mark(\\\"engine\\\");\"}","id":"call_e3f1b7d89e42484186007a28","index":0,"name":"edit"}}
{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Now I have the current structure. The parallel-load fix is there:\n```ts\nconst navPromise = createNavigationPluginAsync({ locateFile: () => \"/recast-navigation.wasm\" });\nconst hknp = await HavokPhysics({ locateFile: () => \"/HavokPhysics.wasm\" });\n```\n\nSo the recast wasm is loaded in parallel with the Havok wasm.\n\nNow let me add the monkey-patch to force the ArrayBuffer path. I'll add it right after the `mark` helper is defined, before the wasm loads.\n\nActually — let me reconsider. The monkey-patch should be applied BEFORE the wasm loads. The first wasm load is `createNavigationPluginAsync` (the recast wasm) and `HavokPhysics` (the Havok wasm). So the monkey-patch should be applied before both.\n\nLet me add the monkey-patch right after the `mark` helper is defined, and add a `mark(\"force-arraybuffer\")` to log it.\n\nWait — but the monkey-patch is a global mutation. It changes `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` for the whole page. This is a bit invasive. But it's a diagnostic fix (to test the hypothesis).\n\nLet me implement it:\n```ts\n// Force the wasm load to use the ArrayBuffer path (WebAssembly.instantiate)\n// instead of the streaming path (WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming), which hangs\n// in this browser. The emscripten glue falls back to the ArrayBuffer path if\n// instantiateStreaming rejects.\nWebAssembly.instantiateStreaming = (async () => {\n    throw new Error(\"force ArrayBuffer path\");\n}) as typeof WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming;\nmark(\"force-arraybuffer\");\n```\n\nLet me add this right after the `mark` helper is defined.\n\nActually — wait. Let me reconsider. The monkey-patch is a global mutation. It might be better to put it at the module level (top of the file), so it's applied as soon as the module loads. But — the convention says no module-level side effects. So let me put it at the start of `main()`.\n\nLet me implement it.\n\nActually — let me reconsider the whole approach. Maybe the issue is NOT `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming`. Maybe it's something else.\n\nLet me think about what else could cause the recast wasm load to hang:\n1. The wasm fetch (network) hangs.\n2. The wasm compilation hangs.\n3. The wasm instantiation hangs.\n4. The navigation plugin initialization hangs.\n\nIf the fetch hangs, the wasm never loads. If the compilation hangs, the wasm never compiles. If the instantiation hangs, the wasm never instantiates. If the initialization hangs, the plugin never initializes.\n\nThe stage markers show \"nav-plugin\" is the last stage (before the hang). So the hang is in `createNavigationPluginAsync` (which loads the wasm and initializes the plugin).\n\nBut — `createNavigationPluginAsync` is a single await. So I can't tell if the hang is in the fetch, compilation, instantiation, or initialization. I need more granular markers.\n\nBut — `createNavigationPluginAsync` is in the babylon-lite package (not my scene code). So I can't add markers inside it (without modifying the package).\n\nHmm. Let me reconsider.\n\nActually — let me step back and think about the most likely cause.\n\nThe recast wasm is ~2MB. It's loaded via `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` (streaming) or `WebAssembly.instantiate` (ArrayBuffer). If the streaming path hangs, the ArrayBuffer path is the fallback.\n\nThe hypothesis: `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` hangs for the recast wasm. The fix is to force the ArrayBuffer path.\n\nLet me implement the fix (monkey-patch `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` to reject). This is a diagnostic fix (to test the hypothesis). If it works, the recast wasm loads via the ArrayBuffer path, and the hang is resolved.\n\nBut — I need to be careful not to break the Havok wasm load. Let me check if the Havok glue uses `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming`.\n\nActually — let me just try it. If the Havok wasm load breaks, I'll see it in the stage markers (the \"havok\" stage won't print). If it works, the \"havok\" stage prints, and the \"nav-plugin\" stage should also print (if the ArrayBuffer path works for the recast wasm).\n\nLet me implement the monkey-patch.\n\nOK I really need to stop going in circles. Let me take action.\n\nLet me implement the monkey-patch at the start of `main()`, right after the `mark` helper is defined.\n\nLet me write the edit.\n","seq":166673,"t":10109193,"text":"\n\nThe parallel-load edit is in place (recast kicks off before Havok). Now I'll force the ArrayBuffer path: patch `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` to reject, which makes the recast glue's `catch` fire and fall back to `WebAssembly.instantiate`. I'll insert it right after the `mark` helper so it's active before either wasm load, and mark it so we can see it fired.\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":118784,"draft_n":2051,"draft_n_accepted":1182,"predicted_ms":30040.0,"predicted_n":1475,"prompt_ms":3710.0,"prompt_n":1907},"to_request":166145,"usage":{"cached_tokens":118784,"completion_tokens":1475,"prompt_tokens":120691}}
