{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"The dev server is up and serving the updated code (with the monkey-patch). \n\nNow let me record what I did and explain to the user what to look for.\n\nLet me summarize:\n1. I switched back to the dev server (the production build is broken — createEngine hangs for all scenes).\n2. I added a monkey-patch to force the ArrayBuffer wasm path (reject `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` so the recast glue falls back to `WebAssembly.instantiate`).\n3. The dev server is serving the updated code.\n\nNow the user should reload and report the stages. If the ArrayBuffer path works, the \"nav-plugin\" stage should print (and the scene should load). If it doesn't work, the \"nav-plugin\" stage won't print (and the scene will still hang).\n\nLet me record this and explain to the user.\n\nActually — let me reconsider. The monkey-patch forces BOTH the recast and Havok wasm to use the ArrayBuffer path. If the Havok wasm load breaks (because the ArrayBuffer path doesn't work for Havok), the \"havok\" stage won't print. But — the ArrayBuffer path is a standard Web API, so it should work for both.\n\nLet me explain to the user what to look for:\n- If the scene loads (no spinner): the ArrayBuffer path works, and the hang is fixed.\n- If the scene still hangs at \"nav-plugin\": the ArrayBuffer path doesn't work for the recast wasm (so the hypothesis is wrong).\n- If the scene hangs at \"havok\" (before \"nav-plugin\"): the ArrayBuffer path broke the Havok wasm load (so the monkey-patch is too aggressive).\n\nLet me record this and explain to the user.\n\nLet me write a clear explanation.\n","seq":167493,"t":10166429,"text":"\n\nDev server is up and serving the patch. Here's what I did and what to look for:\n\n**What changed:** I switched back to the dev server (the production build is the wrong tool — it stalls inside `createEngine` for *every* scene, including stock scene2, so it's a build/preview limitation, not your scene). On the dev server your browser made real progress (engine → havok → terrain) before stalling in the recast wasm load.\n\n**The fix I'm testing:** the recast glue (`recast-navigation.wasm.js`) tries `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` first and only falls back to the ArrayBuffer path if that call *rejects* — a hang (never-settling) leaves the fallback unreachable. So I made `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` reject on purpose, forcing both wasm modules onto the ArrayBuffer path (`WebAssembly.instantiate`). There's a new `force-arraybuffer` stage marker so we can confirm it fired.\n\nReload `http://localhost:5182/lite/scene252.html` and send a screenshot. The green box will now tell us one of three things:\n\n- **It gets past `nav-plugin` and the scene loads** → the ArrayBuffer path is the fix; the streaming compile was the culprit.\n- **It still stops after `terrain` (no `nav-plugin`)** → the ArrayBuffer path doesn't rescue the recast load either, so the stall is somewhere else in the wasm init (I'll instrument deeper).\n- **It stops at `force-arraybuffer` / `havok`** → forcing the ArrayBuffer path broke the Havok load (unlikely, but I'd know the patch is too blunt).\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":123136,"draft_n":1876,"draft_n_accepted":736,"predicted_ms":28510.0,"predicted_n":1004,"prompt_ms":910.0,"prompt_n":278},"to_request":167013,"usage":{"cached_tokens":123136,"completion_tokens":1004,"prompt_tokens":123414}}
