{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"Let me reflect on the step I just completed. In this step, I:\n\n1. Diagnosed that the production build hangs on `createEngine` for all scenes (including stock scene2), while the dev server works — so the production build is the wrong tool.\n2. Decided to abandon the production build/preview approach and go back to the dev server.\n3. Read the recast glue and confirmed the `instantiateStreaming` → `instantiateArrayBuffer` fallback logic (only on rejection, not on hang).\n4. Decided to force the ArrayBuffer path by monkey-patching `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` to reject.\n5. Applied the monkey-patch in scene252.ts (with a `mark(\"force-arraybuffer\")` stage).\n6. Restarted the dev server.\n\nLet me list the decisions from THIS step:\n\n1. DECISION: Abandon the production build/preview path and serve via the Vite dev server — WHY: the production build hangs in `createEngine` for all scenes (including stock scene2) while the same browser cleared `createEngine` on the dev server, so the build is the regression, not the scene code.\n\n2. DECISION: Force the recast (and Havok) wasm loads onto the ArrayBuffer path by making `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` reject — WHY: the emscripten glue only falls back to `WebAssembly.instantiate` inside a `catch`, so a never-settling streaming promise makes the fallback unreachable, and a forced rejection triggers it.\n\nLet me check if these are from this step. Yes, both are from this step.\n\nActually — let me reconsider. The decision to abandon the production build was made in this step (after the user's screenshot showed the build hangs on createEngine for all scenes). And the decision to force the ArrayBuffer path was made in this step (after reading the recast glue).\n\nLet me list them concisely.\n\nActually — I should be careful. The instruction says \"Only decisions from this step, not earlier ones.\" So I should only list decisions made in THIS step (the step where I diagnosed the build problem, read the recast glue, applied the monkey-patch, and restarted the dev server).\n\nLet me list:\n1. DECISION: Abandon the production build/preview and serve via the Vite dev server — WHY: the build hangs in createEngine for all scenes (incl. stock scene2) while the dev server cleared createEngine, so the build is the regression.\n2. DECISION: Force the wasm loads onto the ArrayBuffer path by making WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming reject — WHY: the recast glue's ArrayBuffer fallback only runs on a rejection, so a hung streaming promise leaves it unreachable and a forced rejection triggers it.\n\nThese are the two decisions from this step. Let me write them.\n","seq":168460,"t":10221810,"text":"\n\nDECISION: Abandon the production build/preview path and serve scene252 via the Vite dev server instead — WHY: the build hangs inside `createEngine` for *all* scenes (including stock scene2) while the same browser cleared `createEngine` on the dev server, so the pre-bundled build is the regression, not my scene code.\n\nDECISION: Force the recast (and Havok) wasm loads onto the ArrayBuffer path by making `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` reject — WHY: the recast emscripten glue only falls back to `WebAssembly.instantiate` inside a `catch`, so a never-settling streaming promise leaves that fallback unreachable, whereas a forced rejection triggers it.","timings":{"cache_n":123136,"draft_n":1162,"draft_n_accepted":584,"predicted_ms":17340.0,"predicted_n":750,"prompt_ms":540.0,"prompt_n":129},"to_request":168113,"usage":{"cached_tokens":123136,"completion_tokens":750,"prompt_tokens":123265}}
