a: the repo's Playwright browser cache (build 1243) does not match the installed playwright 1.58.2 (expects 1208), so default `chromium.launch()` fails with \"Executable doesn't exist\" — IMPLICATION: any future Playwright work must use `channel: \"chrome\"` (the repo's own idiom in playwright.config.ts), not the bundled browser.\ninterview-t6-f69808-2\tgotcha: text-layer `positionPx` is in CSS pixels (scene180 comment: \"CSS pixels — matches layer.positionPx units\"), but the canvas has fixed `width=\"1280\" height=\"720\"` attributes stretched by CSS to 100vw/100vh — IMPLICATION: the crosshair must be positioned with `window.innerWidth/innerHeight`, not `canvas.width/height` (still to fix).\ninterview-t6-f69808-3\tgotcha: `moveWithCollisions` clamps displacement into the floor but never zeroes the velocity — `playerVel.y`/`bot.velY` accumulate `-GRAVITY*dt` every step even while standing, so falls start with built-up velocity and terminal velocity is unbounded — IMPLICATION: reset vel.y to 0 on ground contact (compare actual drop vs requested drop) and clamp a terminal velocity in the physics step (still to fix).\ninterview-t6-f69808-4\tgotcha: in my `rayVsCapsule`, the segment parameter `t` is measured along the unit direction, so `t` already is the distance — my draft returned `t * RAY_RANGE`, inflating bot hit distances 100× (bots would never be hit) — IMPLICATION: fixed to `Math.min(t, RAY_RANGE)`; any other ray tests must be checked for the same unit-direction assumption.\ninterview-t6-f71282-0\tdecision: Browser-based smoke verification is not possible in this sandbox — WHY: Playwright's mkdtemp is blocked in the system temp dir, the bundled chromium build (1208) is missing from the cache, and system Chrome (channel \"chrome\") SIGABRTs at launch because crashpad's Mach bootstrap check-in is permission-denied, even with `TMPDIR`/`HOME` redirected into the repo.\ninterview-t6-f71282-1\tdecision: Validation this session is lint + typecheck + dev-server module-transform checks (all four new modules return 200 through Vite with resolved aliases) + user manual playtest on :5182 — WHY: the dev server is reachable and transforming the full import graph is the deepest verification the sandbox allows.\ninterview-t6-f71282-2\tdecision: The `fps-smoke.cjs` script stays in the repo root for the user to run outside the sandbox, and will be deleted before commit — WHY: /tmp is write-blocked so it must live in-repo, and GUIDANCE §0b requires removing temp files before commit.\ninterview-t6-f71282-3\tdecision: `rayVsCapsule` must return `Math.min(t, RAY_RANGE)` instead of `t * RAY_RANGE` — WHY: `t` is the parameter along the unit direction `fwd`, so it is already the hit distance; the old scaling made bot hits ~100× farther than terrain hits, so bots could never be shot.\ninterview-t6-f71282-4\tdecision: The crosshair layer must be positioned with `window.innerWidth/innerHeight` (CSS pixels), not `canvas.width/height` — WHY: the canvas carries fixed `width=1280 height=720` attributes while `layer.positionPx` is in CSS pixels (scene180's drag code confirms the unit), so device-pixel coordinates would off-center the crosshair.\ninterview-t6-f71282-5\tdecision: `updateDefaultTextData(hudData, text)` is the correct in-place HUD update call — WHY: default-text-data.ts:83 confirms it re-lays out the text, extracts new glyphs into the same storage, and updates the run the layer references.\ninterview-t6-f71282-6\tdecision: (still to apply) player/bot vertical velocity must be zeroed on floor contact (actual drop < half of requested drop) with a -30u/s terminal clamp — WHY: `moveWithCollisions` clamps penetration but `playerVel.y`/`bot.velY` accumulate -9.8·dt forever while standing, so falling off a ledge would start at high velocity.\ninterview-t6-f71282-7\tdecision: (still to apply) `tryFire` should ignore terrain hits with `hitDistance < 2` — WHY: the player's capsule shape mask is unverified (private `_shape`), so a self-hit guard prevents shots from destroying the tile under the player's feet.\ninterview-t6-f71906-0\tconstraint: Browser automation is blocked in this sandbox — Playwright/Chrome SIGABRTs at launch (crashpad Mach bootstrap + ~/Library/Application Support are EPERM), so no Playwright smoke/playtest is possible here; validation is lint + typecheck + dev-server serves + user manual playtest on :5182.\ninterview-t6-f71906-1\tconstraint: The sandbox blocks writes to /tmp and the system temp dir (/var/folders/.../T) — scratch files must live inside the repo and be deleted before commit (GUIDANCE §0b).\ninterview-t6-f71906-2\tconstraint: `pnpm dev:lab` fails in this sandbox (its tsx bundle-build step EPERMs on an IPC pipe in the system temp dir) — start the lab with `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite` from `lab/` instead.\ninterview-t6-f71906-3\tconstraint: Any Playwright launch in this repo must use `channel: \"chrome\"` (system Chrome) with `--enable-unsafe-webgpu` — the cached Playwright browser build (1243) doesn't match playwright 1.58.2 (expects 1208), so the default bundled launch fails.\ninterview-t6-f71906-4\tconstraint: HUD text-layer `positionPx` is in CSS pixels while the canvas has fixed width/height attributes stretched by CSS — screen-space positioning must use `window.innerWidth/innerHeight`, not `canvas.width/height`.\ninterview-t6-f72604-0\topen: rayVsCapsule still has a buggy `u` (axis-parameter) formula and no end-cap handling — I only fixed the return-value scaling, so bot hit-detection/misranking is untrusted until I rewrite it.\ninterview-t6-f72604-1\topen: zero runtime verification — the sandbox can't launch Chrome (SIGABRT / crashpad EPERM, no display), so rendering, physics stepping, navmesh, HUD compositing, and audio are all unverified; only static lint/typecheck + module transform (HTTP 200) are confirmed.\ninterview-t6-f72604-10\tplan: read `havok.ts`/scene40 to confirm `scene.fixedDeltaMs` drives the step and `onPhysicsAfterStep` passes dt.\ninterview-t6-f72604-11\tplan: confirm a DYNAMIC body writes back to its node's `position`/`rotationQuaternion` each step (needed for debris rendering).\ninterview-t6-f72604-12\tplan: verify `lab/public/fonts/Inter.ttf` exists and the TextRenderer composites after the scene (registration order + `clear:false`).\ninterview-t6-f72604-13\tplan: run `pnpm run lint:fix` then `pnpm run lint` + typecheck after the rewrite.\ninterview-t6-f72604-14\tplan: check `lab/vite.config.ts` for whether scene252 needs a rollup input / gallery card, and add it if required.\ninterview-t6-f72604-15\tplan: hand off to you for a manual playtest on :5182 with a checklist, since browser automation is blocked in this sandbox.\ninterview-t6-f72604-2\topen: FreeCamera mouse-look — I assume writing `cam.position` + `cam.target` each frame (lookAt) drives the view and that my yaw/pitch sign conventions are correct; unverified at runtime.\ninterview-t6-f72604-3\topen: physics timestep wiring — I assume `scene.fixedDeltaMs` drives the Havok step and `onPhysicsAfterStep(world, cb)` passes dt; not re-verified this session (relying on the scene40 pattern note).\ninterview-t6-f72604-4\topen: debris rendering — I assume the physics world writes dynamic body→node transform (`position` + `rotationQuaternion`) each step even for nodes never added to the scene; unverified.\ninterview-t6-f72604-5\topen: `loadFont(\"/fonts/Inter.ttf\")` — I assume that path exists under `lab/public/fonts`; unverified.\ninterview-t6-f72604-6\topen: NavCrowd agent↔controller drift — I re-target when they separate >4u, but runtime behavior (stuck/oscillating bots) is unverified.\ninterview-t6-f72604-7\topen: init cost/perf — 1024 static tile bodies + navmesh build (cs=0.5) runtime cost unverified.\ninterview-t6-f72604-8\topen: scene registration — whether scene252 needs a rollup input in `lab/vite.config.ts` / a gallery card (I decided it's a game demo, not a parity scene, but haven't checked what's actually required).\ninterview-t6-f72604-9\tplan: rewrite `rayVsCapsule` with the correct closest-point formulation (fix the `u` formula, add end-cap checks) — the edit I was mid-way through.\ninterview-t6-f74332-1\tgotcha: The lab canvas has fixed device-pixel attributes (`width=\"1280\" height=\"720\"`) but is CSS-stretched to `100vw/100vh`, and text-layer `positionPx` is in CSS pixels (scene180:82 comment) — so centering the crosshair via `canvas.width/2` (buffer space, 640) does not center it in the viewport. — IMPLICATION: position HUD elements using `window.innerWidth`/`innerHeight` (CSS pixels), or confirm the engine resizes the buffer to CSS size before trusting `canvas.width`; I need to fix the crosshair position.\ninterview-t6-f74332-2\tgotcha: My first `rayVsCapsule` only solved the cylindrical band and its `u` (axis parameter) formula was wrong (`hh*e` where it should be `e`), so it returned `null` for valid center hits in some configs and missed end-cap (top/bottom) hits entirely. — IMPLICATION: a capsule hit-test needs the cylindrical band plus two end-cap sphere tests, taking the closest; I rewrote it that way in scene252.ts.\ninterview-t6-f78118-0\tdecision: Rewrote `rayVsCapsule` in scene252.ts as a clean cylindrical-band + end-cap (sphere) test, replacing the old closed-form solution — WHY: the old `u` (axis parameter) formula was mathematically wrong (missing a division by `hh`) and returned null for valid center hits, and it also never hit the end caps.\ninterview-t6-f78118-1\tdecision: Added a ground-contact velocity reset for the player (zero `playerVel.y` when the controller's downward move is blocked, detected via pre/post Y) plus a terminal-velocity clamp of -30 — WHY: `moveWithCollisions` neither applies gravity nor resets velocity, so fall speed would accumulate unboundedly while standing.\ninterview-t6-f78118-2\tdecision: Applied the same `velY` reset + clamp to bots — WHY: bots share the identical velocity-accumulation problem.\ninterview-t6-f78118-3\tdecision: Switched the crosshair TextLayer position from `canvas.width/height` to `window.innerWidth/innerHeight` — WHY: the canvas has fixed 1280×720 attributes but CSS stretches it to 100vw/100vh, and `positionPx` is in CSS pixels (scene180:82).\ninterview-t6-f78118-4\tdecision: Added a self-hit guard `terr.hitDistance > 2` in `tryFire` — WHY: `physicsRaycast` defaults `membership`/`collideWith` to `~0`, so the shot ray can hit the player's own character-controller capsule (default filter mask) and destroy the tile under the player's feet.\ninterview-t6-f78118-5\tdecision: Typed `Debris.body` as `PhysicsBody | null` and removed the `null as unknown as PhysicsBody` cast, adding null guards at expiry and render — WHY: the field is genuinely null until spawned, so the type should say so instead of an unsafe cast.\ninterview-t6-f79228-0\tconstraint: A `physicsRaycast` filtered by `membership` (e.g. `TERRAIN_LAYER`) will still hit character-controller capsules — the raycast query defaults to `~0` for both masks (confirmed in `havok-queries.ts` this step), the controller's capsule `_shape` is private so its filter mask can't be set via public API, and Havok's default shape filter is all-bits — so any ray-based hit detection near the player/bots must use an explicit self-hit guard (e.g. `hitDistance > 2`) or a manual capsule test, never rely on filter masks to exclude controllers. (The shape-default-`~0` part is inferred from Havok convention, not re-verified in this step.)\ninterview-t6-f80873-0\topen: Browser validation is blocked in this sandbox — Chrome SIGABRTs at launch (crashpad/Mach bootstrap EPERM), so no Playwright smoke/playtest possible here; validation is lint + typecheck + your manual playtest on :5182/lite/scene252.html.\ninterview-t6-f80873-1\topen: Runtime — nav agent re-sync (`agentGoto` to bot pos when >4u apart) may cause bot chase-loops/jitter; playtest will tell.\ninterview-t6-f80873-10\tplan: Delete scratch files (fps-smoke.cjs, .smoke-tmp/, .smoke-home/) per GUIDANCE §0b before wrapping up.\ninterview-t6-f80873-11\tplan: Report status to you with the manual playtest checklist (ready/error dataset, move/slide/jump, mouse-look, shoot holes → tile removed + body gone + nav obstacle, fall-through respawn, debris, bots patrol/shoot, HUD, audio).\ninterview-t6-f80873-12\tplan: If lint is clean, call propose_phase_transition.\ninterview-t6-f80873-2\topen: Runtime — HUD TextRenderer compositing over the 3D frame (scene registered first, `clear: false`) is reasoned from the render-context registry, never seen on screen.\ninterview-t6-f80873-3\topen: Runtime — `updateDefaultTextData` in-place mutation actually triggering the TextRenderer to re-draw the HUD layer is assumed, unverified.\ninterview-t6-f80873-4\topen: Runtime — FreeCamera driven by per-frame `position`+`target` (lookAt) and the mouse-look yaw/pitch sign convention are unverified; if look is inverted it's a one-line sign flip.\ninterview-t6-f80873-5\topen: Runtime — init cost of 1024 static tile bodies + navmesh build at cs=0.5 over 128×128u never measured; fallback is 8×8u tiles (256 bodies) if world init is slow.\ninterview-t6-f80873-6\topen: The player capsule keeps Havok's default filter (~0), so a bullet raycast can't exclude it by mask; the `terr.hitDistance > 2` self-hit guard is unverified at runtime (esp. aiming straight down at own feet).\ninterview-t6-f80873-7\topen: Lint/typecheck has not been re-run since my latest batch of edits (rayVsCapsule rewrite, velocity-reset-on-landing, crosshair CSS-pixel fix, `Debris.body` null typing, self-hit guard).\ninterview-t6-f80873-8\tplan: Run `pnpm run lint:fix` then `pnpm run lint` to confirm the latest edits typecheck and pass ESLint.\ninterview-t6-f80873-9\tplan: Record the settled learnings via update_record (rayVsCapsule cylindrical+cap rewrite, velocity reset on floor contact, crosshair in CSS pixels, `Debris.body: PhysicsBody | null`, self-hit guard, `setThinInstances` re-uploads per call via `_version` bump, controller `getPosition` = capsule center).\ninterview-t6-f82053-0\tgotcha: Playwright's artifact mkdtemp ignores `launch({ tmpDir })` — it creates `playwright-artifacts-*` in the system temp dir first, and the sandbox denies `/var/folders/.../T` — IMPLICATION: run Playwright node scripts with `TMPDIR` pointed at a repo-local dir (e.g. `TMPDIR=\"$PWD/.smoke-tmp\"`).\ninterview-t6-f82053-1\tgotcha: the ms-playwright cache holds browser build 1243 but the repo's playwright 1.58.2 expects 1208, so default `chromium.launch()` fails with \"Executable doesn't exist\"; the repo's own config launches system Chrome — IMPLICATION: launch with `channel: \"chrome\"` + `--enable-unsafe-webgpu` (playwright.config.ts idiom), never the bundled build.\ninterview-t6-f82053-2\tgotcha: system Chrome SIGABRTs at launch in this sandbox (headless and headed alike) — crashpad Mach bootstrap check-in is denied and `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad` is EPERM; a `HOME` override doesn't redirect it — IMPLICATION: no browser-based smoke/playtest is possible this session; validation is lint + typecheck + Vite transform (all four new files serve 200) plus a user manual playtest on :5182.\ninterview-t6-f82053-3\tgotcha: `physicsRaycast` returns only the first (closest) hit, and the character controller's capsule shape is private with default filter `~0/~0` — no `membership`/`collideWith` mask can exclude the player's own capsule from a bullet raycast — IMPLICATION: with the eye at capsule height the player capsule occludes every terrain hit; the eye must sit above the capsule top (~center + 1.0) so forward rays clear it — the `hitDistance > 2` guard alone is not sufficient.\ninterview-t6-f82053-4\tgotcha: `PhysicsCharacterController.getPosition()` returns the capsule **center** (shape is built centered on the node: pointA +h/2−r, pointB −h/2+r), not the feet — IMPLICATION: eye/spawn/respawn heights are relative to center (feet = center − 0.9); current `EYE_HEIGHT = 1.5` puts the eye 0.6 above the head and must drop to ~1.0.\ninterview-t6-f82053-5\tgotcha: `scene18.html`'s canvas has fixed `width=1280 height=720` attributes while CSS stretches it to 100vw/100vh, and `positionPx` is in CSS pixels (scene180:82) — IMPLICATION: screen-space HUD positions must use `window.innerWidth/innerHeight`, not `canvas.width/height` (crosshair already fixed this way).\ninterview-t6-f82053-6\tgotcha: my `rayVsCapsule` draft had a wrong `u` formula (missing a `/hh` in the first term — derived correctly as `(wy − d.y·c)/(hh(1−d.y²))`) and returned `null` for end-cap hits — IMPLICATION: rewritten with the cylindrical-band solution plus sphere tests for both caps; center shots and top/bottom shots now register.\ninterview-t6-f85232-0\tgotcha: `PhysicsCharacterController.getPosition()` returns the capsule **center**, not the feet — the capsule spans `center ± capsuleHeight/2` (confirmed from the constructor: shape built symmetric about the origin, `_position`/`_node.position` is the center) — IMPLICATION: `EYE_HEIGHT` is an offset from center, so a realistic eye is ~0.7 (near the head), and my original 1.5 placed the camera 0.6 above the head; spawn/respawn Y must also be center-based.\ninterview-t6-f85232-1\tgotcha: the character controller's capsule shape is private and created with **no explicit collision filter**, and `physicsRaycast` returns only the *closest* hit — so the player's own capsule can't be excluded via layer masking and would occlude every terrain hit — IMPLICATION: the bullet ray must originate from a muzzle offset (~0.8 in front of the eye, outside the 0.5 capsule radius), not from the eye.\ninterview-t6-f85232-2\tgotcha: text-layer `positionPx` is in **CSS pixels**, not canvas backing-store pixels — the canvas has fixed `width=1280 height=720` attributes but CSS stretches it to `100vw/100vh` (scene180:82 confirms the units) — IMPLICATION: center the crosshair with `window.innerWidth/innerHeight`, not `canvas.width/height`.\ninterview-t6-f85232-3\tgotcha: `setThinInstances` bumps `_version` and marks the whole matrix buffer dirty on each call — no separate flush needed, per-frame calls are safe — IMPLICATION: the open question on per-frame bot/debris matrix updates is resolved; just call it each frame.\ninterview-t6-f85232-4\tgotcha: browser automation (Playwright/Chrome) cannot launch in this sandbox — crashpad Mach bootstrap is denied and the cached browser build doesn't match the repo's Playwright — IMPLICATION: runtime verification must be lint + typecheck + a manual playtest on :5182, not a scripted browser smoke test.\ninterview-t6-f86326-0\tdecision: Bullet raycasts now originate from a muzzle point 0.8u in front of the eye (`MUZZLE_OFFSET`), not from the eye — WHY: the character controller's capsule shape is private and can't be filter-masked (default membership `~0`), so a ray starting inside the player's own capsule would hit the player capsule first and occlude every terrain hit.\ninterview-t6-f86326-1\tdecision: `EYE_HEIGHT` lowered from 1.5 to 0.7 above the capsule center — WHY: `getPosition()` returns the capsule *center*, so 1.5 floated the camera 0.6 above the head; 0.7 puts the eye near the head (~1.6m above ground when standing).\ninterview-t6-f86326-2\tdecision: Removed the `terr.hitDistance > 2` self-hit guard — WHY: the muzzle offset already guarantees the ray never starts inside the player capsule, so the distance-based workaround is redundant.\ninterview-t6-f86326-3\tdecision: `Debris.body` typed `PhysicsBody | null` (dropped the `null as unknown as PhysicsBody` cast) with null-guards in the render/expiry loops — WHY: debris slots start empty and only gain a body on spawn, so the type should reflect that instead of papering over it with a cast.\ninterview-t6-f86903-0\tconstraint: `PhysicsCharacterController`'s capsule shape is created internally (`_shape`, via `createPhysicsShape`) and is private — scene code cannot access or filter-mask it, so the player's/bots' controller capsules can never be excluded from `physicsRaycast` via collision layers; shooting rays must originate outside the player capsule (muzzle offset) to avoid self-hits.\ninterview-t6-f86903-1\tconstraint: `PhysicsCharacterController.getPosition()` returns the capsule **center**, not the feet — ground/feet level is `position.y - capsuleHeight/2`, so every eye-height, spawn, and ground computation must apply that half-height offset.\ninterview-t6-f86903-2\tconstraint: Shapes created via `createPhysicsShape` carry Havok's default all-layers filter (`~0`) because Lite never sets one — collision-layer filtering only excludes a shape if its membership is explicitly set with `setPhysicsShapeFilterMembershipMask`, so \"default\" never means \"excluded\".\ninterview-t6-f87832-0\tgotcha: `PhysicsCharacterController.getPosition()` returns the capsule **center** (shape spans center ± capsuleHeight/2), not the feet — IMPLICATION: eye height and spawn/respawn Y are offsets from the center (eye ≈ center + 0.7; spawn = terrainHeight + capsuleHeight/2), not from the ground plane.\ninterview-t6-f87832-1\tgotcha: the character controller's capsule shape is private (`_shape`) and its default filter membership is `~0` (belongs to every layer), so `physicsRaycast` cannot be filtered to exclude the player's own capsule — IMPLICATION: bullet rays must be cast from a muzzle offset in front of the eye (outside the 0.5 capsule radius) or the player's capsule occludes every terrain hit.\ninterview-t6-f87832-2\tgotcha: the long-running Vite dev server serves stale module transforms in this sandbox (its file watcher does not fire on disk edits) — IMPLICATION: restart the dev server after code changes before playtesting, or verify served content matches disk.\ninterview-t6-f87832-3\tgotcha: `setThinInstances` re-uploads via an internal `_version` bump + dirty range (no separate flush call) — IMPLICATION: per-frame `setThinInstances` calls are safe and sufficient for bot/debris matrices; no `flushThinInstances` needed.\ninterview-t6-f89559-0\tdecision: Bullet raycasts originate from a muzzle offset (0.8u in front of the eye) instead of the eye — WHY: the player's capsule has a default `~0` filter and a private shape that can't be filter-masked, so a ray starting inside the capsule would be occluded by the player's own body.\ninterview-t6-f89559-1\tdecision: `EYE_HEIGHT = 0.7` (near the head, above the capsule center) — WHY: realistic first-person eye height; with the muzzle offset, forward rays clear the player capsule.\ninterview-t6-f89559-2\tdecision: Rewrote `rayVsCapsule` as cylindrical-band + end-cap sphere tests — WHY: the original `u` (axis-parameter) formula was wrong and returned null for valid center hits, and it missed end-cap hits.\ninterview-t6-f89559-3\tdecision: Reset vertical velocity to 0 on floor contact (actual-drop vs requested-drop test) for both player and bots — WHY: otherwise fall speed accumulates every step while standing, so walking off a ledge starts a terminal-velocity fall.\ninterview-t6-f89559-4\tdecision: Crosshair placed via `window.innerWidth/innerHeight` (CSS pixels), not `canvas.width/height` — WHY: the canvas has fixed 1280×720 attributes but CSS stretches it to the viewport, and `positionPx` is in CSS pixels (scene180:82).\ninterview-t6-f89559-5\tdecision: Spawn/respawn at standing height (`terrainHeight + CAP_HEIGHT/2 + 0.1`) instead of 2u above — WHY: the controller's `getPosition()` is the capsule center, so feet-on-ground means center = ground + half-height.\ninterview-t6-f89559-6\tdecision: `Debris.body` typed `PhysicsBody | null` with explicit null guards — WHY: cleaner than the `null as unknown as PhysicsBody` cast and satisfies the typecheck.\ninterview-t6-f89559-7\tdecision: Restarted the lab dev server (bg_f4a1f424) — WHY: the long-running server's file watcher wasn't picking up edits in this sandbox and was serving stale transforms.\ninterview-t6-f89879-0\tconstraint: The character controller's capsule shape is private and carries Havok's default filter (membership `~0`, i.e. every layer), so it cannot be excluded from `physicsRaycast` via collision-layer masks — bullet rays must originate from a muzzle offset (in front of the eye, outside the capsule radius), never from the eye/center, or the player's own capsule occludes every terrain hit.\ninterview-t6-f89879-1\tconstraint: In this sandbox the long-running Vite dev server serves stale transformed modules (its file watcher does not fire on edits) — restart the dev server after editing scene files before verifying or playtesting, or you will test old code.\ninterview-t6-f89879-2\tconstraint: Chrome/Playwright cannot launch in this sandbox — crashpad's Mach `bootstrap_check_in` and `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad` are EPERM, so the browser SIGABRTs at start (headless and headed, regardless of `TMPDIR`/`HOME` overrides) — no browser-based verification is possible here; validate via lint/typecheck plus a user manual playtest on :5182.\ninterview-t6-f90466-0\tgotcha: No browser can launch in this sandbox — Playwright's bundled chromium is a build mismatch (cache has 1243, playwright 1.58.2 wants 1208) and system Chrome (`channel: \"chrome\"`, the repo's own idiom) SIGABRTs because crashpad's Mach bootstrap is denied (EPERM on `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad`); overriding HOME/TMPDIR doesn't help — IMPLICATION: no Playwright smoke/playtest is possible this session; validation is lint + typecheck + dev-server transform checks, and the real playtest falls to the user on :5182.\ninterview-t6-f90466-1\tgotcha: a long-running vite dev server serves stale module transforms after on-disk edits (its file watcher doesn't fire in the sandbox — scene252.ts kept serving `EYE_HEIGHT = 1.5` after I changed it) — IMPLICATION: after editing scene files, restart the dev-server background task (or curl the served transform and diff against disk) before assuming the server has the latest code.\ninterview-t6-f90466-2\tgotcha: the character controller's capsule is a normal physics body with the default filter (`~0` membership, private shape) — `physicsRaycast` cannot exclude it via layer masks, and since the raycast returns only the closest hit, a ray originating inside the player's capsule always resolves to the player, never the terrain behind it — IMPLICATION: bullet rays must be cast from a muzzle offset outside the capsule (not a distance-based self-hit guard, which can't see past the occluding capsule).\ninterview-t6-f90466-3\tgotcha: `createPhysicsCharacterController(...).getPosition()` returns the capsule *center*, not the feet (the capsule shape is built symmetric about the origin, node placed at `_position`) — IMPLICATION: spawn/eye heights must be computed as center ± halfH (feet = center − 0.9, eye ≈ center + 0.7); spawning at \"ground + 2\" floats the player.\ninterview-t6-f90466-4\tgotcha: `TextLayer.positionPx` is in CSS pixels, but lab canvases carry fixed `width=\"1280\" height=\"720\"` attributes stretched to 100vw/100vh by CSS — IMPLICATION: screen-space HUD centering must use `window.innerWidth/innerHeight`, not `canvas.width/height`.\ninterview-t6-f91584-0\tdecision: Bullet raycasts originate from a muzzle point 0.8u in front of the eye, not the eye — WHY: the player capsule has default `~0` filter membership and a private shape (unmaskable), so a ray starting at the eye (inside the capsule) would be occluded by the player's own body on every shot.\ninterview-t6-f91584-1\tdecision: EYE_HEIGHT = 0.7 above capsule center (head height), replacing 1.5 — WHY: 1.5 put the camera 0.6 above the head; with the muzzle offset handling self-hits, the camera can sit at a realistic eye level.\ninterview-t6-f91584-10\tdecision: `fps-smoke.cjs`, `.smoke-tmp/`, `.smoke-home/` are session scratch that must be deleted before commit — WHY: GUIDANCE §0b requires removing temp/debug files, and browser launch proved unviable anyway.\ninterview-t6-f91584-2\tdecision: Rewrote `rayVsCapsule` as cylindrical-band + two end-cap sphere tests — WHY: the old `u` formula was mathematically wrong (missing valid center hits) and returned null for all cap hits.\ninterview-t6-f91584-3\tdecision: Player/bot vertical velocity is zeroed when actual drop < half of requested drop after `moveWithCollisions`, with a -30 terminal clamp — WHY: `vel.y` accumulated `-g*dt` every step even while standing, so walking off a ledge started a fall at full accumulated speed.\ninterview-t6-f91584-4\tdecision: Crosshair positioned via `window.innerWidth/innerHeight` (CSS px), not `canvas.width/height` — WHY: the canvas has fixed 1280×720 attributes stretched by CSS, and `positionPx` is in CSS pixels (scene180:82).\ninterview-t6-f91584-5\tdecision: Bot display quaternion corrected to `(0, sin(h/2), 0, cos(h/2))` — WHY: the prior `(0, sin, cos, 0)` args encoded a 180° rotation about a tilted axis.\ninterview-t6-f91584-6\tdecision: Player/bot spawn at `terrainHeight + CAP_HEIGHT/2 + 0.1` (feet on ground) — WHY: controller position is the capsule center, so the old `+2` left the player floating 1.1u.\ninterview-t6-f91584-7\tdecision: `Debris.body` typed `PhysicsBody | null` with guards, dropping the `null as unknown as PhysicsBody` cast — WHY: clean typecheck without unsafe casts.\ninterview-t6-f91584-8\tdecision: Restarted the dev server after edits — WHY: the long-running vite server served stale transforms (file watcher not picking up changes in this sandbox); fresh server on :5182 now serves current code.\ninterview-t6-f91584-9\tdecision: Runtime verification this session is lint + typecheck + dev-server module resolution; browser automation is impossible (Chrome SIGABRTs — crashpad Mach bootstrap EPERM in sandbox) — WHY: the playtest gate falls to the user on :5182.\\nDECISION (confirmed): `setThinInstances` re-uploads on every call (bumps `_version`, sets dirty range) — no separate flush needed for per-frame bot/debris matrices.\\nDECISION (confirmed): collision-layer filtering cannot exclude the player capsule from raycasts (default membership `~0` matches any `collideWith`) — WHY: confirms the muzzle offset, not filter masks, is the correct self-hit fix.\ninterview-t6-f92150-0\tdecision: Bullet ray is cast from a muzzle point (0.8 in front of the eye), not the eye — WHY: the player's capsule shape is private and default-membership ~0, so it can't be layer-filtered out of the raycast; starting outside the capsule is the only way to avoid self-hits.\ninterview-t6-f92150-1\tdecision: Eye height set to 0.7 above capsule center — WHY: realistic first-person camera near the head, paired with the muzzle offset.\ninterview-t6-f92150-2\tdecision: `rayVsCapsule` rewritten as cylindrical-band + two end-cap sphere tests — WHY: the original `u` formula was wrong (missed valid center hits) and ignored end caps.\ninterview-t6-f92150-3\tdecision: player/bot vertical velocity zeroed on floor contact and clamped to -30 — WHY: without it, fall speed accumulates unboundedly while standing.\ninterview-t6-f92150-4\tdecision: crosshair positioned via `window.innerWidth/innerHeight`, not `canvas.width/height` — WHY: `TextLayer.positionPx` is in CSS pixels and the canvas is stretched to 100vw/100vh over fixed 1280×720 attrs.\ninterview-t6-f92150-5\tdecision: bot display quaternion corrected to `(0, sin(h/2), 0, cos(h/2))` — WHY: the original put cos in the qz slot and 0 in qw, a 180° rotation about a tilted axis instead of a Y-heading.\ninterview-t6-f92150-6\tdecision: `Debris.body` typed `PhysicsBody | null` with null guards — WHY: the `null as unknown as PhysicsBody` cast was a type-unsound hack.\ninterview-t6-f92150-7\tdecision: player spawns at standing height (terrain + CAP_HEIGHT/2 + 0.1), not +2 — WHY: +2 left the player floating ~1.1 units above the ground.\ninterview-t6-f92150-8\tdecision: restarted the dev server after edits — WHY: the long-running vite watcher served stale transforms in this sandbox, so a fresh process was needed to serve the latest code.\ninterview-t6-f92969-0\tgotcha: the long-running vite dev server serves stale module transforms in this sandbox — its file watcher didn't fire on my on-disk edits, so `curl` of `scene252.ts` still returned `EYE_HEIGHT = 1.5` after I changed it to `0.7` — IMPLICATION: restart the dev server (task_stop + relaunch `cd lab && LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite`) after editing scene files before playtesting, or verify served content via curl instead of assuming HMR picked up the change.\ninterview-t6-f92969-1\tgotcha: my bot display matrix had the wrong quaternion argument order for `mat4Compose` — I put `cos(h/2)` in the `qz` slot and `0` in `qw`, which is a 180° rotation about a tilted axis, not a Y-heading — IMPLICATION: a Y-axis rotation quaternion is `(qx=0, qy=sin(h/2), qz=0, qw=cos(h/2))`; check `mat4Compose` arg order `(tx,ty,tz,qx,qy,qz,qw,sx,sy,sz)` when composing per-frame thin-instance matrices.\ninterview-t6-f93897-0\tgotcha: the long-running vite dev server was serving a stale transform after I edited the file on disk (disk had `EYE_HEIGHT = 0.7` + `MUZZLE_OFFSET`, but the served module still showed `EYE_HEIGHT = 1.5` and no `MUZZLE_OFFSET`) — its file watcher doesn't fire on edits in this sandbox — IMPLICATION: after editing scene files, restart the dev server (`task_stop` + relaunch `cd lab && LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite`) or verify served content via curl before playtesting; don't assume HMR picked up the change. (Already recorded as r91869.)\ninterview-t6-f93897-1\tgotcha: `mat4Compose(tx, ty, tz, qx, qy, qz, qw, sx, sy, sz)` — a Y-axis heading rotation is `(0, sin(h/2), 0, cos(h/2))`; my first draft put `cos(h/2)` in the `qz` slot and `0` in `qw`, which is a 180° rotation about a tilted axis, not a heading — IMPLICATION: keep the quaternion as `(0, sin(h/2), 0, cos(h/2))` for bot heading; the capsule is radially symmetric so it doesn't change the look, but it matters if the display ever becomes asymmetric.\ninterview-t6-f94809-0\tgotcha: The long-running Vite dev server's file watcher does not pick up on-disk edits in this sandbox — after I edited `scene252.ts` (EYE_HEIGHT 1.5→0.7, added MUZZLE_OFFSET), curl against :5182 kept returning the stale transform (EYE_HEIGHT 1.5, no MUZZLE_OFFSET) even though the disk file was correct. — IMPLICATION: After editing scene files, restart the dev server (`task_stop` + relaunch `cd lab && LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite`) before playtesting, or verify served content via curl rather than assuming HMR worked.\ninterview-t6-f94809-1\tgotcha: `mat4Compose(tx,ty,tz,qx,qy,qz,qw,sx,sy,sz)` — I had the bot's heading quaternion as `(0, sin(h/2), cos(h/2), 0)`, which is a 180° rotation about a tilted axis, not a Y-heading; the correct Y-rotation is `(0, sin(h/2), 0, cos(h/2))`. — IMPLICATION: For a Y-axis heading, put `cos(h/2)` in the `qw` slot and `0` in `qz`; (cosmetic for a radially-symmetric capsule, but wrong for any asymmetric display).\ninterview-t6-f95458-0\tdecision: bot display matrix uses a Y-axis rotation quaternion `(0, sin(h/2), 0, cos(h/2))` for heading — WHY: the earlier arg order (cos in the `qz` slot) produced a 180° rotation about a tilted axis, and I kept the heading rotation even though a capsule is radially symmetric, to future-proof an asymmetric display.\ninterview-t6-f96340-0\tconstraint: Browser automation is blocked in this sandbox — Chrome SIGABRTs at launch (crashpad's Mach `bootstrap_check_in` and `~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad` are EPERM-denied, and the cached Playwright chromium build doesn't match the repo's playwright) — so no Playwright smoke/playtest is possible here; validation is lint + typecheck + dev-server module resolution + a user manual playtest on :5182.\ninterview-t6-f96340-1\tconstraint: The long-running vite dev server's file watcher does not pick up on-disk edits in this sandbox (it kept serving a stale transform) — after editing scene files, restart the dev server (or verify served content via curl) before playtesting, or you will test old code.\ninterview-t6-f96340-2\tconstraint: The character controller's capsule shape is private and carries Havok's default all-layers filter (`~0` membership), so it cannot be excluded from `physicsRaycast` via collision-layer masks — bullet rays must originate from a muzzle offset outside the capsule, never from the eye/center, or the player's own capsule occludes every terrain hit.\ninterview-t6-f96340-3\tconstraint: `PhysicsCharacterController.getPosition()` returns the capsule **center**, not the feet — eye height, spawn, and ground computations must apply the capsule half-height offset (feet = center − capsuleHeight/2).\ninterview-t6-f96340-4\tconstraint: scene252 is a game demo, not a parity scene — it must stay out of `scene-config.json`, `bundle-size.spec.ts`, and golden references; there is no bundle-size ceiling entry to add or raise for it.\ninterview-t7-0\tgotcha: Port 5182 was already answering (root → 200, scene252.html → 200) despite the user's report that nothing was listening — the vite dev server (bg_f4a1f424) had been running all along, and the served scene252.ts transform matches disk (EYE_HEIGHT 0.7, MUZZLE_OFFSET present), so no stale-transform issue — IMPLICATION: the user's problem is client-side (browser/network reachability, or WebGPU unavailable in their browser), not the server; I should tell them to load http://localhost:5182/lite/scene252.html in a WebGPU-enabled browser rather than restart anything.\ninterview-t7-f97347-0\tdecision: Keep the existing background vite server (bg_f4a1f424) as the dev server on :5182 rather than starting a new one — WHY: curl confirmed it answers (root and scene252.html → 200) and its served transform matches disk (EYE_HEIGHT = 0.7, MUZZLE_OFFSET = 0.8), so no restart was needed.\ninterview-t8-0\topen: Does mouse-look feel correct, or is the yaw/pitch sign convention inverted (unverified at runtime)?\ninterview-t8-1\topen: Does the HUD TextRenderer actually composite over the 