iterally. — IMPLICATION: retry the edit with the exact indentation from the file; the intended change itself (navmesh `maxObstacles`/`tileSize` + `mark()` stage markers) is still pending.\ninterview-t9-f111526-0\tgotcha: `addBoxObstacle` (navigation.ts:647) throws \"Navmesh has no tile cache. Build with `maxObstacles > 0` to enable obstacles\" — a solo navmesh (my current `createNavMesh` call) can't take dynamic obstacles — IMPLICATION: the navmesh must be built with `maxObstacles > 0` (tile cache; `tileSize` defaults to 32) or every tile destruction throws at runtime — fixed by adding `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` to the params in scene252.ts.\ninterview-t9-f111526-1\tgotcha: my first `edit` failed (0 occurrences) because I reconstructed `main()`'s text from memory — the on-disk file had diverged (separate `hknp` line, camera/light setup between engine and physics, different clearColor values) — IMPLICATION: always `read` the target region before editing; the compaction summary's recollection of exact code text is not reliable.\ninterview-t9-f112133-0\tdecision: scene252's navmesh is now built as a tile-cache navmesh (`maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` in the `createNavMesh` call) — WHY: `addBoxObstacle` (navigation.ts:647) throws \"Navmesh has no tile cache\" on a solo navmesh, so my tile-destruction path would have crashed on the first shot.\ninterview-t9-f112133-1\tdecision: `main()` in scene252.ts is instrumented with `console.warn` stage markers (engine/havok/terrain/nav-plugin/navmesh/bots/font/pre-register/registered/started, with ms offsets) — WHY: the spinner stall is an await that never settles (no error box, no rejection), and stage markers are the fastest way to pin down which stage hangs on the next reload; `console.warn` is the only console channel ESLint allows here.\ninterview-t9-f112133-2\tdecision: Restarted the lab dev server (stopped bg_f4a1f424, started bg_ec39a3f1 on :5182) after the edits — WHY: the long-running vite watcher in this sandbox 