tion\tfiles: listed lab/node_modules/@recast-navigation\nmechanical/listed:lab/public/recast-navigation.wasm\tfiles: listed lab/public/recast-navigation.wasm\nmechanical/listed:node_modules/@babylonjs\tfiles: listed node_modules/@babylonjs\nmechanical/listed:node_modules/@recast-navigation\tfiles: listed node_modules/@recast-navigation\nmechanical/package.json\tfiles: package.json\nmechanical/packages/babylon-lite/package.json\tfiles: packages/babylon-lite/package.json\nmechanical/packages/babylon-lite/src/navigation\tfiles: packages/babylon-lite/src/navigation\nmechanical/packages/babylon-lite/src/navigation/navigation.ts\tfiles: packages/babylon-lite/src/navigation/navigation.ts\nmechanical/scene252.ts\tfiles: scene252.ts\nmechanical/tests/lite/parity/bundle-size.spec.ts\tfiles: tests/lite/parity/bundle-size.spec.ts\nmechanical/vite.config.ts\tfiles: vite.config.ts\nr109646/call_1fbb82370ed6484a973e2436/gotcha\taddBoxObstacle/addCylinderObstacle (navigation.ts:647/663) throw \"Navmesh has no tile cache. Build with `maxObstacles > 0` to enable obstacles.\" unless createNavMesh was given maxObstacles > 0 — tile-cache config also needs tileSize + expectedLayersPerTime per navigation.ts:255 (doc example line 21: { maxObstacles: 32, tileSize: 32 }). scene252 builds a solo navmesh and calls addBoxObstacle in destroyTerrainTile → first terrain shot will throw. This is a runtime bug, NOT the init-spinner hang (which is still being diagnosed via stage markers).\nr11177/call_83149a63ed4b48e18cc9a43c/decision\tScope: turn the getting-started example into a Quake-style FPS as a new lab demo…\nr153869/call_e0ef6e82bad44a1191932a66/decision\tAdded an on-page init overlay to scene252 (the user's browser only yields a screenshot + an empty console). (1) scene252.html has an inline script that creates #fps252-init showing \"scene252.html loaded — waiting for module…\" before the module runs, plus window error/unhandledrejection handlers that append to it. (2) scene252.ts main() takes the element over (\"module loaded — init starting…\") and mark() appends each stage + ms; the catch block appends \"ERROR: <msg>\" in red. Rebuilt (vite build) and re-served via preview (bg_87050321 on :5182); verified the inline script is preserved in dist/lite/scene252.html and the take-over is in the chunk. Screenshot cases: only \"waiting for module…\" = HTML loaded but module never arrived; \"module loaded\" + stages = last stage is where init hangs; + \"ERROR:\" = init threw; no overlay at all = HTML itself didn't load.\nr167013/call_36307d024e324dbdb2f7d2b2/decision\tSwitched back to the dev server (bg_25106995 on :5182) — the production build/preview is the wrong tool: it stalls inside createEngine for ALL scenes (stock scene2 too), so it's a build/preview limitation, not scene252. On the dev server the browser reached engine/havok/terrain then stalled in the recast wasm load. Added a monkey-patch in scene252.ts main() (right after the mark() helper): WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming is replaced with a function that rejects, forcing the emscripten glue's catch to fall back to the ArrayBuffer path (WebAssembly.instantiate) for BOTH the recast and Havok wasm. New \"force-arraybuffer\" stage marker logs when it fires. Rationale: the recast glue (recast-navigation.wasm.js instantiateAsync) only falls back to ArrayBuffer on a rejection, so a never-settling streaming promise leaves the fallback unreachable. Awaiting user reload: past nav-plugin = fixed; still stops after terrain = ArrayBuffer doesn't rescue it; stops at havok = patch too blunt.\nr22627/call_731f2ddafab24ab79ace0962/plan\tFPS plan (Quake-style, tile-removal terrain) — new lab demo, NO engine changes:…\nr25861/call_7a361bc371cf49e581771afd/decision\tTerrain destruction = tile removal (user-approved): index surgery on one dense g…\nr35651/call_65a9672390dd40b18139c3bd/gotcha\tPhysicsCharacterController exposes friction as public fields (staticFriction def…\nr35651/call_6ab8a776fbbe4ff0996cd2e4/gotcha\tTwo distinct text paths exist: scene180 uses createTextRenderer (standalone 2D o…\nr35651/call_847e6d8ad46a49e8a9bd38d6/gotcha\tresizeMeshGeometry(engine, mesh, positions, normals, indices, uvs?, ...) in mesh…\nr37345/call_0005a55ea369431eb2e302a4/gotcha\tFreeCamera has no public yaw/pitch — only @internal _yaw/_pitch (free-camera.ts:…\nr37345/call_2fa6327821d246d6aeadf5c1/gotcha\tThe plan's terrain re-upload seam (raw uploadMeshToGPU + mesh._gpu swap) is wron…\nr37345/call_4bf6d56016a941f899f27e39/gotcha\tcreatePhysicsAggregate is typed `node: Mesh` (havok.ts:1141) — per-tile static b…\nr37345/call_532b6495b9ae43068115bf7f/decision\tController friction IS exposed — as public fields on PhysicsCharacterController:…\nr37345/call_7509c67d5e9749b1b0a76431/gotcha\tscene180's text path is standalone 2D (no scene, no camera — TextRenderer on the…\nr41338/call_caa2ea0f76064dc3b0e7fa9c/constraint\tS1 constraints surfaced: (1) terrain re-upload must use resizeMeshGeometry (bump…\nr63189/call_341bf58c985441b5a75ca83a/gotcha\tPlaywright smoke scripts in this sandbox: (1) system temp dir /var/folders/.../T is write-blocked — run node with TMPDIR pointed at a repo-local dir (e.g. TMPDIR=\"$PWD/.smoke-tmp\" node fps-smoke.cjs) or chromium.launch({tmpDir}) alone is not enough; (2) the repo's Playwright browser cache is missing the chromium headless shell — must run `pnpm exec playwright install` (never npx, per the rogue node_modules/playwright gotcha) before any Playwright launch works.\nr63755/call_be86e39b5d5c4e11ad52368a/gotcha\tOperational gotchas this session (sandbox + tooling): (1) `pnpm dev:lab` EPERMs (tsx IPC pipe in system temp) — use `LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite` from lab/ instead; (2) sandbox blocks /tmp and /var/folders T — scratch files go in-repo (delete before commit), node needs TMPDIR in-repo; (3) Playwright default launch fails (cached browser build 1243 vs playwright 1.58.2 expecting 1208) — launch `channel: \"chrome\"` + `--enable-unsafe-webgpu` (repo idiom); (4) computeNormals is number[]-based and createFlatGroundData/computeNormals need subpath imports (babylon-lite/mesh/*.js), not the barrel.\nr65273/call_1e7cec3d3238496f8a89ec80/gotcha\tBrowser automation is blocked in this sandbox: Playwright mkdtemp fails (sandbox denies /var/folders/T), bundled chromium build missing (cache has 1243, playwright 1.58.2 wants 1208), and system Chrome (channel: \"chrome\", headed or headless) SIGABRTs at launch because crashpad bootstrap + ~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome are EPERM. IMPLICATION: no Playwright smoke/playtest possible this session — validation is lint + typecheck + user manual playtest on :5182.\nr65273/call_e94c2b70aad3480cb99b67bb/gotcha\t`pnpm dev:lab` fails in this sandbox (its tsx bundle-build step needs an IPC pipe in the system temp dir → EPERM). Working alternative: `cd lab && LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite` (verified serving on 5182, scene252.html → 200).\nr91558/call_1569cb1f591a4fe682afe311/decision\tSelf-hit problem solved via muzzle offset, not layer filtering: the character controller's capsule shape is private (can't call setPhysicsShapeFilterMembershipMask on it) and its default membership is ~0 (belongs to every layer), so a physicsRaycast can never be filtered to exclude the player's own capsule. Fix: cast the bullet ray from a point MUZZLE_OFFSET (0.8) in front of the eye (outside the 0.5 capsule radius) so the ray never starts inside the player body. EYE_HEIGHT set to 0.7 (eye near head, center+0.7).\nr91784/call_04d1c180396b4941b6968645/gotcha\tBrowser automation is blocked in this sandbox: Playwright's bundled chromium build is missing (cache has 1243, playwright 1.58.2 wants 1208) and system Chrome (channel:\"chrome\") SIGABRTs at launch because crashpad's Mach bootstrap_check_in + ~/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Crashpad are EPERM-denied. IMPLICATION: no Playwright smoke/playtest possible this session — validation is lint + typecheck + dev-server module-graph resolution (curl each module through vite, confirm 200 + imports resolve to /@fs/... source paths).\nr91869/call_dfb9616e51df42a6bdb365a4/gotcha\tThe long-running vite dev server's file watcher does NOT pick up edits in this sandbox — it kept serving a stale transform (EYE_HEIGHT 1.5) after I changed the file on disk (EYE_HEIGHT 0.7). IMPLICATION: after editing scene files, restart the dev server (task_stop + relaunch `cd lab && LAB_DEV_PORT=5182 pnpm exec vite`) before playtesting, or verify served content via curl rather than assuming HMR worked.\n92 older entries shortened\n","render_budget_tokens":40000,"render_fits":true,"render_over_budget":"tier","render_reduced":92,"render_tokens":39826,"seq":171624,"t":10441965,"tail_tokens":4000,"tool_outputs":"reference","window":163840}
