ansform rewrites to.\n\nPOINTER: `const navPromise = createNavigationPluginAsync(...)` is kicked off *before* `await HavokPhysics` — the parallel-load restructure is actually in the file (main() in scene252.ts), so recast's three modules had to arrive during the engine→havok window\nPOINTER: all of it is temporary instrumentation to delete before commit (GUIDANCE §0b): the `#fps252-init` overlay takeover, `mark()` stage markers, `canvas.dataset.initMs/ready/error`, and the `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` monkey-patch (main() in scene252.ts + the inline script in scene252.html)\nPOINTER: `createNavMesh` already carries `maxObstacles: 64, tileSize: 32` (tile-cache build), so `destroyTerrainTile`'s `addBoxObstacle` won't throw — runtime-verify in playtest (main() in scene252.ts)\nPOINTER: `main().catch` writes `ERROR:` to the overlay and `dataset.error` — any later rejection will be visible on-page; today's silence confirms nothing rejected (tail of main() in scene252.ts)\nPOINTER: still-unverified runtime assumptions parked in the file: `/fonts/Inter.ttf` exists under lab/public, text renderer composites over the 3D frame (`clear: false`, registered after the scene), debris reads `body.node` transforms back from the physics world, and bot agent/controller drift re-sync (`agentGoto` when >4u apart) doesn't oscillate (main() in scene252.ts)\nPOINTER: `scene.fixedDeltaMs = 1000 / PHYSICS_FPS` is what makes the 60 Hz steps exist — if player/bot movement ever freezes, check this first (main() in scene252.ts)","timings":{"cache_n":67584,"draft_n":11697,"draft_n_accepted":3667,"predicted_ms":136700.0,"predicted_n":5338,"prompt_ms":24810.0,"prompt_n":8937},"to_request":176155,"usage":{"cached_tokens":67584,"completion_tokens":5338,"prompt_tokens":76521}}
