{"items":[{"key":"compaction-11/message-78","score":4,"sha256":"bf068e94b280af797161c329a9dfc3175a5eb81b1b057ea2a9fd5762f61c1dc0"},{"key":"compaction-15/message-56","score":3,"sha256":"d6de8cdf8cdd0525b6f3ff66c3cef7986ee3c9d70df82bee59d15f401547f0cd"},{"key":"compaction-15/message-45","score":3,"sha256":"e8e7d3ce1627a53ea470aa2faca6b8bf83d8c9e75cb47617391aaa4a1e3892db"}],"kind":"recalled","recall":"literal","seq":185707,"t":11229111,"text":"<system-reminder>\n## Relevant memory\n\nUse the following memories only when they are directly relevant to the current request. Verify file/function claims before relying on them.\n\n### an answer (compaction-11/message-78)\n\nFixed and serving. Here's what I found and changed.\n\n**Root cause** — the hang is the Recast navmesh wasm being the *second* wasm module to compile (via `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming`) after the 2 MB Havok wasm. Evidence:\n- Node loads Havok→recast cleanly in 64 ms via `WebAssembly.instantiate` (ArrayBuffer path) → no JS/wasm collision between the two emscripten modules.\n- The served `/recast-navigation.wasm` is valid (`application/wasm` MIME, byte-identical to disk).\n- scene252 is the **only** scene that loads both wasm modules — every recast scene (170–175) is recast-only, so there's no working \"both\" reference.\n- Terrain init was <90 ms, so it's not the 1024 static bodies.\n\n**The change** (`scene252.ts`, `main()`) — the two loads are independent, so I kick off the Recast load before the Havok await and await it after the player is set up. Now the two wasm modules compile in parallel instead of serially:\n\n```ts\nconst navPromise = createNavigationPluginAsync({ locateFile: () => \"/recast-navigation.wasm\" });\nconst hknp = await HavokPhysics({ locateFile: () => \"/HavokPhysics.wasm\" });\n// ... terrain, player ...\nconst nav = await navPromise;\n```\n\nLab typecheck passes and the resta […]\n\n> NOTE: Relevant memory truncated for prompt budget.\n\n### a step that called tools (compaction-15/message-56)\n\n[…] ng tool — it stalls inside `createEngine` for *every* scene, including stock scene2, so it's a build/preview limitation, not your scene). On the dev server your browser made real progress (engine → havok → terrain) before stalling in the recast wasm load.\n\n**The fix I'm testing:** the recast glue (`recast-navigation.wasm.js`) tries `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` first and only falls back to the ArrayBuffer path if that call *rejects* — a hang (never-settling) leaves the fallback unreachable. So I made `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` reject on purpose, forcing both wasm modules onto the ArrayBuffer path (`WebAssembly.instantiate`). There's a new `force-arraybuffer` stage marker so we can confirm it fired.\n\nReload `http://localhost:5182/lite/scene252.html` and send a screenshot. The green box will now tell us one of three things:\n\n- **It gets past `nav-plugin` and the scene loads** → the ArrayBuffer path is the fix; the streaming compile was the culprit.\n- **It still stops after `terrain` (no `nav-plugin`)** → the ArrayBuffer path doesn't rescue the recast load either, so the stall is somewhere else in the wasm init (I'll instrument deeper).\n- **It stops at `force-arraybuffer` […]\n\n> NOTE: Relevant memory truncated for prompt budget.\n\n### a tool result (compaction-15/message-45)\n\n[…] tion abort(what){Module[\"onAbort\"]?.(what);what=\"Aborted(\"+what+\")\";err(what);ABORT=true;what+=\". Build with -sASSERTIONS for more info.\";var e=new WebAssembly.RuntimeError(what);readyPromiseReject?.(e);throw e}var wasmBinaryFile;function findWasmBinary(){if(Module[\"locateFile\"]){return locateFile(\"recast-navigation.wasm.wasm\")}return new URL(\"recast-navigation.wasm.wasm\",import.meta.url).href}function getBinarySync(file){if(file==wasmBinaryFile&&wasmBinary){return new Uint8Array(wasmBinary)}if(readBinary){return readBinary(file)}throw\"both async and sync fetching of the wasm failed\"}async function getWasmBinary(binaryFile){if(!wasmBinary){try{var response=await readAsync(binaryFile);return new Uint8Array(response)}catch{}}return getBinarySync(binaryFile)}async function instantiateArrayBuffer(binaryFile,imports){try{var binary=await getWasmBinary(binaryFile);var instance=await WebAssembly.instantiate(binary,imports);return instance}catch(reason){err(`failed to asynchronously prepare wasm: ${reason}`);abort(reason)}}async function instantiateAsync(binary,binaryFile,imports){if(!binary&&typeof WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming==\"function\"){try{var response=fetch(binaryFile,{credential […]\n\n> NOTE: Relevant memory truncated for prompt budget.\n\n</system-reminder>","turn":16}
