{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Interesting findings:\n\n1. The glue file on disk is only **559,543 bytes** (559KB), NOT 2MB! But curl to the served URL returned **2,074,587 bytes** (2.07MB). So the served transform is 3.7x the size of the file on disk!\n\nWait, that's weird. Vite's transform shouldn't bloat a file by 3.7x... unless the transform is doing something special. Or — wait, the served URL I curled earlier was `/@fs/.../wasm/dist/recast-navigation.wasm.js?v=ec16f4b0` and returned 2074587 bytes. Hmm, but the file on disk is 559543 bytes.\n\nHold on — could the served content be something completely different? Or does Vite's transform inline something? Let me think... Vite's dev transform for a JS file: parses with esbuild, rewrites imports, and may prepend helper code. It shouldn't grow 3.7x.\n\nWait — maybe the response I curled wasn't the transform of this file. What if the `?v=ec16f4b0` URL hit a different file? No — the path is explicit.\n\nOr — is Vite serving the file with source maps inlined? No, that's not it.\n\nHmm, wait — actually, let me double-check: is the 2MB response maybe an error page or an HTML fallback? 2074587 bytes of what? Let me curl and look at the content — head/tail and grep for \"recast\" etc.\n\nActually — oh, wait. I think I get what's happening! Vite's dev server, for files excluded from optimizeDeps, that are inside node_modules... the `/@fs/` path serves the file with import analysis. But there's a known Vite behavior: if a file is a dependency and not pre-bundled, Vite may serve it as-is. A 3.7x bloat is bizarre.\n\nLet me look at the actual content of the served response. Also, the second command's grep for the exact glue URL returned nothing — the pattern `import\\(\"[^\"]*wasm/wasm[^\"]*\"\\)` didn't match. Maybe the URL in the transform doesn't contain \"wasm/wasm\" (the subpath `@recast-navigation/wasm/wasm` resolves to `dist/recast-navigation.wasm.js` — the URL contains `@recast-navigation+wasm@0.43.0` and `recast-navigation.wasm.js`, but the literal string \"wasm/wasm\" doesn't appear). My grep pattern was wrong. Let me re-grep with the `recast-navigation.wasm.js` pattern.\n\n2. The glue file has no imports at all (grep found nothing — no `import(...)`, no `from \"...\"`, no `require`). It's a self-contained IIFE that ends with `export default Recast;`. So no nested module load. The file ends properly (`export default Recast;`).\n\n3. The dev server log is clean (no errors).\n\nSo the mystery: the file on disk is 559KB, but the served response is 2.07MB. What is Vite doing?\n\nHmm, wait — actually, let me reconsider. Maybe the 2.07MB response is Vite serving the file with an inlined source map? Or... does Vite add a big banner? No.\n\nOr — maybe the response is a different file: if the `?v=ec16f4b0` URL is being handled by Vite's dep optimizer as a pre-bundled chunk... no, it's excluded.\n\nLet me just curl the served URL and inspect the content: first 500 bytes, last 500 bytes, grep for characteristic strings. And also curl without ?v=.\n\nActually — hmm, wait. I recall that Vite's dev server, for JS files in node_modules that aren't pre-bundled, serves them with the same transform pipeline as source files. The transform output for a file with no imports should be roughly the same size as the input (+ a small header). 559KB → 2.07MB is impossible from a normal transform.\n\nUnless the response is actually an HTML error page repeated, or Vite is concatenating... let me just look.\n\nAnother possibility: is my `wc -c` pointing at the wrong file? The path: `node_modules/.pnpm/@recast-navigation+wasm@0.43.0/node_modules/@recast-navigation/wasm/dist/recast-navigation.wasm.js` — 559543 bytes. And the served URL is exactly that file (via /@fs/). Let me verify by comparing content hashes: curl the served URL (without ?v=) and sha256 it, and sha256 the file on disk.\n\nIf the served content ≠ disk content, then Vite is doing something unexpected — and that \"something\" might be exactly what's hanging the browser (e.g., the transform is huge/slow, or the response is malformed).\n\nWait, actually — hold on. I just remembered! Vite has a behavior where it injects `import.meta.url` handling and also rewrites `new URL(..., import.meta.url)`... but a 3.7x bloat?\n\nOr — maybe the served response includes the file plus an inline source map appended as a data URL? Vite dev serves JS with `sourceMappingURL` as a separate file (not inline). Hmm.\n\nLet me also reconsider: maybe the 2.07MB figure is wrong — could curl have followed a redirect to a big page? No, it was 200.\n\nLet me inspect the content right now.\n\nActually — one more possibility: **the `?v=ec16f4b0` hash makes Vite treat the URL as an optimized dep request**, and the optimizer is serving a cached pre-bundle of something big (like the whole barrel). But the path contains the full /@fs/ path — the optimizer serves under /node_modules/.vite/deps/. Not under /@fs/.\n\nOK, let me just look at the content. Commands:\n1. `curl -s \"http://localhost:5182/@fs/$PWD/node_modules/.pnpm/@recast-navigation+wasm@0.43.0/node_modules/@recast-navigation/wasm/dist/recast-navigation.wasm.js\" -o .smoke-tmp/served_glue.js` — wait, /tmp is blocked; use .smoke-tmp/ in the repo (already exists? I have lab/.smoke-tmp and .smoke-tmp on hand). Let me use lab/.smoke-tmp/.\n2. `wc -c` on the saved file, `head -c 400`, `tail -c 400`, `sha256` of both the saved file and the file on disk.\n3. Grep the navigation.ts transform for the actual glue URL (pattern `recast-navigation.wasm.js`).\n\nLet me run these.\n","seq":190045,"t":11475666,"text":"\n\nI found a discrepancy: the glue file on disk is 559 KB but the served response is 2.07 MB, and the glue module has no imports so evaluation shouldn't hang. I'll inspect the served content to figure out what's different.\n\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":101120,"draft_n":4361,"draft_n_accepted":1305,"predicted_ms":57870.0,"predicted_n":1928,"prompt_ms":4