ended (so served size ≈ 4–5x disk size) — confirmed by sha256 comparison + grep. This is a tooling fact about the dev server's behavior.\n- Confirmed: the recast glue module is self-contained (no imports) — so the import hang is not in a nested module graph.\n- Confirmed: the server side is healthy (log clean, curl fast) — the stall is client-side.\n- Updated working hypothesis: the stall correlates with the 2.07MB served response size (two smaller modules with the same treatment settled) — so the next fix candidate is reducing the served response (stripping/disabling the inline source map for @recast-navigation/*, or another delivery path), not more glue instrumentation.\n\nI haven't yet decided on a concrete tooling change (I haven't edited the config), so I should be honest: these are confirmations + a changed hypothesis, not an implemented decision. The prompt says \"make, confirm, or change\" — so confirmations count.\n\nLet me write it concisely, one per line:\n\nDECISION: (confirmed) Vite dev serves these /@fs/ node_modules modules with an inline base64 source map appended — served size is ~4–5x disk size (glue: 559KB disk → 2.07MB served) — WHY: sha256 mismatch + `sourceMappingURL=data:application/json;base64` at the tail; this is normal dev behavior, not corruption.\n\nDECISION: (confirmed) the recast glue module is self-contained (no imports, ends with `export default Recast`) — WHY: grep found zero import/require statements, so the stuck import cannot be a nested module load.\n\nDECISION: (confirmed) the stall is client-side, not server-side — WHY: dev server log is clean and curl fetches the full 2.07MB in <200ms, while the browser's import never settles.\n\nDECISION: (changed hypothesis) the distinguishing factor is the ~2MB served response size: core (506KB served) and generators (206KB served) settled in the browser, but the glue (2.07MB served) did not — WHY: the next move is testing reduced-size delivery (strip/disable the inline source map for @recast-navigation/*) or isolating with a minimal test page, rather than more emscripten instrumentation.\n\nThat seems right. I'll keep it brief.\n","seq":197274,"t":11861711,"text":"\n\nDECISION: (confirmed) the Vite dev server serves these `/@fs/` node_modules modules with an inline base64 source map appended — served size is ~4–5× disk size (glue: 559 KB disk → 2.07 MB served; core: 102 KB → 507 KB; generators: 43 KB → 206 KB) — WHY: sha256 mismatch plus `sourceMappingURL=data:application/json;base64` at the tail, so the bloat is normal dev behavior, not a truncated/corrupt transform.\n\nDECISION: (confirmed) the recast glue module is self-contained — zero import/require statements, ends `export default Recast;` — WHY: the stuck import therefore cannot be a nested module load; the hang is in delivery/evaluation of this single response.\n\nDECISION: (confirmed) the stall is client-side, not server-side — WHY: the dev-server log is clean and curl fetches the full 2.07 MB in <200 ms, while the browser's import never settles (and never rejects — no error box, spinner still animating).\n\nDECISION: (changed working hypothesis) the distinguishing factor is the ~2 MB served response size — core (507 KB served) and generators (206 KB served) settled in the browser but the glue (2.07 MB served) did not — WHY: the next experiment should be size-reduced delivery (strip/disable the inline source map for `@recast-navigation/*`, or a minimal test page) rather than more emscripten-glue instrumentation.","timings":{"cache_n":108032,"draft_n":3955,"draft_n_accepted":1351,"predicted_ms":56410.0,"predicted_n":1916,"prompt_ms":480.0,"prompt_n":123},"to_request":196127,"usage":{"cached_tokens":108032,"completion_tokens":1916,"prompt_tokens":108155}}
