{"items":[{"key":"compaction-15/message-40","score":1,"sha256":"53a1b2cf040f4779b795892e281700f2002d268d668494a7c9d8401402a55a60"},{"key":"compaction-15/message-56","score":1,"sha256":"d6de8cdf8cdd0525b6f3ff66c3cef7986ee3c9d70df82bee59d15f401547f0cd"},{"key":"compaction-15/message-41","score":1,"sha256":"8b49db4e83bb106819986d8aa2bc910472306c0277185ed1b1b8af07aa6d1e27"}],"kind":"recalled","recall":"literal","seq":197948,"t":11930582,"text":"<system-reminder>\n## Relevant memory\n\nUse the following memories only when they are directly relevant to the current request. Verify file/function claims before relying on them.\n\n### a step that called tools (compaction-15/message-40)\n\nThe nav plugin loads recast via `core.init(wasmFactory(...))` inside `_ensureRecast` (navigation.ts:136) — the emscripten glue tries `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` first and only falls back to the ArrayBuffer path if that *rejects*. A hang (never-settling) leaves the fallback unreachable, which matches your symptom exactly. Let me confirm the glue's fallback logic, then force the ArrayBuffer path.\n\n\nbash {\"command\": \"cd ~/git/reference/Babylon/Babylon-Lite\\necho \\\"=== find the recast wasm glue (factory) ===\\\"\\nfind lab/node_modules/@recast-navigation -name \\\"*.js\\\" 2>/dev/null | head\\necho\\necho \\\"=== instantiateStreaming / fallback in the glue ===\\\"\\nG=$(find lab/node_modules/@recast-navigation -path \\\"*wasm*\\\" -name \\\"*.js\\\" 2>/dev/null | head -1)\\necho \\\"glue: $G\\\"\\ngrep -o \\\"instantiateStreaming\\\\|instantiateArrayBuffer\\\\|instantiate(\\\" \\\"$G\\\" 2>/dev/null | sort | uniq -c\\necho\\necho \\\"=== context around instantiateStreaming (the fallback) ===\\\"\\ngrep -n \\\"instantiateStreaming\\\" \\\"$G\\\" 2>/dev/null | head\"}\n\n### a step that called tools (compaction-15/message-56)\n\n[…] the wrong tool — it stalls inside `createEngine` for *every* scene, including stock scene2, so it's a build/preview limitation, not your scene). On the dev server your browser made real progress (engine → havok → terrain) before stalling in the recast wasm load.\n\n**The fix I'm testing:** the recast glue (`recast-navigation.wasm.js`) tries `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` first and only falls back to the ArrayBuffer path if that call *rejects* — a hang (never-settling) leaves the fallback unreachable. So I made `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` reject on purpose, forcing both wasm modules onto the ArrayBuffer path (`WebAssembly.instantiate`). There's a new `force-arraybuffer` stage marker so we can confirm it fired.\n\nReload `http://localhost:5182/lite/scene252.html` and send a screenshot. The green box will now tell us one of three things:\n\n- **It gets past `nav-plugin` and the scene loads** → the ArrayBuffer path is the fix; the streaming compile was the culprit.\n- **It still stops after `terrain` (no `nav-plugin`)** → the ArrayBuffer path doesn't rescue the recast load either, so the stall is somewhere else in the wasm init (I'll instrument deeper).\n- **It stops at `force-array […]\n\n> NOTE: Relevant memory truncated for prompt budget.\n\n### a tool result (compaction-15/message-41)\n\n=== find the recast wasm glue (factory) ===\n\n=== instantiateStreaming / fallback in the glue ===\nglue: \n\n=== context around instantiateStreaming (the fallback) ===\n\n</system-reminder>","turn":17}
