{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"The config file imports `createReadStream, existsSync, readdirSync, readFileSync, statSync` from \"fs\" — we need `readFile` (async) — let's add it to the import list. And define the plugin before `export default`.\n\nLet's write the plugin. Place it right before `export default defineConfig({...})` (around line 714). Let me check what's immediately before line 716 to position the edit.\n\nActually, let's just insert the plugin function definition before `export default defineConfig(` and add it to the plugins array.\n\nPlugin:\n\n```ts\n/**\n * Serve @recast-navigation dist files raw, bypassing Vite's dev transform.\n * Vite dev appends an inline base64 source map to every served module; for the\n * 560 KB recast glue that bloats the response to ~2 MB, which the lab's\n * constrained test browser cannot finish within its per-page load window (the\n * module import never settles — no rejection, just a stall). The three dist\n * files (core, generators, wasm glue) are self-contained native ESM with no\n * imports to rewrite, so raw bytes are a drop-in replacement.\n */\nfunction serveRecastRawPlugin(): Plugin {\n    return {\n        name: \"serve-recast-raw\",\n        configureServer(server) {\n            server.middlewares.use((req, res, next) => {\n                const url = (req.url ?? \"\").split(\"?\")[0];\n                if (!url.startsWith(\"/@fs/\") || !url.includes(\"/@recast-navigation/\")) {\n                    next();\n                    return;\n                }\n                const fsPath = url.slice(\"/@fs/\".length);\n                readFile(fsPath, (err, data) => {\n                    if (err) {\n                        next();\n                        return;\n                    }\n                    res.statusCode = 200;\n                    res.setHeader(\"Content-Type\", \"text/javascript; charset=utf-8\");\n                    res.setHeader(\"Cache-Control\", \"no-cache\");\n                    res.end(data);\n                });\n            });\n        },\n    };\n}\n```\n\nWait — one issue: URL-decoding of `+`. In `req.url`, the path comes as-is from the HTTP request line. The browser requests `/@fs/.../@recast-navigation+core@0.43.0/...` — does the browser percent-encode `+`? `+` is a valid character in the path segment (sub-delim); browsers don't encode it. curl didn't encode it either. So req.url contains the literal `+`. The filesystem path also contains `+`. A direct slice works.\n\nBut — what if some client percent-encodes something (e.g., `@` → %40)? `@` is also valid unencoded in a path. Vite's own /@fs/ middleware handles the raw path the same way. To be safe, we could decodeURIComponent before readFile and fall back to next() on error. Let's keep it simple: try the raw path first; on error, try decodeURIComponent; on error, next(). Actually — let's just do this:\n\n```ts\nconst fsPath = url.slice(\"/@fs/\".length);\nconst candidates = [fsPath, decodeURIComponent(fsPath)];\n```\n\nHmm, that's getting complicated. Vite's own /@fs/ handler uses the raw path (fs.allow check + fs.readFile on the raw path). The browser that got these URLs from Vite's rewritten transform will request them exactly as Vite wrote them — no encoding. Keep it simple: raw path, fall back to next() on error.\n\nAlso, add `readFile` to the fs import line.\n\nEdit 1: import line:\n`import { createReadStream, existsSync, readdirSync, readFileSync, statSync } from \"fs\";`\n→\n`import { createReadStream, existsSync, readFile, readdirSync, readFileSync, statSync } from \"fs\";`\n\nEdit 2: Insert the plugin before `export default defineConfig({` and add it to the plugins array:\n`plugins: [pagesDemoPlugin(), compatScenesPlugin(), serveReferenceImages(), apiDocsPlugin(), tabContentPlugin()],`\n→\n`plugins: [pagesDemoPlugin(), compatScenesPlugin(), serveReferenceImages(), apiDocsPlugin(), tabContentPlugin(), serveRecastRawPlugin()],`\n\nWhere to insert the function definition — right before `export default defineConfig({`. Let me check the context of lines 710–716.\n\nThen:\n- Run pnpm lint:fix (or just verify with tsc — the lint script covers eslint + tsc).\n- Restart the dev server.\n- Verify the glue being served: size 559543, tail \"export default Recast;\", no sourceMappingURL.\n- Verify the core/gens being served: size 101997 / 42989.\n- Ask the user to hard-reload recast-test.html, then scene252.html.\n\nFirst, let's check the context of lines 705–716.\n","seq":201590,"t":12172557,"text":"","timings":{"cache_n":122880,"draft_n":2233,"draft_n_accepted":851,"predicted_ms":33130.0,"predicted_n":1170,"prompt_ms":10070.0,"prompt_n":2375},"to_request":200954,"usage":{"cached_tokens":122880,"completion_tokens":1170,"prompt_tokens":125255}}
