{"entry":{"id":"r202162/call_28dfcf84043d47d18ae936b5/decision","text":"ROOT CAUSE (confirmed by isolation): the recast glue module import stalls in the user's browser on EVERY page (scene170 too — the \"scene170 works\" premise was never verified). Mechanism: Vite dev appends an inline base64 source map to every served module; the 560KB glue becomes a 2.07MB response that the constrained test browser (≈8s per-page window) never finishes, while ≤507KB modules and 2MB plain fetch() of HavokPhysics.wasm complete. Fix: serveRecastRawPlugin in lab/vite.config.ts — dev-server middleware serving @recast-navigation dist files raw from disk (all three are self-contained native ESM, zero imports, so no Vite rewrite needed). Verified served sizes now = disk sizes (102KB/43KB/560KB). Dev server bg_8cef3683 on :5182. NOTE: this also explains the original \"recast streaming stall\" — the glue never loaded, so instantiateStreaming was never reached; the force-arraybuffer patch in scene252.ts may now be unnecessary (recast-test.html uses the real streaming path and will confirm)."},"kind":"patch","lane":"self-capture","op":"add","seq":202612,"t":12253982}
