{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"The user is asking me to enumerate the constraints that surfaced in the previous step (the step where I added serveRecastRawPlugin, restarted the server, verified the size, and kicked off lint).\n\nConstraints that surfaced in that step:\n\n1. **The lab's constrained test browser has a per-page load window of about 8 seconds** — module responses that don't complete within that window leave the import pending forever (neither fulfilled nor rejected). Anything served to that browser must complete within the window. Specifically: Vite dev's inline base64 source maps bloat module responses (the 560KB glue became 2.07MB), which is what caused the stall. Therefore: large node_modules modules served via Vite dev (with inline maps) can exceed the window — this is the environmental constraint that drove the fix.\n\n2. **The three @recast-navigation dist files must be served raw (bypassing Vite's transform)** — serveRecastRawPlugin in lab/vite.config.ts exists precisely because Vite dev's inline source map bloat breaks the constrained browser. Removing/disabling this plugin will bring the stall back. This is a \"must not do\" constraint: don't re-enable Vite's transform for these files, and don't remove the plugin.\n\nIs the raw-serving plugin constraint \"surfaced in this step\"? Yes — I created it in this step, and its comment block records the reason. The constraint is: @recast-navigation's dist files must be served raw (no Vite transform / inline source map) in the dev server, or the test browser will stall on the glue import.\n\n3. Another point from this step: all three recast dist files are self-contained native ESM with zero imports — this is a fact, not a constraint. It's what makes raw serving possible.\n\n4. The dev server must be restarted after configuration changes (because the plugin lives in vite.config.ts) — this is already a known pattern (stale transform gotcha), and not something new in this step.\n\n5. Lint gate: `pnpm run lint:fix` followed by `pnpm run lint` after code changes — this is an existing constraint, not something new in this step.\n\nSo the constraints from this step are:\n- The lab's test browser has a per-page load window of about 8 seconds; module responses that don't complete within it hang forever (no rejection) — so anything served to that browser must complete within the window.\n- Vite dev inlines base64 source maps into every served module response; for the 560KB recast glue this bloats it to 2.07MB and breaks the window — therefore @recast-navigation's dist files must be served raw via serveRecastRawPlugin (lab/vite.config.ts); removing the plugin, or routing these files through Vite's transform again, will bring the import stall back.\n\nThese two are essentially one constraint with a mechanism attached. Let me write them as separate lines: one for the environmental limit (the browser's window), one for the compatibility rule (raw serving must be maintained).\n\nKeep it concise — only constraints from this step.\n","seq":204869,"t":12402552,"text":"\n\nCONSTRAINT: The lab's test browser has a ~8-second per-page load window; a module response that doesn't complete within it leaves the import pending forever (no rejection, no error) — so anything served to that browser must deliver within the window, and \"no console error + spinner\" means a stalled response, not a failed one.\nCONSTRAINT: Vite dev appends an inline base64 source map to every served module (the 560 KB recast glue becomes a 2.07 MB response, which is what stalls the window) — the @recast-navigation dist files must keep being served raw via `serveRecastRawPlugin` in `lab/vite.config.ts`; removing the plugin or routing those files back through Vite's transform reintroduces the import stall on every recast page (scene170 included).","timings":{"cache_n":130048,"draft_n":1771,"draft_n_accepted":594,"predicted_ms":16270.0,"predicted_n":847,"prompt_ms":900.0,"prompt_n":315},"to_request":204612,"usage":{"cached_tokens":130048,"completion_tokens":847,"prompt_tokens":130363}}
